<node id="Hydrocalumite">
  <data key="d0">Hydrocalumite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrocalumite is a calcium aluminate hydrate compound formed as a stable solid product during the precipitation of calcium and aluminum species.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrocalumite is a green synthesized material used for effective removal of acid red 97 dye from wastewater.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrocalumite is a mineral phase represented by an open triangle symbol in the XRD graph, observed in the 12% CaCO3 sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037</data>
