<node id="Potassium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium sulfate (K₂SO₄) is a versatile, water-soluble sulfate compound that functions primarily as a critical industrial raw material and an effective agricultural potassium fertilizer. In agricultural applications, it serves as a reliable potash fertilizer, while in industrial contexts, it operates as a chemical additive, notably used alongside carbide slag to enhance activation effects. The compound is predominantly synthesized from phosphogypsum (PG), synthetic gypsum, or washed gypsum through various aqueous and wet conversion techniques. Key production pathways include chloride hydrometallurgy, double decomposition reactions with potassium chloride (KCl), co-reactions with potassium feldspar, and direct treatments involving potassium hydroxide (KOH) and carbon dioxide (CO₂) within thermostatic jackets. It can also be generated via one-step or two-step synthesis processes, sometimes utilizing potassium carbonate (K₂CO₃).

Beyond intentional synthesis, potassium sulfate frequently emerges as a secondary byproduct in chemical reactions, particularly during the hydrothermal conversion of phosphogypsum to hydroxyapatite or other PG transformation processes. Following its formation, whether as a primary target or a byproduct, the compound is consistently isolated and purified through filtration, separation, and evaporation techniques to achieve the high purity required for commercial and agricultural use. Despite the development of multiple synthesis routes and its established utility in both chemical and agricultural sectors, a fully commercialized method for large-scale production from phosphogypsum remains undeveloped.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791967536</data>
