<node id="Carbon Dioxide">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Dioxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon Dioxide is a gaseous chemical compound and a rapidly increasing greenhouse gas that plays a multifaceted role across environmental science, industrial chemistry, and biological research. As a prominent atmospheric gas, it is characterized by a distinct spectral peak near 2350 cm^-1. Its rising emissions have spurred the development of advanced capture technologies, such as the PSC Technology, to mitigate its environmental impact. Industrially, Carbon Dioxide is frequently generated as a byproduct during processes like the water-gas shift reaction in lignite gasification, the reaction between calcium sulfate and coke, sulfate reduction by carbon, and the total oxidation of volatile organic compounds, and is commonly denoted as CO2↑ to indicate its gaseous state.

A significant focus of Carbon Dioxide management lies in mineral carbonation and sequestration, particularly when utilizing backfill materials, mine tailings, and phosphogypsum. During the thermal treatment of phosphogypsum, Carbon Dioxide is released in the third stage of mass loss and can be extracted from slag and hydrolyzed liquid phases. It is subsequently processed in low-cost carbonation reactions to yield stable calcium carbonate and occasionally potassium sulfate. When incorporated into ternary binder systems, this approach reduces Carbon Dioxide release by up to 57%. The gas readily dissolves in water during carbonation to initiate acid formation, with its solubility increasing in basic media to facilitate carbonate ion absorption during synthesis. Additionally, Carbon Dioxide can be adsorbed or captured from the atmosphere during chemical precipitation processes.

In material synthesis, Carbon Dioxide exhibits versatile chemical behaviors, particularly in the precipitation synthesis of hydroxyapatite. It dissolves in water during this process, influencing lattice parameters and acting as an atmospheric impurity that becomes trapped in the hydroxyapatite structure. This impurity partially substitutes phosphate groups without adverse effects, though it typically disappears upon calcination. Carbon Dioxide also actively reacts with Portlandite to form calcite, a property utilized in feldspar pellet processing, and is employed in controlled atmospheres to synthesize type A apatite from hydroxyapatite. The efficiency of these catalytic processes is often evaluated using carriers like PG-CuFe2O4.

Beyond industrial and materials applications, Carbon Dioxide is extensively utilized in biological and laboratory contexts. It is maintained at a 5% concentration in incubators to support cell culture physiology, while in specialized botanical setups, it is naturally supplied by plant hairs into micro-basins to facilitate targeted chemical interactions. Collectively, these diverse applications highlight Carbon Dioxide's versatility as both a critical environmental factor requiring mitigation and a highly functional reagent across scientific and industrial domains.&lt;SEP&gt;A gas whose content is determined via titration with potassium hydroxide, utilizing a conversion factor of 44.01 g/mol.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon Dioxide is a gaseous byproduct generated during the initial carbon reduction of calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;A gaseous product generated from the carbothermal reduction of calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon dioxide is a gaseous product formed during the reduction of iron(III) oxide and is accelerated in diffusion by aluminosilicate glass.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon dioxide is a gaseous byproduct released during the initial reaction stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Gaseous byproduct released during the initial reaction stage of the process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
