<node id="Deionized Water">
  <data key="d0">Deionized Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Deionized water is a highly purified liquid characterized by the near-complete removal of ionic impurities, making it a critical chemical substance and reagent across analytical, industrial, and materials science applications. As a foundational medium, it serves as an ideal high-purity solvent, diluent, and reaction medium. It is routinely employed to dissolve analytical grade chemicals and reagents for preparing aqueous solutions and simulated body fluids, effectively handling a broad range of substances including Ct, CTAB, and (NH4)2HPO4. In experimental workflows, deionized water functions as a control medium and is utilized in experimental water washing pretreatments to prevent analytical errors. It dilutes digested and dissolved particle samples prior to trace element analysis, dissolves solids before filtration and subsequent testing, and acts as a baseline solvent for measuring the initial solubility of materials such as phosphogypsum and gypsum. Additionally, it is mixed with compost samples for physicochemical evaluation to ensure accurate, contamination-free measurements.

In materials engineering and synthesis, deionized water acts as the essential liquid component that combines with powder constituents to form homogeneous cement pastes and specialized composite bone cements, while having almost no detrimental effect on the filling body's strength or structure. It plays a vital role in the extraction and carbon dioxide mineralization of milled feldspar pellets. Within hydroxyapatite research, it serves as the primary solvent for hydrothermal synthesis, dissolution, and desorption experiments, and is repeatedly used to wash hydroxyapatite precipitates and solid products three times following centrifugation. Furthermore, it is utilized as a rinsing agent to wash precipitates after synthesis, as a solvent in synthesis suspensions such as those supplied by Hydrolab, and as a solvent added to Teflon vessels to replenish sample volume. It is also recognized as a purified water source used as a reagent in standardized testing procedures like SW-846.&lt;SEP&gt;Deionized water is used to wash the precipitates and remove excess ions after the reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfur Dioxide">
  <data key="d0">Sulfur Dioxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfur Dioxide is a gaseous chemical compound, chemically represented by the formula SO₂ and frequently denoted as 2SO₂↑ in reaction equations. It is primarily generated as a byproduct through various industrial and chemical processes. Specifically, it is released during the thermal and reductive decomposition or conversion of phosphogypsum, the processing of feldspar pellets, the broader reduction of sulfate compounds, and the reaction between carbon or coke with calcium sulfate. In the context of calcium sulfate breakdown, Sulfur Dioxide acts as a gaseous decomposition product that forms alongside calcium oxide, particularly at high temperatures. Beyond its role as an industrial byproduct, the gas serves as a valuable intermediate for further chemical synthesis and is subsequently processed in sulfuric acid production. Environmentally, it is classified as a pollutant, although its emissions can be significantly mitigated through the application of PSC Technology. Despite its industrial importance, the precise decomposition behavior of phosphogypsum and related sulfate materials during Sulfur Dioxide generation remains an area with limited scientific understanding.

In analytical and computational contexts, Sulfur Dioxide is treated as a chemical compound with an equivalent molar mass of 15.02 g/mol, a value utilized in concentration calculations. Its mass fraction is determined using specific analytical formulas, notably Equation 23, and it functions as a correction factor in Equation 22. Furthermore, the compound serves as the target analyte for quantification in Section 14, where it is measured using spectrophotometric methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur Dioxide is a gaseous byproduct released during the high-temperature decomposition and reaction phases.&lt;SEP&gt;A gaseous product released during the self-decomposition and reduction of calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur dioxide is a gaseous product generated when calcium sulfide reacts with undecomposed calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur dioxide is a gas generated during phosphogypsum decomposition that diffuses out of the slag.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur dioxide is a gaseous byproduct released during the secondary reaction stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Gaseous byproduct that escapes during multiple reaction stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen is a chemical element that functions as an inert gas and serves diverse roles across industrial, analytical, and environmental contexts. In industrial applications, it is released as a gaseous component during the gasification of lignite and provides a protective inert atmosphere during the calcination of feldspar pellets. In analytical chemistry, nitrogen is utilized as the adsorbate gas in adsorption-desorption isotherm analysis to accurately determine the porosity and surface area of various materials.

From an agricultural and biological perspective, nitrogen is an essential plant nutrient that is solubilized by microorganisms and commonly supplied to crops through biofertilizers. Additionally, in scientific data documentation, nitrogen is frequently cataloged as a chemical element with specified concentration values recorded in tabular formats.&lt;SEP&gt;A gas used as the adsorbate in the surface area and porosity analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is a gas used to create an atmospheric condition for testing environmental effects on the thermal treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is a plant nutrient element supplied by ammonium sulfate for agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;A central atom in the cation structure, carrying a positive charge and bonded to four substituents.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is an element not detected in the HAp-CTAB-9 sample, indicating the absence of CTAB impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791965487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weathering">
  <data key="d0">Weathering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Weathering is a carbonation process applied to the PGA solid phase to produce the PGAW solid phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
