<node id="Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate (CaSO4·2H2O), commonly known as gypsum, is a chemical compound that serves as the primary mineral and chemical constituent of phosphogypsum (PG) and phosphogypsum effluent (PGEF), typically comprising 75% to 95% of their mass. It is generated as a solid byproduct during industrial acidulation and wet-process reactions for phosphoric acid extraction, specifically along the left pathway of the wet process. The compound also forms through the exothermic hydration of calcium sulfate hemihydrate with water during setting processes, PGCM flaking, and pore-filling between RPG particles. Structurally, it naturally crystallizes in plate-like or prismatic formations, though treated samples may appear globular with preferred orientation growth. This distinct morphology facilitates identification and serves as a standard reference in diffraction analyses, where peak intensity correlates with concentration and vanishes when fully consumed during hydration below 15%.

Chemically, Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate exhibits notable stability, lacks initial gelling activity, and increases setting times in PG mixtures. It frequently co-occurs with quartz, fundamentally dictating the physical and chemical properties of PG waste streams, and acts as the main source of calcium in relevant reaction equations. The material cross-links calcium and sulfate ions to improve strength, dissolves during conversion processes to release ions, undergoes redox reactions, and serves as the predominant solubilized compound in nitric acid and alkaline treatments. It also undergoes a phase transition to an anhydrous form during potassium persulfate decomposition, which aids in impurity removal.

In industrial applications, Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate functions as a solid starting material for plaster manufacturing, undergoing dehydration to form hemihydrate and anhydrite, or being modified to produce hemihydrate phosphogypsum. Advanced recovery workflows utilize mass spectrometry combined with EDTA to extract high-purity gypsum from calcium-EDTA complexes, and the compound is routinely targeted for high-purity analysis, often exceeding 95%. Environmentally, it rarely incorporates radium due to differences in solubility and crystal structure. Conversely, it plays a significant role in resource sequestration, reportedly capturing between 70% and 80% of a system's total rare earth elements. Through these combined structural, chemical, and environmental characteristics, Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate remains a central focus in the study, purification, and industrial management of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate is a primary component of high-silica phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A compound in phosphogypsum that decomposes into calcium oxide at high temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate dihydrate is a chemical compound ($CaSO_4 \cdot 2H_2O$) identified as the primary component in the sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-00