  <data key="d0">Solid Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Solid waste represents the public perception category that creates market resistance against Phosphogypsum-based building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid waste represents the public perception category that creates market resistance against Phosphogypsum-based building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid waste represents the public perception category that creates market resistance against Phosphogypsum-based building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid waste is a soil emission listed in the emissions table.&lt;SEP&gt;A byproduct of all three processes that is 100% reused.&lt;SEP&gt;Solid waste is the primary material being tested for leaching toxicity and pollutant risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791712454</data>
