<node id="Calcium Carbonate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Carbonate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Carbonate (CaCO3) is a stable chemical compound and mineral powder with a molar mass of 100.09 g/mol, serving as a biogenic calcium precursor that constitutes 95-97% of chicken eggshells. Its industrial production heavily emphasizes resource recovery and recycling, utilizing feedstocks such as phosphogypsum, gypsum waste, steel converter slag, and feldspar pellets. Synthesis pathways are highly diverse, encompassing the reductive decomposition of phosphogypsum (which yields calcium oxide alongside the compound), aqueous conversion, carbonation processes, reactions with hydroxide solutions or soda, carbon dioxide capture into alkaline solutions or decomposition slag, and the processing of hydrolysates or calcium sulphide. Depending on the process stage, it functions variously as a reactant in ammonium sulfate production from phosphogypsum, an intermediate compound, or a byproduct formed during carbonation and recrystallization. These reactions typically involve the precipitation of carbonate and calcium ions, followed by filtration, drying, and crystallization or recrystallization, a cycle that frequently concludes within a 74-minute interval. Notably, certain carbonation routes concentrate rare earth elements within the resulting material, as the compound is often formed indirectly to facilitate element leaching from phosphogypsum for direct industrial application.

In aqueous and soil environments, Calcium Carbonate participates in dynamic equilibriums through dissolution and hydrolysis. Its solubility, quantified by the Calcium Carbonate Equivalent (CCE), is highly responsive to ionic conditions; it deposits when calcium, bicarbonate, and carbonate ions are removed and dissolves in response to carbonate fluctuations. Functionally, it acts as a modified material and chemical additive that provides calcium ions to immobilize phosphates and fluorides, reacts with soluble impurities to form insoluble substances, and accelerates condensation while maintaining a high solution pH. Specific production conditions can yield it as a byproduct when STMP concentration is 0.01 mol/L, resulting in inhomogeneous morphologies. It is also a component mixed with phosphate ore during the wet method production process and is found in sodium bicarbonate-leached materials, where it is primarily utilized as a building material or for lime production.

Owing to its versatile properties, Calcium Carbonate is extensively deployed across environmental, industrial, and construction sectors. Environmental applications include acidic water neutralization, contaminated water treatment, and acid mine drainage remediation. In construction and materials engineering, it is incorporated into mortar, widely utilized in cementous materials, and serves as a functional substitute for phosphogypsum in quick lime-GGBFS-cement systems and modified polymer materials. Analytical characterizations, such as X-ray diffraction studies, frequently identify it alongside Portlandite, Calcite, and Quartz within complex material matrices.

Beyond traditional industrial uses, the compound has specialized roles in material science and analytical chemistry. It is used as a primary standard to standardize potassium hydroxide solutions. In biomedical and advanced material applications, it serves as a substrate material and a spherical substance utilized in prior art for depositing hydroxyapatite layers. Furthermore, it is studied for its degradation patterns within porous microspheres designed for bone tissue engineering, highlighting its biocompatibility and structural utility in regenerative medicine.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Carbonate is recovered from waste gypsum alongside sulfur.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
