<node id="Carbonation Process">
  <data key="d0">Carbonation Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonation Process is a chemical transformation method that converts gypsum-derived compounds into calcium carbonate using CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical transformation process that converts gypsum and Portlandite into calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonation Process is the second step involving the injection of CO2 flow into a Portlandite solution to form calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific phase of the conversion process involving the dissolution of carbon dioxide and subsequent ion formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonation process is a chemical treatment method applied to phosphogypsum to alter its environmental behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbonation process transforms phosphogypsum into calcium carbonate, concentrating rare earth elements in the byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791813449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Hydrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrolysis is a chemical reaction process fundamentally characterized by the interaction of water with various substances, leading to their breakdown, dissolution, or transformation into ions and other compounds. In its general mechanism, the process involves the cleavage of chemical bonds by water or hydroxide ions, often occurring concurrently with the dissolution of minerals such as calcium carbonate. This aqueous-driven transformation is essential for converting solid phases into soluble ionic species and other chemical compounds.

In specific industrial and materials science applications, hydrolysis is utilized across a range of distinct chemical systems. It is applied to calcium sulfide to produce an alkaline solution containing free calcium ions, hydrogen sulfide ions, and hydroxide ions, and is similarly employed to break down phosphogypsum decomposition slag into calcium sulfide and various impurities. The process also facilitates the aqueous dissolution of calcium-aluminum-silicate phases. Furthermore, hydrolysis plays a critical role in molecular bond cleavage, such as the breakdown of pyrophosphate bonds by hydroxide ions to yield water and phosphate ions, and is actively used in the synthesis of hydroxyapatite from precursor solutions. Collectively, these varied reactions demonstrate hydrolysis as a versatile chemical mechanism driven by aqueous interaction, essential for both material processing and compound synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrolysis is a chemical process used to synthesize hydroxyapatite from brushite, resulting in decomposition starting around 700 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical reaction process used to generate hydrogen from hydrides.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process resulting from raw material breakdown that releases SiO2 and facilitates ettringite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical reaction that the stripping process aims to prevent by using faintly acidified water.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process likely illustrated by the equation, where polyphosphates break down in the presence of hydroxide ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
