<node id="Precipitation">
  <data key="d0">Precipitation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Precipitation encompasses two distinct but related phenomena: a versatile chemical and physical separation process, and an atmospheric weather event. In industrial, environmental, and materials science applications, precipitation is a multifaceted chemical technique used to separate, immobilize, and transform dissolved substances. It operates by causing dissolved ions to solidify into distinct mineral phases or tangible solids, such as calcium carbonate, aluminum hydroxide, nano-calcium sulfate, or composite nanomaterials. This mechanism is routinely applied to extract target elements like aluminum and rare earth elements from solutions following initial leaching, effectively eliminating slightly soluble and insoluble impurities. It also serves as a conventional wet method for fabricating hydroxyapatite with controlled morphology and is indicated in the bottom left region of chemical phase diagrams. Additionally, precipitation functions as a critical environmental factor in leaching simulations and is employed to immobilize potentially toxic elements within stabilized phosphogypsum, where it facilitates the formation of relatively pure mineral phases from the material's major elements. The process can also yield tangible solid products when high-temperature autoclave mixtures cool to room temperature or when dissolved salts revert to their solid state.

In atmospheric and environmental contexts, precipitation manifests as both meteorological rainfall and a primary removal mechanism for airborne substances. Meteorologically, it is depicted as rainfall in the top left section that falls directly onto phosphogypsum stacks. Chemically, it acts as a dominant atmospheric cleansing process by extracting highly soluble compounds like hydrogen fluoride from the air. It also serves as the main pathway for removing phosphogypsum and its associated particulate matter, facilitating their deposition and reducing environmental dispersion. Together, these diverse applications underscore precipitation as both a fundamental chemical transformation and purification technique and a vital natural process for atmospheric purification and material deposition.&lt;SEP&gt;The chemical process where La, Ce, and Nd ions precipitate out of solution at pH values higher than 6.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation is the procedure where oxalic acid is added to the stripping solution to form RE oxalate.&lt;SEP&gt;Precipitation is a chemical synthesis technique involving the formation of solid particles from a solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A retention mechanism resulting in the formation of a new solid phase from a supersaturated liquid species.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792039718</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphate Industry">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Phosphate Industry is the industrial sector dedicated to the mining and processing of phosphate rock. Its core operations are responsible for producing phosphoric acid and generating raw phosphogypsum, which serves as the initial feedstock for subsequent valorization processes. In addition to these primary outputs, the sector produces significant byproducts and residues, notably hazardous phosphogypsum and Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material (NORM) residues.

The substantial volume and potential hazards of these waste streams have made the Phosphate Industry a focal point for environmental and resource management research. Consequently, the sector's byproducts are extensively studied to assess environmental impacts, develop sustainable waste management strategies, and explore efficient resource recovery techniques. These ongoing efforts aim to mitigate ecological risks while enhancing the overall sustainability and circular economy potential of phosphate production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791592065</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Washing Process">
  <data key="d0">Washing Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Washing Process is a purification step that removes soluble impurities from Raw PG to produce Washed PG.&lt;SEP&gt;A purification step that removes soluble impurities from raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The washing process removes sodium sulfate and facilitates further increases in rare earth element concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Washing Process involves hot water and ethanol to remove surfactant residues from the synthesized samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Washing Process is a purification step using hot water and ethanol to remove surfactant residues from the synthesized samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791627879</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonation System">
  <data key="d0">Carbonation System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonation System is the industrial apparatus where Portlandite reacts with CO2 to produce Calcite.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial equipment where Portlandite reacts with CO2 to form calcite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcite">
  <data key="d0">Calcite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcite is a common, naturally occurring, and industrially produced crystalline mineral phase and chemical compound of calcium carbonate. Characterized by a rhombohedral crystal structure, it functions as a stable carbonate mineral that forms through carbonation, carbonization, and conversion reactions. Calcite is widely distributed across various materials, serving as the primary component of eggshells, a standard mineral in concrete mixes alongside quartz and portlandite, and a detectable phase in phosphogypsum and sodium bicarbonate-leached materials, where it can constitute approximately 21.664% of the composition. Its formation and abundance are influenced by specific material compositions, such as reduced production in cement-phosphogypsum systems incorporating fly ash.

In industrial and environmental applications, calcite acts as a secondary raw material in phosphogypsum recycling, where it competes with cheaper alternatives, and is primarily utilized as a building material or for lime production. Analytically, it is routinely identified and characterized using X-ray diffraction, particularly in samples containing 12% CaCO3, where it is represented by a solid circle symbol and identified as peak 6, exhibiting characteristic diffraction clusters around 29°–30° and throughout the 30°–60° range. Beyond structural uses, synthesized calcite has demonstrated the ability to preferentially accumulate radionuclides and exhibits greater solubility than phosphogypsum in acidic environments. It has also been evaluated as an adsorbent for environmental remediation, specifically for fluoride removal, although studies indicate it achieves significantly lower adsorption uptake compared to hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcite is a calcium carbonate mineral (CaCO3) identified in the mineralogical composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791938112</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KOH">
  <data key="d0">KOH</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">KOH is a chemical reagent added during the processing step to facilitate the production of Portlandite and Potassium Sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;KOH, or potassium hydroxide, is a chemical reactant used in the thermostatic jacket to convert washed PG into Portlandite.&lt;SEP&gt;KOH is a chemical reagent used in the transformation of PG to produce calcium sulfate and potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium hydroxide, a solution tested for its reaction with calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound used to prepare a 200 g/L solution as specified in the standard.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium hydroxide, a chemical compound used in a formula to calculate CO2 concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792067577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw PG">
  <data key="d0">Raw PG</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw PG is the unprocessed phosphogypsum material extracted directly from the phosphate industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw PG refers to raw phosphogypsum produced by the phosphate industry before processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Abbreviation for raw phosphogypsum, used in Table 3 to denote pre-treatment composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw PG is an unprocessed form of phosphogypsum exhibiting higher unconfined compressive strength than treated PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw PG is a granular material evaluated for use in embankments and road mixes.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw PG is a pulverulent material with tabular crystalline morphology, highly sensitive to water, and used in construction layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Unprocessed phosphogypsum baseline material characterized by high acidity and poor geotechnical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Washed PG">
  <data key="d0">Washed PG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Washed PG is the purified phosphogypsum material obtained after the washing process removes soluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Washed PG is phosphogypsum that has undergone a washing process to remove soluble impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Methanogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanogenesis is a biological process occurring in anaerobic layers where methanogens produce methane.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanogenesis is a biological process occurring in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies where methane is produced from organic matter decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;A biochemical process occurring in the anaerobic layer that produces methane.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Acetogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetogenesis is a metabolic pathway in anaerobic conditions that converts substrates into acetate.&lt;SEP&gt;A biochemical process occurring in the anaerobic layer alongside methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetogenesis is a biological process occurring in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter">
  <data key="d0">Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter is the breakdown process of organic material in lower anaerobic soil layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A breakdown process of organic material that occurs in the deep anaerobic layer.&lt;SEP&gt;Decomposition of soil organic matter occurs in the deep anaerobic layer, providing substrates for methanogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanogens">
  <data key="d0">Methanogens</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanogens are microorganisms residing in anaerobic layers that drive methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanogens are microorganisms residing in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies that drive the process of methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Microorganisms present in the anaerobic layer that drive methanogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rhizosphere">
  <data key="d0">Rhizosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Rhizosphere is the soil region surrounding plant roots, characterized by microbial activity and methane consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhizosphere is the root zone region whose depth determines the appropriate soil horizon for mechanical processing.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots where biological processes maintain a pH close to 7.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots whose development is hindered by standard technology but improved by intra-soil milling.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhizosphere is the root zone region whose depth determines the appropriate soil horizon for mechanical processing.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots where biological processes maintain a pH close to 7.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots whose development is hindered by standard technology but improved by intra-soil milling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790950059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaerobic Layer">
  <data key="d0">Anaerobic Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaerobic Layer is the lower soil zone with negative redox potential where methanogenesis and acetogenesis occur.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil zone characterized by negative redox potential containing methanogens and specific biochemical processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca3Al2(OH)12">
  <data key="d0">Ca3Al2(OH)12</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ca3Al2(OH)12 is a complex calcium aluminate hydrate that decomposes into calcium hydroxide and other compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790848098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH)2), also widely recognized as portlandite, is a versatile alkaline base compound that functions as both an active reactant and a byproduct across industrial, environmental, and materials science applications. It is formed through multiple distinct pathways, including the decomposition of calcium aluminate hydrate, hydrolysis of calcium sulfide, stabilization processes, and the precipitation of dissolved calcium and hydroxide ions. The compound is frequently recovered or synthesized from phosphogypsum via soda conversion, derived from eggshell powder processed with hydrochloric acid, or procured as a pure reagent from suppliers such as Aldrich and CHEMPUR for specific experimental protocols, where it serves as a primary source of calcium ions.

In environmental and waste management contexts, calcium hydroxide is extensively employed for water treatment and phosphogypsum remediation. It effectively neutralizes and modifies the internal structure of phosphogypsum, immobilizes soluble phosphorus and fluorine impurities, and reacts with calcium phosphate salts, phosphoric acid, and freed phosphate ions during thermal treatment to generate inactive compounds. During fluorine immobilization, calcium fluoride precipitates form on its surface, which can subsequently limit its reactivity with additional fluorine. The compound also participates in mineral carbonation processes, appearing at specific reaction intervals and serving stoichiometrically during initial stages.

Within construction and materials engineering, calcium hydroxide serves as a primary mineral in phosphogypsum slag cement and composite filling bodies. As a chemical additive, it directly influences bleeding rate, porosity, and the unconfined compressive strength of resulting materials. While its diffraction peak intensity remains stable in modified and unaltered phosphogypsum samples, it progressively diminishes and vanishes at 30% phosphogypsum content, signaling promoted hydration. Although it can adsorb onto gypsum crystals and potentially inhibit further hydration in certain cement mortars, it simultaneously reacts with phosphogypsum, fly ash, and slag on recycled aggregate surfaces to significantly enhance the interfacial transition zone.

In chemical synthesis, calcium hydroxide acts as a fundamental base reactant and precursor. It is calcined to form calcium oxide, thereby improving lime reactivity, and is utilized in neutralization reactions to synthesize hydroxyapatite, including HAp Type 1, via both hydrothermal and precipitation methods. During hydrothermal synthesis, it appears as a transient side phase at 150 °C before being eliminated at higher temperatures, and when homogenized using a planetary mill in modified wet chemical precipitation processes, it acts as a precursor for synthesizing thermally stable hydroxyapatite. Its dehydroxylation kinetics and thermodynamics are actively studied, underscoring its broad utility as both a functional material and a chemical additive.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium hydroxide, also known as slaked lime, is obtained from calcium oxide and used in construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
