<node id="Agriculture">
  <data key="d0">Agriculture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agriculture serves as a fundamental component of the global food supply chain and a critical downstream sector for crop cultivation, frequently functioning as a primary destination for processed materials and industrial byproducts. Within this domain, the sector plays a notable role in the comprehensive utilization of phosphogypsum (PG), a material extensively tracked in scientific literature. Treated PG is applied in agricultural settings as a soil amendment, low-grade fertilizer, nutrient replacer, and as a feedstock for producing compounds such as potassium sulfate and calcite. These applications provide tangible benefits for soil improvement and support broader industrial recycling initiatives.

The scale and maturity of PG utilization in agriculture present varying perspectives across different contexts. While some frameworks classify agriculture as a primary field for PG valorization, other data indicate it constitutes a minor usage sector, accounting for approximately 1% of total applications. Nevertheless, it is recognized as a rapidly developing application field, with commercialized implementations established in Russia and more limited adoption in the United States. Large-scale, high-value deployment is currently constrained by practical challenges, including high costs and product instability. Furthermore, the agricultural use of PG necessitates rigorous evaluation of potential radiological impacts, contamination risks, and occupational dosimetry concerns. Consequently, its deployment remains contingent upon comprehensive safety assessments, underscoring the sector's ongoing effort to balance industrial resource recovery with environmental protection and agricultural safety.&lt;SEP&gt;An application sector where a small percentage of phosphogypsum waste is recycled.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-012</data>
