<node id="Construction Materials">
  <data key="d0">Construction Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Construction Materials represent a broad category of building supplies and fundamental matrices, encompassing products such as cement pastes, geopolymers, mortars, blocks, plasterboards, and roadbed or paving materials. This sector frequently incorporates calcite and related compounds, serving as a primary application pathway for the final Calcite product. Within the broader context of industrial byproduct utilization, Construction Materials constitute the largest and most major application sector for recycled and processed phosphogypsum (PG). PG is valorized and reused extensively within this field, particularly across multiple Chinese provinces, where it is integrated into building matrices to enhance mechanical properties. The application of recycled PG in construction is often discussed alongside other utilization fields such as agriculture and engineering.

From an industrial and economic perspective, Construction Materials are conventional products manufactured by integrated phosphogypsum companies. Despite their significance, the widespread promotion and adoption of PG-based construction materials face notable constraints, primarily driven by high transportation costs and existing technical and economic limitations. Environmental and safety assessments are also integral to this sector, as these materials are rigorously evaluated for their potential to emit Radon-222 into the surrounding environment.

In academic and data visualization contexts, Construction Materials serve as a primary research focus area for scholars such as Dr. Marc Azab. Additionally, in specific classification systems or legends, these building supplies are distinctly identified by a light blue color code. Overall, the sector functions as a critical intersection of material science, sustainable resource management, and environmental monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad category of building products and structural elements incorporating phosphogypsum and other industrial byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction Materials is a sector where phosphogypsum is recycled and applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction Materials represent the application category for recycled phosphogypsum, including plaster and concrete.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
