<node id="Composting">
  <data key="d0">Composting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Composting is a biological decomposition and soil treatment process primarily utilized to prepare phosphogypsum-based biofertilizers by combining the material with biomass and microbial agents. This preparation typically spans approximately 50 days and requires periodic turning. Throughout the process, the physicochemical environment is significantly altered, which in turn drives the evolution, succession, and structural stabilization of microbial communities. During this biological transformation, Actinobacteria consistently remain the dominant microbial group.

In addition to its role in microbial and physicochemical dynamics, composting functions as an effective soil treatment method that mitigates environmental and agricultural risks. By stabilizing the treated material, the process effectively reduces heavy metal transfer and limits cadmium penetration into plants, thereby enhancing soil safety and crop protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Composting is a process for livestock manure where phosphogypsum and zeolite are used as co-amendments to manage nutrient losses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791428038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pH">
  <data key="d0">pH</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">pH is a fundamental physicochemical property and measurement parameter that quantifies the acidity or alkalinity of substances, particularly within aqueous, soil, and industrial environments. Typically represented on a scale from 1 to 10, though values frequently range from approximately 4 to 12 or extend higher during specific processes, it serves as a critical baseline indicator across chemical, environmental, and biological research. As a decisive regulatory variable, pH directly governs deprotonation, surface charge, adsorption behavior, chemical speciation, corrosiveness, carbon dioxide solubility, and zeta potential. It dictates dominant sorption mechanisms, favoring dissolution-precipitation under acidic conditions and ion exchange under alkaline conditions, while frequently functioning as an independent variable in analytical graphs.

In experimental, industrial, and materials science applications, pH is actively controlled or adjusted using reagents such as hydrochloric acid, sodium hydroxide, or ammonium hydroxide to target specific values, such as 2.5 during extraction processes. Its measurement is strictly regulated, including under standards like GB/T 5484-2012, and is routinely documented in chemical analysis, toxicity assessment, leaching toxicity tables, and Table 3. pH strongly influences the crystallization, phase purity, structure, composition, particle morphology, size, and agglomeration of synthesized compounds, which is vital for scaling hydroxyapatite nanoparticle production and optimizing hydrothermal synthesis. Across various formulations, pH is systematically recorded for each designed mix and monitored to evaluate and ensure the neutralization of acidity in materials, with values ranging from 2.2 to 10.8 depending on the specific formulation.

In agricultural, environmental, and waste management contexts, pH acts as a primary driver of geochemical and biological processes. It controls the solubility, mobility, leaching behavior, and removal efficiency of elements such as phosphorus, fluoride, orthophosphate, cadmium, lead, thorium, and rare earth elements, directly impacting plant uptake, competitive metal ion adsorption, and the stability of chemical precursors like REE-EDTA chelates. Consequently, pH is optimized during solvent extraction for rare earth recovery and managed daily in processes like phosphogypsum storage and composting. Raw phosphogypsum exhibits acidity levels between 2.2 and 4.17, with some samples ranging from 2 to 3, varying by depth and leaching, but these values consistently increase in stabilized mixes. Alkalinity in slurry management must be maintained above 10 to inhibit hazardous gas generation, while deliberate interventions like biofertilizer use or phosphogypsum application can alter natural pH levels to mitigate environmental acidification from industrial runoff. Throughout these diverse domains, pH remains an indispensable variable for optimizing chemical processes, ensuring material quality, and monitoring ecosystem health.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of acidity or alkalinity that is monitored during the chemical analysis process.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a measure of acidity or alkalinity that is carefully controlled and measured during the analytical procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a measure of acidity that is strictly controlled at specific values during different analytical steps.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a critical parameter that must be adjusted to specific ranges during the titration procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a chemical parameter measuring acidity or alkalinity, listed in the experimental data table.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-019&lt;