<node id="Inert Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Inert Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An inert atmosphere is a controlled environment used during the thermal decomposition and pyrolysis of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An inert atmosphere is a controlled environment used during the thermal decomposition and pyrolysis of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An inert atmosphere is a controlled environment used during the thermal decomposition and pyrolysis of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Inert Atmosphere is the environmental condition maintained during the thermal reduction of gypsum and phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
