<node id="Fly Ash">
  <data key="d0">Fly Ash</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fly ash is a fine, aluminate-rich industrial by-product and combustion waste primarily generated from coal burning in power plants, containing measurable baseline levels of radionuclides. Functioning as a supplementary cementitious material and pozzolanic blending agent, it is widely utilized across construction, geotechnical engineering, and environmental remediation. Its integration into composite materials promotes ettringite precipitation and pore filling, which significantly enhances mechanical properties, compressive strength, and long-term durability, while exhibiting high mullite concentrations in concrete applications.

A prominent application involves blending fly ash with phosphogypsum, yellow phosphorus slag-based binders, and often lime, to create stabilizing composites, filling slurries, road base materials, and construction specimens. In these mixtures, fly ash acts as an essential additive that improves strength, durability, and water resistance, a synergy facilitated by sulfate ions released from AFt crystal breakdown. It is combined with both treated and raw phosphogypsum to form strong cementitious bonds and enhance structural strength, and it serves as a supplementary material in brick formulations, though it may increase water absorption in certain cases. The pozzolanic reaction can sometimes be inhibited by impurities within the phosphogypsum. Additionally, fly ash is employed to immobilize phosphorus and comprises 35% of the CPGFM formulation at Qingping Phosphate Mine.

Beyond phosphogypsum applications, fly ash is co-processed with red mud and phosphogypsum to facilitate resource recovery, and it is incorporated into cemented paste backfill, geopolymer cement, PSC technology, and CCM formulations. It is also combined with steel slag to mitigate greenhouse gas emissions, used with cement for marine construction, and paired with slag for recycled aggregate concrete. In environmental contexts, fly ash is investigated for mitigating greenhouse gas emissions from paddy fields and utilized in accelerated carbonation processes for brine remediation. To ensure optimal industrial and construction performance, its behavior has been extensively evaluated under extreme conditions, including elevated temperatures, thermal shock cycles, and constant magnetic fields.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial by-product used as a stabilizer in phosphogypsum formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly Ash is a supplementary material mixed with lime and phosphogypsum to create tested pavement layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly Ash is a raw material blended with phosphogypsum to modify mix properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is an industrial solid waste high in silica, alumina, and magnesium oxide added to meet slag wool composition requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is a material used in small quantities alongside phosphogypsum and activated carbon to improve material burning properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A solid waste containing small amounts of iron oxides that affect slag properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004</data>
