<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water (H₂O) is a fundamental chemical compound with a standard enthalpy of formation of -285.8 kJ/mol. Spectroscopically, it exhibits O-H stretching and bending vibrations, creating a broad absorption feature between 3400 and 3445 cm⁻¹ in materials like biochar and Curve A, and appears as structural water in hemi-hydrate gypsum. Thermogravimetric analysis distinguishes it as surface or structural water, with initial heating removing humidity and crystallization water. Chemically, Water functions dually as a reactant and byproduct. As a reactant, it drives gasification, hydrolysis (general, calcium aluminum silicate hydroxide, fluorapatite acidulation), sulfuric acid processes, slurry preparation, and hydrothermal conversion. Conversely, it is generated as a secondary or sole byproduct during the water-gas shift reaction, pyrophosphate hydrolysis, VOC oxidation, hydroxyapatite dissolution, gypsum and phosphogypsum transformations, neutralization reactions, and reactions involving calcium phosphate, calcium hydroxide, or phosphoric acid. It is also explicitly produced as H₂O during hydrogen phosphate condensation and hydroxyapatite dehydroxylation.

In material science and industry, Water acts extensively as a solvent and reaction medium. It dissolves calcium carbonate, modulates phosphatic and fluoride compound solubility (often with aqueous citric acid), and washes hydroxyapatite to remove polyvinyl alcohol. It facilitates hydrothermal synthesis (80–400°C), wet phosphoric acid production, and phosphogypsum adsorption studies. In extraction, Water strips rare earth ions from ionic liquids, reduces their viscosity to improve kinetics and mass transfer, and migrates with hydrated calcium nitrate, increasing spectral band intensity. In radiochemical settings, it solubilizes Radon-222 temperature-dependently and reduces recoiling atom energy, increasing emanation coefficients while decreasing atmospheric transport. Water is critical for PCR, PBG, and PSC processes, phosphoric acid filtration, and as an additional resource consumed during phosphogypsum valorization and brick production. It forms PGEF mixtures and CPGFM slurries with phosphogypsum, actively washing impurities and driving calcium sulfate hemihydrate-to-gypsum conversion. In construction and geotechnics, Water sets bone cement (requiring ethanol for displacement measurements), influences pH and ion migration in cementitious materials, and adjusts soil liquid limits for softening tests.

Within hydroxyapatite, Water exists as crystallization and adsorbed forms, with spectral bands weakening after calcination, while nanoscale OH groups influence protein adsorption. Throughout these scenarios, Water is systematically tracked in environmental impact analyses. However, water bodies face significant pollution risks from phosphogypsum discharged via rivers, ponds, and landfills.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is a component of atmospheric conditions that interacts with surface-disposed phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-05