<node id="Copper">
  <data key="d0">Copper</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Copper is a chemical element functioning as both an essential trace nutrient and a regulated heavy metal pollutant, with applications spanning geological, environmental, and materials science domains. Geologically, it is depleted in phosphorites relative to crustal abundance and associates with organic matter. In the industrial byproduct phosphogypsum, copper is a highly mobile trace element routinely quantified via LA-ICP-MS and ICP-MS, with concentrations typically ranging from 21 ± 2 to 24.72–28.00 μg/g. During processing, it exhibits a 64 to 100 percent transfer rate. Its leaching behavior is characterized by high liquid/solid fractionation due to weak bonding or adsorption to gypsum surfaces, causing its leaching rate to increase over time. In phosphogypsum solutions, copper concentrations tend to decrease alongside cadmium as pH rises. Experimental tracking measures copper in micrograms per liter over time, while the TCLP test quantifies it in milligrams per liter.

Environmentally and regulatorily, copper is strictly controlled as a heavy metal contaminant in surface and irrigation waters, with a maximum allowable concentration of 1 mg L⁻¹. While no specific US-EPA limit is listed in certain mixture contexts, its presence is monitored against leaching toxicity thresholds, particularly in phosphogypsum-amended soils where it can cause slight contamination. Atmospheric emissions drive terrestrial ecotoxicity potential. In life cycle inventories, copper is tracked as a liquid emission during phosphogypsum disposal and a groundwater emission, quantified at 7.94 × 10⁻⁴ kilograms. Mitigation involves removing copper from polluted waters using adsorption and ion-exchange technologies, including phosphogypsum-based adsorbents (which show high efficiency but can drop approximately 82 percent under specific conditions) and nano-NaX zeolite. Strategic phosphogypsum reuse also aids remediation.

In materials science, copper acts as a versatile functional dopant and catalyst. Combined with phosphogypsum, it synthesizes compound oxygen carriers that lower reaction temperatures. Doping hydroxyapatite matrices with copper enhances photocatalytic properties for formaldehyde oxidation and selective nitric oxide reduction with ammonia, while altering degradation kinetics, such as slowing 17α-methyltestosterone breakdown. It is also impregnated into synthetic nanohydroxyapatite for agricultural use. Analytically, copper may occasionally appear as an elemental component during Scanning Electron Microscopy sample preparation, highlighting its broad relevance across scientific and industrial monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-026</data>
