<node id="Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite nanoparticles are advanced, fine particulate forms of the naturally occurring mineral hydroxyapatite. They are primarily synthesized from waste phosphogypsum, effectively transforming an industrial byproduct into a functional nanomaterial. A major application of these nanoparticles lies in environmental remediation, specifically for the removal of fluoride from aqueous solutions and the treatment of fluoride-polluted wastewater.

Beyond water purification, their distinct physicochemical properties make them valuable in biochemical and biomedical research. They are frequently employed in protein adsorption studies, where their surface characteristics facilitate the binding and analysis of biological molecules. Collectively, these uses demonstrate the dual utility of hydroxyapatite nanoparticles in both ecological cleanup and advanced scientific investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles are synthesized chemical compounds widely studied as nano-fertilizers and for environmental remediation applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite nanoparticles are synthesized from phosphogypsum via thermal activation to retain metals and anions in water treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles are synthesized from PG via thermal activation and exhibit rapid adsorption capabilities for wastewater treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles are nanostructured materials synthesized from eggshells to mimic biological apatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite nanoparticles are nanoscale calcium phosphate structures synthesized via various routes including hydrothermal and microwave methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite Nanoparticles are synthesized nanostructured particles with tunable diameters used in biomedical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-000</data>
