<node id="Zhang">
  <data key="d0">Zhang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhang is a researcher whose work primarily focuses on environmental remediation, pollutant immobilization, and the valorization of industrial byproducts, particularly phosphogypsum. A significant portion of Zhang's research investigates fluoride and fluorine removal and stabilization. Specifically, Zhang evaluated the adsorption behavior of phosphogypsum-derived nanoparticles for fluoride removal and explored fluorine immobilization mechanisms that involve ion exchange. To enhance these processes, Zhang utilized the microwave irradiation method to synthesize nano-hydroxyapatite directly from phosphogypsum.

In addition to adsorption and synthesis, Zhang examined chemical stabilization techniques, discovering that polymeric aluminum chloride can solidify fluorides to improve the strength of filling bodies. Furthermore, Zhang applied calcium hydroxide for broader pollutant immobilization efforts. Due to the relevance and rigor of these findings, Zhang's studies are frequently cited as primary data sources in comparative scientific tables. Collectively, Zhang's contributions advance the understanding of sustainable waste utilization and effective fluoride remediation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who performed Life Cycle Analysis assessments of phosphogypsum utilization in fertilizer and cement production in China.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-001</data>
