<node id="Table 1">
  <data key="d0">Table 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 1 functions as a recurring, context-dependent data compilation label widely utilized across scientific disciplines rather than representing a single fixed dataset. It serves as a standardized repository that dynamically adapts its structure and content to report key experimental parameters, analytical results, and methodological details specific to each publication. In materials science and chemistry, it typically catalogs chemical compositions of raw materials, documents reaction conditions, and provides standard enthalpy of formation data for thermodynamic calculations. Within phosphogypsum research, Table 1 organizes sample codes, industrial sources, and detailed chemical profiles, including major elemental concentrations and impurities from regions such as Morocco, Hubei, Yunnan, and Guizhou provinces. It frequently presents spectroscopic characterization data, trace element concentrations, and chemical analysis results of nitrate leach liquids. The table also summarizes α-Hemihydrate production methods, macro-ion content in water extracts, associated Haplic Chernozem soil profiles, and the lixivium content of heavy metal pollutants in PGEF, where most are typically undetected. Additionally, it defines the waste composition of the functional unit in relevant studies.

In biomedical and biomaterials contexts, Table 1 extensively details hydroxyapatite and bone cement characteristics. It outlines various methods for obtaining hydroxyapatite, including starting materials, synthesis processes, end products, and the substrates affecting the primary product's properties. The table records preparation conditions such as molar ratios, pH, temperature, and duration, while documenting resulting morphologies. It specifically tabulates the crystallographic characteristics of hydrothermally produced hydroxyapatite variants and materials, the degree of crystallinity for prepared samples, and particle sizes of hydroxyapatite samples prepared with CTAB and P123 surfactants. Structural parameters and textural characteristics are also presented, including BET surface area, mean pore size, and pore volume measurements. Furthermore, it records weight percentages of calcium and phosphorus with Ca/P ratios for synthetic hydroxyapatite and bone ash samples analyzed via ICP-OES. For composite bone cements, the table documents physical properties such as density, porosity, setting times, and performance across varying sodium chloride concentrations, alongside precise reagent specifications for preparing simulated body fluid.

Beyond materials and biomedical applications, Table 1 extends into agricultural, environmental, and industrial research. It compiles physicochemical data for soils and biofertilizers, including the physical properties of selected adobe soil, and supports microbial fermentation and material decomposition studies. The table provides detailed sieve analysis results with cumulative contributions for each material fraction, outlines life cycle inventory analyses detailing resource and energy consumption for technologies like PCR, PBG, and PSC, and tracks adsorption capacities for various sorbents targeting formic acid, cadmium, and cobalt ions. Across all domains, Table 1 consistently delivers a structured, context-specific framework for essential experimental and analytical data.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 summarizes the BET surface area, pore volume, and mean pore size for microspheres synthesized at different hydrothermal times.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 is a data presentation summarizing the major and trace element composition of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 presents quantitative concentration data for various elements detected in the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A data table presenting the chemical compositions of phosphogypsum in weight percent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
