<node id="Surfactant">
  <data key="d0">Surfactant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surfactant is a versatile chemical additive and agent utilized across various material synthesis and sample preparation processes. Primarily functioning as a crystal modifier, it plays a critical role in controlling the growth and morphology of specific compounds, such as α-Hemihydrate. During synthesis, surfactant alters particle morphology, significantly reduces primary particle size, and increases overall surface area while simultaneously suppressing the formation of secondary phases. Its presence or absence is often strategically employed to differentiate experimental sample groups, serving as a key variable in material development studies.

In specialized applications, surfactant contributes to precise structural engineering of synthesized materials. For instance, during the synthesis of Powder Surf, the evaporation of surfactant directly influences pore formation within the resulting matrix. Similarly, when incorporated during hydroxyapatite powder preparation, surfactant is utilized to potentially enhance the material's bioactivity and improve its heavy ion removal capacity. Collectively, these functions highlight surfactant's importance as a multifunctional agent in tailoring the structural, morphological, and functional properties of advanced materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A surfactant is a substance often used as a phase transfer catalyst, similar to the cation described.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-008</data>
