<node id="Thorium">
  <data key="d0">Thorium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Thorium is a naturally occurring radioactive chemical element and radionuclide that primarily exists in the +4 oxidation state. It occurs as a trace component in phosphate rocks, phosphorites, and marketable rock phosphate, with concentrations in phosphorites comparable to those in shales, thereby contributing to the natural radioactivity of these geological formations. During industrial acid processing, particularly via sulfuric acid and wet phosphoric acid methods, thorium is mobilized and migrates in a polymeric colloidal form before converting into a soluble sulfate. Approximately 70 to 85 percent of its isotopes are retained in the phosphoric acid stream, while the remainder accumulates in the phosphogypsum byproduct, necessitating careful handling and management protocols due to its radioactive properties.

Within phosphogypsum, thorium exhibits a strong preferential retention in coarse and larger grain size fractions, localizing more heavily in these particles than radium. Its concentration in phosphogypsum has been measured at values such as 10 ppm and 4 ± 0.64, depending on the specific sample and analytical context. The distribution and partitioning of thorium across different phosphogypsum fractions are typically evaluated using the 228Th/228Ra activity ratio, with its concentration (C_Th) measured by particle size and utilized in Ra-Eq calculations. Analytical assessments frequently employ alpha-particle spectrometry to measure thorium alongside uranium-238 and radium in environmental and waste samples, cataloging specific concentration values to study radionuclide behavior.

Due to its distinct accumulation behavior during phosphate processing and its specific fractionation in phosphogypsum, thorium serves as a critical parameter for radiological monitoring and industrial waste management. It is also referenced in worldwide activity concentration standards, underscoring its significance in both environmental science and industrial applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium occurs as the radioisotope Th-232 and is partially retained in phosphogypsum during acid treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium is a trace element detected in significant concentrations in the fluorite phase of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium is a trace metal that exhibits an increasing leaching rate as leaching time increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium is a trace element that is highly retained in the phosphogypsum matrix, requiring full matrix dissolution for release.&lt;SEP&gt;A trace metal categorized as having intermediate mobility in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium is present in phosphogypsum but exhibits low mobility due to the formation of insoluble complexes with fluorides, hydroxides, and phosphates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
