<node id="Potassium Feldspar">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Feldspar</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium Feldspar is a mineral compound utilized across several industrial and chemical processes. In carbon management applications, it serves as a key component in mechanism B, where it facilitates synergistic carbon solidification. The mineral also functions as a source for the synergistic leaching of potassium and phosphorus, particularly when coupled with phosphogypsum. Its interaction with phosphogypsum is further characterized by its demonstrated ability to influence the material's decomposition rate.

In metallurgical and ceramic manufacturing, Potassium Feldspar acts as a functional additive designed to elevate the melting and molten temperatures of various materials. This thermal modification is specifically employed to prevent unwanted sintering during cement clinker firing. Additionally, when combined with kaolin, it is utilized to raise the molten temperature during the reduction processing of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001</data>
