<node id="J. Cryst. Growth">
  <data key="d0">J. Cryst. Growth</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Journal of Crystal Growth (J. Cryst. Growth) is a peer-reviewed academic and scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on crystal synthesis and growth techniques. As a specialized publication in the materials science and crystallography fields, it serves as a primary venue for scholarly work exploring the formation, properties, and development of crystalline structures.

The journal's publication record encompasses a diverse range of specific studies and notable contributors. It has featured multiple investigations into synthesizing gypsum derivatives from phosphogypsum, alongside a 1991 study that examined gypsum growth and cadmium incorporation. Furthermore, the journal has published extensive research on hydroxyapatite synthesis, including distinct studies released in 2004 and 2010. In addition to these thematic contributions, the publication has disseminated works by prominent researchers such as J. Torrent-Burgues and B.R. Heywood, among others, reinforcing its standing as a key resource for crystal growth research.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific journal dedicated to crystal growth research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006</data>
