<node id="Sci. Total Environ.">
  <data key="d0">Sci. Total Environ.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Science of the Total Environment, commonly abbreviated as Sci. Total Environ., is a scientific and academic journal dedicated to publishing research in environmental science. The journal features a broad spectrum of studies and critical reviews, with a notable emphasis on the geochemical evolution of phosphogypsum brines and the environmental impacts and radionuclide distribution associated with phosphogypsum deposits. It actively promotes research on the circular economy of phosphogypsum, including its recycling alongside red mud and steel slag into green cementitious materials. Additionally, the journal publishes investigations into fluoride toxicity in cropping systems and associated mitigation strategies, as well as fluoride immobilization techniques in cemented backfill. Further research featured in the journal addresses municipal solid waste incineration ash leaching and natural attenuation processes related to radionuclide distribution. Collectively, these publications highlight the journal's role in advancing knowledge on industrial waste management, geochemical processes, and sustainable environmental practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Sci. Total Environ. is an academic journal that published a comparative study on circular economy strategies in the ASEAN region.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-006</data>
