<node id="α-Hemihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">α-Hemihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">α-Hemihydrate gypsum is a processed form of phosphogypsum prepared for use in construction materials and sound absorbing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;α-Hemihydrate gypsum is a processed form of phosphogypsum prepared for use in construction materials and sound absorbing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;α-Hemihydrate gypsum is a processed form of phosphogypsum prepared for use in construction materials and sound absorbing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;α-Hemihydrate gypsum is a processed material prepared from phosphogypsum, with its performance evaluated in recent studies.&lt;SEP&gt;α-Hemihydrate gypsum is a synthesized material derived from cleaner phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A gypsum form characterized by regular hexagonal prisms, high strength, and excellent fluidity, suitable for reinforcement and mortar.&lt;SEP&gt;A processed form of gypsum prepared from phosphogypsum after impurity removal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791771443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supersulfated Cement">
  <data key="d0">Supersulfated Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Supersulfated cement is a construction material whose hydration properties are affected by calcination-modified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cement is a construction material whose hydration properties are affected by calcination-modified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A cement type whose hydration properties are affected by modified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cement is a specialized cement type whose hydration properties are affected by modified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cement is a specific type of cement listed as an application for phosphogypsum in the cement industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cement is a construction material whose hydration properties are modified by phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cement is a construction material whose hydration properties are affected by calcination-modified phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791119375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lime">
  <data key="d0">Lime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime (calcium oxide, CaO) is a versatile alkaline chemical reagent and mineralogical compound primarily utilized for the treatment, stabilization, and valorization of phosphogypsum. Produced through carbothermal reduction reactions or generated as a byproduct during phosphogypsum conversion processes, it functions as a critical alkaline activator, neutralizing agent, and chemical stabilizer. Lime rapidly adjusts pH levels and neutralizes the initial acidity of phosphogypsum mixes, reacting with soluble phosphorus and fluorine compounds to precipitate them into insoluble forms. This neutralization effectively reduces hazardous soluble content, mitigates environmental risks, and serves as an essential agricultural supplement for safe soil amendment. The process is highly valued for its cost-effectiveness, precision, low harmful emissions, and faster neutralization kinetics compared to alternative samples.

In civil engineering and construction, lime is extensively blended with phosphogypsum, fly ash (including Class C), yellow phosphorus slag, sand, and other supplementary materials to produce durable construction binders, building blocks, concrete mixtures, road surfaces, and low-cost housing materials. It significantly enhances the unconfined compressive strength, durability, stability, plasticity, and finesse of these cementitious matrices, particularly in filling bodies and supersulfated cement production. Lime also plays a key role in brick manufacturing, where it is mixed with phosphogypsum and sand, or where calcined phosphogypsum partially or fully substitutes traditional materials. When subjected to temperatures around 830°C, lime decomposes into micropores that improve the thermal conductivity and porosity of construction composites. Additionally, it is incorporated as a traditional additive in specific industrial formulations, such as comprising 4% of the CPGFM formulation at the Qingping Phosphate Mine, and is added to secondary mixes to further optimize material properties. Beyond structural applications, lime functions as a binding agent in adobe construction and acts as a multifaceted environmental remediation agent, ultimately facilitating the comprehensive valorization of phosphogypsum into a sustainable resource for both construction and agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is a byproduct produced alongside sulfuric acid in the traditional phosphogypsum processing method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
