<node id="Hydrothermal Conversion">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Conversion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal conversion is a chemical treatment process specifically applied to phosphogypsum to facilitate the extraction and leaching of rare earth elements. This technique serves as a preparatory step that modifies the raw material's composition, thereby enabling the efficient recovery of valuable rare earths from the phosphogypsum matrix.

The underlying mechanism operates as a two-step synthesis process that converts phosphogypsum into hydroxyapatite at a controlled temperature of 200 °C. This transformation is driven by an initial hydrolysis stage followed by a subsequent chemical reaction. By restructuring the phosphogypsum through these precise thermal and chemical conditions, the process optimizes the material for downstream rare earth leaching.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004</data>
