  <data key="d2">Equation 12 is a chemical formula presented at the beginning of the text, likely representing a reaction involving ammonium and sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 12 is a chemical formula presented at the beginning of the text, likely representing a reaction involving ammonium and sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 12 is a chemical formula presented at the beginning of the text, likely representing a reaction involving ammonium and sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 12 is a chemical equation excerpted from a scientific paper discussing phosphogypsum chemistry.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 12 describes the chemical reaction forming Ca(H₂PO₄)₂ from CaHPO₄, P₂O₅, and water.&lt;SEP&gt;Equation 12 rearranges previous equations to relate peak broadening to crystallite size and strain.</data>
