<node id="Fig. 4">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 4 is a recurring figure label utilized across numerous independent scientific publications rather than representing a single, unified diagram. Its content varies significantly depending on the specific study, though it is predominantly featured in research concerning phosphogypsum utilization, materials science, and environmental remediation. In industrial processing and rare earth element recovery, Fig. 4 illustrates primary extraction technologies, procedural steps, and leaching efficiency under various acid types and reaction conditions. It also functions as a flowchart for nano-hydroxyapatite production via phosphogypsum decomposition with hydrochloric acid, displays thermal degradation data showing mass loss variations across heating rates, outlines challenges and solutions for phosphogypsum recycling, and maps the distribution of comprehensive phosphogypsum utilization routes in China for 2022. Additionally, it presents the mathematical model of natural convection for PGEF.

Within materials science and biomedical engineering, the label documents microstructural and compositional analyses. It presents scanning electron microscopy micrographs of composite bone cements at varying magnifications, often supplemented by energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy data, and transmission electron microscopy images comparing hydroxyapatite samples prepared via hydrothermal and microwave methods. The figure also tracks hydroxyapatite morphology transformations during calcium and citrate solution stirring, displays X-ray diffraction patterns and attenuated total reflectance spectra, and compares the compressive strength of bricks across studies by Zhou et al., Raut et al., and Azam et al. Furthermore, it visualizes the microstructures of filling bodies at a 28-day curing age under different phosphorus conditions.

In environmental and geochemical research, Fig. 4 visualizes diverse datasets related to soil chemistry, radiometric analysis, and adsorption performance. It maps macro-ion equilibrium concentrations in soil solutions following phosphogypsum application, catalogs international phosphogypsum chemical compositions in tabular format, and visualizes U-238/Ra-226 and U-238/Pb-210 activity ratios in phosphate rock and phosphogypsum. The label is also employed to demonstrate adsorption dynamics, illustrating the effects of pH, contact time, doping amounts, initial concentrations, and zeta potentials on the removal of Co2+, Cd2+, Pb(II), Cu(II), and Zn(II) using various adsorbents like BC, HAP-BC, and HPA. Finally, it presents adsorption isotherms, pore width distributions for synthesized powders, and the relationship between TBP-TOPO concentration in kerosene and both phosphogypsum leaching efficiency and contaminant removal rates. Collectively, these iterations underscore the label's extensive, context-dependent application across analytical, industrial, and environmental scientific domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 is a graphical representation visualizing Equation 15 for various synthesized HAp samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 is a visual representation comparing impact categories for the soil amendment scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 illustrates California Bearing Ratio test results and Proctor compaction test data for raw PG samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating CBR and dry density results as a function of moisture content for raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 presents nitrogen adsorption/desorption isotherms, pore size distributions, particle size distributions, and mean particle diameter histograms.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 presents optical microscopy and BSE images illustrating the morphological textures of phosphogypsum grains.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-00