<node id="Hydrogen Sulfide">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Sulfide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen sulfide is a byproduct generated during the crystallization process, which can be used to reduce phosphogypsum or prepare thiourea.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a gaseous byproduct produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen Sulfide is a decomposition product of PG produced alongside calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;A hazardous gas released during CPGFM preparation that exceeds safety limits and can be inhibited by oxidizing agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen sulfide is a compound whose production is inhibited by silicon dioxide during chemical looping gasification, making the process desirable for clean production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbon">
  <data key="d0">Carbon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon (symbol C) is a fundamental chemical element that plays critical roles across biological, industrial, and materials science domains. Ecologically, it serves as an essential component actively cycled by Actinobacteria and other soil microorganisms. Industrially and in materials processing, carbon functions as a major constituent in substances like phosphogypsum, typically comprising mass fractions between 0.030% and 0.230%. It is also recognized as a distinct, chemically reactive solid product derived from the thermal decomposition of lignite, reflecting its dual classification as both a ubiquitous elemental building block and a specific industrial material.

In chemical and metallurgical applications, carbon frequently acts as a reducing agent added to mixtures to facilitate high-temperature reactions. It participates in carbothermal reduction, reduces iron oxides, and is consumed during the thermal reduction of calcium sulfate, notably reacting slowly with calcium sulfate under reducing atmospheres during phosphogypsum decomposition.

Analytically, carbon is routinely identified in various samples, including hydroxyapatite and 20HPA-HAP matrices, using techniques such as X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy and energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy. In energy-dispersive spectra, it appears in the low-energy region near 0.28 keV. Depending on the material, it may constitute approximately 11% by weight or appear as granular clusters indicative of organic impurities, often detected in trace amounts. Its presence in these contexts generally stems from multiple origins, including biochar substrates, atmospheric capture, surfactant residues, surface contamination, or inherent organic molecules. Collectively, these characteristics underscore carbon’s versatility as a naturally occurring element vital to ecological cycles and a detectable, functionally significant component in engineered or processed materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
