<node id="Elsevier">
  <data key="d0">Elsevier</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Elsevier is a prominent academic and scientific publishing organization and the parent company of the Academic Press imprint. Operating as both a traditional publishing house and a major digital journal platform, it distributes a wide array of scholarly works across diverse scientific disciplines. Its extensive catalog includes foundational texts on apatite chemistry, specialized technical books such as Hydrometallurgy of Rare Earths, and specific publications like a 2020 work on sustainable remediation alongside a book chapter on sustainable remediation using low-carbon cement. Additionally, Elsevier publishes the book chapter Advanced bioceramics within the volume Advances in Biological Science Research.

Beyond content distribution, Elsevier manages intellectual property and distribution rights for numerous specialized scientific studies. It holds copyrights for research focusing on environmental topics, particularly the valorization of phosphogypsum in construction materials, and serves as the official publisher granting reprint permissions for these works. The organization also publishes prominent academic journals, including the Journal of Environmental Radioactivity. To support ongoing scholarly communication, Elsevier's digital platform incorporates user interface features such as a Check for Updates function and a ribbon bookmark element, which facilitate tracking revisions and updates to published papers.&lt;SEP&gt;A major academic publishing company that utilizes the CrossMark service for its scientific articles.&lt;SEP&gt;A publisher that granted permission for the reproduction of Figure 13.&lt;SEP&gt;A publisher granting permission for reprinted material related to phosphogypsum preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital academic journal website platform associated with the UI icon for checking updates.</data>
