  <data key="d2">Magnesium fluoride is a specific precipitate formed from PG impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium fluoride is a specific precipitate formed from PG impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium fluoride is a specific precipitate formed from PG impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium Fluoride is a chemical compound present in the final stabilized material.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound with the formula MgF2.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnesium fluoride is an insoluble fluoride compound that forms when fluorine co-crystallizes with magnesium in PG.</data>
