<node id="Calcium Fluoride">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Fluoride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium fluoride (CaF₂) is an insoluble chemical compound and fluoride species that primarily exists as an impurity within phosphogypsum (PG) and other industrial matrices. It originates through multiple chemical and industrial pathways, including the purification, solubilization, and sulfuric acid acidification of rock phosphate, as well as various fluoride precipitation, medium transformation, and solution conversion procedures applied to PG waste. Structurally, the compound features a central atom bonded to two others, and it is frequently detected in both starting materials and final stabilized products, where it often deposits alongside calcium phosphate on cement particle surfaces.

In composite backfill and cementitious systems, calcium fluoride forms as a precipitate when fluoride ions react with quicklime or calcium hydroxide. This precipitation process serves as a key mechanism for the chemical immobilization of fluorine, effectively reducing the detrimental impact of fluoride on hydration. The compound deposits directly on calcium hydroxide particles, which can hinder further chemical reactions. Physically and chemically, calcium fluoride is characterized by its insolubility and inert behavior in specific environments, such as attaching to oxygen carrier surfaces without participating in the reaction. Its crystalline structure is notably enhanced through thermal treatment and can be analytically identified via X-ray diffraction, which shows prominent peaks at approximately 29° and 48°. The compound exhibits a moderately complexed, non-total interaction with EDTA and plays a functional role in regulating fluorine solubility within phosphogypsum matrices. However, its stability diminishes at high pH levels, leading to the release of fluoride ions. In composite applications, it causes minimal modification to crystal morphology and results in only a marginal reduction in mechanical strength.

Industrially and academically, calcium fluoride is recognized as a high-value crystallized component in Beneficiated Solid, Washed Beneficiated Solid (WBS), and Calcined Washed Beneficiated Solid (TWBS). It serves as a primary target for the transformation and valorization of phosphogypsum waste, attracting significant research into hydrofluoric acid production and PG conversion processes. Beyond waste management, the compound has established commercial applications across the fluorine industry, optical fiber manufacturing, and dental care.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium fluoride is a chemical form of fluoride present in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003</data>
