<node id="Calcium Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate is a class of insoluble chemical compounds and bioceramics characterized by high stability and low solubility, often representing refractory phosphorus. Its general stoichiometry is frequently approximated as Ca10(PO4)6Y2, encompassing various salts such as dicalcium phosphate dihydrate and tricalcium phosphate (Ca3(PO4)2). The compound typically forms under alkaline conditions through the precipitation of calcium ions with soluble phosphorus or phosphate ions. It is recognized as an insoluble form of total phosphorus and constitutes a chemical phase consistent with the elemental composition of various analyzed samples.

Calcium phosphate can be synthesized through multiple pathways, including the reaction of calcium carbonate with orthophosphate, the interaction of quicklime with phosphoric acid (which simultaneously removes harmful impurities), or the combination of calcium ions with phosphorus in treated leachate. In specialized synthesis environments, it forms layers on the surface of surfactant assemblies upon the addition of calcium precursors, which subsequently convert to hydroxyapatite during further processing. Structurally, it is identified as a distinct chemical phase, often labeled CP, corresponding to diffraction peaks around 25 and 34 degrees, and is detectable via calcium-oxygen bonds in X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy spectra.

In industrial and materials science contexts, calcium phosphate is commonly found as a precipitate originating from phosphogypsum impurities. It is frequently mixed with phosphogypsum, hypothesized to precipitate directly onto phosphogypsum crystal surfaces, and identified as a key component within the material. Within cementitious systems, it acts as an inactive component that coats cement particles, significantly retarding setting times due to its phosphorus impurity content. Beyond cement, it is utilized to form protective coatings and serves as an adhesive agent binding particles together in specialized oxygen carrier systems, with industrial processes actively targeting its stabilization and recovery.

From a biomedical perspective, calcium phosphate is recognized as a vital class of bioceramics due to its excellent biological compatibility and medical significance. It is extensively utilized in advanced drug and gene delivery applications. Ongoing research continues to investigate its spectroscopic and X-ray diffraction properties in relation to varying calcium-to-phosphate ratios, underscoring its distinct chemical, structural, and functional versatility across both industrial material systems and biomedical technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound consistent with the detected elemental composition of the sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate is an abundant raw material component that provides calcium for the phosphogypsum building blocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006</data>
