<node id="Crystal Lattice">
  <data key="d0">Crystal Lattice</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The structural framework of PG that is destroyed by physical conditions to accelerate dissolution.&lt;SEP&gt;The structural framework of PG that is destroyed by physical conditions to accelerate dissolution.&lt;SEP&gt;The structural framework of PG that is destroyed by physical conditions to accelerate dissolution.&lt;SEP&gt;The crystal lattice is the structural framework of calcium sulfate crystals where lead and thorium ions are expected to incorporate.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal lattice is the structured arrangement of host ions that accommodates foreign ions through various incorporation mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The crystal lattice refers to the structured arrangement of atoms in minerals like apatite and gypsum where ion substitution occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal Lattice is the structural framework of hydroxyapatite where phosphate and calcium ions adsorb and desorb.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003</data>
