<node id="Hemihydrate Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Hemihydrate Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemihydrate Phosphogypsum is a processed industrial byproduct derived from phosphogypsum, primarily composed of calcium sulfate hemihydrate and manufactured via the hemi-wet process. It is distinguished by its inherent self-hardening characteristics and serves as a versatile material in industrial and mining contexts. Functionally, it operates as a binder, curing agent, aggregate, and cementitious material. These attributes enable its effective use in formulating low-cost, high-efficiency filling materials and paste backfill systems.

The material is extensively applied in underground filling operations, mining backfill, and industrial goaf experiments. Ongoing research focuses on its rheological behavior, mechanical performance, and its utilization in synthesizing cementitious materials directly from raw phosphogypsum. Furthermore, environmental studies have investigated its chemical stability, specifically analyzing the leaching behavior of phosphorus and fluorine when deployed as an underground filling medium.&lt;SEP&gt;A processed form of phosphogypsum prepared through a specific manufacturing route.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate phosphogypsum is an intermediate product formed when calcium sulfate dihydrate loses crystal water during modification processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
