<node id="Cement Production">
  <data key="d0">Cement Production</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement production is a core industrial manufacturing and construction industry process that serves as a major application sector for phosphogypsum utilization. Within this framework, treated phosphogypsum is actively incorporated as a raw material, functioning specifically as an alternative set regulator and mineral addition. The process has been widely studied for its potential to effectively integrate treated phosphogypsum into cement formulations, underscoring its importance in both material science and sustainable industrial practices.

Separately, the provided data also references an industrial application where calcium sulfide is utilized as a target product or precursor. This distinct operational facet highlights the broader chemical processing and material recovery dimensions associated with the sector, reflecting the complex transformations and secondary product opportunities inherent in related industrial workflows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023</data>
