  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Flue gas desulfurization gypsum is a material used as a raw source for preparing α-calcium sulfate hemihydrate in concentrated electrolyte solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Flue gas desulfurization gypsum is a material used as a raw source for preparing α-calcium sulfate hemihydrate in concentrated electrolyte solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Flue gas desulfurization gypsum is a material used as a raw source for preparing α-calcium sulfate hemihydrate in concentrated electrolyte solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Flue gas desulfurization gypsum is an alternative gypsum source whose supply gap highlights the importance of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial byproduct used as a raw material for preparing calcium sulfate whisker via atmospheric acidification.&lt;SEP&gt;Flue gas desulfurization gypsum is used alongside CaCO3 to facilitate potassium recovery from K-feldspar.</data>
