<node id="Clay Bricks">
  <data key="d0">Clay Bricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Clay bricks are traditional construction materials and building units that can be engineered to incorporate phosphogypsum as a primary component. In these modified formulations, phosphogypsum is typically used to substitute conventional ingredients such as sand or raw clay, a process that directly alters the engineering and structural properties of the resulting bricks. This compositional adjustment allows for the production of building materials with tailored mechanical characteristics, making them suitable for various construction applications.

The utilization of phosphogypsum in clay brick production is prominently featured in scientific research, particularly in studies dedicated to the valorization and characterization of Tunisian phosphogypsum. Beyond phosphogypsum, the engineering and structural performance of clay bricks can be further optimized through the addition of other industrial by-products and supplementary materials, such as fly ash. Collectively, these modifications highlight the adaptability of clay bricks as sustainable construction materials that effectively integrate industrial waste streams while maintaining or enhancing their functional building properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Clay bricks are construction materials that incorporate Tunisian phosphogypsum for valorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Clay bricks are construction materials that can incorporate valorized phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791876137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Chloride">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium chloride serves as a versatile chemical reagent and salt component across various industrial, analytical, and biomedical applications. In industrial chemical synthesis, it functions as a primary reactant in double decomposition reactions designed to produce potassium sulfate from phosphogypsum. It is similarly employed as a chloride salt reagent that reacts directly with gypsum to yield potassium sulfate. Additionally, potassium chloride acts as a reactant to convert sodium sulfate into glaserite, after which it is utilized as a solvent to facilitate the subsequent transformation of glaserite.

In biomedical and physiological research, potassium chloride is a critical reagent in the preparation of simulated body fluid, where it is specifically added to maintain proper ionic balance. Analytically, it is formulated as a chloride solution to investigate the solubility characteristics of phosphogypsum. Experimental studies have also examined potassium chloride as a solid salt component within chemical solutions at a precise concentration of 5.00 mmol L⁻¹. Furthermore, its behavior and reactivity have been extensively investigated at elevated concentrations, reaching up to 180 g L⁻¹ when dissolved in hydrochloric acid solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Chloride is a reactant used in both one-step and two-step processes to synthesize potassium sulfate from PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Chloride is an inorganic salt dissolved to prepare a standard solution at 50 g/L.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
