  <data key="d0">Double Decomposition Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Double Decomposition Reaction is a chemical process used to convert potassium chloride and phosphogypsum into potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Double Decomposition Reaction is a chemical process used to convert potassium chloride and phosphogypsum into potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Double decomposition reaction is a chemical process that converts phosphogypsum and potassium chloride into potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Double Decomposition Reaction is a chemical process used to convert potassium chloride and phosphogypsum into potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;The double decomposition reaction is a chemical process used to produce potassium sulfate from potassium chloride and phosphogypsum.</data>
