<node id="Harmless Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Harmless Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Harmless Treatment is a specialized processing method applied to phosphogypsum (PG) to ensure its safe handling and utilization. The primary objective of this process is to neutralize the material and safely manage it, thereby mitigating potential environmental risks. Specifically, Harmless Treatment removes the inherent acidity and corrosive properties of phosphogypsum, transforming it into a stable and non-hazardous substance.

This processing step is a mandatory prerequisite before the material can be repurposed for various beneficial applications. Once treated, phosphogypsum becomes viable for use as ecological filling material, fertilizer, and in broader agricultural contexts. By addressing its chemical hazards, Harmless Treatment enables the sustainable reuse of phosphogypsum while protecting surrounding ecosystems and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmless treatment is a necessary process for the comprehensive utilization of phosphogypsum to address impurities and radioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Process required to eliminate health and environmental threats posed by phosphogypsum before application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-009</data>
