<node id="Phosphogypsum (PG)">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum (PG)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum (PG) is a solid industrial byproduct and chemical waste residue generated during the production of phosphate fertilizers and phosphoric acid. It typically manifests as a finely granulated powder, silt, or silty-sand material. Chemically, PG is primarily composed of calcium sulfate dihydrate alongside silica or quartz, and contains high concentrations of calcium ions, phosphorus, major and trace elements, heavy metals, and valuable rare earth elements. Radioactive elements and other impurities are frequently concentrated within its finest particles.

Due to its massive production volume, complex composition, and inherent hazards, PG poses significant environmental and waste management challenges. Improper disposal practices, such as dumping into marine environments, can lead to ecological contamination and pH alterations. Consequently, extensive physico-chemical characterization, elemental analysis, and studies regarding its solubility, stability, and treatment methods are routinely conducted to evaluate its properties and develop effective management strategies.

Despite these challenges, PG is increasingly targeted for recycling and valorization into value-added products, often utilizing hydrometallurgical and hydrothermal synthesis routes. Its high calcium ion content enables chemical reactivity with atmospheric carbon dioxide to form stable calcite, and it serves as a primary calcium source and starting material in processes that convert calcium sulfate into hydroxyapatite, including nano-hydroxyapatite. Industrially, PG is utilized as a raw material for cement retarders, building gypsum, roadbed construction, and as an aggregate in cemented backfill materials. It also functions as an oxygen carrier in gasification processes, a matrix for recovering rare earth elements, and is employed in thermal decomposition applications. With notable utilization efforts in regions such as Morocco and China, PG successfully transitions from a problematic waste stream into a multifunctional secondary raw material with substantial industrial and economic potential.&lt;SEP&gt;A hazardous byproduct of phosphoric acid production, classified as TE-NORM due to its radionuclide content.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is a solid material from which radionuclides and rare earth elements are leached using a TBP-TOPO solvent mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000</data>
