  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface adsorption is a mechanism by which impurities attach to the surface of phosphogypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface adsorption is a mechanism by which impurities attach to the surface of phosphogypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface adsorption represents a mode of rare earth element occurrence where metals adhere to the external surfaces of gypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A mode of REEs occurrence involving binding to the surface of gypsum crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface adsorption is a mechanism by which impurities attach to the surface of phosphogypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface adsorption is a mechanism by which radium-bearing sulfate phases attach to calcium sulfate crystals during phosphogypsum formation.</data>
