<node id="Aluminum">
  <data key="d0">Aluminum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aluminum is a chemical and metallic element that plays a multifaceted role across environmental, agricultural, and industrial domains. In phosphogypsum systems, it functions as both a major constituent and an impurity, with mass fractions typically ranging from 0.090% to 1.920%. It is also tracked as a key parameter in phosphogypsum process water, where concentrations vary depending on the specific source. Within these industrial contexts, aluminum influences fluorine precipitation mechanisms and serves as a metal component that lowers the decomposition temperature during gasification. Additionally, aluminum is recognized as a valuable metal that can be recovered from red mud and phosphogypsum through various recycling methods, including sintering, leaching, and co-sintering processes.

In agricultural and soil chemistry applications, aluminum acts as a binding agent for phosphate, precipitating the nutrient into insoluble forms that reduce its bioavailability to plants. The release rates of aluminum are utilized to estimate the efficiency of gypsum applications in soils, while certain materials demonstrate an approximate 92% increase in its removal rate. In construction and material processing, aluminum appears as an ion in cemented paste backfill mixtures and is often represented by a grey circle in technical diagrams. Furthermore, aluminum compounds are added alongside fluorine to enhance the mechanical properties of alpha-hemihydrate gypsum. Collectively, these characteristics highlight aluminum's diverse chemical behavior and its significant relevance in environmental monitoring, soil management, and advanced material processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum is a metallic impurity found in small amounts in the phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum is a major chemical species analyzed in the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element detected as peaks at approximately 226 and 227/237 nm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-027</data>
