<node id="Arsenic">
  <data key="d0">Arsenic</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Arsenic is a toxic and harmful chemical element, frequently classified as a heavy metal in environmental and agricultural literature, that occurs naturally and is notably enriched in phosphorites relative to crustal abundances. It is commonly associated with organic matter and frequently detected as a trace component in phosphogypsum, where its presence varies by region and is typically characterized using Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass-Spectrometry (ICP-MS). In phosphogypsum, arsenic concentrations generally range from 2.00 to 4.50 μg/g, with measured levels often remaining below detection limits or falling beneath the rare effect concentration threshold. It is routinely quantified in phosphogypsum process water, samples, and various mixtures to assess environmental availability, leaching toxicity, and potential contamination risks. Analytical measurements are conducted using methods such as the Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure (TCLP), with concentrations reported in milligrams per liter, and specific leaching studies have recorded values as low as 0.2 µg/L, noting that leaching rates tend to increase over time.

Due to its persistence and tendency to accumulate in soil without significantly decreasing at higher pH levels, arsenic poses substantial environmental and public health threats. Its bioavailability facilitates uptake by various crops, leading to bioaccumulation and entry into the human food chain through contaminated agricultural produce. To mitigate these risks, specific agricultural practices, such as sprinkler irrigation, have proven effective in reducing arsenic concentrations in rice grains. Additionally, the environmental management of arsenic is enhanced through material combinations; for instance, its adsorption capacity as a contaminant improves when phosphogypsum is mixed with other minerals, and its sorption on red mud increases with phosphogypsum addition. Regulatory frameworks strictly control arsenic levels to protect water resources and crop cultivation, establishing limits such as 0.05 mg/L in general water quality standards and 5 mg/L under US-EPA guidelines for mixtures, alongside precise thresholds for dry crop irrigation. Through integrated monitoring, agricultural adaptation, and regulatory oversight, the management of arsenic seeks to balance the industrial utilization of byproducts like phosphogypsum with the safeguarding of ecological and human health.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013</data>
