<node id="Morocco">
  <data key="d0">Morocco</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Morocco is a sovereign North African country and geographic region that holds approximately three-quarters of the global phosphate reserves, making it one of the world’s largest phosphate mining regions and a major producer of phosphoric acid. The nation’s extensive sedimentary and igneous phosphate rock reserves, notably the Bou Craa deposit which contains rare earth elements between 0.14% and 0.16%, underpin its industrial significance. As a leading industrial hub, Morocco generates approximately 15 million tons of phosphogypsum annually, supported by critical infrastructure like the Jorf Lasfar phosphoric acid plant and extensive storage facilities. Historically, the country has managed this massive waste output by storing or discharging most phosphogypsum into the Atlantic Ocean, a practice that has raised significant environmental concerns due to heavy metal pollution, soil cadmium accumulation, and ecological impacts, including scale deposits linked to regional desalination activities.

In response to these environmental challenges, Morocco is actively implementing circular economy strategies and sustainable waste reuse practices. These initiatives focus on processing phosphogypsum to recover valuable chemical compounds such as calcium and sodium, while also exploring its application in construction, particularly for rural road development and embankments. The suitability of this material for such projects is governed by specific local building rules, geotechnical criteria, and settlement limits for ordinary road embankments. To address the material's inherent properties, prioritized radium removal technologies are being developed, as appropriate treatment can effectively reduce the phosphogypsum's radioactivity.

Scientifically, Morocco serves as a primary geographic reference and sampling location for extensive geochemical, radiological, and industrial research. Phosphogypsum, phosphate rocks, and natural water samples from the region are frequently analyzed for their chemical compositions, impurities, distinct elemental profiles, thermal behavior, and natural radioactivity levels. These samples are characterized by elevated radionuclide concentrations, relatively low sulfur trioxide and calcium oxide content, and significant impurities, including a high unlisted component value of 32.16. Investigations also examine radiological hazard impacts, the behavior of heavy metals and radionuclides during phosphogypsum carbonation, and chemical recovery methods, with specific analytical datasets representing the country at approximately 43% by weight. This research is heavily supported by prominent academic institutions, including Mohammed VI Polytechnic University, the Geology &amp; Sustainable Mining Institute, and the University Hassan II of Casablanca, and is highlighted in studies by Abouloifa et al. (2023) and Bouargane et al. (2023), as well as regional academic events like the 2018 National PhD Students Days conference.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is a country that produces approximately 15 million tonnes of acid phosphogypsum residues annually.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is a major global producer of phosphates and the source location for the studied phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is the country where the Jorf Lasfer industrial complex and sample collection site are located.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is a country that has established a large chemical industry to manufacture phosphoric acid.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002</data>
