<node id="Aluminum Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Aluminum Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aluminum sulfate is a chemical additive used in foamed gypsum formulations to generate gas.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum sulfate is a chemical additive used in foamed gypsum formulations to generate gas.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum sulfate is a chemical additive used in foamed gypsum formulations to generate gas.&lt;SEP&gt;Aluminum sulfate is a chemical agent used to neutralize phosphogypsum acidity and immobilize soluble P2O5 and heavy metals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791424600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Bicarbonate">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Bicarbonate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium bicarbonate serves as a versatile chemical reagent and additive across multiple industrial and laboratory applications. In construction materials, it functions as a chemical additive utilized alongside aluminum sulfate in the formulation of foamed gypsum. In biomedical and laboratory settings, it acts as a key reagent for preparing simulated body fluid; specifically, it is dissolved in deionized water to achieve a solid salt component concentration of 27.00 mmol L⁻¹.

A primary application of sodium bicarbonate lies in the chemical treatment of phosphogypsum waste. Under basic conditions, it is prepared and applied as an alkaline leaching reagent, often in conjunction with other acids and carbonates. This treatment process is designed to transform gypsum into a hydride form and yields a resulting compound mixture comprising approximately 76.299% gypsum, 21.664% calcite, and 2.037% radionuclides. The application of sodium bicarbonate is generally evaluated for its capacity to reduce harmful impurities and lower radionuclide concentrations in phosphogypsum to 0.600 wt%, with the treated output appearing chemically similar to sodium carbonate. However, the leaching process exhibits complex behavior, as certain applications have been observed to increase the relative proportion of radionuclides, highlighting the nuanced chemical interactions and context-dependent outcomes involved in phosphogypsum remediation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
