<node id="Virolainen, S.">
  <data key="d0">Virolainen, S.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Virolainen, S. is a researcher whose work centers on the recovery of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum. Their research specifically investigates the application of a resin-in-leach process to extract these valuable materials from industrial byproducts. This focus highlights their expertise in hydrometallurgical techniques and sustainable resource recovery.

Regarding their publication record, Virolainen, S. served as the lead author on a 2019 study that detailed the use of the resin-in-leach method for rare earth element recovery. They also appear as a co-author on a 2021 study that further examines the extraction of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum. These contributions collectively document their ongoing involvement in advancing efficient extraction methodologies for phosphogypsum-derived resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-054</data>
