<node id="Energy Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Energy Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy consumption is a major bottleneck of thermal pretreatment due to the high temperatures required for the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy consumption is a major bottleneck of thermal pretreatment due to the high temperatures required for the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy consumption is an operational cost factor excluded from the preliminary economic assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy consumption is a major bottleneck of thermal pretreatment due to the high temperatures required for the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy consumption refers to the quantitative measurement of energy sources used in the analyzed technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy consumption is a technical and economic constraint that may limit the viability of chemical transformations of phosphogypsum.</data>
