<node id="Gypsum Plaster">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Plaster</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum plaster is a construction and building material primarily manufactured through the recycling and calcination of phosphogypsum. The production process frequently utilizes purified phosphogypsum or phosphogypsum hemihydrate as its core raw material, a preparation method notably detailed in a 2017 study. The efficiency of this manufacturing process is highly dependent on the specific calcination temperature applied during processing.

When produced from purified phosphogypsum, the resulting material exhibits distinct physical characteristics, including reduced normal consistency and increased strength. Furthermore, the physical properties of gypsum plaster are not fixed; they vary and are systematically detailed across different design formulations, allowing for tailored performance and adaptability in various construction applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040</data>
