<node id="Self-Leveling Mortar">
  <data key="d0">Self-Leveling Mortar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-Leveling Mortar is a construction material primarily utilized in building and construction applications. It is fundamentally prepared using original phosphogypsum as its core raw material, which classifies it as a phosphogypsum-based and PG-based product. This composition establishes it as a specialized building solution engineered for specific structural and finishing requirements within the construction sector.

The material is commercially produced by companies to meet industry demands. By utilizing original phosphogypsum as its foundational ingredient, Self-Leveling Mortar functions as a reliable construction product that supports modern architectural and engineering practices. Its formulation and production processes are consistently focused on delivering standardized performance in building projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-leveling mortar incorporating phosphogypsum experiences reduced wear resistance but increased drying shrinkage.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-leveling mortar is a construction product prepared using original phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-leveling mortar is a construction material prepared using original phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-leveling mortar is an application suitable for α-hemihydrate gypsum due to its excellent fluidity.</data>
