  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulphate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound constituting phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound constituting phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound constituting phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound forming the structure of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphate dihydrate is a mineral compound studied for its spontaneous precipitation behavior in the presence of metal ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulphate dihydrate is the primary chemical compound identified in the PPG precursor material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006</data>
