<node id="SEM-EDS">
  <data key="d0">SEM-EDS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM-EDS is an analytical characterization technique that integrates microscopic imaging with spectroscopic analysis to perform detailed mineralogical and chemical examinations of solid materials. By combining high-resolution structural visualization with elemental composition data, this method provides comprehensive insights into the physical and chemical properties of various substances.

The technique is extensively applied across diverse industrial and geological contexts. It is frequently utilized to study phosphogypsum, where it facilitates thorough mineralogical and chemical analysis. SEM-EDS is also employed for the mineralogical characterization of coal waste, specifically to detect and analyze rare earth elements within the material. Additionally, the method serves as a general analytical tool for characterizing solid products and is adapted to examine the microstructure of slag at elevated temperatures, such as 1250 °C. Through these varied applications, SEM-EDS remains a versatile instrument for advanced material characterization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
