<node id="XRF">
  <data key="d0">XRF</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is the abbreviation for X-ray Fluorescence, the analytical method used for elemental analysis of PG waste.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical measurement technique used alongside XRD and IR to determine the phase composition of phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical method used to determine the chemical composition and radionuclide proportions in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical technique used to determine that calcium and sulfur are the predominant elements in phosphogypsum.</data>
