<node id="Calcium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium oxide (CaO), commonly known as quicklime, is a solid alkaline chemical compound with a molar mass of 56.08 g/mol. It is a major constituent of phosphogypsum, with reported weight percentages varying by geographic origin and analytical methodology, typically ranging from approximately 30% to 30.2%, 37.07%, and up to 43 wt% within the gypsum phase. Additionally, it serves as a primary component of slag wool (comprising 28–47 wt%) and is present in building materials such as Portland and slag cement, where concentrations fluctuate based on the reagents used. Its concentration in industrial byproducts generally decreases following calcination pre-treatment.

Calcium oxide primarily forms through the high-temperature decomposition of phosphogypsum and calcium sulfate at approximately 1250°C, often acting as an intermediate or final product during secondary reaction stages. It can also be generated via the calcination of calcium hydroxide to enhance reactivity, or through specialized synthesis pathways including the reaction of calcium sulfate with coke (producing sulfur dioxide and carbon dioxide), low-temperature decomposition and reduction techniques, the oxidation of calcium sulfide in air at roughly 1000°C, and the simultaneous reaction of calcium sulfide and calcium sulfate. During these decomposition processes, it frequently combines with silica, silicon dioxide, and undecomposed calcium sulfate. The resulting material is consistently characterized as high-purity and can be further refined using two-stage low-temperature purification technology. Its presence and behavior are also documented in phase diagrams relevant to the phosphogypsum system, and its weight percentage is routinely quantified through titration processes utilizing EDTA and specific volume measurements.

Chemically, calcium oxide functions as a reactive alkaline substance that interacts with P₂O₅ to form calcium phosphate reactants and combines with silicon dioxide. It fulfills diverse industrial and chemical roles, including serving as a primary calcium source in synthetic hydroxyapatite production and providing catalytically active basic sites that facilitate biodiesel synthesis. In phosphate processing, it acts as a chemical additive to reduce phosphorus and fluorine content in phosphogypsum, functions as a neutralizing agent for precipitation mother liquid, and is incorporated into CPGFM slurry to inhibit hazardous gas generation by elevating alkalinity. Furthermore, it is a key component in cement clinker manufacturing. Through these varied production routes and functional applications, calcium oxide effectively transforms waste materials into valuable chemical and construction resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
