<node id="Silicon Dioxide">
  <data key="d0">Silicon Dioxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicon dioxide (SiO₂) is a chemically stable, acid-insoluble oxide compound that naturally occurs in vitreous glass, quartz, and gypsum, typically at higher concentrations in natural gypsum than in phosphogypsum. It frequently represents quartz and is detected as either a major crystalline component or a minor impurity depending on the specific sample context. In industrial settings, particularly within wet-process phosphoric acid production, silicon dioxide enters phosphogypsum as a component of calcium phosphate rock, functioning as an initial oxide component and a secondary chemical constituent. Its quantitative presence varies significantly across regional samples, notably appearing at higher levels in Hubei and Yunnan, with specific compositional analyses reporting concentrations of 2.27 wt% overall and 0.79 wt% in upper sections. The compound's concentration is known to decrease following calcination pre-treatment and is explicitly mapped within phase diagrams relevant to the phosphogypsum system.

Analytically, silicon dioxide is routinely monitored and targeted for quantitative laboratory procedures, with its mass ratio utilized in calculating oxide ratios and pH values. It is identified through X-ray diffraction, which reveals a characteristic diffraction peak labeled Q at approximately 20 degrees. Within phosphogypsum processing, it acts as a high-content impurity that influences thermal decomposition and phase behavior. Chemically, it reacts with generated calcium oxide, iron oxide, and calcium sulfide to form calcium silicate. Depending on the application, it can enhance sintering resistance when the material serves as an oxygen carrier, participate in syngas production, or be added to raw material mixtures to meet slag wool production requirements. Conversely, it is often treated as a major component requiring systematic elimination during standard beneficiation operations, where it is removed via flotation, initial separation stages, or high-concentration agitation.

In specialized industrial and experimental applications, silicon dioxide is combined with other substances to modify material properties. It forms eutectic mixtures that reduce melting points while remaining as unfused particles, and it is susceptible to hydrofluoric acid-based etching. Beyond phosphogypsum contexts, it serves as a reactant in solid-state reactions for synthesizing lanthanum silicate and has been integrated with bovine serum albumin in experimental systems specifically designed to analyze thermal properties. Throughout these diverse roles, silicon dioxide remains a critical compound referenced in analytical measurements, calculations, and material synthesis processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
