<node id="Phosphorus Pentoxide">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus Pentoxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorus Pentoxide (P2O5) is a chemical oxide compound that functions primarily as a significant impurity and trace constituent within phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct of phosphate processing. Its presence is intrinsically tied to production processes, where it is typically entrained and often found at concentrations exceeding those of fluorine. While some analytical frameworks classify it as a trace marker indicating industrial origin, others regard it as a major impurity that contributes to environmental pollution. In phosphogypsum, particularly in hemihydrate forms, it exists as a soluble impurity that negatively impacts material properties by combining with calcium ions, thereby hindering hydration, diminishing the retarder effect, and complicating practical applications. Consequently, its concentration varies across samples, with documented values including 1.56 wt%, 1.45 wt% in the top section of composition tables, and a measured concentration of 0.69 ± 0.01 in other contexts, though it is generally present in low to minor amounts. Regional variations also exist, with notably higher concentrations observed in Hubei phosphogypsum, which contributes to elevated total phosphorus levels in leachate.

To mitigate its environmental and industrial impacts, various treatment protocols are employed to reduce or eliminate Phosphorus Pentoxide prior to utilization. These methods include thermal processing such as calcination, chemical immobilization, and citric acid treatments. During purification, removal rates are actively monitored, and depending on the chemical processes, the compound can sometimes be recovered alongside rare earth elements during sulfuric acid processing. In analytical and industrial contexts, Phosphorus Pentoxide is formally tracked as a key chemical parameter, with its concentration and mass fraction routinely quantified in standardized datasets and data tables, often utilizing specific superscript notation to denote precise analytical values or experimental conditions. Statistical plots are also utilized to analyze its mass fraction within phosphogypsum. Furthermore, in broader environmental and industrial assessments, it is quantified as an air emission in Life Cycle Inventory data for brick production and is linked to a documented savings of 6.2 kilograms in inventory records. Overall, Phosphorus Pentoxide represents a critical chemical factor in phosphogypsum processing, necessitating careful monitoring, targeted removal, and precise analytical documentation to manage its effects on material properties and environmental compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide (P2O5) is a compound associated with P-O bonding identified in the P 2p spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus pentoxide is a component present in the phosphogypsum waste with a concentration of 0.80%.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound ($\mathrm{P_2O_5}$) targeted for quantitative analysis in the laboratory procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Pentoxide is the chemical compound analyzed using the spectrophotometric parameters and formulas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-00