<node id="Iron(III) Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Iron(III) Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron(III) oxide (Fe2O3) is a chemical and mineral oxide compound referenced with a molar mass of 79.84 g/mol. It functions as a standard material for calibrating iron measurements and is routinely targeted as a primary analyte in laboratory quantitative procedures. Depending on the specific analytical protocol, its concentration is determined through various techniques, including spectrophotometric methods detailed in Section 15, titration calculations utilizing EDTA volume and sample mass, and compositional table evaluations.

In industrial and geological matrices, particularly within phosphogypsum waste, Iron(III) oxide is consistently identified as a minor impurity or trace constituent. Reported concentrations exhibit significant variability across different samples and measurement methods, ranging from 89.10 to 102.60 ppm, 0.07 wt% in the top section of composition tables, 0.08% (notably the lowest recorded value in Yunnan samples), 0.10%, and up to 1.74 wt%. During phosphogypsum purification processes, the compound demonstrates a removal efficiency of 80.32%. Conversely, when evaluated in WBS and TWBS samples, it is classified as a main metal element compound, though its trace concentrations remain slightly lower than those observed in phosphogypsum.

Beyond its presence in industrial byproducts and geological matrices, Iron(III) oxide holds specialized significance in materials science. It functions as a critical iron oxide component within composite oxygen carriers, where it actively participates in oxygen release pathways and exhibits a defined release priority. Collectively, these attributes underscore the compound's variable presence, analytical importance, and functional utility across diverse chemical, industrial, and technological environments.&lt;SEP&gt;An iron oxide added in modest amounts to the ingredients system, impacting pH and viscosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) Oxide is an additive added to the mixture to satisfy raw material specifications for slag wool.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) Oxide is a chemical compound whose presence has a negligible effect on the lowest eutectic point of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) oxide is a reactant that decomposes into iron(II) oxide and carbon dioxide when reacted with carbon.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactant that undergoes reduction to form iron(II) oxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
