<node id="Magnesium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Magnesium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnesium oxide (MgO) is a chemical and mineral compound with a molar mass of 40.31 g/mol. It occurs naturally in gypsum, though typically in negligible amounts, and is frequently identified as a trace or minor impurity in phosphogypsum, where documented concentrations range from 180.49 to 235.40 parts per million or 0.02 to 0.20 weight percent. As an oxide component in the initial phosphogypsum mixture, it is integral to the system's phase diagram. During industrial processing and beneficiation, magnesium oxide concentrations typically increase and are often found alongside rare earth elements, yet the compound remains relatively stable before and after treatment, with its distribution routinely tracked in compositional and comparative analysis tables. Analytically, its weight percentage is commonly determined through standardized back titration using ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) and volume difference calculations, while its mass ratio is also factored into broader oxide and pH value calculations.

In materials engineering and industrial applications, magnesium oxide serves multiple functional roles. The precise ratio of magnesium oxide to monopotassium phosphate is a critical factor that directly enhances cement strength. It is also utilized as an additive in slag systems to adjust quaternary acidity coefficients and lower melting points through eutectic mixture formation. Specifically, magnesium oxide combines with calcium oxide to form eutectic phases such as spinel. Furthermore, it is incorporated into industrial solid wastes, including blast furnace slag and fly ash, to meet specific slag wool composition requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792095416</data>
