</node>
<node id="Potassium Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium oxide (K2O) is a chemical compound that functions as a minor constituent within the composition of phosphogypsum. It is routinely measured and recorded in chemical composition tables that document the material's elemental makeup. Quantitative analysis shows that potassium oxide comprises approximately 0.08 weight percent in phosphogypsum, classifying it as a trace or negligible component in this specific context.

Comparative evaluations also list potassium oxide in natural gypsum, where it similarly occurs in negligible quantities. As a standard chemical parameter, potassium oxide is consistently tracked alongside other constituents to assess the compositional profile and potential industrial applications of both phosphogypsum and natural gypsum sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium oxide is a chemical compound present in phosphogypsum with a measured concentration of 0.01 ± 0.001.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium oxide is a minor impurity detected in phosphogypsum before and after treatment, showing no significant changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical oxide present at 0.01 wt% in the top section of the phosphogypsum composition table.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound whose molar ratio is part of the denominator in the M_eta equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004</data>
