<node id="Carbonate">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate (CO3 2-) is a chemical anion that participates in various aqueous reactions and crystallographic substitutions. In liquid-phase systems, it forms as the final ion before reacting with calcium ions. Within chemical speciation models, carbonate interacts with cadmium and dictates the specific type of lead precipitate generated during immobilization processes. Structurally, it substitutes for phosphate ions within both apatite and hydroxyapatite crystal lattices. This incorporation into hydroxyapatite can diminish material stability by increasing its solubility.

Experimentally, carbonate is monitored across multiple stages, with concentration levels typically starting at the lowest initial values and demonstrating a consistent, steady decline. Analytical data further indicates that the molar fraction percentage of carbonate decreases at elevated phosphogypsum doses when compared to standard analytical values.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate is an ion that can be incorporated into the HAp structure or adsorbed onto the surface, decreasing crystalline stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate is a chemical group associated with absorption peaks in the 1400–1500 cm⁻¹ range of the FTIR spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate is a component in hydroxyapatite believed to affect protein adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate is the primary substituent in biological hydroxyapatite, typically present at 5 to 8 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Naturally occurring compound acting as a cementing and cohesive agent responsible for mechanical improvements.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate is a chemical compound that forms insoluble precipitates with lead in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017</data>
