<node id="Fig. 7">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 7 is a figure label employed across multiple distinct scientific publications rather than representing a single unified entity. Consequently, its content and purpose vary significantly depending on the specific study. In environmental and soil chemistry research, Fig. 7 illustrates the percentage of active cadmium in soil solution relative to total cadmium content. Within the extensive literature on phosphogypsum processing and conversion, the label appears in several distinct contexts: it depicts the dynamic concentration variations of cerium and calcium during hydrochloric acid leaching, specifically highlighting calcium concentration peaks; outlines the Boren-Haber reaction cycle for catalytic decomposition; shows the conversion procedure using a carbonate solution; and presents powder diffractograms comparing raw phosphogypsum with thermally treated samples. It also classifies the setting time and hardening rates of hydraulic binders derived from phosphogypsum, and tracks compressive strength variations in phosphogypsum cement mortar samples across different curing ages in air and water.

In materials science and engineering applications, Fig. 7 frequently plots mechanical properties, such as compressive and bending strength as a function of sodium chloride content, or examines the effects of competing cations, sodium chloride concentration, and uptake percentages across multiple adsorption-desorption cycles. In synthetic chemistry and pharmaceutical research, the label serves as a flowchart for the proposed synthesis route of nHA production. Additionally, Fig. 7 is utilized for analytical characterization across various studies, including XPS survey and high-resolution spectra for elemental analysis, FTIR spectra comparing pure HAp, pure drugs, and drug-loaded HAp samples, and FTIR spectra evaluating the Brij-93 surfactant against materials synthesized at varying surfactant concentrations. Given these divergent subjects, Fig. 7 must be interpreted contextually as a standard figure identifier across independent studies covering soil analysis, chemical leaching, mechanical testing, adsorption behavior, material synthesis, and spectroscopic characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 7 details the production and construction technology of PGEF.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the Halder-Wagner method analysis for synthesized HAp nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the classification areas of mixes according to torque measurements at 90 curing days.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite figure presenting various photoelectrochemical performance measurements including LSV, transient responses, and impedance analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the wavelengths of spectral lines and concentration decreases of major elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014</data>
