<node id="Soil">
  <data key="d0">Soil</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil is a fundamental natural, terrestrial, and geological substrate that functions as a dynamic physical and biological matrix and a critical environmental compartment. Serving as the primary foundation for agricultural and ecological systems, it facilitates chemical mixing, root growth, microbial activity, nutrient cycling, and plant development. As a geological material, Soil contains uranium concentrations and radionuclide activity levels that vary by parent material, acts as the largest source of background environmental radon with a baseline emanation fraction of 20%, and features Radium-226 concentrations that dictate its suitability for agricultural and residential use. It also serves as a natural medium for cation and anion leaching, uranium series radionuclide behavior, and plant uptake, while frequently facilitating leaching into groundwater systems. Due to its complex physicochemical properties, Soil is extensively utilized as a natural reference medium for comparative trace element analysis, chemical concentration baselines, and scientific evaluations of heavy metal accumulation. Additionally, it functions as the base material for preparing adobe samples and stabilizer mixtures.

Soil is highly vulnerable to environmental contamination and readily accumulates fluorides and potentially toxic elements from atmospheric deposition and industrial activities. It frequently receives phosphogypsum applications via stack deposition, which can leach toxic gases and polluted water into the ground, disrupting its functioning and contaminating it through leaching processes. This accumulation often triggers soil acidification, altered chemical balance, reduced organic matter, and compromised structural integrity, prompting batch incubation studies to monitor shifts in element speciation and pH. Conversely, phosphogypsum is also applied to Soil to improve its physio-chemical properties, treat acidity, and support plant growth, highlighting a dual role that depends on management practices and application context. Given its critical role, Soil is a primary focus for pollution research and agricultural management. Passivation and remediation technologies are deployed to immobilize accumulated contaminants, while agricultural amendments such as biofertilizers and straw are applied to actively enhance porosity, density, structural stability, fertility, and nutrient availability. Fertilizers, including phosphorus-based applications, are routinely introduced to increase nutrient supply and boost crop yield. Ultimately, Soil operates as a complex environmental medium where ecological health, agricultural productivity, and pollution control intersect.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is an environmental medium affected by the seepage of impurities from phosphogypsum stockpiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is an environmental medium where phosphogypsum pollutants accumulate and undergo leaching migration.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil is a terrestrial environment where phosphogypsum fluorides accumulate and where phosphorus migrates via leaching.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-00