<node id="Florida">
  <data key="d0">Florida</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Florida is a U.S. state and geographic region that serves as a major global hub for phosphate rock mining and processing, particularly for wet-process phosphoric acid production. As a primary source of phosphogypsum, a byproduct of phosphate processing, the state generates over 30 million tons annually, which is frequently stored in large industrial stacks and ponds. The region's phosphogypsum has been extensively analyzed for its chemical composition, impurities, and radionuclide activity concentrations, revealing characteristics such as the presence of contaminated material, monoclinic crystals, and varying Radon-222 flux rates across different surfaces. Comparative studies indicate that Florida's phosphogypsum contains lower concentrations of certain rare earth elements than Brazilian sources. Despite this, the material has been actively researched for rare earth recovery and gypsum upgrading, utilizing chelating polymers and acidic extracts derived from phosphate mining materials.

Environmental and radiological assessments in Florida have been particularly rigorous due to the industrial scale of phosphate operations. Scientific investigations have routinely measured uranium-238 and radium-226 activities in local phosphate materials, while also identifying abundant Polonium-210 in groundwater aquifers beneath mined lands. Central and northern phosphogypsum stockpiles have been specifically assessed for radionuclide release, with studies focusing on nuclide migration and environmental radiochemistry. Consequently, Florida has become a focal point for research addressing phosphogypsum disposal, soil amendments, and environmental management. The state hosts the Florida Institute of Phosphate Research and has been the venue for specialized symposia dedicated to phosphogypsum policy and scientific advancement, underscoring its critical role in both industrial phosphate production and the ongoing study of its radiological and chemical impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Florida is a region studied for nuclide migration and the environmental radiochemistry of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Florida is a geographic region referenced as the source of phosphogypsum in a 2017 recovery study.&lt;SEP&gt;Florida is the geographic region where phosphogypsum radiochemistry was studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Florida is a region in the USA where phosphorites contain natural radioactive elements, limiting phosphogypsum application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003</data>
