<node id="Fertilizer Production">
  <data key="d0">Fertilizer Production</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fertilizer production is an industrial process primarily defined by its generation of phosphogypsum as a solid byproduct. This waste material is notably enriched with radionuclides, which distinguishes it from other industrial residues and necessitates careful handling. As the dominant source of this material, fertilizer manufacturing fundamentally drives global phosphogypsum production rates.

The scale of this industrial activity is expanding rapidly, with current projections indicating a sevenfold increase in phosphogypsum output by the year 2050. This anticipated surge in waste generation has directly catalyzed significant associated environmental research, focusing on the ecological impacts, safe disposal methods, and potential recycling pathways for phosphogypsum within the broader fertilizer industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011</data>
