<node id="USEPA">
  <data key="d0">USEPA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States Environmental Protection Agency (USEPA) is a federal regulatory body tasked with establishing environmental rules and safety standards. Although primarily a United States government agency, it has been identified in certain research scopes as an international entity of interest. A major component of its regulatory mandate involves phosphogypsum and associated radioactive materials. The USEPA classifies phosphogypsum as Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material (TENORM) and designates radium-226 (Ra-226) as a Group A human carcinogen. Accordingly, the agency establishes rules governing radioactive emissions and safety limits for phosphogypsum sources, while actively regulating radon emissions from phosphogypsum stacks. Due to these radioactive properties, the USEPA restricted the general use of phosphogypsum in 1992, permitting exceptions only for applications that remain below specific radium thresholds.

In addition to its work with radioactive materials, the USEPA has engaged in broader environmental modeling and research initiatives. The agency conducted and sponsored a workshop review dedicated to metals fate and transport modeling in streams and watersheds. The proceedings and findings from this workshop were subsequently documented and reviewed in a 2008 publication, highlighting the agency's ongoing commitment to advancing environmental science and regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Environmental Protection Agency that classified PG as TE-NORM.&lt;SEP&gt;The USEPA establishes regulatory limits for trace element concentrations, which the tested mixes generally meet.&lt;SEP&gt;USEPA is the regulatory body that establishes standard specifications and limits for heavy metal leaching in construction materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
