<node id="TENORM">
  <data key="d0">TENORM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TENORM, an acronym for Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material, is a classification used to describe substances that exhibit heightened radioactivity concentrations as a direct consequence of human industrial activities. Unlike naturally occurring background radiation, these materials have been concentrated or mobilized through technological processes, resulting in increased levels of radionuclides that require specific environmental and safety considerations.

In practical applications, TENORM is most frequently associated with phosphogypsum, a byproduct of the phosphorus fertilizer industry, particularly when evaluating disposed phosphogypsum samples. Scientific assessments often study TENORM alongside its baseline counterpart, NORM (Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material), with a focused measurement of uranium, thorium, potassium, and radon levels. To properly manage the environmental impact of these materials, regulatory and research frameworks frequently re-evaluate their environmental limitations using specialized methodologies such as the Biogeosystem Technique, ensuring accurate tracking and mitigation of technologically enhanced radioactive elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015</data>
