<node id="Ecosphere">
  <data key="d0">Ecosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ecosphere is the global ecological system through which cadmium spreads via eolian and water transfer.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the global ecological system where barriers for heavy metal transfer are reinforced.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the global ecological system managed by the transcendental nature-similarity approach.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the global ecological system through which cadmium spreads via eolian and water transfer.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the global ecological system managed by the transcendental nature-similarity approach.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the global ecological system where barriers for heavy metal transfer are reinforced.&lt;SEP&gt;The ecosphere is the natural environment boundary that the system boundaries separate the studied system from.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-002</data>
