<node id="Mathematical Equation">
  <data key="d0">Mathematical Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A formula defining the k_asCd parameter by summing interactions between Cadmium and five anions.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical equation calculates the adsorption coefficient for cadmium by summing terms representing ligand concentrations and inverse stability constants.&lt;SEP&gt;A formula $F_p = \frac{3f\gamma_b}{2r}$ describing forces in phosphogypsum physics.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical equation P = P_p - P_c represents a pressure balance calculation used in engineering contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;A linear equation displayed on a black background that defines a direct proportionality between two variables.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard scientific formula used to calculate Removal Efficiency in adsorption studies.&lt;SEP&gt;The structured representation of the formula connecting titration variables to the chloride percentage result.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792068764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
