<node id="Nickel">
  <data key="d0">Nickel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nickel is a chemical element classified as both a transition metal and a heavy metal, extensively studied across environmental, geological, and industrial domains. Ecologically, it is frequently investigated alongside cadmium and lead due to its phytotoxicity and extraction potential, while geologically it is characteristically depleted in phosphorites relative to average crustal abundances and often associates with organic matter. Industrially, nickel appears as a trace element in phosphogypsum, where its concentration is systematically documented in micrograms per gram and often measured at less than 1. It is routinely analyzed in phosphogypsum samples and mixtures for leaching toxicity assessments, including the Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure, where concentrations are recorded in milligrams per liter. Regulatory oversight varies, as some contexts note concentrations aligning with US-EPA limits, while others indicate no specific US-EPA limit is established for nickel in these applications.

As a contaminant in phosphogypsum-amended soils, nickel contributes to moderate pollution and poses notable environmental and public health risks, though its mobility in seepage waters is typically constrained by natural buffering processes. Its concentration in phosphogypsum solutions is actively monitored against established regulatory thresholds. In extraction processes, nickel is found alongside rare earth elements in source materials and necessitates separation, a task commonly achieved through specific ionic liquid extraction methods.

In chemical engineering and materials science, nickel serves multiple advanced functions. It acts as a key component in compound oxygen carriers, particularly when combined with phosphogypsum or iron, to effectively lower reaction temperatures. Simultaneously, it is a primary target for environmental remediation via adsorption using hydroxyapatite-based composites, with research by M. Ferri and R. Foroutan detailing its rapid ion exchange and adsorption mechanisms. Beyond remediation, nickel is utilized as a metal dopant within hydroxyapatite structures to modify photocatalytic properties, a modification that notably slows the degradation rate of 17α-methyltestosterone compared to undoped variants. Collectively, these attributes highlight nickel’s multifaceted role in ecological monitoring, industrial byproduct management, and advanced material engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a trace element measured in phosphogypsum minerals using LA-ICP-MS.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a heavy metal element present in phosphogypsum at concentrations lower than the rare effect concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a trace element listed in the tabular data associated with phosphogypsum analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
