</node>
<node id="Microelements">
  <data key="d0">Microelements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microelements are trace elements in soil solution, including heavy metals, whose equilibrium is calculated.&lt;SEP&gt;Microelements are trace elements in soil solution, including heavy metals, whose equilibrium is calculated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biosphere">
  <data key="d0">Biosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The biosphere is the ecological system affected by cadmium pollution and soil contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;The global ecological system referenced in studies optimizing matter flow and climate at the stage of technogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;The biosphere is the ecological system affected by cadmium pollution and soil contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;The global ecological system referenced in studies optimizing matter flow and climate at the stage of technogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Phosphogypsum Waste Utilization Technology">
  <data key="d0">Standard Phosphogypsum Waste Utilization Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard phosphogypsum waste utilization technology is a conventional method that increases soil contaminant levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard phosphogypsum waste utilization technology is a conventional method that increases soil contaminant levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contaminants">
  <data key="d0">Contaminants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contaminants are harmful substances in soil whose spread is reduced by intra-soil passivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants are harmful substances in soil whose spread is reduced by intra-soil passivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Substances originating from phosphogypsum that may leach into groundwater or contact soil materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants are pollutants present in gas, liquid, and solid phases that hydroxyapatite helps remove during remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Contaminants such as strontium ions favor the formation of isomorphous phases with radium sulfate, enhancing radium incorporation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018</data>
