<node id="Lime Milk">
  <data key="d0">Lime Milk</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime milk is a chemical agent used to neutralize phosphogypsum sludge acid residue.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime milk is a chemical agent used to neutralize phosphogypsum sludge acid residue.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime milk is mixed with phosphogypsum to neutralize water-insoluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;A washing agent used to treat phosphogypsum, resulting in cement with higher long-term strength compared to natural gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791593333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Runoff">
  <data key="d0">Surface Runoff</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;A pathway through which high phosphorus concentration leachates are discharged into the Yangchang River.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological process that transports heavy metal complexes from land to surface water and the ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a concern related to phosphogypsum storage sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological pathway through which pollutants migrate rapidly in mountainous regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791900207</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground Water">
  <data key="d0">Ground Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground water is an underground water resource polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground water is an underground water resource polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground Water is an aquifer system studied for natural radioisotopes and barium contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;An environmental medium into which uranium-thorium series radioisotopes are transported from solid materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ground Water is an environmental compartment receiving leaching and seepage, providing potable water to humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground water is the environmental medium evaluated against the GB/T 14848-2017 standard.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground water is a natural solvent used by Pulhani for leaching radium-226 and uranium-238 from vertisol soil.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791791530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lead Ion">
  <data key="d0">Lead Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead ion is a heavy metal pollutant present in phosphogypsum at significant concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead ion is a heavy metal pollutant present in phosphogypsum at significant concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead ions are toxic heavy metals captured by three-dimensionally ordered macroporous hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead Ion (Pb2+) is the target adsorbate for which nano-structured pig bone hydroxyapatite was developed.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead ions are toxic heavy metal ions that can replace calcium ions in the C-S-H matrix through ion exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead ion (Pb²⁺) is an ion that may replace calcium ions in C-S-H.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023</data>
