<node id="Sulfuric acid">
  <data key="d0">Sulfuric acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfuric acid is a strong acid that reacts with thorium(IV) phosphate to drive the chemical transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is a chemical reagent used in the wet process to attack phosphate rock for phosphoric acid production.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical used to decompose PG in the synthesis route proposed by Nasrellah.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is the chemical reactant used to dissolve phosphate ore in the production of phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is the chemical reagent used in the wet acid method to digest phosphate rock.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000</data>
