<node id="Phosphate rocks">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate rocks</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate rocks serve as the raw material feedstock and naturally contain trace amounts of thorium.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rocks are natural ore deposits containing rare earth elements, estimated at 60-100 billion tons globally.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw material used in the production process of phosphoric acid, from which phosphogypsum is obtained.</data>
