<node id="Sulfur">
  <data key="d0">Sulfur</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfur is a fundamental chemical element that maintains atomic balance across chemical reactions and plays critical roles in industrial, geological, and agricultural applications. In the context of phosphogypsum, a common industrial byproduct, sulfur serves as a predominant and major elemental component, typically found alongside calcium. It is primarily derived from sulfuric acid and is highly abundant, often covering nearly the entire surface area of samples, which confirms the bulk material's gypsum nature. X-ray fluorescence (XRF) analysis consistently identifies sulfur as the most abundant or a predominant element in these samples. While some analyses suggest sulfur can dominate the composition, accounting for over ninety percent of the mass, measured concentrations vary significantly across different studies, ranging from 0.006% to 44.450%, with specific dried samples recording values of 15.00%, 17.04%, and 17.6%. Within phosphogypsum particles, sulfur is widely distributed and frequently exhibits the highest mass fraction among major elements. It is also classified as a volatile chemical species and is spectroscopically identifiable by a distinct peak around 2.3 keV, making its detection essential for accurate material characterization.

Beyond its prevalence in mineral byproducts, sulfur exhibits dynamic behavior during processing. Its concentration decreases by approximately 13% in leached samples compared to raw materials, highlighting its mobility and reactivity. In industrial settings, sulfur is present in syngas mixtures, where it can be effectively captured by oxygen carriers, and it plays a central role in the thermal processing of phosphogypsum, acting as a primary decomposition product during thermal transformation and serving as a key focus in thermodynamic studies. Agriculturally, sulfur functions as an essential plant nutrient. It is supplied to soils through phosphogypsum, which acts as a low-grade fertilizer component, and is also delivered via dedicated agricultural products like ammonium sulfate. Across these diverse chemical, industrial, and environmental applications, the presence, distribution, and concentration of sulfur remain vital for material analysis, resource utilization, and agricultural supplementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is the target resource recovered from phosphogypsum, with over 97.44 wt % recovery achieved in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is a valuable element recycled efficiently via carbothermal reduction smelting for sulfur acid production.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is an element whose chemical state on the reduced sample surface is determined by XPS analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is a chemical element present in phosphogypsum that is targeted for removal during the desulfurization process.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is a key element tracked in the slag, with mass fractions measured below 1.0 wt% in specific analyzed spots.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfur is a key component within phosphogypsum that researchers aim to recover for industrial use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
