  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen is a fundamental chemical element that plays critical roles across chemical, mineralogical, and industrial domains. In its standard molecular state, it exists as a diatomic molecule and can also function as an ion in specific mixtures. As a cornerstone of chemical stoichiometry, oxygen actively drives oxidation reactions, with its atomic count strictly balanced in reaction equations to maintain mass conservation, as demonstrated in instances where 44 atoms are balanced on both sides. Structurally, oxygen atoms surround the central phosphorus atom in the orthophosphate ion and serve as a primary constituent of quartz, where it undergoes substitution by fluorine during the rate-determining step of certain mineralogical reactions. Its presence is consistent with oxide or sulfate matrices in various materials.

In geological and industrial materials, oxygen is consistently detected in high concentrations and is uniformly distributed within gypsum matrices. It is one of the most abundant elements in phosphogypsum, comprising between 52.01% and 58.02% of the dried material by weight, alongside sulfur and calcium. Energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy identifies oxygen with the tallest peak and a medium-height peak at approximately 0.5 to 0.52 keV, establishing it as a definitive analytical marker for phosphogypsum identification. Oxygen is also a primary component in hydroxyapatite and BC nanoparticles, where it is detected via EDX and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy in samples such as 20HPA-HAP prior to adsorption. Notably, its weight percentage in hydroxyapatite decreases as surfactant concentration increases. Functionally within hydroxyapatite, oxygen acts as an atmospheric component that accepts electrons transferred from material vacancies or through electron trapping mechanisms, facilitating radical formation that instigates the oxidation of organic compounds. It is also explicitly depicted in the molecular diagrams of PTEs and interacts with surface-disposed phosphogypsum under atmospheric conditions.

Industrially, oxygen extracted from or utilized within phosphogypsum is strategically deployed as an oxygen carrier in chemical looping gasification processes. Furthermore, during the thermal breakdown of calcium sulfate, oxygen is released as a gaseous product alongside sulfur dioxide, a behavior observed during both the self-decomposition and further high-temperature decomposition stages of the mineral.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
