<node id="Adsorption Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Adsorption Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The adsorption coefficient, denoted as $k_{asCd}$, is a parameter calculated to represent cadmium binding behavior in solution.&lt;SEP&gt;The adsorption coefficient is a physical parameter denoted by alpha in the Tauc plot equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stability Constant">
  <data key="d0">Stability Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stability constant is an equilibrium parameter used to quantify the formation of cadmium complexes with various anions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ligands">
  <data key="d0">Ligands</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ligands are molecules or ions that compete for binding with cadmium ions in aqueous solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqueous solutions are the medium in which cadmium speciation and ligand competition occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The medium in which the competitive adsorption of heavy metal ions onto the nanocomposite was studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous Solutions are the solvent medium in which CTAB forms micelles and hydroxyapatite precipitates.&lt;SEP&gt;Water-based solutions in which phosphogypsum and synthetic gypsum solubility is investigated.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous solutions are water-based solvents used by Azouazi for extensive leaching studies on phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous solutions serve as the medium from which rare earths are extracted via solvent extraction techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791813629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cadmium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Cadmium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cadmium sulfate is a chemical complex formed between cadmium and sulfate ions, characterized by a specific stability constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cadmium Chloride">
  <data key="d0">Cadmium Chloride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cadmium chloride is a chemical complex formed between cadmium and chloride ions, characterized by a specific stability constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cadmium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Cadmium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cadmium hydroxide is a chemical complex formed between cadmium and hydroxide ions, characterized by a specific stability constant.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadmium hydroxide precipitates at high pH values, slightly improving cadmium removal from wastewater.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadmium hydroxide is a precipitate formed when toxic cadmium ions react with calcium and hydroxide ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791719530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Green Ponds">
  <data key="d0">Green Ponds</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Green ponds are large rectangular settling ponds or storage lagoons within the industrial complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="White/Grey Areas">
  <data key="d0">White/Grey Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">White or grey areas represent phosphogypsum piles, dried sludge, or containment dikes at the facility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agricultural Land">
  <data key="d0">Agricultural Land</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Agricultural land is a strip of farmland separating the industrial complex from the main urban area.&lt;SEP&gt;Agricultural land separates the industrial site from the main urban area.&lt;SEP&gt;Agricultural Land is the target environment for PG soil amendment to correct calcium levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Agricultural land is the target environment for soil amendment applications.</data>
