<node id="SiO2">
  <data key="d0">SiO2</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">SiO2, chemically known as silicon dioxide, is a fundamental chemical compound and the definitive chemical formula for quartz. It is a widely distributed substance found in various industrial and geological materials, including cement clinker and granulated slag. In compositional analyses, silicon dioxide is frequently identified as a variable chemical component and a major species within phosphogypsum (PG). It is also recognized as a significant impurity in this material, with its presence consistently documented in data tables that provide specific numerical concentration ranges.

Beyond its natural and industrial occurrences, SiO2 serves several specialized functional roles in chemical and materials processing. It is utilized as an inert carrier material designed to inhibit grain growth during the CLG process. Additionally, silicon dioxide functions as a traditional catalyst support in environmental chemistry applications, where it is routinely evaluated and compared against apatite carriers in studies focused on DeNOx activity. These diverse applications highlight its versatility as both a structural component and a functional material in various scientific and engineering contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;SiO2 is a chemical compound present in the slag system, influencing quaternary acidity and melting temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;SiO2 is an additive used in the reductive decomposition of waste gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CaO">
  <data key="d0">CaO</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium oxide (CaO) is an alkaline chemical compound that serves as a major constituent in cement clinker, granulated slag, and phosphogypsum (PG). It is routinely identified during the compositional analysis of PG and is frequently measured as a potential constituent within PG samples. In high-temperature processing environments, CaO plays a dynamic role during the decomposition of PG; it is generated through the oxidation of calcium sulfide (CaS) and simultaneously competes with CaS throughout the decomposition pathway. To better understand these thermal reactions, CaO is routinely compared thermodynamically during PG decomposition processes.

Beyond its natural occurrence and thermal behavior, CaO is utilized in various industrial and chemical applications. It functions as an alkaline substance in base-washing procedures, where it is employed to adjust the pH of PG systems. Additionally, when integrated into alkaline activators, an increased concentration of CaO stimulates sulphate activation, which directly enhances the mechanical strength of cement. These multifaceted properties highlight CaO's critical role across material composition, thermal decomposition dynamics, and cementitious performance optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium oxide is a major chemical component consistently measured in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound measured in weight percent in the provided analytical data.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is a chemical compound representing calcium oxide, showing significant concentration variations in the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical component present in the phosphogypsum at 28.68 wt %.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is a chemical compound present in the slag system, contributing to quaternary acidity and phase formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al2O3">
  <data key="d0">Al2O3</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aluminum oxide (Al2O3) is a chemical compound that serves as a key component in various industrial and geological materials, including cement clinker, granulated slag, and phosphogypsum. Compositional analyses identify it as a minor constituent within phosphogypsum samples. In quantitative datasets, Al2O3 is consistently recorded with numerical concentration ranges and varying levels across different samples, yielding a documented average concentration of 4536.63 ppm.

From a chemical and industrial perspective, the concentration of Al2O3 plays a critical role in phase formation; a reduction in its levels prevents the formation of ettringite and simultaneously weakens its characteristic phase peak. Beyond its presence in construction and waste materials, Al2O3 functions as a traditional catalyst support. In environmental catalysis research, it is routinely evaluated and compared against apatite carriers to assess DeNOx activity performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Al2O3 is an aluminum oxide compound whose concentration is quantified using the described titration method.&lt;SEP&gt;Al2O3 is a chemical compound whose mass fraction is calculated using the provided titration formula.&lt;SEP&gt;Al2O3 is a chemical compound present in the slag system, influencing quaternary acidity and phase formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Al2O3 is an additive used in gypsum decomposition and its transmission is tracked during the process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fe2O3">
  <data key="d0">Fe2O3</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fe2O3, chemically identified as iron(III) oxide or iron oxide, is a significant chemical compound utilized across various industrial and analytical contexts. In energy applications, it functions as a primary iron oxide component within mixed oxygen carriers designed for chemical looping combustion.

In material science and industrial byproduct analysis, Fe2O3 is consistently identified as a key chemical constituent in both cement clinker and phosphogypsum. Comprehensive compositional and mineralogical analyses classify it as a major species and notable impurity within phosphogypsum matrices. Quantitative evaluations further document its presence in concentration and data tables, where it is associated with specific numerical concentration ranges and an average measured value of 990.65 ppm. These analytical records highlight its prevalent occurrence and measurable concentration in phosphogypsum samples, underscoring its importance in both compositional profiling and industrial material characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Fe2O3 is an iron oxide compound whose concentration is quantified using the described titration method.&lt;SEP&gt;Fe2O3 is a chemical compound whose mass fraction is calculated using the provided titration formula.&lt;SEP&gt;An impurity compound present in the phosphogypsum at 0.13 wt %.&lt;SEP&gt;Fe2O3 is a chemical compound added to the system, affecting melting points and eutectic behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Fe2O3 is an additive used in gypsum decomposition and its transformation is monitored.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MgO">
  <data key="d0">MgO</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnesium oxide (MgO) is a chemical compound that occurs as a constituent in cement clinker, granulated slag, and phosphogypsum, where it is frequently measured as a trace component. Analytical data tracks its concentration across various samples, reporting values in both weight percent and parts per million (ppm), with a documented average concentration of 834.86 ppm. These measurements are compiled in concentration and data tables that provide numerical ranges, and the specific concentration values are derived using a defined calculation formula.

During laboratory analysis, MgO samples undergo calcination at 950 °C ± 25 °C to prepare them for accurate measurement. Beyond its presence in industrial materials, MgO serves a functional role as an alkaline activator in binder mixtures utilized for phosphogypsum remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;MgO is an analytically pure compound added to phosphogypsum to satisfy empirical parameters for slag wool production.&lt;SEP&gt;MgO is a chemical compound present in the slag system, contributing to quaternary acidity and phase formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
