<node id="SO3">
  <data key="d0">SO3</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">SO3, chemically known as sulfur trioxide, is a significant chemical compound that is measured in both cement clinker and phosphogypsum (PG). It is frequently noted as a potential constituent in phosphogypsum samples, with compositional analyses consistently identifying it as a major component. Data tables routinely list SO3 alongside associated numerical measurements, and it has been specifically recorded as a chemical component present in phosphogypsum at a concentration of 38.74 wt %.

Beyond its compositional prevalence, SO3 plays a critical functional role in cementitious systems. When combined with calcium oxide (CaO), it significantly affects the mechanical characteristics of phosphogypsum slag cement. Furthermore, SO3 is generated as a chemical byproduct during the thermal decomposition of phosphogypsum, where it is subsequently utilized in the industrial production of sulfuric acid. Collectively, these attributes establish SO3 as a key chemical component that is routinely quantified and utilized across cement and phosphogypsum processing contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
