<node id="Fluorides">
  <data key="d0">Fluorides</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluorides are a class of chemical compounds, predominantly sodium- and calcium-based, that function as significant impurities and chemical residues within phosphogypsum, a byproduct generated during the wet-process phosphate rock industry. Common species include CaF, Na2SiF6, Na3AlF6, and NaF. Their concentrations are intrinsically tied to the source rock and governed by anion substitution mechanisms, frequently occurring alongside phosphates, acid residues, and heavy metals. In certain contexts, fluorides exist as dispersed soluble rare earth element salts, although their dissolution can be hindered by gypsum coatings. Classified as primary potentially toxic elements, these chemical impurities pose substantial ecological pollution risks and public health hazards. Due to their high solubility, they readily migrate into surrounding soils and groundwater aquifers, creating a persistent risk of secondary release during groundwater leaching. Consequently, their sorption behavior and mineral stability in leachate-affected soils are actively examined, and they are strictly monitored as air and liquid emissions during the brick firing and soil application of phosphogypsum.

To mitigate these environmental and health risks, fluorides are systematically targeted for removal during phosphogypsum purification. They can be effectively immobilized at rates exceeding 99% through treatment with calcium carbonate. Beyond environmental protection, precise control and removal of fluorides are critical for preserving the engineering viability of phosphogypsum when repurposed as construction backfill. Elevated fluoride concentrations undermine material performance by forming inactive protective coats on cement particle surfaces, which extends setting times, degrades pore structure formation, and inhibits hydration product precipitation within cemented paste backfill matrices. This directly correlates with marked declines in material workability, mechanical performance, and overall structural strength. Therefore, managing fluoride content is essential not only for preventing ecological contamination but also for ensuring the functional reliability of phosphogypsum-based construction applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical parameter measured in phosphogypsum samples for leaching toxicity analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorides are impurities exposed when leaching with sodium carbonate and sodium bicarbonate, but absent in raw and acid-treated samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineral classes highlighted by some authors as potential main rare earth element-bearing minerals in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorides are chemical compounds that thorium can form insoluble complexes with, limiting its mobility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
