<node id="Table 2">
  <data key="d0">Table 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2 is not a single, unified dataset but rather a generic reference label used across independent scientific studies in chemistry, materials science, agriculture, and environmental engineering. Its specific content is strictly dictated by the experimental design, research focus, and admixture selection of each individual study, primarily centering on the characterization, utilization, and analysis of phosphogypsum and its derivatives. In chemical and mineralogical analyses, it documents the weight percentages of major species and impurities in raw phosphogypsum, alongside detailed chemical composition data for typical global samples such as DA, HDS, PG1, and PG2. It frequently presents trace elements, heavy metals, and rare earth elements, utilizing techniques such as X-ray fluorescence, inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry, and inductively coupled plasma optical emission spectrometry. The table classifies impurities by type, chemical form, and solubility, provides fractionation data, and compiles experimental solubility measurements. Radiological assessments employ gamma spectrometry to evaluate natural radionuclide activity concentrations, Lead-210 levels, activity ratios, and removal efficiency percentages before and after treatment.

The table also presents geotechnical properties and measurements of raw studied materials, including their mineralogical composition. Specifically, it summarizes leaching data and toxicity results for phosphogypsum samples sourced from enterprises in Hubei, Yunnan, and Guizhou provinces in China. In materials science and synthesis research, Table 2 serves as a comprehensive data presentation document for synthesized powders and composite formulations. It outlines quantitative phase compositions for bone cement, summarizes brick properties with Life Cycle Inventory data, and records cost and weight analyses comparing phosphogypsum-derived materials to commercial reinforced concrete. For hydroxyapatite variants, it details microstructural properties analyzed via X-ray diffraction models, lists FTIR adsorption bands for samples synthesized with different surfactants, and tabulates optical band gap energies. It records calculated crystal sizes, crystallite dimensions, stress values, estimated carbonate percentages, Ca/P ratios, lattice parameters, d-spacing, and crystallinity degrees. Particle sizes are documented for hydroxyapatite synthesized at 150, 165, and 180 °C, alongside synthesis parameters like duration and pressure. Thermal analysis applications record maximal dehydration rates, corresponding temperatures, and times across varying heating rates.

In agricultural and environmental engineering contexts, the table documents phosphogypsum applications as a biofertilizer, noting positive impacts on ryegrass and pakchoi growth and yield. It supports fuel quality assessments by reporting biodiesel parameters such as density, viscosity, and flash point, and compares hydroxyapatite-produced biodiesel against established standards. Environmental modeling iterations provide Langmuir and Freundlich isotherm constants to describe ion adsorption kinetics on biochar and hydroxyapatite-biochar substrates. Finally, thermodynamic studies list standard enthalpies of formation for reactants and products at 298.15 °C. Collectively, these diverse instances confirm that Table 2 functions as a recurring placeholder for distinct analytical results across multiple disciplines, with its exact contents strictly dictated by the specific experimental design, admixture selection, and research focus of each individual study.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 is a structured data table presenting the elemental composition of hydroxyapatite in weight and atomic percentages.&lt;SEP&gt;A data table presenting the average chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples in weight percent.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 presents calculated data on Phosphogypsum Ingredients compositions and varying Mk systems based on alumina and magnesium oxide dosages.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 is a reference document containing sample composition data, specifically for PGI-1.4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-00