<node id="Orthophosphate">
  <data key="d0">Orthophosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Orthophosphate is another name for the phosphate ions produced in the reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Orthophosphate is another name for the phosphate ion produced during polyphosphate hydrolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Orthophosphate is a chemical compound whose fate in phosphogypsum leachate was predicted using GEOCHEM.&lt;SEP&gt;Orthophosphate is a component of process water and leachate that can be removed by geological materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound whose removal is influenced by iron(III) hydroxide and calcium phosphate complexes.&lt;SEP&gt;Orthophosphate is a commonly used phosphorus source for hydroxyapatite synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-001</data>
