</node>
<node id="Portland Slag Cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland Slag Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Portland Slag Cement is a cementitious binder and construction material primarily produced through the intergrinding of granulated slag, cement clinker, and gypsum. As a fundamental building material, its baseline composition and manufacturing process establish its core structural and binding capabilities.

The physical, engineering, and overall performance characteristics of Portland Slag Cement are notably influenced by the incorporation of phosphogypsum, which can be processed and added in various forms. When purified phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material during manufacture, the resulting cement successfully complies with standard requirements for critical metrics such as autoclave expansion and heat of hydration. Additionally, the addition of phosphogypsum samples or thermally treated phosphogypsum has been documented to modify and influence the material's physical and engineering properties. These findings highlight phosphogypsum's versatility as an additive that can be integrated into Portland Slag Cement production while maintaining adherence to established performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binding material whose properties are influenced by thermally treated phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binding material used in the development of a new CCM formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binder material used in cementitious composites alongside phosphogypsum and fly ash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791718726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Citric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Citric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqueous citric acid is a solution used to measure solubility and purify phosphogypsum by reacting with impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous Citric Acid is a chemical solution used to treat phosphogypsum for purification by removing impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous citric acid is the specific form of citric acid used to treat phosphogypsum samples, with optimal concentrations varying by sample type.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004</data>
