<node id="M. Singh">
  <data key="d0">M. Singh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">M. Singh is a researcher and author whose work primarily focuses on the utilization, purification, and processing of phosphogypsum for construction and building materials. Throughout their career, Singh has investigated various methods for treating waste phosphogypsum, developing improved processes for its beneficiation and purification to make it suitable for industrial applications. A significant portion of their research is dedicated to transforming this industrial byproduct into valuable resources for cement and plaster manufacture.

Singh has authored and co-authored numerous studies exploring the development of phosphogypsum-based composite binders and the treatment of waste phosphogypsum for use in cement production. Their specific investigations include the creation of anhydrite plaster derived from waste phosphogypsum, as well as comprehensive analyses on the durability of phosphogypsum-lime-fly ash binders. Additionally, Singh published foundational research in 1988 detailing the utilization of phosphogypsum for building materials, establishing early groundwork in this niche.

The scholarly output of M. Singh extends to prominent academic venues, including publications in the journal Cement and Concrete Research. Collectively, their body of work demonstrates a sustained commitment to advancing sustainable construction practices by repurposing phosphogypsum waste into high-performance cementitious and plaster materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007</data>
