<node id="Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d0">Compressive Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Compressive strength is a fundamental mechanical and physical property that quantifies a material's maximum load-bearing capacity under compression, typically measured in megapascals (MPa). It is routinely evaluated using a universal testing machine on cylindrical samples and exhibits a linear relationship with material density. As a critical performance metric, it serves as a vital indicator of structural integrity across diverse engineering, construction, and biomedical applications, heavily influenced by material formulation, processing methods, environmental conditioning, and curing duration.

In standard cement, plaster, and cementitious applications, compressive strength is routinely assessed at specific intervals, such as 1, 3, 7, and 28 days, to evaluate the performance of cured specimens. The property is highly sensitive to curing age, testing methods, and additive dosages. For instance, in composite bone cement, strength increases with longer incubation times but decreases as sodium chloride concentrations rise. In phosphogypsum cementitious materials (PGCM), compressive strength varies significantly with curing conditions and is notably improved by the incorporation of quicklime, cement, and silica fume admixtures.

Within construction materials like concrete, mortar, bricks, and cemented paste backfill, compressive strength is frequently optimized through strategic material substitution and processing. The incorporation of phosphogypsum and related binders demonstrates a non-linear relationship with strength: in concrete and mortar, it typically peaks at replacement levels between 10% and 12% before declining, while Plaster of Paris integration peaks at 7.5%. For bricks, the property is directly influenced by press-forming pressure and phosphogypsum content. Although unpurified phosphogypsum generally reduces strength compared to natural gypsum, techniques such as ball-milling, optimal thermal pretreatment, and purification can reverse this trend and enhance performance. Ultimately, the development of dense network structures and specific mineral contents further supports strength enhancement, underscoring the importance of precise mix designs and processing in gypsum-based mortars, composites, and broader engineering applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property measured to evaluate the effectiveness of gypsum additions in adobe samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property measured on cubic adobe samples at 28 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a key mechanical property measured to evaluate the structural integrity of stabilized adobe samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property measuring the maximum load an adobe sample can bear before failure, which increases with stabilizer addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property of phosphogypsum filler that increases after citric acid treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Setting Time">
  <data key="d0">Setting Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting Time is a fundamental physical property and measured parameter that quantifies the duration required for various cementitious and plaster materials to harden. It is typically recorded across two distinct phases: the initial and final hardening stages. As a critical characteristic, it directly influences the handling properties of the material and is optimized differently depending on the intended application, such as dental versus orthopedic uses. The property is evaluated across several material types, including general cement, cement paste, cement mortar, gypsum plaster, and composite bone cement.

The setting time exhibits distinct sensitivities to specific chemical additives and base material compositions. In general cement, cement paste, and cement mortar, the presence of phosphogypsum and soluble phosphorus considerably prolongs the setting time, a phenomenon often attributed to the formation of protective coatings on the material particles. This prolongation typically extends proportionally with increasing phosphogypsum content, making it a critical parameter when phosphogypsum is utilized as a cement substitute. Soluble phosphate and other contaminants within phosphogypsum similarly exert a retarding effect. Conversely, the introduction of soluble fluorine shortens the setting time. In the specific context of bone cement and composite bone cement, the setting time decreases as the concentration of sodium chloride increases. Additionally, when gypsum plaster is manufactured from purified phosphogypsum, its setting time increases. These variations highlight how chemical additives and base material purity directly modulate the hardening duration, necessitating precise control to meet specific clinical or industrial handling requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Setting time is a metric measuring the duration required for gypsum-based materials to harden, categorized into initial and final phases.&lt;SEP&gt;A duration measured in minutes, segmented into initial and final phases for gypsum analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Setting time is a cement property severely retarded by the presence of phosphorus and fluorine impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792096029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Normal Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal Consistency is a physical property of gypsum plaster that decreases when produced from purified phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007</data>
