<node id="Alkalis">
  <data key="d0">Alkalis</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkalis are impurities in phosphogypsum that are targeted for reduction to make the material suitable for cement and plaster manufacture.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkalis are impurities present in phosphogypsum that are removed during the purification process.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkalis, represented as Na2O + K2O, are residual impurities in phosphogypsum that are reduced through citric acid treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkalis are impurities in phosphogypsum that are removed during fluidized calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkalis are contaminants in phosphogypsum that require limitation for safe application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
