<node id="India">
  <data key="d0">India</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">India is a country that plays a substantial role in the research, production, and application of phosphogypsum. The nation is home to the Central Building Research Institute, which operates under Indian Standards and has conducted extensive analysis and tabulation of phosphogypsum's chemical compositions. India contributes significantly to scientific production in this field and accounts for 6.35% of the global distribution of phosphogypsum production or reserves. Significant amounts of phosphogypsum are produced domestically, supporting both academic and industrial advancements.

In terms of practical application and manufacturing, India commercially utilizes the Merseburg ammonocarbonation process and employs phosphogypsum for the reclamation of sodic soils. The country also manufactures various construction products, including gypsum board, blocks, bricks, and cement, by incorporating phosphogypsum into their production lines. Data visualizations further highlight India's prominence in this domain, with the country listed on the vertical axis of relevant charts where the longest bar indicates a weight percentage of approximately 47%.&lt;SEP&gt;India utilizes a majority of PG for cement production and minor amounts for agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;India uses phosphogypsum for producing cement, bricks, and fertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a geographic location referenced in the data table regarding material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a geographic region featured in a study by Pratap et al. (2023).&lt;SEP&gt;India is a country where Pratap et al. conducted a 2023 study on chemical components.&lt;SEP&gt;India is a geographic origin for phosphogypsum samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791714757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Citric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Citric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Citric Acid is a water-soluble, weak organic acid naturally produced by microorganisms, widely utilized across industrial, environmental, and materials science applications. In phosphogypsum processing, it serves as a highly effective aqueous leaching and treatment reagent, typically applied via soaking at concentrations between 2.0% and 5.0%, with optimal levels identified at 3.0% for HDS samples and 4.0% for DA samples. Chemically, it reacts with soluble fluorine, phosphorus, and phosphate impurities, converting them into water-soluble compounds that are easily washed away, while also lowering the pH during bioleaching processes. It is recognized as the most effective, cost-efficient, and environmentally friendly agent for reducing hazardous constituents in phosphogypsum, specifically decreasing radionuclide levels by approximately 22% to about 0.34 wt%, which represents the lowest radionuclide content among tested methods. Additionally, it transforms calcium sulfate into gypsum and functions as a selective leaching agent for recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum and coal fly ash, although sulfuric acid is occasionally noted to provide superior leaching efficiency for this specific purpose. Citric Acid also serves as a reference solution in solubility charts to evaluate calcium phosphate dissolution behavior.

Beyond waste remediation, Citric Acid plays a critical role in materials science and biomineralization as a surfactant and morphological control agent. Under hydrothermal conditions, it suppresses the nucleation and growth of hydroxyapatite, effectively reduces particle size, and directs crystal formation into specific structures, notably yielding rod-like hydroxyapatite morphologies. It similarly alters the crystalline phase shape of gypsum and facilitates the breakdown of Plaster of Paris into flakes. In construction and environmental management, it is employed as a pretreatment agent to enhance the performance of phosphogypsum-based cemented paste backfill and to control fluoride pollution within the mixture. Despite its significant improvements in impurity removal and process efficiency, the application of Citric Acid is noted to substantially increase overall operational costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
