<node id="Dicalcium Phosphate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Dicalcium Phosphate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Dicalcium phosphate dihydrate is a calcium phosphate compound that shows intermediate solubility in citric acid solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The full chemical name for the crystalline phase known as brushite, identified in the cement composition.&lt;SEP&gt;A mineral reference pattern also known as Brushite, represented by black vertical tick marks.&lt;SEP&gt;A calcium phosphate salt that reacts in chemical equations to form hydroxyapatite and is commonly found in fertilizers.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium Phosphate Dihydrate is a precursor phase involved in the recrystallization process leading to hydroxyapatite formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791857470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
