<node id="Compressive strength">
  <data key="d0">Compressive strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Compressive strength is a physical property tested for in the produced cements.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a mechanical property of cement that is reduced when phosphogypsum is used.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property of bioactive carbonate apatite cement that was enhanced via incorporation of silica calcium phosphate composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressive strength is a measured property used to evaluate and compare the performance of different concrete variants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
