<node id="Table 6">
  <data key="d0">Table 6</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 6 refers to multiple distinct data presentations across various scientific studies, each serving a specific research context. In materials science and construction research, one iteration of Table 6 details the physical properties of gypsum plaster, specifically reporting setting time, bulk density, and compressive strength. Another study utilizes Table 6 to document the conversion of phosphogypsum into valuable compounds under diverse experimental conditions, alongside presenting calculated radium equivalent activity and total absorbed dose rate values for phosphogypsum waste samples.

In environmental and public health research, a separate Table 6 functions as a reference document outlining drinking water guidelines for Radium-226. Concurrently, another instance of Table 6 provides a comparative analysis of water quality parameters, focusing specifically on pH ranges between the regions of Gabes and Djerba.

In chemical engineering and materials formulation contexts, Table 6 serves as a reference for specific formulations and component ratios. One version lists detailed conversion yields and process metrics for fluoride medium transformations. Another iteration specifies a recommended percentage-based formulation for CPGFM, explicitly detailing the proportional composition of phosphor slag, phosphogypsum, an activator, a water reducer, and the overall concentration. Collectively, these distinct references demonstrate how the label Table 6 is utilized across different publications to organize specialized experimental data, environmental assessments, and material formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 6 catalogs the physical characteristics and industrial applications of various downstream products derived from phosphogypsum calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 6 details the distinct characteristics and purposes of different gypsum forms based on their crystal morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 6 compares crystallite sizes in various natural apatites like bones and teeth.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 6 presents the ranking of the four PG waste management methods based on total scores from three perspectives.&lt;SEP&gt;A table detailing predictable consolidation settlements calculated for embankment height fractions under operating loads.&lt;SEP&gt;A data table predicting the settlement in centimeters of a phosphogypsum embankment at various heights.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
