<node id="Dihydrate Process">
  <data key="d0">Dihydrate Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dihydrate Process is a specific pathway and the most widely adopted variant of the wet phosphoric acid production method. It serves as the most common industrial technique for manufacturing phosphoric acid from apatite ore. Its widespread implementation is primarily attributed to its mature technology and consistently stable operation.

A defining characteristic of the Dihydrate Process is its generation of phosphogypsum as a primary byproduct. This material is dominated by calcium sulfate dihydrate and typically forms filter cakes that contain notable impurities. Furthermore, the process directly influences the adjustment and crystal shapes of the resulting phosphogypsum, making it a critical factor in the overall production and handling of the byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemihydrate Process">
  <data key="d0">Hemihydrate Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The hemihydrate process is a two-step method for manufacturing phosphoric acid that produces phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process is a widely used industrial method that produces purer phosphoric acid with higher P2O5 concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hemihydrate Process is a production method that yields phosphogypsum with relatively high impurities and lacks uranium extraction capability.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process is a wet phosphoric acid method that yields higher uranium content (5-100 μg/g) due to its crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A source reduction technology developed for newly generated phosphogypsum to improve recycling rates and quality.&lt;SEP&gt;A manufacturing process for phosphoric acid that influences the adjustment and crystal shapes of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammonium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Ammonium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonium Hydroxide (NH4OH) is a basic aqueous solution and alkaline hydroxide reagent widely utilized across industrial and chemical processing applications. Characterized by a standard enthalpy of formation of -361.2 kJ/mol, it functions primarily as a reactant and pH modifier introduced into reactors or conversion vessels. Its alkaline nature allows it to effectively shift precursor mixtures into basic conditions, with specific pH targets tailored to the process requirements, including maintaining levels above 9, achieving a pH of 10 when paired with ammonium chloride, or adjusting to pH 11.

A major application of Ammonium Hydroxide lies in phosphogypsum conversion experiments and processing. In these procedures, it serves as a critical reactant that adjusts the reaction environment and subsequently reacts with sulfuric acid to facilitate the production of ammonium sulfate. The compound is also integral to various synthesis methodologies, where it is employed to control reaction conditions during hydrothermal synthesis, precipitation, and microwave synthesis procedures.

Beyond chemical synthesis, Ammonium Hydroxide plays a vital role in environmental remediation and materials engineering. It is extensively used to treat phosphogypsum waste and phosphogypsum-based cemented paste backfill. In these remediation and material preparation processes, it is frequently combined with citric acid to effectively lower phosphate and fluoride concentrations. Furthermore, when applied to cemented paste backfill, it mitigates set retardation, thereby improving the material's curing properties. Through these diverse functions, Ammonium Hydroxide operates as a versatile agent for precise pH control, chemical waste remediation, and reaction facilitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
