<node id="Lead-210">
  <data key="d0">Lead-210</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead-210 is a radioactive isotope and a downstream daughter nuclide within the Uranium-238 decay series, specifically originating as a decay product of radon-222. Primarily derived from phosphate rocks, it is a significant radionuclide component of phosphogypsum (PG) waste, where it frequently coprecipitates with calcium sulfate (accounting for approximately 80–90% of its presence) and likely incorporates into the material's crystal lattice. Chemically, Lead-210 can exist in both +2 and +4 oxidation states and undergoes radioactive decay to form Polonium-210. It possesses a characteristic energy level of 46.5 keV, which corresponds to the highest minimum detectable activity observed in measurement datasets. Within phosphogypsum, Lead-210 exhibits enhanced activity concentrations compared to the natural radioactive equilibrium of the original phosphate rocks, with a measured concentration of 418 ± 11.7 Bq/kg. Its distribution shows moderate fluctuations across different PG fractions, notably higher activity in coarse fractions, and it precipitates with sulfates or carbonates to control environmental solubility.

Environmentally, Lead-210 demonstrates high mobility and behavior closely resembling that of radium. Geographic variations are evident, such as phosphogypsum leachate from Alberta demonstrating significantly higher concentrations than those from Ontario. It is actively monitored across various media, including air samples near phosphogypsum ponds and plants cultivated on reclaimed phosphate mine lands, where it accumulates at significantly elevated levels. Analytically, Lead-210 is routinely measured alongside Uranium-238 and Radium-226 to assess activity levels, activity ratios, and secular equilibrium conditions in undisturbed environments. Its activity concentration is frequently quantified in phosphogypsum samples and utilized in standard reference materials for efficiency determination. Given its radiological significance and environmental transport potential, the isotope is extensively evaluated for dose conversion factors and environmental parameters to support radiological safety protocols.

Due to its presence in phosphogypsum and derived compounds, Lead-210 is targeted for removal during leaching processes to meet safety standards and reduce environmental bioavailability. Remediation strategies, particularly the use of hydroxyapatite nanopowders, have been developed to adsorb and extract the isotope. The removal and stripping efficiencies vary depending on process parameters and sample composition; stripping efficiency increases steadily over time, plateauing at approximately 46%, while extraction efficiency peaks at specific molar ratios (around 65%) and records 88.9% for PG-Se and 84.6% for PG-AT samples. Furthermore, agitation time significantly influences removal outcomes, with efficiency initially peaking at approximately 53.5% at 2 hours before declining to 48.5% at 8 hours. Radiometric measurements are routinely employed to track these stripping percentages and evaluate the overall effectiveness of developed leaching and remediation procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead-210 is a radionuclide in the uranium decay series that contributes significantly to the radioactivity of raw phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001</data>
