<node id="P2O5">
  <data key="d0">P2O5</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorus pentoxide (P2O5) is a chemical compound primarily produced during the combustion of yellow phosphorus and serves as a fundamental metric across the phosphate industry. It is widely utilized to quantify phosphorus content in crude phosphoric acid, particularly from the dihydrate process, as well as in purified gypsum products and phosphate fertilizers. In industrial and scientific contexts, P2O5 is consistently recorded with specific weight percentages and concentration ranges in analytical data tables, compositional analyses, and mineralogical studies. Its concentration is frequently determined through drying and weighing procedures, calculated via specific formulas, and visualized in scientific data representations such as violin plot legends. Additionally, P2O5 functions as a standard reference metric for tracking total phosphate fertilizer production volumes and the production ratio of phosphogypsum waste.

Within phosphogypsum and phosphate rock processing, P2O5 is a key chemical constituent identified in compositional analyses, typically measured at an average mass fraction of approximately 1.31%, which generally exceeds its fluorine concentration. Although classified as a processing impurity requiring mitigation, P2O5 exists in phosphogypsum in multiple forms, including soluble contaminants, lattice-bounded impurities trapped within the gypsum crystal structure, and specific chemical species such as H3PO4 and Ca(H2PO4)2.H2O4. The lattice-bounded form is highly resistant to removal via conventional water-washing techniques. Despite its impurity status, P2O5 retains significant agricultural and industrial utility. Typically comprising less than one percent of phosphogypsum material, its residual presence acts as a direct phosphorus source that enhances soil management and plant nutrition, effectively transforming an industrial byproduct into a valuable agricultural resource when applied as a soil amendment. In high-quality cement applications, P2O5 appears in a syncrystallized form that conditions the material as a setting regulator.&lt;SEP&gt;An impurity compound present in the phosphogypsum at 1.70 wt %.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
