<node id="Sodium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium sulfate (Na2SO4) is a sulfate compound and solid salt that functions as both an intermediate byproduct and a valuable industrial material. It is primarily synthesized from phosphogypsum waste, including deposits sourced from Morocco, or from gypsum, through aqueous conversion, chloride hydrometallurgy, and various chemical transformation processes. The compound is typically generated by reacting the source material with sodium-based reagents such as sodium carbonate (washing soda), sodium hydroxide, or sodium chloride. During these conversion and carbonation reactions, sodium sulfate is frequently co-produced alongside calcium silicate and can be isolated following evaporation or specific washing operations, a step that notably decreases sodium oxide concentration. The recovered compound can also undergo further chemical reactions to form glaserite.

In commercial and experimental applications, sodium sulfate is widely utilized in the detergent and paper manufacturing industries. It has also been evaluated as a chemical additive in leaching processes, where it was introduced alongside sulfuric acid into cycled aqueous solutions to mitigate drops in leaching efficiency. However, experimental trials demonstrated that its addition did not improve the leaching efficiency of rare earth elements. Beyond industrial manufacturing, sodium sulfate is incorporated into simulated body fluid preparations as a solid salt component at a concentration of 0.50 mmol L⁻¹. Despite specific experimental limitations in certain leaching trials, it remains a recognized and recoverable product from phosphogypsum and gypsum treatment, maintaining established utility across multiple sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate is a chemical substance that causes microcrack expansion and reduces hydration products in the filling body.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate is an impurity present in phosphogypsum generated by the kiln process, which can cause alkali flooding.&lt;SEP&gt;A raw material input combined with phosphate ore in the kiln phosphoric acid process.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound produced from phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium sulfate is a compound produced through the transformation of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-016</data>
