<node id="Scanning Electron Microscope">
  <data key="d0">Scanning Electron Microscope</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Scanning Electron Microscope is a sophisticated imaging instrument and microscopy technique designed to capture high-magnification, grayscale micrographs of various materials. It functions as a critical diagnostic and analytical tool for visualizing and examining the microstructural characteristics, particle morphology, and surface features of diverse samples.

In scientific research, the Scanning Electron Microscope is applied across multiple disciplines to analyze specific materials and phenomena. It is utilized to assess the distinct particle morphology and spatial distribution of rare earth elements, as well as to visualize the morphology and surface characteristics of phosphogypsum particles and composites. The instrument effectively captures detailed images of irregular, chunky particles with rough surfaces, observes crust structures in soil research, and analyzes the microstructure of bone cement samples, often operating at specific technical parameters such as a 15 kV accelerating voltage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is an analytical instrument used to examine mineral phases and detect trace elements in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-magnification imaging device used to capture surface topography and particle morphology at the nanoscale.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscope is an imaging instrument used to capture high-magnification grayscale views of granular material structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning electron microscope is an imaging device used to capture micrographs of phosphogypsum at 5,000x magnification.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scanning Electron Microscope is an instrument used to capture a grayscale micrograph of the material's surface morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;The imaging instrument used to capture the grayscale micrograph of the material surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
