<node id="Bastnaesite">
  <data key="d0">Bastnaesite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A mineral source of rare earth elements located in California and China.&lt;SEP&gt;Bastnaesite is a known Rare Earth Element ore used as a benchmark for comparing the potential value of Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Bastnaesite is a mineral source of rare earth elements found at Mountain Pass and Bayan Obo.&lt;SEP&gt;Bastnaesite is a mineral-bearing rock source from which rare-earth elements are bioleached using actinobacteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055</data>
