</node>
<node id="Acid Mine Drainage">
  <data key="d0">Acid Mine Drainage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A source of rare earth elements located in Pennsylvania, USA.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid Mine Drainage is a waste product source of rare earth elements found at Pennsylvania sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid mine drainage is an environmental issue remediated using calcium carbonate derived from phosphogypsum conversion.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid mine drainage is an environmental issue that can be remediated using calcium carbonate from phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid mine drainage is a highly acidic water flow resulting from mining activities, which phosphogypsum is sometimes used to remediate.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid mine drainage is a pollutant that affects water reservoirs, prompting studies on natural attenuation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid Mine Drainage is an environmental phenomenon studied for its potential to yield rare earth elements and yttrium through passive remediation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-020</data>
