<node id="Praseodymium">
  <data key="d0">Praseodymium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Praseodymium is a rare earth metal element that has been extensively analyzed for its concentration, enrichment, and distribution across various environmental and industrial matrices. It is routinely measured in WBS and TWBS samples, as well as in phosphogypsum (PG), where it notably dominates the elemental composition of dried PG. Comprehensive data tables consistently document Praseodymium alongside specific concentration values, revealing that it occurs in significantly higher concentrations in Brazilian phosphogypsum compared to Florida phosphogypsum.

In analytical and recovery contexts, Praseodymium is actively monitored and selectively recovered during chemical leaching processes. It is known to form a complex with EDTA in analyzed samples. Despite its recovery potential, Praseodymium exhibits a relatively lower leaching selectivity of 71.9% when processed with a 1.0 mol/L citric acid solution. These characteristics underscore its distinct geochemical behavior and its importance in elemental analysis and resource recovery studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
