<node id="Reaction Time">
  <data key="d0">Reaction Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reaction Time is a fundamental experimental and process parameter that represents the controlled duration, typically measured in hours or minutes, over which a chemical reaction, leaching process, or hydrothermal synthesis is allowed to proceed. As a critical variable in materials science and chemistry, it is frequently manipulated to correspond with different data series in experimental graphs and is generally understood to drive crystal growth and phase development.

The specific duration assigned to Reaction Time varies significantly depending on the experimental protocol and target material. In leaching processes, it is often set to a fixed 3 hours, while certain chemical reactions require a 60-minute duration to proceed. Conversely, hydrothermal synthesis studies frequently employ a broader range of 12 to 24 hours to facilitate adequate heating and structural formation.

The influence of Reaction Time on material properties is highly context-dependent. It directly affects the crystallization of specific phases, such as NaYF4:Yb3+/Er3+, and is systematically investigated for its impact on crystal size, morphology, and the orientation and intensity of hydroxyapatite crystal planes. While extended reaction durations generally promote crystal growth, experimental results have occasionally shown inconsistent effects, highlighting the need for precise optimization in each specific synthesis pathway.&lt;SEP&gt;Reaction time is a parameter explored during process optimization to affect desulfurization rates and slag phase structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Reaction Time is the duration of the reduction test, optimized at 20 minutes for effectiveness and economy.&lt;SEP&gt;Reaction time measures the duration of the desulfurization process in minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097275</data>
