<node id="Mineral Carbonation">
  <data key="d0">Mineral Carbonation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mineral carbonation is a chemical process designed for the sequestration and fixation of carbon dioxide by combining it with minerals to form stable carbonate compounds. The technique generally involves reacting carbon dioxide with mineral sources in a liquid solution, serving as a targeted method for carbon capture and long-term storage.

In industrial applications, mineral carbonation is specifically utilized to treat phosphogypsum and other gypsum-based solid wastes. The process typically operates under increased carbon dioxide pressure and may incorporate various chemical agents and conditions, including ammonia, calcium hydroxide, and the formation of calcium oxide nanoparticles. It can also encompass the remineralization of brine water. By modifying phosphogypsum waste, mineral carbonation effectively sequesters carbon dioxide while simultaneously converting the material into valuable carbonate and sulfate salts, establishing it as a key application domain for transforming industrial byproducts into useful chemical products.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process used to convert phosphogypsum for carbon dioxide sequestration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792096852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organic Extractants">
  <data key="d0">Organic Extractants</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Organic extractants are chemical agents used to treat phosphogypsum waste and facilitate the extraction of valuable components.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic extractants are chemical compounds applied in the treatment of phosphogypsum waste to facilitate element separation.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic extractants are chemical substances used in the leaching process to extract materials from the phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic extractants are chemical agents used to treat and separate components from phosphogypsum waste.</data>
