</node>
<node id="J. Hazard. Mater.">
  <data key="d0">J. Hazard. Mater.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Journal of Hazardous Materials is a peer-reviewed academic and scientific journal dedicated to publishing research on hazardous materials, environmental hazards, and waste management. It serves as a key resource for studies focused on the treatment, characterization, and safe application of industrial byproducts and waste streams, with a strong emphasis on environmental remediation and pollution control. The journal's editorial scope encompasses a wide range of topics, including the assessment of binders and solid waste, investigations into hazardous substances like fly ash, soil stabilization techniques, and the chemistry and applications of synthetic hydroxyapatite, including zoledronate-functionalized variants and heavy metal adsorption.

A substantial portion of the journal's literature is dedicated to phosphogypsum, documenting its radiological and chemical characterization, ecotoxicity, and various treatment and safe application methods. Notable publications include a 2009 study on phosphogypsum stack radioactive characterization, a 2012 study on its utilization for fluoride removal, research on the effect of phosphorus in phosphogypsum-based cemented backfill, investigations into lanthanide leaching, nanoparticle synthesis, and methods for increasing arsenic sorption on red mud using phosphogypsum. Beyond phosphogypsum, the journal has published multiple studies on sulfurisation gypsum, arsenic leaching dynamics, metal-bearing sludge characterization, and the broader use of industrial byproducts in environmental remediation. Collectively, these publications highlight the journal's commitment to advancing scientific understanding and developing mitigation strategies for hazardous materials and industrial waste.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific journal publishing research on hazardous materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792003010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Miner. Eng.">
  <data key="d0">Miner. Eng.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Miner. Eng. is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research within the field of mineral engineering. It serves as a comprehensive platform for scholarly work covering a diverse range of technical and environmental topics, including rare earth element extraction and concentrate production, sulfuric acid bioproduction, and the management of industrial byproducts. The journal has featured notable publications such as a 2019 study on rare earth concentrate production and a critical review of acid rock drainage prediction methods.

A significant focus of the journal's literature involves the processing and utilization of phosphogypsum. Research published in Miner. Eng. explores methodologies for extracting rare earth concentrates from phosphogypsum, alongside investigations into the stabilization and controlled release of hazardous substances within this material. Additionally, the journal disseminates studies on solid waste binders and the development of dihydrate phosphogypsum aggregate backfill materials, underscoring its role in advancing sustainable waste valorization and engineering solutions in the mineral processing industry.&lt;SEP&gt;A journal featuring research on impurity removal from phosphogypsum during gypsum preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019</data>
