<node id="Total Rare Earth Elements">
  <data key="d0">Total Rare Earth Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total Rare Earth Elements represents the aggregate concentration of all REEs in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Total rare earth elements represent the sum of rare earth element concentrations in the analyzed samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Rare Earth Elements (TREEs) represents the sum of all rare earth elements present in the sample, as defined in the experimental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Rare Earth Elements are chemical elements whose concentration in phosphogypsum decreases alongside radionuclide removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Rare Earth Elements represent the sum of rare earth metals in phosphogypsum, measured at 395 ppm.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Rare Earth Elements (∑REE) represent a group of elements whose combined concentration in phosphogypsum was measured.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792037229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="900 °C">
  <data key="d0">900 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">900 °C is the temperature at which calcium fluoride crystallization typically occurs according to Dash et al.&lt;SEP&gt;A temperature at which F exists as solid-phase CaSiFO and gas-phase HF.&lt;SEP&gt;900 °C is the specific temperature applied during the heat treatment process for hydroxyapatite powders.&lt;SEP&gt;900 °C is a higher calcination temperature that increases crystallinity and triggers partial decomposition into tricalcium phosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;900 °C is a higher calcination temperature that induces spherical morphology and partial decomposition of hydroxyapatite into beta-tricalcium phosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;A calcination temperature applied to PG and PGI-1.4 samples to study decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098909</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="600 °C">
  <data key="d0">600 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">600 °C is the reduced crystallization temperature of calcium fluoride when doped with Ytterbium and Erbium.&lt;SEP&gt;A temperature threshold at which gas phase HF starts to appear.&lt;SEP&gt;A temperature threshold at which gas-phase HF begins to appear.&lt;SEP&gt;600 °C is a specific calcination temperature that results in poorly crystalline hydroxyapatite without extraneous phases.&lt;SEP&gt;600 °C is a specific calcination temperature applied to hydroxyapatite samples, resulting in rod-like morphology and poor crystallinity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002021</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="700 °C">
  <data key="d0">700 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">700 °C is the temperature used in the thermal treatment that explains the crystallization of calcium fluoride in CWBS.&lt;SEP&gt;700 °C is the temperature threshold up to which dehydroxylation of hydroxyapatite occurs, leading to partial conversion into beta-tricalcium phosphate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002021</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
