  <data key="d2">Samarium is a chemical element whose concentration and enrichment were measured in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Samarium is a rare earth element measured in WBS and TWBS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Samarium is a rare earth element selectively recovered from phosphogypsum leachate.&lt;SEP&gt;Samarium is a rare earth element analyzed in Idaho phosphogypsum with a mean concentration of 5.4 mg/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare earth element targeted for extraction with a reported recovery rate of 73.2%.&lt;SEP&gt;Samarium is a rare earth element whose extraction process and complex formation were previously studied by Hoogerstraete and Binnemans.&lt;SEP&gt;Samarium is a rare earth element found in phosphogypsum phases at concentrations between 100 and</data>
