<node id="X-Ray Diffraction">
  <data key="d0">X-Ray Diffraction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-Ray Diffraction is a comprehensive analytical, characterization, and crystallographic technique primarily utilized to determine and characterize the crystalline structures, internal atomic arrangements, phase compositions, and crystal indexing of diverse materials. By measuring how X-rays interact with matter, the method generates diffraction patterns that are typically visualized as stacked line graphs plotting crystalline phase intensities across diffraction angles. This fundamental framework enables precise qualitative and quantitative assessments of material purity, composition, and crystallinity across multiple scientific disciplines. The technique serves as a critical tool for mapping crystal structures in both synthesized materials and naturally occurring substances, extensively applied to identify phase compositions, detect impurities within mixed powders, and evaluate structural integrity and phase purity.

Specific applications of X-Ray Diffraction span a wide range of materials science and chemical analysis. It is employed to characterize crystalline phases in ceramic bodies, analyze composite bone cement, biochar, sylvite, and dolomite, and effectively distinguish between various mineral phases to provide detailed insights into the physical architecture of solids. The method is also frequently used to study structural transformations, such as those observed in phosphogypsum before and after treatment, and in amorphous calcium phosphate. Furthermore, X-Ray Diffraction is instrumental in confirming the crystalline phase purity of hydroxyapatite, collecting diffraction patterns of nano-hydroxyapatite powders for crystallite size calculation and distribution analysis, and correlating with infrared data to comprehensively analyze hydroxyapatite composition. Through these diverse applications, X-Ray Diffraction remains a fundamental framework for advancing materials characterization and crystallographic research.&lt;SEP&gt;A characterization technique used to identify the main mineral composition of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
