<node id="Crystalline Structure">
  <data key="d0">Crystalline Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystalline structure refers to the ordered atomic arrangement of materials analyzed via XRD patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline structure describes the consistent atomic arrangement of the material across different samples and treatment times.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystalline Structure refers to the hexagonal arrangement and P63/m space group identified in hydroxyapatite and natural bone samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005</data>
