<node id="Diffraction Angle">
  <data key="d0">Diffraction Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffraction Angle serves as the fundamental horizontal axis variable in X-ray Diffraction (XRD) pattern analysis, representing the specific angle in degrees at which X-ray scattering and diffraction occur. It functions as the primary scale for plotting and interpreting XRD graphs, charts, and patterns.

While the unit of measurement is consistently degrees, the operational range varies depending on the specific experimental setup or dataset. Typical ranges span from 10 to 80 degrees, with some specific charts utilizing narrower intervals such as 15 to 80 degrees or 20 to 55 degrees. Beyond its role as a graphical axis, the Diffraction Angle is a critical geometric parameter utilized in trigonometric calculations. It directly facilitates the quantitative relationship between diffraction peak broadening and material strain, making it essential for structural and mechanical analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement metric in degrees representing the X-axis scale for the XRD pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffraction angle is a metric measured in degrees representing the angle on the horizontal axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relative Intensity">
  <data key="d0">Relative Intensity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Relative intensity represents the Y-axis measurement indicating the strength of diffraction peaks.&lt;SEP&gt;Relative Intensity ($I/I_0$) is a quantitative metric recorded in the X-ray diffraction table to compare peak strengths.</data>
