  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IR">
  <data key="d0">IR</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">IR is the abbreviation for Infrared Spectroscopy, the analytical method used for bond characterization of PG waste.&lt;SEP&gt;IR is an immersion resistance index that highlights water sensitivity criteria for capping layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A load-bearing capacity metric that undergoes significant improvement with lime addition in P2 Mix.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact Ratio, a measure of material resilience recorded in Table 10.&lt;SEP&gt;IR is an analytical method used to verify that all hydroxyapatite samples retain the apatite structure before and after heat treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002021</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CaSO4">
  <data key="d0">CaSO4</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CaSO4, the chemical formula for calcium sulfate, is a compound with distinct roles in both waste composition and advanced chemical processing. It serves as the primary phase in phosphogypsum (PG) waste, where it constitutes the characteristic gypsum matrix. The compound can be generated through the oxidation of calcium sulfide (CaS) and is also produced as a complex salt during ion exchange reactions.

In industrial and energy applications, CaSO4 functions as an oxygen carrier in chemical looping gasification (CLG) and combustion systems. Within these processes, it actively reacts with gasification products and undergoes subsequent reduction steps. From a computational and physical standpoint, CaSO4 forms the granular structure of the oxygen carrier and is assigned a defined surface energy in kinetic models to accurately simulate its reaction dynamics. Collectively, these properties highlight its versatility across environmental waste management and high-temperature chemical conversion technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;CaSO4 (calcium sulfate) is a precipitate formed during sulfate removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical formula for anhydrous calcium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791543688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alpha-particle Spectrometry">
  <data key="d0">Alpha-particle Spectrometry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alpha-particle spectrometry is the analytical technique used to measure the activity concentrations of uranium isotopes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790995813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radioactive Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Radioactive Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Radioactive equilibrium is a fundamental state within naturally occurring uranium and thorium decay chains, characterized by a balanced ratio between parent and daughter isotopes, most notably between Uranium-238 and Radium-226 or their respective decay products. This isotopic balance serves as a critical reference framework for analyzing uranium series isotopes and functions as a valuable scientific tool for studying radionuclide fractionation. In undisturbed natural environments, this equilibrium remains stable, allowing for predictable radiometric behavior across the decay series.

However, the state is frequently disrupted during the chemical processing of phosphate-related materials, including phosphorite ore and the industrial phosphoric acid production process. These operations physically and chemically alter the natural distribution of radionuclides, causing significant fractionation that must be carefully monitored. Consequently, processed materials such as phosphogypsum and phosphate rock samples must be allowed to re-establish this balanced isotopic state before accurate gamma spectrometry measurements can be reliably conducted. Understanding and restoring radioactive equilibrium is therefore essential for both the precise radiometric analysis of uranium series isotopes and the accurate assessment of radionuclide distribution in chemically modified phosphate materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791915733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disequilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Disequilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disequilibrium refers to the unbalanced ratio between U-238 and its decay daughters in phosphogypsum waste samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Disequilibrium refers to the existing imbalance between main radioactive contaminants in phosphogypsum and their decay progenies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002</data>
