<node id="International Atomic Energy Agency">
  <data key="d0">International Atomic Energy Agency</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Organization that provided reference materials with known activity concentrations for detector efficiency calibration.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency is an organization based in Vienna, Austria, that published reports on intercomparison runs for radionuclide measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency is an international government agency investigated for its relevance to phosphogypsum research.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency conducted studies on radiation exposure levels from phosphogypsum in construction.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency is the international organization that supplies reference materials for radiometric calibration.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency is an organization that conducted intercomparison runs to measure radionuclides in environmental samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency published safety reports on radiation protection and management of NORM residues in the phosphate industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-014</data>
