<node id="Construction">
  <data key="d0">Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Construction is the dominant and primary sector for the comprehensive utilization of phosphogypsum, accounting for approximately 64% of all its applications. This industrial field encompasses a wide range of activities, most notably the production of building materials, road construction, and cement manufacturing. Due to its significance, Construction represents a major application category that has attracted substantial academic and industrial attention, with nearly 980 dedicated publications exploring its potential and implementation.

Within this sector, there is a high demand for specific chemical derivatives of phosphogypsum, particularly calcium carbonate obtained through phosphogypsum mineralization processes. Additionally, the field frequently employs calcium hydroxide as a foundational base material in various construction applications. However, the integration of phosphogypsum into construction projects necessitates careful regulatory oversight, as its use requires a thorough radiological safety assessment to ensure environmental and public health compliance. Overall, Construction remains a critical domain for the sustainable and comprehensive valorization of phosphogypsum waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002</data>
