<node id="Brazil">
  <data key="d0">Brazil</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Brazil is a South American country that serves as a major global hub for the production, research, and utilization of phosphogypsum and related phosphate materials. As a prominent geographic origin for phosphogypsum, particularly igneous varieties characterized by lower concentrations of iron, titanium, and phosphorus alongside elevated magnesium and silicon, Brazil generates approximately 5.4 million tons of the material annually, accounting for roughly 10.62 percent of global production and reserves. The phosphogypsum produced in Brazil typically exhibits a smaller particle size compared to that of China. The country actively utilizes a significant proportion of its phosphogypsum output for agricultural applications and building materials, including its application as a setting retarder in Portland cement hydration studies.

Extensive scientific investigations have been conducted across Brazil to evaluate the geochemical, radiochemical, and environmental profiles of phosphogypsum and phosphate-derived substances. Researchers have systematically analyzed the chemical composition, impurities, and radionuclide activity concentrations of phosphogypsum samples sourced from locations such as Imbituba. Notable studies, including those by Costa et al. in 2021 and Saueia et al. in 2013, have specifically examined the chemical components and natural radioactivity within Brazilian phosphogypsum and phosphate rock. These efforts, frequently referenced in material property data tables, have thoroughly mapped the distribution of associated radionuclides throughout the material lifecycle. Consequently, Brazil stands as a critical region for understanding the environmental and chemical availability of phosphogypsum and phosphate fertilizers, establishing the nation as a focal point for ongoing geochemical and radiological research in this industrial sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is a country where phosphogypsum exhibits significantly lower radioactivity levels that meet national standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Brazil is a country with significantly lower phosphogypsum radioactivity that meets national standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A country where phosphogypsum from Imbituba was studied for radioactive content.&lt;SEP&gt;A country cited in literature where phosphogypsum samples containing calcium sulphate hemihydrate are documented.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003</data>
