  <data key="d2">Rn-220 is comparable to Rn-222 as a short-lived radon gas.&lt;SEP&gt;A radon gas that may diffuse out of phosphate rock, reducing the activity of subsequent radionuclides in the decay series.&lt;SEP&gt;Radon-222 is a radioactive noble gas produced by the alpha decay of Ra-226, known for its high mobility and environmental significance.&lt;SEP&gt;A radon isotope that escapes from solid phases and decays from Ra-226, with a 3.82-day half-life.&lt;SEP&gt;Rn-222 is the specific radioactive isotope of radon gas that is the primary focus of exposure studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Rn-222 is a gaseous radionuclide produced by the alpha-decay of Ra-226, contributing to atmospheric contamination.</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791428172</data>
