  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Silicate is a chemical compound synthesized from the transformation of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound synthesized from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium silicate is a compound produced through the transformation of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A compound formed as part of eutectic mixtures that encapsulate materials and hinder the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium silicate is the final reduction product formed through the decomposition of calcium sulfate and reaction with silica.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium silicate is a compound formed from silicon dioxide and calcium oxide that encapsulates calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical compound formed as a product when iron(II) oxide reacts with silicon dioxide and calcium sulfide.</data>
