<node id="Ordinary Portland Cement">
  <data key="d0">Ordinary Portland Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ordinary Portland Cement is a conventional and standard cementitious binder material primarily manufactured from limestone and clay. Due to its extensive global application, the large-scale demand and industrial production of Ordinary Portland Cement generate substantial greenhouse gas emissions and significant carbon footprints. Consequently, it is frequently established as a baseline for evaluating and comparing alternative, more sustainable binder technologies.

In construction materials research and engineering applications, Ordinary Portland Cement serves as the primary cementitious constituent in CPB mixtures. The precise proportion of Ordinary Portland Cement within these formulations directly dictates their mechanical performance, enabling practitioners to effectively balance structural safety with sustainability objectives. Additionally, Ordinary Portland Cement is commonly integrated with industrial by-products such as phosphogypsum and blast furnace slag. It is routinely blended with these materials in research settings, actively employed in phosphogypsum remediation processes, and can even be produced directly by utilizing raw phosphogypsum as a manufacturing additive.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland cement serves as the primary binding agent in the composite mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard cement used as a baseline for comparison, against which the modified material shows advantages in fast setting and high early strength.&lt;SEP&gt;A cementitious material added to leachates to rapidly reduce phosphorus concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland cement is partially or fully replaced by ground granulated blast furnace slag to control pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction material in which modified phosphogypsum is applied.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
