<node id="Workability">
  <data key="d0">Workability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A property of construction materials that decreases with phosphogypsum incorporation, leading to deformation risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A practical utility parameter of CPB mixtures influenced by particle interactions and mix proportions.&lt;SEP&gt;Workability is a fundamental characteristic of concrete specimens that is analyzed in studies utilizing phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Workability is a concrete mixture property that generally decreases with increasing Plaster Of Paris content due to higher specific surface area.&lt;SEP&gt;Workability refers to the ease of mixing and placing concrete, which generally decreases with higher PG concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021</data>
