<node id="Ground Granulated Blast Furnace Slag">
  <data key="d0">Ground Granulated Blast Furnace Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground Granulated Blast Furnace Slag is an industrial byproduct derived from processed blast furnace slag, functioning as a versatile supplementary and composite material in construction and environmental applications. Primarily utilized as a partial substitute for ordinary Portland cement, it enhances cement properties, forms effective binders, and improves the overall strength and durability of mortar. Its role is highly adaptable, allowing it to partially replace cement in standard mixes or serve as a key component in cement-free systems.

In environmental remediation and specialized construction, Ground Granulated Blast Furnace Slag is frequently combined with phosphogypsum to create backfill mixtures, cement-free pathways, and alkali-activated materials. These combinations are specifically engineered to immobilize radon, control phosphate and fluoride pollution, and develop stable binders. Additionally, when blended with FGD gypsum, it further enhances mortar performance. Through these diverse applications, Ground Granulated Blast Furnace Slag effectively repurposes industrial waste to deliver both mechanical robustness and environmental mitigation benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007</data>
