  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Metakaolin is a supplementary cementitious material adopted in solidification and stabilization processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metakaolin is a product derived from kaolin through thermal treatment at 600-800°C, used to reduce CO2 emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;An additive studied for its synergistic effects on hydration and strength when combined with phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Metakaolin is an additive used synergistically with phosphogypsum in eco excess-sulphate cement to improve hydration and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Metakaolin is a component used alongside calcined gypsum and lime to design optimal binder compositions.&lt;SEP&gt;Metakaolin is an additive used synergistically with phosphogypsum to enhance hydration, strength, and microstructure in cement.</data>
