<node id="Solidification/Stabilization">
  <data key="d0">Solidification/Stabilization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Solidification/Stabilization is a remediation process designed to manage Phosphogypsum stockpiles and control hazardous element exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification/stabilization is a treatment process used to immobilize hazardous substances within construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification and stabilization are techniques applied to treat lead-contaminated soils and immobilize harmful impurities in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification and stabilization is a treatment process applied to electrolytic manganese residue using phosphate resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Solidification/Stabilization is a waste treatment technique used to immobilize contaminants in phosphogypsum through chemical activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030</data>
