<node id="Limestone">
  <data key="d0">Limestone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Limestone is a naturally occurring alkaline mineral that commonly exists as a solid form of calcium carbonate. In industrial and construction applications, it serves multiple critical functions. Primarily, it acts as a supplementary cementitious material and is calcined as the primary raw material to produce quicklime through traditional carbonate calcination processes. It is frequently combined with phosphogypsum and steel slag to manufacture cement, where its alkaline properties help modify phosphogypsum to meet production standards, provided the dosage is carefully controlled.

Beyond cement manufacturing, limestone functions as a substitution material in mortar mixes when blended with slag, and it is actively utilized in solidification and stabilization processes. The broader industrial utilization of phosphogypsum in Portland cement production also impacts the natural resource market by reducing the quarrying demand for limestone.&lt;SEP&gt;Limestone is the natural form of calcium carbonate, now primarily used as a raw substance for building materials due to weathering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791916543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
