  <data key="d0">Wastewater</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Wastewater is a complex aqueous byproduct generated in substantial volumes through industrial operations such as leaching processes, water-washing methods, and other related procedures. Characteristically, it often contains high concentrations of acids and dissolved minerals, specifically manifesting as acidic, calcium sulfate-saturated water, while also serving as a carrier for heavy metals like lead ions. Due to its high volume, acidity, and contaminant load, wastewater typically poses significant environmental challenges and generally necessitates secondary treatment or active minimization strategies. However, depending on the specific industrial framework, it can also be managed through complete recovery systems where it is 100% reused.

In scientific and environmental research contexts, wastewater functions as the actual environmental matrix and target environment for evaluating advanced remediation technologies. It is specifically utilized to test the removal efficiency of heavy metal ions, particularly lead, using specialized materials such as hydroxyapatite nanoparticles, PG, and the HAP-BC nanocomposite. These applications highlight its dual role as both a challenging industrial effluent requiring careful management and a critical real-world medium for developing and validating heavy metal extraction solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Wastewater is a medium that may be treated using precipitation processes to remove phosphate ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791722395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wet sieving">
  <data key="d0">Wet sieving</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet sieving is a screening method integrated into washing protocols to separate impurities from PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791021920</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flotation">
  <data key="d0">Flotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flotation is a physical separation and pretreatment technique primarily applied to phosphogypsum for purification and quality enhancement. The process involves introducing phosphogypsum and water into specialized machinery, where targeted components or contaminants rise to the surface and are subsequently scraped off. Its main objectives include removing undesirable impurities such as fine mud and organic debris, isolating gypsum, and extracting valuable components, particularly rare earth elements. By effectively targeting these specific materials, flotation significantly improves the industrial suitability and overall purity of the processed phosphogypsum.

In practical applications, flotation is frequently integrated with other processing methods to maximize efficiency. It is commonly employed alongside wet sieving or combined with lime addition to further eliminate residual contaminants and optimize the final product's composition. As a versatile pretreatment strategy, flotation plays a critical role in transforming raw phosphogypsum into a refined material capable of meeting stringent industrial standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Flotation is a laboratory-scale purification method. Flotation removes impurities from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Flotation is a laboratory-scale purification technology for phosphogypsum that faces scalability challenges for large-scale industrial use.&lt;SEP&gt;A purification technique applied to whiten and purify phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791610710</data>
