<node id="Sustainable Development">
  <data key="d0">Sustainable Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sustainable Development is a long-term environmental and economic goal that serves as a core framework and guiding principle for broad ecological and industrial initiatives. It functions as the overarching objective that circular economy strategies and waste crisis management systems aim to achieve. In the energy sector, this principle drives the transition away from fossil fuels by promoting the substitution of conventional energy sources with renewable alternatives such as biodiesel. By prioritizing ecological balance alongside economic growth, it establishes a foundational standard for evaluating and directing large-scale resource management efforts.

In practical applications, Sustainable Development acts as a critical requirement and primary motivation for the comprehensive utilization and commercial valorization of industrial byproducts, particularly phosphogypsum. It strongly aligns with national green economy policies, notably within China's industrial economy, where it supports targeted research, resource optimization, and the development of beneficial applications for waste materials. Through these integrated efforts, the concept bridges policy objectives, industrial innovation, and environmental stewardship to address contemporary resource and ecological challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001</data>
