<node id="Dolomite">
  <data key="d0">Dolomite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Dolomite is an example mineral listed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Dolomite is a mineral attributed to XRD peaks at 29.5° and 31°, corresponding to CaMg(CO3)2.&lt;SEP&gt;Dolomite (CaMg(CO3)2) is a mineral whose diffraction peaks disappeared from the BC sample during the adsorption process.&lt;SEP&gt;Dolomite is a mineral phase detected in phosphogypsum through multi-analytical characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Dolomite is a calcium magnesium carbonate mineral (CaMg(CO3)2) identified in the mineralogical composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-003</data>
