  <data key="d5">1791722976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcination Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Calcination Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcination temperature is a critical process parameter affecting the performance of phosphogypsum-derived materials like supersulfated cements and gypsum plaster.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination temperature is a parameter that influences the yield of biodiesel production using hydroxyapatite catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination Temperature refers to the specific heat treatments applied at 800 °C and 1000 °C to analyze sample structures.&lt;SEP&gt;The temperature during calcination that influences the preferred orientation growth of calcium sulfate dihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination temperature refers to the 600°C and 900°C conditions applied to the hydroxyapatite powder for 2 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination Temperature refers to the 650°C to 700°C range applied to the sample during preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792068630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supersulfated Cements">
  <data key="d0">Supersulfated Cements</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Supersulfated cements are construction materials whose performance is influenced by the calcination temperature of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Supersulfated cements are specialized binding materials whose performance is influenced by phosphogypsum calcination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791723719</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
