<node id="Spain">
  <data key="d0">Spain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Spain is a country located in southwestern Europe that serves as a major global producer and manager of phosphogypsum, generating approximately 2.5 million tons annually and accounting for 10.84% of global production and reserves. The nation hosts extensive phosphogypsum deposits and stockpile sites, primarily utilizing stockpiling methods while conducting limited research into applications such as fertilizers and soil amendments. Within Spain, the Huelva region and the Huelva Estuary are particularly significant as primary locations for studying phosphogypsum geochemistry and historical trace metal toxicity, with research indicating that geogenic weathering is the dominant factor influencing trace pollutant distribution. The country also contains a large Technologically Enhanced Naturally Occurring Radioactive Material waste disposal site that has been evaluated for preliminary restoration efforts.

Scientific and environmental assessments of Spanish phosphogypsum have systematically analyzed its chemical composition, including mean weight percentages of various chemical oxides, with specific datasets indicating a weight percentage of approximately 46 percent, alongside evaluations of impurities and radiological profiles. Spain is notably recognized for phosphogypsum containing higher levels of radionuclides, making it a focal point in environmental scientific literature for examining ecological implications and management strategies. Additionally, recycled gypsum has been assessed within the country as a potential replacement for natural gypsum in cement production. As the base location for the associated research institution and authors, Spain is frequently cited in data tables and scientific publications, contributing significantly to the global body of phosphogypsum research and serving as a critical geographic reference for understanding the material's chemical, radiological, and environmental characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Spain is a country where phosphogypsum exhibits significantly higher radioactivity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Spain is a country exhibiting significantly higher phosphogypsum radioactivity levels compared to global averages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000</data>
