<node id="Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy">
  <data key="d0">Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is an analytical and spectroscopic technique designed to identify chemical bonds, functional groups, and molecular vibrations within a wide variety of materials. The method functions by plotting light transmittance against wavenumber to generate transmittance spectra, which are then compared to determine the precise chemical composition and structural characteristics of a given sample. By analyzing these vibrational modes, the technique effectively reveals the presence of organic functional groups and elucidates the underlying chemical structure and components of the tested substances.

While broadly applicable to diverse materials and samples, Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy has been specifically utilized to study the chemical and structural compositions of hydroxyapatite. Additionally, the technique has been applied to reveal functional group vibrations and analyze the detailed chemical makeup of phosphogypsum. Through its capacity to correlate spectral data with molecular interactions, Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy serves as a fundamental tool for material characterization and chemical analysis across scientific research.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is a characterization technique used to analyze the chemical composition of synthesized hydroxyapatite powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is a spectroscopic technique used to identify functional groups in hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy is a spectroscopic technique used to identify vibrational bands of chemical groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used to analyze the functional groups of raw phosphogypsum and elaborated hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is a characterization technique used to analyze the chemical properties of synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to study the conversion of amorphous calcium phosphate to hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
