<node id="Fig. 8">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 8 is a figure label that appears across multiple independent scientific studies, each depicting distinct experimental processes, material characterizations, and mechanical observations. In the context of phosphogypsum processing and characterization, Fig. 8 illustrates a three-step schematic for extracting rare earth elements from recycled phosphogypsum, depicts undissolved particles remaining after dissolving the gypsum matrix with dilute hydrochloric acid, outlines the Boren-Haber reaction cycle for the catalytic decomposition of phosphogypsum, and presents infrared spectra comparing phosphogypsum before and after thermal treatment.

Regarding biomaterials and hydroxyapatite applications, Fig. 8 displays scanning electron microscopy micrographs of composite bone cements following varying immersion durations in SBF solution. It also schematically represents the photocatalytic mechanism of titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite under simulated solar light irradiation, and presents the release profiles of BSA and LSZ from HAp samples alongside the corresponding Higuchi plot.

Finally, in mechanical testing contexts, Fig. 8 displays compressive strength observations documented by Wei, Zhou, and Li. Collectively, these descriptions indicate that Fig. 8 serves as a generic reference label across different publications, with each instance tailored to specific research domains including mineral extraction, catalytic decomposition, biomaterial degradation, photocatalysis, drug release kinetics, and mechanical performance evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 illustrates the length variation of PGCM specimens across different curing ages.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 displays SEM micrographs illustrating the morphological changes of hydroxyapatite materials with varying surfactant amounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 illustrates the phosphogypsum conversion procedure using a chloride solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure displaying rod-like crystals consistent with the preferential crystalline growth of HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 8 displays the SSM plots for synthesized HAp nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure presenting diametric compression strength and elastic modulus measurements after curing periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
