<node id="Immobilization">
  <data key="d0">Immobilization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immobilization is the process of restricting the movement of PTEs through adsorption at hydration product surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Immobilization refers to the retention of harmful substances within the filling body system, which can be negatively affected by excessively high pH.&lt;SEP&gt;Immobilization is the process of trapping contaminants like fluorine and heavy metals within the backfill matrix through precipitation and adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Immobilization is the process of stabilizing and fixing pollutants to prevent their migration into groundwater.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-017</data>
