<node id="Acidulation">
  <data key="d0">Acidulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acidulation is a chemical process where sulfuric acid reacts with phosphorite ores to produce phosphoric acid and PG.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical treatment process applied to phosphate rock to extract phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidulation is an industrial process that solubilizes elements from phosphate rock and generates acidic process water.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidulation is a chemical process that solubilizes various elements and compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidulation is a chemical process that releases fluorine and hydrogen fluoride from phosphate rocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permeability Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Permeability Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The permeability coefficient is a data metric for PG that fluctuates across nearly three orders of magnitude and is categorized as low permeability.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydrological property measured at 1.02 x 10^-7 m/s for the raw phosphogypsum sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
