<node id="pH Value">
  <data key="d0">pH Value</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">pH value is a chemical data metric for PG that ranges from strongly acidic (&lt;3) to neutral (~6) during weathering.&lt;SEP&gt;pH Value is a measured feature in the comparative table, indicating the acidity or alkalinity of the water in each region.&lt;SEP&gt;The pH value of phosphogypsum increases as calcination temperature rises.&lt;SEP&gt;pH value is a measured parameter indicating the acidity or alkalinity of phosphogypsum samples during washing.&lt;SEP&gt;pH value is a critical parameter that affects the stability of calcium fluoride, decreasing stability when exceeding 10.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of the reaction environment's acidity that decreases when phosphoric acid is added too quickly.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical property of slag influenced by iron oxides and calculated using a specific equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004</data>
