</node>
<node id="Volcanic Ash">
  <data key="d0">Volcanic Ash</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Volcanic ash is a geological material that can contribute to soil fluoride contamination and enhance exposure risks to creatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flora">
  <data key="d0">Flora</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Flora refers to vegetation that is negatively impacted by fluoride accumulation, which can limit growth or inhibit enzyme systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fauna">
  <data key="d0">Fauna</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fauna refers to animals that are exposed to toxic impurities through the food chain and environmental contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mammals">
  <data key="d0">Mammals</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Mammals face severe risks from excessive fluoride uptake in the food chain, including through contaminated crops and groundwater.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silicon Tetrafluoride">
  <data key="d0">Silicon Tetrafluoride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicon tetrafluoride is a gaseous form of emitted fluoride that can directly enter plant leaves through cuticles or stomata.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is a chemical compound produced from silicate impurities in phosphate rock that hydrolyzes to form fluorosilicic acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is a gaseous compound produced from the reaction of hydrofluoric acid with silicate impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is an air emission estimated from the Phosphogypsum stack.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon Tetrafluoride is an air emission measured in the LCI data for PG disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is a gaseous emission quantified in grams within the inventory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791880572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Volcanic Eruptions">
  <data key="d0">Volcanic Eruptions</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Volcanic eruptions are geological hazards that contribute to soil fluoride contamination and enhance exposure risks through volcanic ash deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brine-Evaporation Deposits System">
  <data key="d0">Brine-Evaporation Deposits System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The brine-evaporation deposits system is a geochemical system whose evolution is controlled by mechanisms affecting fluoride and phosphate in phosphogypsum deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023386</data>
