<node id="Wet Sieving">
  <data key="d0">Wet Sieving</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet Sieving is a concentration technique that increased rare earth element content from 309 to 1071 ppm in the recovered fraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet sieving is a gravity separation method used to separate particles based on size and density.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical separation technique used to concentrate rare earth elements in fine particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet sieving is a pre-treatment method studied for processing phosphogypsum for secondary usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030</data>
