<node id="Recrystallization">
  <data key="d0">Recrystallization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Recrystallization is a physical-chemical process and leaching reinforcement technique primarily applied to gypsum and phosphogypsum matrices. The phenomenon typically begins with the dissolution of the gypsum matrix surface during leaching, followed by the in situ transformation of hemihydrated gypsum into a dense crystalline microstructure of dihydrate gypsum. As the gypsum plates reform, the controlled manipulation of this microstructure triggers the release of entrained or soluble components into the surrounding solution. Depending on the operational requirements, the process is often driven using acidic media to facilitate these phase transformations and chemical separations.

In industrial and environmental contexts, Recrystallization serves multiple specialized purposes. It is utilized as a chemical separation method to remove radium isotopes from phosphogypsum, while simultaneously acting as a leaching reinforcement strategy to enhance the extraction and recovery of soluble rare earth elements. Furthermore, the technique is employed to decompose phosphogypsum slag, enabling carbon dioxide capture and the subsequent production of high-purity calcium carbonate. By leveraging these controlled physicochemical transformations, Recrystallization effectively optimizes the processing of gypsum-based materials for resource valorization and waste remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a process used alongside carbonation to modify phosphogypsum for rare earth element recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a physical process applied alongside carbonation to modify phosphogypsum microstructure during indirect leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a method used alongside carbonation to dissolve phosphogypsum and form fertilizer compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a synthesis process where smaller particles dissolve to allow larger particles to grow.&lt;SEP&gt;Recrystallization is a physicochemical pre-treatment technique applied to increase rare earth element concentration in phosphogypsum prior to extraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041352</data>
