  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Matrix refers to the calcium sulfate dihydrate structure within Phosphogypsum that dissolves and recrystallizes during leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;The gypsum matrix is the structural component of phosphogypsum that can absorb organic reagents, causing losses during leaching.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-022</data>
