<node id="Elsevier B.V.">
  <data key="d0">Elsevier B.V.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Elsevier B.V. is a major publishing company that functions as the official publisher and copyright holder for a diverse array of academic and scientific publications. The entity is primarily responsible for disseminating research articles and review articles, while consistently maintaining the intellectual property rights and copyright for the works it releases. As a central figure in academic publishing, Elsevier B.V. ensures that all associated articles are properly managed, distributed, and legally protected under its publishing rights.

The company’s publishing scope encompasses a variety of specialized scientific topics and collaborative arrangements. Its portfolio includes the publication of a 2016 research article on hydroxyapatite synthesis, a 2005 publication, and a research article dedicated to phosphogypsum waste treatment. Furthermore, Elsevier B.V. actively supports open access initiatives by releasing specific review articles under open access models. The entity also engages in institutional partnerships, serving as the publisher for review articles on behalf of Tsinghua University Press. Through these varied operations, Elsevier B.V. continues to play a critical role in the global dissemination of scholarly research.&lt;SEP&gt;Elsevier B.V. is the publishing organization responsible for the conference proceedings and copyright.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the open access article.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-000</data>
