<node id="Japan">
  <data key="d0">Japan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Japan is a sovereign nation and geographic region recognized for its strategic resource management and technological innovations. It has officially classified rare earth elements as strategic resources due to inherent supply risks. Additionally, Japan holds the distinction of being the country of origin for the Rigaku X-ray diffractometer, highlighting its contributions to scientific instrumentation.

In the realm of industrial chemistry and resource utilization, Japan pioneered research on phosphogypsum in the 1970s and currently achieves a 100 percent comprehensive utilization rate for this byproduct. Driven by naturally gypsum-devoid volcanic soil and a consequent lack of domestic gypsum resources, the country economically recovers approximately three million tons of phosphogypsum annually. Japan is notably the only nation that currently finds phosphogypsum recovery for plaster manufacturing profitable, primarily utilizing the material to produce gypsum construction products that offset domestic shortages. Furthermore, within its chemical manufacturing sector, the hemihydrate process for phosphoric acid production is relatively widespread.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is a PG-generating country that has achieved notable success in utilizing PG for building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan utilizes phosphogypsum primarily for the production of building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Japan is the country where Jeol is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Union">
  <data key="d0">European Union</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Union is a political and economic union that operates as a pivotal regional entity in addressing critical resource and material management challenges. It has officially classified rare earth elements as strategic materials due to significant supply risks. Furthermore, the Union actively addresses the gypsum supply gap by promoting the industrial utilization of phosphogypsum, a byproduct that requires careful handling and regulatory oversight.

To ensure environmental and public safety, the European Union has established comprehensive regulations and legislation governing phosphogypsum and related waste materials. These frameworks mandate specific hazard categorization standards for phosphogypsum and strictly regulate hazardous substances contained within it, such as radium-226. The Union also sets precise regulatory standards and activity concentration limits for radionuclides in both phosphogypsum applications and general waste materials, ensuring that industrial byproducts are managed safely.

In addition to its regulatory and strategic roles, the European Union functions as a primary funding body that supports scientific research programs focused on these material challenges. By financing studies related to phosphogypsum utilization and radionuclide management, the Union facilitates the development of sustainable practices for managing industrial waste and mitigating resource supply risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-022</data>
