<node id="XRD Pattern">
  <data key="d0">XRD Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">XRD Pattern is analytical data showing the crystal structure of the initial Phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;The XRD pattern is a stacked line graph displaying diffraction intensity versus diffraction angle for multiple samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD Pattern is a diffraction pattern used to analyze crystallite size and lattice spacing of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD Pattern is a diffraction pattern used to analyze the phase structure of the slag.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD pattern is an analytical technique used to determine the crystalline phase composition of slag.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD pattern is analytical data confirming the formation of calcium silicate at 1200 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;The XRD pattern is a 2D line graph displaying signal intensity versus diffraction angle to identify crystalline structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
