<node id="Titanium">
  <data key="d0">Titanium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Titanium is a chemical element that exhibits distinct geochemical and chemical behaviors across various phosphate-related materials and experimental settings. In geological contexts, titanium occurs as a trace element that is notably depleted in phosphorites when compared to shale. Within phosphate rock processing byproducts, specifically phosphogypsum, titanium is present as a major component, with measured mass fractions typically ranging from 0.090% to 0.400%. It frequently appears in scattered patches, serving as an indicator of titanium-bearing impurities originating from the parent phosphate rock. Regional variations in concentration are observed, with titanium consistently reported at lower levels in Brazilian phosphogypsum compared to Moroccan phosphogypsum. In processing streams, titanium acts as an interfering metal ion within phosphogypsum leach liquor, commonly measured at concentrations around 10 mg/L.

Beyond its geochemical distribution, titanium plays a specific functional role in mineral structures. It readily substitutes for calcium within hydroxyapatite lattices, a substitution that imparts the material with photocatalytic activity capable of functioning in the dark. In laboratory and industrial extraction processes, titanium is utilized in its Ti4+ ionic form, where it is deliberately introduced into synthetic solutions to facilitate and monitor extraction experiments. Collectively, these characteristics highlight titanium's varied presence as both a naturally occurring impurity in phosphate systems and a functional ion in chemical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Titanium is a major chemical species analyzed in the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Titanium is an element detected in variable concentrations within the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Titanium is a trace element found in phosphogypsum phases, including gypsum and quartz.&lt;SEP&gt;Titanium is a trace element measured in phosphogypsum minerals using LA-ICP-MS.&lt;SEP&gt;Titanium is a trace element that can be eliminated by simple water washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
