<node id="Water Washing">
  <data key="d0">Water Washing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Water washing is a pretreatment technique developed for the purification of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Water washing is a physical treatment process that removes soluble contaminants from phosphogypsum crystal surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Water washing is a common purification method for phosphogypsum that eliminates many contaminants but generates effluent requiring treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Water washing is a pretreatment method applied to phosphogypsum to prepare it as an aggregate for cemented backfill.&lt;SEP&gt;A pretreatment method applied to phosphogypsum to prepare it as an aggregate for cemented backfill.&lt;SEP&gt;Water washing is a physical separation step used to remove reaction products after treating phosphogypsum with citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Water washing is a simple physical method used to eliminate certain trace elements from the phosphogypsum matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
