  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Neutralization is a pretreatment technique developed for the purification of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a chemical treatment process used to safely handle PG modifiers and byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a laboratory-scale purification method. Neutralization removes impurities from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a laboratory-scale purification technology for phosphogypsum that requires further research for industrial scalability.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutralization is a pre-treatment process applied to electroplating wastewater to adjust pH levels.</data>
