  <data key="d0">Walawalkar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Walawalkar is a researcher who reported that nitric and hydrochloric acids are superior to sulfuric acid for leaching Rare Earth Elements from Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Walawalkar is a researcher cited for describing the mineral phases of gypsum in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Walawalkar is a researcher who developed a nitric acid-based technique achieving an 85 percent recovery rate for rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Walawalkar denotes a researcher who developed a nitric acid technique for rare earth element recovery, achieving 85 percent efficiency.</data>
