<node id="Figure 8">
  <data key="d0">Figure 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 8 presents elemental mapping images of phosphogypsum after complete dissolution of the gypsum matrix by hydrochloric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 displays the Raman spectra of synthesized powders across specific wavenumber ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 presents a dark field TEM image and a particle size distribution histogram for HAp Type 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 illustrates the diverse shapes and sizes of Type 3 HAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure presenting the liquid/solid fractionation of chemical species following phosphogypsum leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 presents experimental data on the decomposition rate and XRD patterns of phosphogypsum and PGI-1.4 under varying conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure displaying the decomposition rate and XRD patterns of PG and PGI-1.4 at various temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 9">
  <data key="d0">Figure 9</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 9 outlines strategies for recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum based on their occurrence states.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 presents the FTIR spectra results for analyzing functional groups in HA.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 provides additional details regarding the trace and radioelements distribution in PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 contains TEM characterizations that confirm the influence of Brij-93 surfactant on HAp nanorod crystal size.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 presents a dark field TEM image and a particle size distribution histogram for HAp Type 4.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure presenting the XPS analysis of PGI-1.4 reduced at 1450 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 displays the binding energies of different element valence states in the slag samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 10">
  <data key="d0">Figure 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 10 illustrates the leaching efficiency of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum over four cycles using hydrochloric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the effects of phosphogypsum and natural gypsum contents on cement setting time and compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 presents a dark field TEM image and a particle size distribution histogram for HAp Type 5.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 provides SEM-EDS analysis results of the PGI-1.4 sample reduced at 1250 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 shows the microstructure and chemical composition distribution of the longitudinal section of slag from PGI-1.4.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 presents the slag SEM-EDS analysis conducted at 1250 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
