<node id="Figure 11">
  <data key="d0">Figure 11</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 11 demonstrates the effect of sulfuric acid concentration on the leaching efficiency of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A graphical representation showing nitrous oxide conversion rates for various RhO/M-P-O catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the mechanism of phosphogypsum acting as a soil conditioner in saline-alkali land.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 11 displays the surface morphology of the five synthesized HAp sample variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 11 presents a dark field TEM image and a particle size distribution histogram for HAp Type 6.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 11 presents SEM-EDS analysis of PGI-1.4 samples with a C/S molar ratio of 0.5 reduced at 1350 and 1450 °C.</data>
