<node id="NaCl">
  <data key="d0">NaCl</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride (NaCl) is a chemical compound utilized across various scientific and industrial applications, most notably as a functional additive in composite bone cements. In this context, it serves as a critical modifier incorporated during cement synthesis to precisely control material properties. The varying concentrations of NaCl directly influence the phase composition, setting duration, and overall physical characteristics of the cement mixture. Furthermore, it acts as a porogen and microstructural regulator, promoting a highly porous architecture that enhances surface properties and grain growth. These structural modifications are strategically employed to optimize the mechanical performance and biological integration of the resulting bone cement.

Beyond orthopedic materials, NaCl functions as a fundamental component in biological and chemical systems. It is routinely employed as a salinity component and control solution within culture media to maintain optimal osmotic and ionic conditions for biological assays. In aqueous environments, NaCl is utilized to adjust solution ionic strength, which plays a specific role in metal ion interactions. Research indicates that while NaCl exhibits minimal impact on the removal of lead (Pb(II)), it demonstrates slight competitive behavior for copper (Cu(II)) and zinc (Zn(II)) ions at elevated concentrations. These dual applications highlight the compound's versatility as both a structural modifier in biomaterials and a regulatory agent in solution chemistry.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl is a chemical compound used in dietary solutions for treating phosphogypsum to produce rare earths concentrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride, a chloride solution tested for reaction with calcium carbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is a chemical compound used in the interface studies with hydroxyapatite samples.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl is a chemical compound forming the solution interface for HAP1 and HAP2 in zeta potential measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl is used in the interface studies with hydroxyapatite samples to measure electrochemical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl is a chemical compound mentioned in the context of preparing standard solutions or reagents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792069208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAP">
  <data key="d0">HAP</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite (HAP) is a versatile calcium phosphate compound and mineral that serves as a foundational material across biomedical, environmental, and composite applications. Chemically, it typically crystallizes in a hexagonal structure, though its physical state can vary from nanocrystalline powder to amorphous calcium phosphate depending on synthesis conditions. The material is predominantly prepared through hydrothermal methods that enable controlled nucleation and self-assembly, with phosphogypsum (PG) waste frequently utilized as a sustainable calcium source. Depending on the specific preparation parameters, HAP exhibits diverse morphologies, including agglomerates, hierarchical microparticles, hierarchical microspheres, and nanoparticles. Its structural integrity and crystalline nature are rigorously validated using X-ray diffraction and various spectroscopic techniques.

In biomedical contexts, HAP functions as a critical biomaterial integrated into composite bone cements, where it actively reinforces the structural matrix. It also serves as a foundational substrate for hydrothermal deposition and surface functionalization, including the attachment of calcium sulfide crystals and AL molecules. Beyond healthcare, HAP is extensively employed as an adsorbent for capturing heavy metal ions from aqueous solutions. It is commonly utilized as an undoped baseline material to benchmark the performance of advanced composites, such as the 20HPA-HAP composite. Furthermore, HAP nanoparticles are homogeneously grown onto biochar sheets to create HAP-BC composites, which demonstrate significantly enhanced heavy metal adsorption capabilities compared to standalone hydroxyapatite. Collectively, these attributes establish HAP as a multifunctional, hydrothermally synthesized calcium phosphate material with well-documented structural, biomedical, and environmental utility.&lt;SEP&gt;An abbreviation for hydroxyapatite, the primary product in the chemical reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP is a powder material analyzed for its structural and chemical properties before and after heat treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003</data>
