<node id="Porous Structure">
  <data key="d0">Porous Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Porous Structure is a microstructural feature of the bone cement that facilitates drug loading and biological functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Porous Structure is a structural characteristic of composite bone cement promoted by NaCl addition, influencing mechanical performance and bioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;A material architecture characterized by interconnected pores that enhances crystal precipitation and surface area.&lt;SEP&gt;Material characteristic defined by significant void space between crystal aggregates.&lt;SEP&gt;Porous structure formed in the slag interior due to gas diffusion from the inside to the surface during reduction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-013</data>
