<node id="Composite Bone Cement">
  <data key="d0">Composite Bone Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite Bone Cement is a synthetic biomaterial engineered specifically for medical and bone tissue-engineering applications, with a primary focus on bone repair. It is formulated from calcium sulfate and hydroxyapatite in a 0.70CaS–0.30HAP ratio, with sodium chloride incorporated at varying concentrations to tailor its performance. Throughout experimental procedures, this material serves as the central engineered substance under investigation.

Researchers have extensively evaluated its physical, microstructural, and mechanical properties, alongside its phase composition, washout resistance, and setting time. The deliberate modification of sodium chloride levels directly influences these characteristics, prompting detailed analyses of fracture surfaces to assess porosity levels. Furthermore, the cement's surface properties and apatite formation capability are closely examined to determine its bioactivity. In addition to structural and mechanical assessments, the material undergoes rigorous biological testing, including cytotoxicity and biocompatibility evaluations, to ensure its safety and efficacy for bone-related and broader biomedical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Surface Area">
  <data key="d0">Specific Surface Area</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific Surface Area is a fundamental physical and structural metric that quantifies the total surface area available per unit mass of a material, typically expressed in square meters per gram. It is commonly measured directly using techniques such as the BET isotherm method for nanopowders, or calculated structurally by incorporating crystallite size, specific density, and X-ray diffraction data. This measured or calculated value is frequently utilized to verify nanopowder crystallite dimensions and to compare derived particle sizes against X-ray diffraction results.

The magnitude of Specific Surface Area is not static and generally ranges from 51 to 258 square meters per gram depending on the substance. It is inversely related to particle size and density, typically decreasing as materials transition from fine to coarse fractions or as synthesis times are extended. This reduction in the property drives the thermodynamic tendency to minimize surface energy during particle growth. Its value varies significantly based on material composition, particle size distribution, and processing conditions.

Across different substances, Specific Surface Area reflects unique structural and chemical properties while directly influencing critical functional attributes. In hydroxyapatite, natural forms exhibit lower values than synthetic variants, which often measure around 86.29 square meters per gram; in this material, the property governs water adsorption capacity and shows a direct correlation with radionuclide ion incorporation. For phosphogypsum, calcination processes significantly increase the metric, while in construction materials like Plaster of Paris, it decisively determines the workability and setting characteristics of concrete mixtures. Ultimately, as a defining characteristic for porous and particulate materials, Specific Surface Area directly impacts loading rates, active site availability, and overall biocompatibility, making its precise understanding and control essential for optimizing performance in biomedical, environmental, and industrial applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791854849</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="(0.70CaS–0.30HAP)/xNaCl Composite Bone Cement">
