</node>
<node id="Sodium Chloride (NaCl)">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride (NaCl)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical compound added to the composite bone cement to modify its physical and functional properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference compound used in the XRD pattern analysis, identified by ICDD No. 01-078-0751.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is used to adjust the ionic strength of the solution and to introduce sodium ions for competitive adsorption studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A chloride salt whose solution properties and optimal concentration significantly impact phosphogypsum solubility.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Chloride is a chemical compound prepared to create a standard solution in Section 5.62.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792068764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulfide (CaS)">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfide (CaS)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A base material component of the composite bone cement.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical phase identified by black circles in the diffraction graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfide is a chemical compound produced by the carbon reduction of calcium sulfate and subsequently oxidized by unreacted calcium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyapatite (HAP)">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite (HAP)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite is a calcium phosphate-based biomaterial and major component of bone inorganic matrix, widely used for bone augmentation and tissue engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;A base material component of the composite bone cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a calcium phosphate biomaterial studied for its biocompatibility and surface modification potential.&lt;SEP&gt;A calcium phosphate material synthesized on FTO glass via hydrothermal methods.&lt;SEP&gt;An inorganic compound serving as the base material for hybrid nano-adsorbents, often modified with organo-phosphonates.&lt;SEP&gt;A crystalline material whose diffraction peaks decrease and eventually disappear upon HPA incorporation, transforming into an amorphous state.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791654123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Porosity">
  <data key="d0">Porosity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Porosity is a fundamental physical and structural property that quantifies the percentage or volume fraction of void space within a material. In materials science and powder evaluation, it is routinely assessed alongside surface area and analyzed using gas adsorption-desorption isotherms. This property serves as a critical determinant of a material's physical profile and functional behavior across diverse applications.

In cement and composite bone cements, porosity represents the proportion of empty spaces within the hardened matrix and is directly modulated by additives such as sodium chloride. Increasing sodium chloride concentration elevates porosity, which reduces overall density and exerts an inverse, exponential effect on bending strength. Despite this mechanical trade-off, the enhanced void structure is functionally advantageous in biomedical contexts, as it facilitates apatite crystal precipitation, thereby promoting effective bone integration. Similarly, in cemented paste fill materials and filling bodies, porosity acts as a structural feature that increases with fluoride content and inversely correlates with mechanical strength, while conversely decreasing with higher calcium hydroxide content, which also influences overall structural integrity.

In the context of hydroxyapatite (HA) and hydroxyapatite phosphate (HAP) crystals, porosity is recognized as a key structural property and feature intrinsically linked to their three-dimensional architecture. Furthermore, in soil science, porosity is defined as the ratio of void volume to total soil volume and exhibits dynamic responses to agricultural amendments. Specifically, the application of biofertilizers significantly enhances soil porosity through calcium-induced flocculation processes, which reorganize soil particles into stable aggregates. This structural improvement yields a more open matrix that enhances overall soil structure and aeration, demonstrating how porosity universally governs material performance and environmental interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Porosity is a physical property of raw phosphogypsum that decreases with increased compaction energy, leading to higher density.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791938112</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Absorption">
  <data key="d0">Water Absorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical property of the composite bone cement analyzed to understand its interaction with aqueous media.&lt;SEP&gt;A functional property of the composite bone cement that increases with higher sodium chloride concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of bricks that decreases with higher PG content in certain formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of bricks that is reduced by Phosphogypsum addition but increases when both Phosphogypsum and Fly Ash are combined.&lt;SEP&gt;Water absorption is a physical process in PGCM where aggregates and quicklime take in water, causing volume changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rate of Absorption">
  <data key="d0">Rate of Absorption</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A functional property of the composite bone cement that increases alongside sodium chloride concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Shrinkage">
  <data key="d0">Linear Shrinkage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A dimensional property of the composite bone cement that reduces as sodium chloride additive increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear shrinkage is a material property that decreases with higher NaCl additive concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012</data>
