<node id="Mechanical Properties">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Properties</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural performance metrics of the composite bone cement that are maintained or improved compared to unmodified formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance characteristics of the composite bone cement that are directly linked to porosity and dissolution behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical properties are the structural performance metrics of PGCM that decrease due to crack formation and reduced adhesion.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical properties are improved in hydroxyapatite synthesized from biogenic calcium sources compared to inorganic sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical Properties are physical characteristics assessed to determine the structural integrity and damage constitutive models of backfill materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical properties are enhanced in alpha-hemihydrate gypsum through chemical modifications and optimized synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791772783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Cells">
  <data key="d0">Bone Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Biological cells that proliferate, mineralize, and repair bone defects when supported by adequate scaffold porosity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009</data>
