<node id="Brushite">
  <data key="d0">Brushite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brushite, chemically identified as dicalcium phosphate dihydrate, is an insoluble calcium phosphate mineral phase and complex that frequently manifests as a secondary crystalline or mixed phase within various cementitious systems. It is routinely detected through X-ray diffraction and multi-analytical characterization, often appearing as a highly intense crystal. In composite bone cements and cement pastes formulated with waste river sludge and hemihydrate phosphogypsum, brushite develops as a by-product phase resulting from the interaction of calcium and hydrogen phosphate ions. This formation is particularly prominent during the acidic attack of phosphogypsum, where the mineral phase is consistently observed in the resulting matrix.

Functioning as a critical precursor material, brushite undergoes hydrolysis to produce hydroxyapatite, highlighting its role in calcium phosphate phase transformations. Thermally, the compound exhibits a defined stability limit, beginning to decompose at approximately 700 °C. These combined chemical, structural, and thermal properties establish brushite as a significant indicator phase in the analysis of advanced cement composites and phosphogypsum-based materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Brushite is a calcium phosphate compound used for optimizing fluoride adsorption in aqueous solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Brushite is a calcium phosphate compound identified as a product after drying in the synthesis process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791857078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
