<node id="Particle Size">
  <data key="d0">Particle Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Particle Size is a fundamental physical dimension and quantitative metric that represents the diameter, spatial extent, or dimensions of individual particles, agglomerates, crystallites, or nanoparticles within a given material. As a critical physical parameter, it significantly influences the functional, chemical, and processing behaviors of various substances, directly dictating reaction kinetics, separation efficiency, structural properties, and overall material performance. The measurement and control of this parameter are essential across multiple scientific and industrial domains, with specific characteristics and impacts varying by material context.

In cement components, Particle Size directly governs the material's setting time. For phosphogypsum, it serves as a key physical characteristic that changes during milling, directly impacts material performance, and governs impurity content and removal rates, with the majority of particles typically concentrated between 0.04 and 0.075 millimeters and experimental samples often characterized as less than 63 micrometers. In hydroxyapatite applications, Particle Size is a critical parameter controlled by synthesis conditions and determined via methods such as electrophoresis for dispersions. It dictates adsorption efficiency, where smaller dimensions yield superior performance; nanocrystals generally measure between 10 and 25 nanometers in diameter and 75 to 150 nanometers in length, while synthesized nanoparticles across different types typically range from 18.4 to 35 nanometers, with other synthesized variants precisely controlled between 6 and 30 nanometers. When applied to rare earth element-bearing minerals and general raw materials, Particle Size is a decisive factor determining bioleaching effectiveness and overall leaching efficiency. Additionally, in microscopic analyses and scientific chart distributions, it denotes the diameter of individual agglomerates or crystallites, which may range from 0.1 to 0.3 micrometers. Across all these contexts, precise characterization and control of Particle Size remain vital for optimizing material processing, enhancing functional outcomes, and tailoring synthesized crystal or nanoparticle properties.&lt;SEP&gt;The horizontal axis metric measured in millimeters on a logarithmic scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
