<node id="Bioactivity">
  <data key="d0">Bioactivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bioactivity is the ability of the material to interact favorably with biological systems, such as forming bone bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;A key material property evaluated in vitro, which is enhanced by the addition of sodium chloride to the composite bone cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioactivity is a desired characteristic of biomaterials evaluated by their ability to form apatite layers in simulated environments.&lt;SEP&gt;The material's inherent capability to promote bone-like apatite formation directly on its surface.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioactivity is a functional property of hydroxyapatite powders that may be enhanced by surfactant preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injectability">
  <data key="d0">Injectability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A critical performance characteristic of the composite bone cement that is expected to remain excellent across different sodium chloride concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;A functional property of the cement paste indicating its ease of delivery and resistance to disintegration in solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Injectability is a physical property of the composite bone cement evaluated during the research work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
