<node id="Mortar">
  <data key="d0">Mortar</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortar refers to two distinct concepts in scientific and engineering literature. In laboratory settings, Mortar is a physical grinding tool utilized to pulverize thermally decomposed bone samples into finer particles during hydroxyapatite synthesis. In construction and materials engineering, Mortar is a cementitious building material formulated using binders such as β-building gypsum powder recovered via PBG technology, Plaster Of Paris, and phosphogypsum (PG) as a partial replacement or supplementary additive. Extensive research evaluates this construction variant’s mechanical and chemical performance, focusing on compressive strength, acid corrosion resistance, and microstructural evolution. A primary area of investigation involves optimizing its setting time, particularly analyzing how varying PG replacement levels and the integration of supplementary materials influence hardening properties, overall durability, and performance characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;A mortar is a tool used to pulverize the desiccated HAP products.&lt;SEP&gt;Mortar is a construction material that contains calcium hydroxide as a constituent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791917129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Washout Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Washout Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A performance metric evaluated for the composite bone cement to determine its stability in wet environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance metric measuring the cement's ability to retain its structural integrity and shape when immersed in fluid.&lt;SEP&gt;Washout resistance is a physical property of the composite bone cement evaluated during the research work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016</data>
