<node id="X-axis">
  <data key="d0">X-axis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The X-axis of the spectrum graph represents Energy measured in keV.&lt;SEP&gt;The X-axis displays the categories FDP and GWP for the environmental impact chart.&lt;SEP&gt;The x-axis represents the pH level on the scientific graph.&lt;SEP&gt;The horizontal axis of Figure A, labeled The doping amount of HPA(mol %), representing HPA concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;X-axis is the horizontal axis of the chart, labeled with particle size in nanometers ranging from 0 to 60.&lt;SEP&gt;The horizontal axis of the charts, used to display time intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Y-axis">
  <data key="d0">Y-axis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Y-axis of the spectrum graph represents Intensity measured in counts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Y-axis represents the Environment impact percentage ranging from -800 to 1000.&lt;SEP&gt;The y-axis represents the Zeta Potential in millivolts on the scientific graph.&lt;SEP&gt;The Y-axis represents the intensity of the diffraction signal in the stacked line graph.&lt;SEP&gt;The vertical axis of Figure A, labeled Qe(mg/g), representing equilibrium adsorption capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Y-axis is the vertical axis of the chart, labeled with counts ranging from 0 to 30.&lt;SEP&gt;The vertical axis of the charts, used to display concentration values in micrograms per liter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy">
  <data key="d0">Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy is the physical quantity measured along the X-axis of the spectrum graph in keV.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy is a scientific journal that published research on full-loop CFD simulation of lignite chemical looping gasification.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy is a journal featuring thermodynamic analysis and syngas production studies using chemical looping methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy is a resource category measured alongside minerals in the assessment method.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement metric in kilo-electron volts representing the X-axis scale for the EDS spectrum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792003010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intensity">
  <data key="d0">Intensity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intensity functions as the primary metric plotted along the vertical (Y) axis of X-ray Diffraction (XRD) charts and spectrum graphs. It quantifies the relative strength of diffracted X-ray signals, serving as a direct representation of diffraction intensity. Depending on the specific instrumentation and data acquisition protocols, this physical quantity is typically measured in arbitrary units, though it may alternatively be recorded in counts or counts per second. In certain standardized datasets, the vertical axis scale explicitly ranges from 0 to 6000.

Beyond its role as a graphical axis label, Intensity provides essential analytical insights into material composition and structure. It directly correlates with the relative abundance of distinct crystalline phases present within a sample. By examining the values along this vertical axis, researchers can accurately assess relative peak positions and shapes, which are critical for interpreting diffraction patterns and characterizing the physical properties of the analyzed substances.&lt;SEP&gt;The vertical axis metric in the XRD chart, measured in scientific notation up to 4.50E+03.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement metric in arbitrary units or counts used to quantify signal strength in both XRD and EDS charts.&lt;SEP&gt;The vertical axis measurement in arbitrary units representing signal strength for each sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensity is a metric measured in arbitrary units representing signal strength on the vertical axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
