  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A gas phase compound (KF) that appears in small quantities and increases in content as temperature rises.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium fluoride is a compound formed when fluoride ions combine with alkaline elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Fluoride is a water-soluble compound formed when fluorine combines with potassium cations.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Fluoride is a fluoride salt used to prepare standard solutions at varying concentrations of 20 g/L and 150 g/L.</data>
