<node id="Wollastonite">
  <data key="d0">Wollastonite</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Wollastonite is a calcium silicate mineral identified as a solid product in the phosphogypsum reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A pink segment in the product stack that disappears when the PG to lignite ratio exceeds 0.2.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a mineral phase that carbonate clays have the potential to generate during the brick baking process.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical phase labeled "W" in the legend, corresponding to a peak in the cluster between 28 and 32 degrees.&lt;SEP&gt;Wollastonite is a standard material used for calibrating Si and Ca measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792039255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FeS Solid">
  <data key="d0">FeS Solid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">FeS solid is an iron sulfide compound formed as a solid product during the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A teal top layer that forms in the product stack at higher ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791090506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gehlenite">
  <data key="d0">Gehlenite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gehlenite is a calcium aluminum silicate compound identified as a solid product in the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A blue segment that sits on top of the red Rankinite layer at higher ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;A mineral phase that becomes more prevalent as Phosphogypsum levels increase in the brick samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Gehlenite is a calcium aluminum silicate phase that forms within the quaternary system and influences melting temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Gehlenite is a eutectic mixture formed from calcium oxide, aluminum oxide, and silicon dioxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
