  <data key="d0">Bricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bricks are construction materials and building products specifically engineered to facilitate the large-scale application and utilization of phosphogypsum. These construction units are manufactured by incorporating phosphogypsum as a core component or additive, frequently combined with other solid wastes such as fly ash and lime. The production process relies on various hydration techniques and, in certain formulations, firing methods, yielding distinct variants including fired bricks and clay bricks. By transforming industrial byproducts into structural elements, this manufacturing approach directly addresses waste management challenges while promoting sustainable construction practices.

The integration of phosphogypsum into brick production serves to significantly reduce environmental impact by repurposing discarded materials. Despite the inclusion of industrial waste, these bricks are designed to maintain low radiation exposure risks, ensuring they meet safety standards for widespread architectural and infrastructural use. Ultimately, bricks represent a versatile and eco-conscious building material that successfully bridges industrial waste recovery with practical construction needs through specialized compositional and processing methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791589393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
