<node id="Ammonia">
  <data key="d0">Ammonia</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonia is a versatile chemical compound with extensive applications across industrial processing, agriculture, material science, and environmental catalysis. In agricultural systems, it is chemically combined with phosphoric acid to manufacture ammonium phosphate fertilizers, and its application alongside phosphogypsum as a fertilizer amendment significantly reduces ammonia volatilization from urea-based fertilizers. Within industrial frameworks, such as the PBG technology process, ammonia serves as a fundamental raw material that is actively consumed during operations. It also functions as a reactant in the production of ammonium sulfate and potassium sulfate from phosphogypsum.

In chemical processing and synthesis, ammonia is utilized as a pure reagent to enhance the carbonation of phosphogypsum under increased carbon dioxide pressure, although this application can elevate operational costs and energy consumption. It acts as an additive in chloride aqueous solutions to direct chemical reactions and facilitate the selective crystallization of salts. Furthermore, ammonia is employed as a pH-adjusting agent in various synthesis procedures, including its use alongside nitric acid to lower the pH to 1 for precipitation, as well as its role in modulating the pH of alkaline reaction media.

Beyond conventional processing, ammonia plays a critical role in material science and emission control technologies. It operates as a chemical agent in conjunction with hydroxides to facilitate the loading of nickel onto phosphogypsum surfaces. In catalytic applications, it serves as a primary reactant for the selective catalytic reduction of nitrogen oxides, effectively reducing nitric oxide over copper-loaded hydroxyapatite catalysts under oxidizing conditions. However, ammonia handling requires caution, as it can be released as a hazardous gas during the mixing of CPGFM slurry containing yellow phosphorus slag. Collectively, these diverse applications underscore ammonia’s significance as both a valuable industrial reagent and a compound requiring careful management due to its environmental and safety implications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
