</node>
<node id="Urban Mining">
  <data key="d0">Urban Mining</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urban mining is a resource recovery strategy that targets waste streams like phosphogypsum, e-waste, and sewage sludge to reduce environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban Mining is a concept focused on recovering resources from various waste streams to reduce pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban Mining is a conceptual framework for recovering valuable materials and rare earth elements from industrial waste like phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A conceptual approach to reclaiming valuable materials like rare earth elements from discarded products.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban mining is a conceptual framework for recovering valuable materials like rare earth elements from industrial waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban mining refers to the recovery of rare earth elements from manufacturing waste and recycled products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphate Fertilizer Industry">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Fertilizer Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The Phosphate Fertilizer Industry is a growing industrial sector established to meet global agricultural demands. It is recognized as the primary industrial source of phosphogypsum, generating this material in large quantities as a byproduct of fertilizer production. The continuous expansion of this sector has intensified the accumulation of phosphogypsum waste, creating substantial sustainability challenges and operational overcapacity. As a result, the industry actively drives the development and implementation of sustainable waste management and recycling solutions to address these environmental burdens.

The ecological footprint of the Phosphate Fertilizer Industry is particularly pronounced in specific geographic regions, most notably in Gabes City. Industrial operations in this area have been directly linked to significant environmental impacts on the adjacent Gulf of Gabes. Despite these localized and global challenges, the sector remains essential for worldwide food production, necessitating a balanced approach that integrates agricultural output with rigorous environmental stewardship and phosphogypsum mitigation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;The industrial sector responsible for producing phosphogypsum as a byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791900207</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Recycling Industry">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Recycling Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The phosphogypsum recycling industry encompasses the applications, drivers, obstacles, and solutions for processing and reusing phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The industry focused on recycling phosphogypsum, which faces challenges and opportunities in China.&lt;SEP&gt;The phosphogypsum recycling industry encompasses companies, technologies, and markets dedicated to processing and utilizing phosphogypsum by-products.&lt;SEP&gt;An industrial sector focused on processing phosphogypsum waste, facing challenges in recognition, technology standards, and market adoption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791451490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Desulfurization Process">
  <data key="d0">Desulfurization Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The desulfurization process is a chemical treatment method studied thermodynamically to remove sulfur compounds from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791091252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold-Bonded Aggregates">
  <data key="d0">Cold-Bonded Aggregates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cold-bonded aggregates are construction materials made from surface-reinforced phosphogypsum, evaluated for macroscopic properties and leachability.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold-bonded aggregates are phosphogypsum-based construction materials studied for their physical properties and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction aggregates produced using phosphogypsum, evaluated for physical properties and impurity stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791364411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Slag Cement">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Slag Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum slag cement is a stabilized base-course mixture containing excess-sulphate phosphogypsum and artificial aggregates.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum slag cement is a material whose primary minerals include gypsum, ettringite, and a-SiO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum slag cement is a construction material that incorporates phosphogypsum-based artificial aggregate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791813629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acid Red 97 Dye">
  <data key="d0">Acid Red 97 Dye</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acid Red 97 Dye is a pollutant targeted for removal from water using green synthesized hydrocalumite derived from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791091252</data>
