<node id="Isotactic Polypropylene">
  <data key="d0">Isotactic Polypropylene</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Isotactic polypropylene is a polymer material that utilizes surface-modified anhydrous phosphogypsum as an application component.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791091252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulphur">
  <data key="d0">Sulphur</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulphur is a chemical element recovered from phosphogypsum alongside calcium with zero by-product generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulphur is an element that is drastically leached out when phosphogypsum is treated with oxalic acid, sodium carbonate, and sodium bicarbonate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulphur is recovered from waste gypsum during the extraction process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lime Activated Ground Granulated Blast-Furnace Slag">
  <data key="d0">Lime Activated Ground Granulated Blast-Furnace Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime activated ground granulated blast-furnace slag is a stabilizing agent used to enhance the mechanical properties of phosphogypsum-soil mixtures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791091252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nanoparticles">
  <data key="d0">Nanoparticles</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanoparticles are microscopic particles released from phosphogypsum that pose potential health impacts and environmental concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Nanoparticles in phosphogypsum adsorb heavy metal elements, contributing to environmental contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Microscopic particles released from phosphogypsum that are assessed for potential environmental and health impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Uniform rod-like structures formed during the synthesis of HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Nanoparticles (NPs) refer to the synthesized hydroxyapatite particles with dimensions in the nanometer range.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
