<node id="World Health Organization">
  <data key="d0">World Health Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An international health authority that recommends safe concentration limits for fluoride exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;The World Health Organization establishes international concentration limits for hazardous substances to prevent adverse health conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The World Health Organization is an international health agency that publishes drinking water quality guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;An international body whose guideline for beta particle activity was exceeded by lead-210 levels in Alberta phosphogypsum leachate.&lt;SEP&gt;The World Health Organization published a reference work on fluorides cited in the literature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791428038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphine Gas">
  <data key="d0">Phosphine Gas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphine gas is generated through microbial reduction of phosphates in exposed phosphogypsum and contributes to atmospheric warming.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphine gas is a toxic compound generated by microbial decomposition of phosphates within phosphogypsum storage facilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791109093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
