  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface Water">
  <data key="d0">Surface Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface water is a surface aquatic environment impacted by the runoff of contaminated water from phosphogypsum sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface water, such as lakes, receives migrating heavy metal complexes via surface runoff.&lt;SEP&gt;The Surface Water is an environmental compartment receiving direct erosion from the stack and soil erosion, acting as a water source.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface water is an environmental medium contaminated by leakage from phosphogypsum tailings ponds.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface water is a natural water source that acts upon solid waste to induce leaching of inorganic pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Water adsorbed on the particle surface of hydroxyapatite, evaporating up to 200 °C during heating.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013</data>
