<node id="Total Phosphorus">
  <data key="d0">Total Phosphorus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Total Phosphorus is a nutrient element that exists in various soluble and insoluble forms, naturally migrating through soil and groundwater systems where it is absorbed by plants. In the context of industrial waste management, it functions as a primary, non-heavy metal pollutant closely associated with phosphogypsum. It is a characteristic contaminant found in phosphogypsum stockpiles and their resulting leachate, where it poses significant environmental management challenges. When improperly managed, Total Phosphorus leaches into the surrounding environment, contributing substantially to water and soil pollution while negatively impacting ecosystem health.

As a critical water quality and environmental metric, Total Phosphorus is routinely analyzed for concentration variations and pollution levels across river basins. It is frequently measured in phosphogypsum samples to assess leaching toxicity, and elevated concentrations in downstream water bodies serve as a reliable indicator of phosphogypsum leachate contamination. Regulatory monitoring reveals that Total Phosphorus levels in phosphogypsum leachate often exceed national discharge limits, with particularly pronounced violations documented in Hubei Province. Consequently, effective control and monitoring of Total Phosphorus remain essential for mitigating environmental contamination and ensuring compliance with water quality standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003</data>
