<node id="Yangtze River Basin">
  <data key="d0">Yangtze River Basin</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yangtze River Basin is a major geographic region in China characterized by abundant phosphate rock resources and a highly concentrated industrial sector dedicated to phosphate mining and chemical production. This industrial activity has led to the widespread generation and distribution of phosphogypsum, a byproduct of phosphate fertilizer manufacturing. Consequently, the basin hosts the majority of China’s phosphogypsum production facilities, numerous tailings ponds, and extensive storage reservoirs. The region’s well-developed water system plays a crucial role in facilitating the cross-regional transport of these phosphogypsum resources.

Due to the heavy concentration of industrial phosphorus emissions, the Yangtze River Basin stands as the primary region in China affected by phosphorus pollution, presenting significant environmental challenges tied to industrial operations. This reality has made it a focal point for extensive scientific research aimed at understanding the temporal and spatial variations of total phosphorus, analyzing pollution sources, and developing effective control strategies. Furthermore, the basin is the subject of numerous studies dedicated to phosphorus pollution mitigation and the broader protection of its water ecoenvironment. Geographically, the region is closely linked to Hubei Province, serving as a key market for its cement and gypsum products while remaining central to national efforts in environmental management and resource distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791899168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guizhou Province">
  <data key="d0">Guizhou Province</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Guizhou Province is a mountainous, southwestern Chinese region situated on the Yunnan-Guizhou Plateau within the Yangtze River Basin, characterized by extensive karst landforms that facilitate rapid pollutant migration via surface runoff. As a major phosphate mining and chemical cluster in China, the province concentrates phosphorus emissions from three key phosphorus industries and serves as a significant contributor to national phosphogypsum generation. Phosphogypsum produced in the region, particularly by clustered enterprises around Guiyang City, exhibits consistently low silicon dioxide levels (maximum 5.18%) and has been subject to radioactivity evaluations and chemical sampling. The province is also recognized as one of the primary surveyed regions for phosphorus fertilizer enterprises and is frequently featured in regional phosphogypsum metric tracking.

To manage substantial industrial waste, Guizhou Province has achieved high phosphogypsum comprehensive utilization and recycling rates, reported at 94% with recent years exceeding 100%. The region actively employs phosphogypsum filling technology, primarily for mine backfilling, as well as for manufacturing cement retarders and gypsum building materials. These efforts are supported by pioneering policy frameworks, including the mandatory "production determined by slag disposal" initiative and the 2018 mandate to integrate phosphogypsum-based products into government projects. Despite these advancements, the province faces structural challenges, as its absorption capacity remains constrained relative to annual production volumes, compounded by market saturation and high transportation costs. Environmental assessments have been conducted to address seepage pollution from phosphogypsum storage yards. Through sustained enterprise-driven initiatives and a focus on ecological restoration, Guizhou Province continues to refine its waste management infrastructure and advance its comprehensive utilization framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-002</data>
