<node id="Hubei Province">
  <data key="d0">Hubei Province</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Hubei Province is a central-western region in China situated within the Yangtze River Basin, characterized by a topography of plains and hills and home to major urban centers such as Wuhan. It holds a dominant position in China's phosphate sector, serving as a key hub for the phosphorus chemical industry and a major producer of phosphate rock and phosphorus fertilizers. Consequently, Hubei is the nation's leading producer of phosphogypsum, accounting for 37.8 percent of the national total. To manage this substantial industrial output, the province has implemented targeted policies that have significantly improved phosphogypsum utilization, achieving a recycling rate of 44.35 percent, which ranks second nationally. This recycling industry capitalizes on the developed water transportation networks along the Yangtze River, with companies primarily concentrated in Yichang City. The utilized phosphogypsum is predominantly applied in cement retardants and gypsum-based building materials, though the local market for fundamental products remains saturated.

Despite these operational advancements, Hubei faces significant environmental challenges related to phosphogypsum management. The province hosts numerous active and closed phosphogypsum tailings ponds, which pose severe environmental risks. Notably, a tailings pond leakage in the region has caused severe water contamination. Chemically, phosphogypsum in Hubei exhibits high concentrations of silicon dioxide, phosphorus pentoxide, and fluoride, resulting in elevated pollutant levels in leachate. These environmental impacts are further influenced by the province's specific geological and climatic conditions, which dictate pollutant migration and diffusion patterns.

Hubei Province is also a focal point for environmental and industrial research. It has been surveyed as one of three key regions for phosphorus fertilizer enterprises and serves as a primary site for environmental studies, including composting and sampling experiments related to phosphogypsum management. Chemical analysis of phosphogypsum samples collected in the province has been documented, and the region is featured in metrics tracking phosphogypsum production and utilization. Additionally, research notes from the area reference specific environmental parameters, such as a recorded pH value of 2.71, underscoring the ongoing scientific scrutiny of the region's industrial and ecological landscape.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
