</node>
<node id="Figure 1">
  <data key="d0">Figure 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 1 refers to multiple distinct scientific visualizations originating from different research studies, rather than a single unified entity. Each instance serves as a primary illustrative component within its respective publication, covering diverse analytical and environmental topics.

In the context of phosphogypsum research, one version of Figure 1 functions as a chart tracking the utilization of phosphogypsum in China between 2010 and 2020. Another iteration presents XRD patterns alongside structural refinement data specifically for a phosphogypsum waste sample. A third variation within this thematic cluster displays the activity concentration of Radium-226 in phosphogypsum across various countries.

Within materials science and adsorption studies, a separate Figure 1 provides a visual representation of XRD patterns and FT-IR spectra comparing biochar and hydroxyapatite-loaded biochar. A related depiction illustrates XRD analysis results that contrast s-HAp and BA samples against a standard reference file. Additionally, another instance in this category graphically illustrates the zeta potential of the HAP1/NaCl solution interface as a function of pH.

In the domain of microscopic and thermal analysis, a distinct Figure 1 presents Scanning Electron Microscopy images of samples labeled S1 through S4, along with their corresponding thermal treatments designated S1T through S4T.

Finally, in process engineering contexts, a separate Figure 1 serves as a graphical representation that maps the effects of various operational parameters on a specific extraction process. Collectively, these independent visualizations demonstrate how the label Figure 1 is conventionally applied as a primary reference point across disparate scientific literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 1 is a visual representation showing the general draft, prototype view, and load/unload system principle of the MSS2 reactor.&lt;SEP&gt;A visual representation of the X-ray diffraction pattern used to analyze the mineralogy of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 1 illustrates the overall methodological approach used for the phosphogypsum characterization study.&lt;SEP&gt;A visual compilation showing the XRD pattern, TG-DTG curves, and SEM-EDS results of high-silica phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
