<node id="Industrial Solid Waste">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Solid Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industrial Solid Waste refers to the category of waste that phosphogypsum belongs to, targeted for reduction by national policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial solid waste refers to non-hazardous waste generated from industrial processes, often coupled with phosphogypsum for material preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial solid waste is a broad category of waste materials addressed in disposal and utilization research.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial Solid Waste refers to bulk waste materials, including phosphogypsum, that are targeted for multidirectional resource utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;The traditional classification of PG, which companies are urged to shift away from towards a resource for reuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial solid waste is the traditional classification of phosphogypsum that recycling aims to reframe as a resource.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
