<node id="Acidity">
  <data key="d0">Acidity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical property of phosphogypsum resulting from residual acids, characterized by a low pH value.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidity is a primary environmental concern associated with phosphogypsum due to its chemical nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidity is a chemical parameter present in the Gypsum Stack that leaches into soil and water.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter measured in mol/L of nitric acid that influences the effectiveness of the stripping process.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidity refers to the concentration of acid in the stripping solution, identified as optimal at 0.0001 mol/L for quantitative stripping.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009</data>
