<node id="Acid Rain">
  <data key="d0">Acid Rain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acid Rain is an environmental phenomenon whose formation, harm, and prevention are documented in a 2017 publication.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid rain is an environmental problem originating from nitric oxides produced during fuel combustion processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid Rain is an environmental factor under which the leaching characteristics of calcium and strontium from phosphogypsum are studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid rain is an environmental consequence formed when acidic substances from phosphogypsum volatilize into the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Acid rain is a natural phenomenon causing weathering that limits the direct use of limestone in construction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005</data>
