<node id="Tomato">
  <data key="d0">Tomato</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Tomato is a plant that uptakes trace elements from phosphogypsum-amended soil in SW Spain.&lt;SEP&gt;A vegetable crop studied for cadmium accumulation when grown in soils amended with phosphogypsum, with levels monitored against food safety limits.&lt;SEP&gt;A vegetable crop whose shoots and fruits accumulate cadmium when grown in phosphogypsum-amended soils.&lt;SEP&gt;Tomato is an agricultural crop evaluated for growth and antioxidant enzyme responses to phosphogypsum amendment.&lt;SEP&gt;Tomato is an agricultural crop that absorbs trace elements from phosphogypsum-amended soils, raising food safety concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024</data>
