<node id="Actinobacteria">
  <data key="d0">Actinobacteria</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Actinobacteria is a prominent bacterial phylum that has been extensively characterized across various ecological and experimental studies. In composting environments, it consistently emerges as the most dominant microbial group both before and after the process, initially accounting for approximately 41.82% of the total microbial community. Despite this initial prevalence, its abundance exhibits a significant decreasing trend throughout the fermentation and composting stages. Beyond its numerical dominance, Actinobacteria plays a crucial functional role in these systems by facilitating essential biogeochemical processes, particularly the cycling of carbon, nitrogen, and phosphorus.

Research has also investigated Actinobacteria in marine ecosystems, where both culture-dependent and culture-independent methodologies have been utilized to analyze its diversity in association with marine sponges. In scientific data visualization and microbial profiling, the phylum's abundance is frequently quantified and tracked, often represented in Circos plots with specific color codes and abundance scales. For example, in certain sample cohorts such as Group A2, Actinobacteria is depicted using light blue ribbons and demonstrates massive dominance. Collectively, these findings highlight Actinobacteria as a highly prevalent, functionally important bacterial group whose diversity and abundance are routinely analyzed across terrestrial composting and marine sponge microbiomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Actinobacteria are microorganisms used in the bioleaching process to extract rare-earth elements from bastnaesite-bearing rock.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-055</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423891</data>
