<node id="Vitamin C">
  <data key="d0">Vitamin C</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vitamin C is a nutrient content measured in ryegrass and pakchoi to determine plant nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C is a compound whose concentration is quantified using a calibration plot established through spectrophotometric measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C is a nutrient measured in the plants to evaluate nutritional quality under different fertilizer treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant compound whose content was tested to highlight growth in the fertilization group.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C concentrations in plant leaves are elevated following biofertilizer application.&lt;SEP&gt;A nutritional metric measured in milligrams per kilogram for specific crops.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-021</data>
