  <data key="d2">Vertical lines on data points in the scatter plot indicating variability or standard deviation in measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual indicators on data points representing measurement variability or standard deviation.&lt;SEP&gt;Small graphical indicators on the chart bars representing data variability or uncertainty.&lt;SEP&gt;Vertical lines on the chart indicating the variability or standard deviation of the zeta potential measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Error bars are graphical markers applied to data points to indicate the variability or standard deviation of the stripping efficiency measurements.</data>
