<node id="Acetic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Acetic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetic Acid is a chemical component used to prepare the acetic acid-sodium acetate buffer for vitamin C measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetic acid is a weak organic acid used in solubility measurements of gypsum, showing concentration-dependent effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A reagent used to test the solubility of synthetic gypsum, showing variable solubility based on concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetic acid is a chemical reagent listed in the table for solubility studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetic acid is used to adjust the pH value to 9 during the hydrothermal synthesis procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetic acid is a chemical additive used in combination with ball milling to decrease impurities and increase phosphogypsum purity.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetic Acid is a weak organic acid utilized alongside sodium salts to formulate buffer systems at specific pH levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-002</data>
