<node id="FIPR">
  <data key="d0">FIPR</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">FIPR is an organization that published proceedings for multiple international symposia on phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;FIPR is an organization that publishes proceedings and publications related to phosphogypsum research and symposiums.&lt;SEP&gt;A research organization that published proceedings for international symposia on phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization that published research papers and symposium proceedings on radioelement migration and phosphogypsum management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791183869</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. Environmental Protection Agency">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency is a federal agency dedicated to environmental regulation, research, and public health protection, with a notable focus on radionuclides and industrial by-products. It regulates the agricultural application of phosphogypsum by enforcing maximum concentration limits for Radium-226. The agency has authored extensive technical reports examining the environmental footprint of the phosphate industry, including analyses of radioactivity distribution in phosphate by-products, the impact of phosphate operations on Radium-226 contamination in groundwater, and the behavior of radionuclides within soil and rock media. Furthermore, it has documented methods for mitigating industrial pollution, such as publications detailing techniques to minimize fluoride emissions from gypsum ponds.

In addition to its research and regulatory publications, the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency issues environmental impact statements and establishes emission standards specifically targeting radionuclides. It also provides critical technical resources, including the official user’s guide for the Industrial Source Complex dispersion model. To foster ongoing advancements in environmental remediation, the agency hosts decontamination research conferences. Through these combined regulatory, analytical, and collaborative efforts, the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency maintains a comprehensive approach to managing radioactive materials and industrial environmental hazards.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization referenced in the citation list.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-007</data>
