  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alberta">
  <data key="d0">Alberta</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Alberta is a Canadian province that functions as a notable geographic region for environmental monitoring and industrial research. The province has implemented specific maximum air quality guidelines targeting fluoridation levels to safeguard public and environmental health. Within its boundaries, Alberta hosts active phosphogypsum stacks managed by fertilizer manufacturers, which are constructed on glacial till and contain water-filled ponds.

Extensive scientific investigations have been conducted across the province to evaluate the radioactivity and chemical characteristics of phosphogypsum. Research efforts have specifically analyzed soil interactions with phosphogypsum leachate and explored decommissioning strategies for phosphogypsum tailings. Furthermore, Alberta is referenced in scientific datasets for radioactive isotope measurements, encompassing the analysis of radionuclide activities in phosphogypsum samples, some of which trace their origin to Idaho. Collectively, these studies position Alberta as a critical location for assessing the environmental impact, chemical behavior, and regulatory management of phosphogypsum and related radioactive materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a region where phosphogypsum was studied for its radioactivity and chemical characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791722395</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
