</node>
<node id="Bismuth">
  <data key="d0">Bismuth</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bismuth is a trace element enriched in phosphorites, likely substituting for calcium in apatite due to similar ionic radii.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791186914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vanadium">
  <data key="d0">Vanadium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vanadium is a chemical element that functions as a trace component across various geological and industrial contexts. Geologically, it is notably enriched in the Phosphoria Formation relative to surrounding shale deposits. In industrial phosphogypsum processing, vanadium exhibits a transfer rate ranging from 1 to 100 percent, while the processing material demonstrates an approximate 53 percent drop in removal efficiency.

Analytically and environmentally, vanadium is identified as a trace element in phosphogypsum, with measured concentrations recorded at 4.75 ± 0.63. Its quantification is commonly performed using Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass-Spectrometry, and it can be extracted or determined in geological samples through chemical methods utilizing 8-hydroxyquinoline. Acting as a heavy metal contaminant, vanadium is discharged into the atmosphere and accumulates in soils amended with phosphogypsum, leading to slight pollution. Due to its environmental mobility and presence, it is considered a key factor in assessing terrestrial ecotoxicity potential.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element measured in milligrams per liter during the TCLP test.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element measured in the mixtures, with no specific US-EPA limit listed in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with no specific US-EPA limit listed in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Vanadium is an element detected in variable concentrations within the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Vanadium is a trace element measured in phosphogypsum minerals using LA-ICP-MS.&lt;SEP&gt;Vanadium is a trace element that can be eliminated by simple water washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792039593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U-238 Decay Series">
  <data key="d0">U-238 Decay Series</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The U-238 decay series is a primary source of natural radioactivity in phosphate ores.&lt;SEP&gt;The U-238 decay series is a sequence of radioactive elements found in phosphogypsum that can leach into groundwater.&lt;SEP&gt;The U-238 decay series is a radioactive decay chain that produces radionuclides found in the sediments of the Gulf of Gabes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-017</data>
