<node id="Total Dissolved Solids">
  <data key="d0">Total Dissolved Solids</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total dissolved solids measure the ionic strength of groundwater, which can enhance Ra-226 leachability by competing for adsorption sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Total dissolved solids are present in high levels in the process water.&lt;SEP&gt;Water quality parameter found at elevated levels in groundwater near phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Dissolved Solids are chemical constituents in the Gypsum Stack that migrate into soil and water systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emanation Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Emanation Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The emanation coefficient quantifies the fraction of Radon-222 atoms that escape from solid crystal structures during radioactive decay.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured parameter representing the fraction of Rn-222 atoms escaping the solid phase relative to those formed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaerobic Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Anaerobic Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaerobic conditions promote bacterially mediated redox reactions that indirectly solubilize heavy metals and radionuclides like Ra-226.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lactate">
  <data key="d0">Lactate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactate is a carbon supplement added to laboratory samples that significantly increased dissolved Ra-226 release.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uranium Mine Sludges">
  <data key="d0">Uranium Mine Sludges</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uranium mine sludges contain (Ba, Ra) sulfate compounds from which Ra-226 can be released under anaerobic conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uraninite">
  <data key="d0">Uraninite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uraninite is a crystal mineral whose Radon-222 emanation coefficient has been measured between 0.5% and 25%.&lt;SEP&gt;A crystal mineral in which Rn-222 emanation coefficients have been measured.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cothern">
  <data key="d0">Cothern</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cothern documented that Radon-222 solubility in organic liquids may be several orders of magnitude greater than in water.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher cited alongside UNSCEAR regarding natural background radiation dose estimates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026</data>
