<node id="Sand">
  <data key="d0">Sand</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sand is a natural, granular geological material widely recognized as a traditional and conventional component in construction and industrial applications. In structural engineering, it serves as a primary aggregate when mixed with cement and phosphogypsum to formulate various construction materials, and it is a fundamental ingredient in reinforced concrete. Additionally, sand functions as a key soil component in adobe mixtures, constituting exactly 18.00% of the grain size distribution. Its physical properties, particularly its density relative to phosphogypsum, directly influence the workability of construction mixes.

In the context of brick manufacturing, sand is extensively utilized as a standard baseline material that is frequently compared against phosphogypsum. The industrial valorization of phosphogypsum waste often involves partially substituting or completely replacing sand in brick production processes. While this substitution conserves natural sand reserves, it is noted that replacing sand with phosphogypsum increases the overall environmental footprint of the production cycle.

Beyond its structural roles, sand exhibits specific chemical and environmental interactions. It can act as a source of silica impurities within phosphogypsum, typically originating from process water supplies. Conversely, sand also demonstrates adsorption capabilities, effectively removing small quantities of fluoride from aqueous solutions through anion adsorption mechanisms. Collectively, these characteristics define sand as a versatile material with significant applications in construction, material substitution, and environmental chemistry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791878275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
