  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead is a heavy metal contaminant with strict regulatory limits in U.S., Canadian, EEC, and WHO drinking water standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead is a heavy metal ion that exhibits the lowest adsorption capacity among the tested metals.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element tracked in the inventory data with a measured quantity of 2.13 x 10^-3 kg in high population contexts.</data>
