<node id="Dihydrate Method">
  <data key="d0">Dihydrate Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The dihydrate method is a wet phosphoric acid process resulting in a uranium content of 5-25 μg/g in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific wet phosphoric acid process that results in phosphogypsum with high impurity content and poor quality.&lt;SEP&gt;The dihydrate method is a production process for phosphogypsum that results in a form unsuitable for direct construction use.&lt;SEP&gt;The dihydrate method is a production process for phosphogypsum that results in material unsuitable for raw construction use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791916543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uranous Ion">
  <data key="d0">Uranous Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The uranous ion (U4+) forms complexes with fluoride under reduced conditions and low pH.</data>
