  <data key="d2">Oxidation state represents the charge state of an element, with Thorium typically at +4 and Lead at +2 or +4.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidation State refers to the chemical state of elements like calcium and phosphate ions, determined from spectral peaks.</data>
