<node id="Crystal Morphology">
  <data key="d0">Crystal Morphology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The shape and size distribution of gypsum crystals, influenced by process conditions and raw materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal morphology refers to the shape and structure of phosphogypsum crystals, influenced by production process conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal morphology describes the elongated, rod-like shape and agglomerated arrangement of phosphogypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal Morphology refers to the physical shape and structure of HAp crystals, which varies with surfactant concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal Morphology is a physical characteristic of the synthesized particles, described as uniform rod-like monocrystals.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical shape and structure of the synthesized hydroxyapatite particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
