<node id="Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity Analysis is a technique used to determine how variations in input parameters affect life cycle assessment results and identify sensitive factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A method identifying parameters like lime consumption and cement retarder substitution rates that significantly affect LCA results.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation technique used to assess how variations in assumptions like transportation distance affect results.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique conducted to evaluate the impact of uncertain parameters like Phosphogypsum dose, stack height, and transport distance.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity analysis is a method used to assess the effect of distance assumptions on LCA results.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitivity analysis is a procedural evaluation testing how parameter variations affect environmental scores.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004</data>
