<node id="Carbothermal Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Carbothermal Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A high-temperature chemical reaction process used to convert calcium sulfate into lime and sulfur dioxide.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process during which iron oxide reactions occur in the ingredients system.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-temperature chemical process used to reduce calcium sulfate, influenced by the C/S molar ratio and material mixing.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbothermal reduction is a chemical reaction process involving carbon and metal oxides, illustrated in Figure 13.&lt;SEP&gt;High-temperature chemical process where phosphogypsum is reduced by carbon to produce calcium sulfide and carbon monoxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbothermal reduction is a chemical process that reduces phosphogypsum by carbon at high temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
