<node id="Stockpiling">
  <data key="d0">Stockpiling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stockpiling is a common PG disposal method involving the storage of waste material, evaluated against resource utilization technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is a Plaster of Paris disposal process that shows the highest environmental burden due to land occupation and pollutant release.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is the primary Phosphogypsum disposal method responsible for the majority of environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is a waste management practice widely used for phosphogypsum, which poses environmental and health risks over extended periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is a traditional waste management method for PG that is gradually being replaced by comprehensive utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is a common disposal method for phosphogypsum, particularly in the United States.&lt;SEP&gt;Stockpiling is the current primary method for managing phosphogypsum solid waste, though it consumes land and poses environmental risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-002</data>
