<node id="Thermal Stability">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Stability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal Stability is a critical characteristic determining catalyst lifetime and material suitability for high-temperature applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal stability is a material property that hydroxyapatite enhances for supported gold nanoparticles, preventing degradation at high temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of materials analyzed through heating processes to observe mass loss and decomposition patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792098909</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sintering">
  <data key="d0">Sintering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sintering is a process that converts hydroxyapatite into β-Tricalcium Phosphate, increasing calcium and phosphate ion availability for protein binding.&lt;SEP&gt;Sintering is a catalyst degradation process that hydroxyapatite's phosphate and hydroxyl groups help prevent.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal process indicated by necking among coalesced particles in heat-treated powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Sintering is a high-temperature process used to decompose phosphogypsum and red mud for metal extraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791772783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acidic Centers">
  <data key="d0">Acidic Centers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acidic centers are surface features on hydroxyapatite that facilitate electrophilic attack of adsorbed oxygen, boosting oxidation activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen Activation">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Activation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen activation is a chemical process facilitated by electrons trapped in hydroxyapatite's vacancies, crucial for oxidation reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246377</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ha">
  <data key="d0">Ha</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ha is a researcher who investigated palladium-loaded hydroxyapatite for methane oxidation applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020</data>
