<node id="Stoichiometric Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Stoichiometric Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A pure variant of hydroxyapatite with a chemical formula of Ca10(PO4)6(OH)2 and a Ca/P ratio of 1.67.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoichiometric hydroxyapatite is a variant of hydroxyapatite that is predominantly basic in air but acidic in water.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoichiometric hydroxyapatite is a standard support material compared against calcium-deficient variants for methanol oxidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoichiometric hydroxyapatite is the final, chemically balanced product formed under the optimized experimental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoichiometric hydroxyapatite is a specific chemical form of hydroxyapatite with a Ca/P ratio of 1.67.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-000</data>
