<node id="Environmental Remediation">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Remediation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Remediation is a dedicated ecological application field focused on eliminating and mitigating pollution across air, water, and soil environments. This domain serves as a critical context for developing and implementing strategies that purify contaminated natural resources, with a specific emphasis on treating polluted wastewater and soil. By targeting multiple environmental matrices, the field aims to restore ecological balance and reduce the overall footprint of anthropogenic contaminants.

Within this application area, hydroxyapatite plays a central role due to its versatile chemical properties. The material is extensively utilized for its strong adsorption and sorption capacities, which effectively capture and remove pollutants from various media. Furthermore, synthesized and sustainable forms of hydroxyapatite function as advanced photocatalysts, enabling the light-driven degradation of persistent contaminants. Together, these mechanisms establish Environmental Remediation as a comprehensive framework for evaluating and deploying hydroxyapatite-based treatments to achieve sustainable pollution control and ecological restoration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791967640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Titanium Dioxide (TiO2)">
  <data key="d0">Titanium Dioxide (TiO2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Titanium dioxide is a photocatalyst that presents low adsorption ability and high electron-hole recombination but shows superior activity when combined with hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyapatite (Hap)">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite (Hap)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite is a material combined with titanium dioxide to form composites that enhance photocatalytic activity and reduce toxic intermediate production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silver Phosphate (Ag3PO4)">
  <data key="d0">Silver Phosphate (Ag3PO4)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silver phosphate is a compound coupled with hydroxyapatite to form a composite that improves photodegradation activity tenfold compared to the pure compound.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diclofenac (DCF)">
  <data key="d0">Diclofenac (DCF)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Diclofenac is a pharmaceutical compound effectively photodegraded by multiphasic hydroxyapatite–titanium dioxide material, reducing water toxicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluoxetine">
  <data key="d0">Fluoxetine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluoxetine is a micropollutant degraded with 100% maximum efficiency by the hydroxyapatite–titanium dioxide photocatalyst.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ofloxacin">
  <data key="d0">Ofloxacin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ofloxacin is an antibiotic photodegraded by zinc oxide-hydroxyapatite nanocomposites, which show greater activity than the oxide phase alone.&lt;SEP&gt;Ofloxacin is an antibiotic pollutant whose removal kinetics are evaluated using hydroxyapatite-based composite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ciprofloxacin">
  <data key="d0">Ciprofloxacin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ciprofloxacin is an antibiotic photodegraded by zinc oxide-hydroxyapatite nanocomposites.&lt;SEP&gt;Ciprofloxacin is an antibiotic pollutant whose removal kinetics are evaluated using hydroxyapatite-based composite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
