</node>
<node id="Formaldehyde">
  <data key="d0">Formaldehyde</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Formaldehyde is a carcinogenic volatile organic compound targeted for catalytic oxidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is an organic pollutant efficiently photodegraded over titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is a volatile organic compound whose catalytic oxidation was investigated over organic molecule-modified hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Formaldehyde is a volatile organic compound oxidized by hydroxyapatite-stabilized gold nanoparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;A compound combusted at room temperature using hydroxyapatite foam as a catalyst.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetaldehyde">
  <data key="d0">Acetaldehyde</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaldehyde is the dehydrogenation product of ethanol primarily produced over hydroxyapatite catalysts with high Ca/P Ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaldehyde is a compound decomposed photocatalytically by chromium(III)-doped titanium-hydroxyapatite particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitric Oxide (NO)">
  <data key="d0">Nitric Oxide (NO)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitric oxide is a gas produced during fuel combustion that is harmful to health and the environment, and is removed by titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen Dioxide (NO2)">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Dioxide (NO2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen dioxide is a harmful gas whose production as a toxic intermediate is considerably lessened over titanium dioxide-hydroxyapatite composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methylene Blue">
  <data key="d0">Methylene Blue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Methylene Blue is a dye efficiently degraded by hydroxyapatite acting as a photocatalyst under UV irradiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Methylene Blue is a synthetic dye and organic pollutant whose photodegradation is effectively enhanced by the TiO2/Hap composite.&lt;SEP&gt;Methylene blue is an organic dye whose photodegradation activity increased by 50% when titanium dioxide was combined with hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016</data>
