</node>
<node id="Photocatalytic Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Photocatalytic Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Photocatalytic Degradation is the process of breaking down organic pollutants using light-activated catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is a process used to break down organic pollutants and pharmaceuticals using modified hydroxyapatite materials and composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is an environmental remediation process that breaks down organic pollutants like dyes using composite materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalytic degradation is a process studied for breaking down gaseous formaldehyde using hydroxyapatite-based catalysts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791246505</data>
