<node id="Photocatalysis">
  <data key="d0">Photocatalysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Photocatalysis is a chemical process used for disinfecting bacteria-contaminated waters and degrading pollutants using light-activated catalysts.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalysis is a chemical process where hydroxyapatite composites degrade pollutants and oxidize gases under light.&lt;SEP&gt;A degradation and removal process enhanced by titania/hydroxyapatite composites for pollutants like pentachlorophenol and nitrogen monoxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalysis is a process evaluated in hydroxyapatite research involving oxygen vacancies and optical band gaps.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-016</data>
