<node id="Fluoride Ions">
  <data key="d0">Fluoride Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluoride Ions are ions incorporated into the apatite lattice to modify crystal properties and stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions are anions present in soluble form that combine with alkaline elements or ammonium.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions are contaminants eliminated from drinking water using hydroxyapatite as an adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions are chemical contaminants that hydroxyapatite can adsorb from aqueous environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride Ions are contaminants removed from water using hydroxyapatite as an adsorbent.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions are undesirable contaminants adsorbed in phosphogypsum that are transferred to the solution during treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride ions are contaminants in phosphogypsum that are transferred to the solution during treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
