  <data key="d2">Biological waste material, including fish and chicken bones, identified as a valuable source for obtaining hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal bones are biological waste sources from which hydroxyapatite can be successfully obtained.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal bones serve as a natural reference containing hydroxyapatite, used to compare synthetic equivalents.</data>
