<node id="Photocatalyst">
  <data key="d0">Photocatalyst</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Photocatalyst is a role hydroxyapatite can fulfill in environmental remediation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Photocatalyst is a specific application role where hydroxyapatite facilitates chemical reactions under light exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;A material designed to accelerate chemical reactions using light, with heterostructured 1D/2D designs optimized for energy applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791967780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Phase Support">
  <data key="d0">Active Phase Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active phase support is a specific application role where hydroxyapatite serves as a substrate for catalytic active components.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
