<node id="Carbonate Groups">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonate groups are surface components that enrich hydroxyapatite when copper acetate is used, negatively impacting SCR activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonate groups are chemical functional groups identified by absorption dips around 1600 cm⁻¹ representing asymmetric stretching.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical groups detected via FT-IR spectroscopy, suggesting the presence of c-HAp impurities in synthetic hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005</data>
