<node id="Surface Complexation">
  <data key="d0">Surface Complexation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface complexation is a less commonly mentioned mechanism for metal adsorption by hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface complexation is the chemical mechanism driving formic acid adsorption onto hydroxyapatite via calcium ion interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The dominant adsorption mechanism for cadmium ions, involving binding to surface functional groups without new crystal formation.&lt;SEP&gt;The dominant adsorption mechanism of 20HPA-HAP for cadmium ions, occurring without forming new crystalline phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface Complexation is a dominant adsorption mechanism involving the formation of chemical bonds between the adsorbent and metal ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-015</data>
