<node id="Solid Diffusion">
  <data key="d0">Solid Diffusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Solid diffusion is a less commonly mentioned mechanism for metal adsorption by hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791247568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca/P Molar Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Ca/P Molar Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ca/P molar ratio is a compositional parameter of hydroxyapatite that influences its surface properties and metal removal efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Ca/P molar ratio is an experimental parameter maintained at 1.67:1 across all HAP preparation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P molar ratio is a fixed compositional parameter set to 1:1 for all HAP samples prepared in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Ca/P Molar Ratio indicates the stoichiometric proportion of calcium to phosphorus in the synthesized samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ca/P molar ratio is a quantitative metric used to characterize the high nonstoichiometry and calcium deficiency of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical parameter indicating calcium to phosphorus proportion, controlled via precursor modification to 1.52 ± 0.01.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
