<node id="Bone Tissue Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Bone Tissue Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone tissue engineering is a biomedical field that utilizes hydroxyapatite scaffolds as substitutes for bone regeneration.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone tissue engineering is a field of application where modified apatite materials are utilized for regenerative purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone tissue engineering is a medical application area where hydroxyapatite crystals are widely used as bioceramic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone tissue engineering utilizes nanomaterials like upconversion hydroxyapatite for regenerative medical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A biomedical field focused on developing biological substitutes to restore or improve tissue function, utilizing materials like hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Tissue Engineering is a biomedical field focused on developing biological substitutes to restore or improve bone function.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone Tissue Engineering is a medical field focused on repairing bone defects using biomaterials and scaffolds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008</data>
