<node id="Chloride Ions">
  <data key="d0">Chloride Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chloride ions are chemical species that replace hydroxide ions in the hydroxyapatite lattice during catalytic reactions, forming chloroapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Chloride ions are a chemical parameter measured on a dry basis, with specified maximum percentage limits for different purity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Chloride ions represent the chemical species whose weight percentage is calculated in the first formula.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76e07d75a9f5124d07b9dafa2dacfba7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-025</data>
