<node id="CTAB">
  <data key="d0">CTAB</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CTAB, chemically identified as hexadecyltrimethylammonium bromide, is a cationic surfactant and chemical compound extensively utilized as a structural modifier, crystallization controller, and sacrificial template in advanced material synthesis. In aqueous systems, CTAB ionizes to form tetrahedral cations and self-assembles into positively charged micelle assemblies above its critical micelle concentration, though it can also form smaller spherical micelles under specific conditions. Its primary application centers on the synthesis of hydroxyapatite nanoparticles and microcrystals, where it regulates nucleation and crystal growth by directing oriented development along the c-axis through specific adsorption onto crystal lattice planes. When combined with citrate, CTAB effectively controls particle morphology, promoting the formation of one-dimensional rod-like nanorods and enhancing overall particle size uniformity.

Beyond morphological control, CTAB significantly alters the physicochemical characteristics of synthesized hydroxyapatite. Its incorporation during hydrothermal and aqueous synthesis processes increases material crystallinity, modulates the calcium-to-phosphorus ratio, and induces one- and two-dimensional structural modifications. These structural enhancements collectively improve light absorption, facilitate charge separation, increase carrier density, and substantially boost photocatalytic performance. In experimental protocols, CTAB is typically dissolved in solution B and maintained at a constant mass while its ratio with Ct is systematically varied to optimize synthesis conditions. Functioning as a sacrificial template, CTAB is subsequently washed away during post-synthesis processing and confirmed absent in the final product. Additionally, CTAB is employed in the synthesis of Surf powder, where its complete evaporation during calcination inhibits excessive particle growth and generates fine porosity within the final material. Collectively, these multifaceted properties establish CTAB as a highly versatile and indispensable agent across multiple specialized nanoparticle fabrication and manufacturing processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
