<node id="FT-IR">
  <data key="d0">FT-IR</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">FT-IR is an analytical technique used to obtain patterns of samples before and after calcining.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy used to identify functional groups and confirm HAP loading on BC.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic technique used to identify chemical vibration bands and functional groups in samples.&lt;SEP&gt;FT-IR is an analytical technique used for the characterization of the solid product.&lt;SEP&gt;FT-IR is a method used to characterize chemical groups and bonds in the hydration products of PGEF.&lt;SEP&gt;Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy is utilized to identify functional groups and track phase evolution in the samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002</data>
