<node id="Dipole Field">
  <data key="d0">Dipole Field</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dipole Field is a field that weakens when citrate concentration decreases, affecting the assembly mode of building blocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XRD Analysis">
  <data key="d0">XRD Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XRD Analysis is a comprehensive analytical, characterization, and crystallographic technique primarily utilized to examine crystalline structures and determine the phase composition of various materials. By identifying diffraction peaks, this method enables the precise determination of crystalline and mineral phases, as well as the assessment of the degree of crystallinity within prepared samples. The technique is also instrumental in quantifying specific structural parameters, including lattice parameters, crystallite sizes, and peak widths.

In practical applications, XRD Analysis is widely employed across diverse fields to characterize complex materials. It is frequently used to identify diffraction peaks of both hydrated and unhydrated compounds in PG-based mortar and concrete samples. Furthermore, the method serves as a powerful tool for examining crystalline phase changes, identifying dissolution-precipitation mechanisms, and comparing synthetic hydroxyapatite with natural biological samples. Specific applications include characterizing synthetic hydroxyapatite to indicate low crystalline structures and detect the presence of specific phases such as b-TCP and quartz. Overall, XRD Analysis provides critical insights into the structural and compositional properties of solid materials through systematic diffraction pattern evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;A mineralogical characterization technique used to identify the crystalline phases in raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD analysis is an analytical technique used to confirm the presence of pure-phase Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD Analysis is a technique employed to study the phase and crystalline structure of the prepared samples.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD Analysis is a characterization method used to determine the crystal structure and phase composition of the synthesized material.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical technique used to confirm particle sizes and crystallinity of the samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791964406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FT-IR Analysis">
  <data key="d0">FT-IR Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">FT-IR analysis is a spectroscopic method used to identify chemical groups such as phosphate and carbonate in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic method used to identify functional groups and detect absorbed water within the sample structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Spectroscopic method used to verify the presence of characteristic functional groups in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A spectroscopic technique used to identify functional groups in synthetic gypsum and HAp samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEM Imaging">
  <data key="d0">SEM Imaging</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM imaging is a microscopic technique used to visualize the morphology of the products, revealing microspheres and microflakes.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM imaging is used to observe and document the morphology of as-prepared HAP samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Microscopy technique used to visualize the material, where darker areas indicate lower elevations or voids.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopic imaging technique for which the sample is mounted using conductive materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Process">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hydrothermal Process is a synthesis technique and experimental condition that utilizes elevated temperature and pressure, typically within aqueous solutions, to produce hydroxyapatite and its various structural forms. This method is frequently employed to synthesize hydroxyapatite particles, nanocrystals, microspheres, and mesoporous rod-shaped structures, with operating temperatures commonly ranging between 120 and 180 °C. By precisely controlling key parameters such as temperature, pressure, reagent concentrations, and pH, the process enables the targeted fabrication of nanocrystalline hydroxyapatite with tailored size and morphology.

Beyond basic synthesis, the application of heat and pressure serves multiple functional roles within this technique. It significantly enhances the stability and crystallinity of the resulting material while facilitating the cleavage of Ca-NTA bonds to release calcium ions. Additionally, the controlled environment allows surfactants to effectively influence the final morphological characteristics of the product. Overall, the Hydrothermal Process provides a versatile and highly regulated method for producing hydroxyapatite-based materials with optimized physicochemical properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microspheres">
  <data key="d0">Microspheres</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microspheres are spherical structures approximately 50 μm in size composed of microflakes perpendicular to the surface.&lt;SEP&gt;Microspheres are the synthesized spherical particles that transition from solid ACP to core-shell HA structures based on hydrothermal duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985846</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetonedicarboxylate Complex">
  <data key="d0">Acetonedicarboxylate Complex</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetonedicarboxylate complex is a decomposition product of citrate under high temperature that participates in HAp crystallization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PO4 3- Groups">
  <data key="d0">PO4 3- Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">PO4 3- groups are phosphate ions identified in all samples through FT-IR and XRD analysis, exhibiting characteristic stretching and bending modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate functional groups identified through strong stretching vibration bands in the FT-IR spectrum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791559146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nucleation">
  <data key="d0">Nucleation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nucleation is a crystallization process suppressed by citrate during the hydrothermal synthesis of HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleation is the initial process in crystal formation that is regulated by the CTAB template.&lt;SEP&gt;A process regulated by CTAB during the synthesis of hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791664401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetone">
  <data key="d0">Acetone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetone is a decomposition product of citrate under high temperature and pressure during the hydrothermal process.&lt;SEP&gt;A solvent used for ultrasonic cleaning of the FTO substrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasonic Dispersing Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasonic Dispersing Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasonic dispersing treatment is a process that causes the microsphere structure to collapse into dispersive flask-like particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultrasonic dispersing treatment is applied to collapse the microsphere structure into dispersive flake-like particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CC">
  <data key="d0">CC</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CC (calcium citrate) acts as a precursor that decomposes to regulate the nucleation, growth, and final structure of HAp crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
