<node id="Nanorod clusters">
  <data key="d0">Nanorod clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanorod clusters are the final HAp product morphology when stirring time reaches 120 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electrostatic repulsion">
  <data key="d0">Electrostatic repulsion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrostatic repulsion maintains the dispersive status of CC nanoparticles during the initial formation stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nucleation sites">
  <data key="d0">Nucleation sites</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nucleation sites are locations provided by CC particles that initiate the crystallization of HAp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallization process">
  <data key="d0">Crystallization process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The crystallization process is the mechanism by which HAp forms and grows, influenced by CC decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface energy">
  <data key="d0">Surface energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface energy drives the orderly assembly and parallel alignment of particles along their long axis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decomposition rate">
  <data key="d0">Decomposition rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The decomposition rate of CC controls the release of calcium ions and influences cavity structure formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791259997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lattice planes">
  <data key="d0">Lattice planes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lattice planes are crystal surfaces where CTAB specifically adsorbs to modify HAp growth direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-004</data>
