</node>
<node id="Trisodium Citrate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Trisodium Citrate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Trisodium citrate dihydrate is a chemical reagent dissolved to form the precursor solution for hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Trisodium citrate dihydrate is a chemical used alongside CTAB to synthesize 3D hierarchical superstructures of Hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791967536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Nitrate Tetrahydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Nitrate Tetrahydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium nitrate tetrahydrate is a chemical reagent and primary calcium precursor utilized across various synthesis and preparation methodologies. Functioning as a key calcium source, it is typically dissolved in distilled water to generate a calcium salt solution that supplies essential calcium ions for subsequent reactions. In specific protocols, the compound may be dehydrated through heating to prepare a synthetic calcium nitrate solution tailored for extraction trials.

This versatile starting material plays a central role in multiple advanced synthesis routes, including the NoSurf synthesis method, precipitation techniques, microwave-assisted synthesis, and hydrothermal preparation processes. Notably, it is extensively employed as a fundamental reactant in the production of hydroxyapatite, serving both in solution-based synthesis and in the fabrication of hydroxyapatite powder. Overall, calcium nitrate tetrahydrate acts as a critical chemical starting material that initiates and facilitates diverse material synthesis and extraction procedures by delivering controlled calcium ion concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammonium Phosphate">
  <data key="d0">Ammonium Phosphate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammonium phosphate is a chemical reagent dissolved to provide phosphate ions for hydroxyapatite synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Phosphate is a class of phosphate fertilizer products derived from phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium Phosphate is a chemical compound dissolved in water to react with calcium chloride for nanocomposite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ammonium phosphate is a chemical precursor dissolved to initiate the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-001</data>
