<node id="Panel C">
  <data key="d0">Panel C</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Panel c is a scanning electron microscopy micrograph revealing a chaotic network of long, thin needle-like crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel C is an electron micrograph showing a network of rod-like structures with a 4 µm scale bar.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopy panel revealing thin, translucent, sheet-like or flake-like structures that are overlapping and scattered.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel C is the label assigned to the Scanning Electron Microscope micrograph within the larger scientific figure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791331657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Panel D">
  <data key="d0">Panel D</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Panel d is a scanning electron microscopy micrograph showing organized starburst clusters of sharp needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel D is a high-magnification electron micrograph focusing on a single rod-like structure with a 0.6 µm scale bar.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopy panel showing a dense accumulation of thin, plate-like crystals with sharp edges stacked to form a textured surface.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel D shows the interface with red cracks penetrating the grey matrix and present ion clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791721285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Panel E">
  <data key="d0">Panel E</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Panel e is a scanning electron microscopy micrograph introducing a plate-like morphology of flat stacked sheets.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel E is an electron micrograph depicting a porous, sponge-like network with a 4 µm scale bar.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel E displays a phase diagram showing ion distribution changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791721285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Panel F">
  <data key="d0">Panel F</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Panel f is a scanning electron microscopy micrograph depicting the final morphological condition observed in the composite figure.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel F is a high-magnification electron micrograph revealing star-burst clusters forming the porous network with a 0.6 µm scale bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-006</data>
