<node id="Adsorbed Water">
  <data key="d0">Adsorbed Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorbed water is a chemical component identified by a broad absorption dip around 3400 cm⁻¹ in the spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbed water is linked to broad bands appearing at 3450 and 1636 cm^-1 in the IR spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbed water is water molecules present on the sample surface, identified by a specific bending mode peak.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbed Water is identified by a broad infrared absorption band in the 3100–3500 cm⁻¹ range.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbed Water is identified by a broad FTIR absorption band at 3100–3500 cm⁻¹ in the synthesized samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Adsorbed water is present in the hydroxyapatite sample, indicated by a broad FTIR band between 3100 and 3500 cm^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791664401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wavenumber">
  <data key="d0">Wavenumber</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Wavenumber is a spectral measurement parameter expressed in inverse centimeters (cm⁻¹) that functions as the standard horizontal axis metric for infrared (IR) and Fourier-transform infrared (FTIR) spectroscopic graphs. In these spectral analyses, the wavenumber is plotted along the x-axis to represent spectral frequency. The standard operational range typically spans from 500 to 4000 cm⁻¹, although certain graphical conventions display the axis in a descending format from 4000 to 500 cm⁻¹.

Within molecular spectroscopy, the wavenumber serves as a critical analytical tool for identifying specific molecular vibrations and mapping the precise locations of infrared absorption bands or peaks. By correlating these measured values with distinct vibrational modes, it enables the accurate characterization of chemical compounds and functional groups. Consequently, the consistent application of the cm⁻¹ unit across spectral data ensures standardized interpretation and remains an indispensable parameter in analytical chemistry and molecular structure determination.&lt;SEP&gt;Wavenumber is the unit and axis used to plot FTIR spectral peaks and vibrational modes.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement plotted on the horizontal axis of the infrared transmittance spectrum, ranging from 4000 to 500 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured data variable representing the frequency of infrared light used in spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Absorption Bands">
  <data key="d0">Absorption Bands</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Absorption bands are the characteristic dips in the spectral curves corresponding to specific chemical vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Absorption bands in the 1000–1100 cm⁻¹ range are characteristic spectral features indicating the presence of sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791486417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmittance">
  <data key="d0">Transmittance</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmittance is a potential measurement scale for the y-axis intensity in the spectroscopy plot.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmittance is a measured data parameter plotted on the y-axis of FTIR spectra to indicate infrared light absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmittance serves as the vertical axis metric for the FTIR spectrum, representing the amount of infrared light passing through the sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of signal intensity in infrared spectroscopy, represented on the vertical axis of the spectrum graph.&lt;SEP&gt;The vertical axis metric indicating the amount of light passing through the sample, measured in arbitrary units.&lt;SEP&gt;A relative measurement plotted on the vertical axis of the infrared transmittance spectrum graph.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured data variable representing the amount of infrared light passing through a sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
