  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PO4^3- Group">
  <data key="d0">PO4^3- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The PO4^3- group is responsible for strong FT-IR bands between 920-1200 cm⁻¹ in HAP-BC.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P-O Bond">
  <data key="d0">P-O Bond</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The P-O bond bending vibration is identified by a peak at 933 cm⁻¹ in the HAP-BC spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical bond within the phosphate group analyzed via FTIR spectroscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;P-O Bond is the chemical bond within the phosphate group responsible for a specific FTIR absorption peak.&lt;SEP&gt;The P-O bond represents the chemical linkage in phosphate groups and P2O5, identified at specific binding energies in the P 2p spectra.&lt;SEP&gt;The P-O bond is a chemical component within HAp that exhibits notably diminished spectral intensity.&lt;SEP&gt;The P-O bond represents the stretching and bending vibrations characteristic of phosphate groups in the synthesized materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CO3^2- Group">
  <data key="d0">CO3^2- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The CO3^2- group is identified by a peak at 1467 cm⁻¹ in the HAP-BC spectrum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="COO Group">
  <data key="d0">COO Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The COO group is identified alongside CO3^2- at 1467 cm⁻¹ in the HAP-BC spectrum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791288310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methylene Group">
  <data key="d0">Methylene Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The methylene group (C-H) is identified by additional peaks at 2996 and 2947 cm⁻¹ in HAP-BC.</data>
