  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ce is a symbol representing the equilibrium concentration of a pollutant remaining after adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerium, a rare earth element whose extraction efficiency was measured under varying concentrations and temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ce is a rare earth element ion whose stripping efficiency from loaded ionic liquid is investigated under varying experimental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A trace element measured in parts per million in the provided analytical data.&lt;SEP&gt;Ce is a chemical element listed in a tabular dataset with associated numerical measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerium is a chemical element represented by the symbol Ce.</data>
