<node id="Electrostatic Repulsion">
  <data key="d0">Electrostatic Repulsion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrostatic Repulsion is a force that hinders heavy metal adsorption when the biochar surface carries a positive charge.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrostatic repulsion is a phenomenon affecting adsorption at lower pH levels due to positively charged adsorbent surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrostatic repulsion is a force that reduces the adsorption process when adsorbents are positively charged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008</data>
