<node id="IAEA">
  <data key="d0">IAEA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The organization providing standard reference materials for calibration.&lt;SEP&gt;IAEA provides reference data on the worldwide mean Ra-226 activity in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;The IAEA provides research indicating that radionuclides migrate to calcium carbonate during PG transformation, lowering radioactivity in the fertilizer product.&lt;SEP&gt;The IAEA is an international organization that published guidelines on radiation protection and the management of NORM residues.&lt;SEP&gt;The IAEA published reports on radiation protection and the management of NORM residues in the phosphate industry.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Atomic Energy Agency, cited for data on Phosphogypsum consumption rates in road base applications.</data>
