<node id="PGA">
  <data key="d0">PGA</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">PGA is a specific type of phosphogypsum sample derived from a 1/1 (w/w) blend of Syrian and Tunisian phosphorites. In analytical contexts, this phosphogypsum variant is extensively characterized for its physical and isotopic properties. It is routinely evaluated for particle size distribution and grain size correlations, and it constitutes 30.1% of the F01 fraction in compositional assessments. Additionally, PGA demonstrates the highest isotope deviation ranges among comparable materials and is specifically examined for isotopic activity ratios.

In graphical data presentations, such as grouped bar charts analyzing phosphogypsum fractions, PGA is consistently represented by dark grey bars. Collectively, these attributes establish PGA as a distinct phosphogypsum reference material defined by its precise geographic origin, measurable fraction contribution, and notable granulometric and isotopic characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791312641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gypsum Phase">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The gypsum phase is a calcium sulfate crystal structure that forms during phosphogypsum production and serves as a substrate for radionuclide adsorption.&lt;SEP&gt;The dominant mineral phase in phosphogypsum, primarily composed of calcium oxide and sulfur trioxide.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulfate Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulfate crystals are the structural components of phosphogypsum where foreign ions incorporate during growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulfate Crystals are hydration products in PGCM that improve macroscopic mechanical properties and water resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
