<node id="Plaster">
  <data key="d0">Plaster</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Plaster is a construction and finishing material primarily manufactured using phosphogypsum (PG) as a direct substitute for natural gypsum. The production process typically involves purifying, treating, or recovering phosphogypsum waste, which is subsequently processed into hemihydrate to create the final building compound. By repurposing this industrial byproduct, the material maintains the essential chemical and structural properties required for standard construction applications while offering a sustainable alternative to traditional gypsum extraction.

In practical applications, plaster functions as a protective wall covering designed to shield constructed surfaces from water contact and environmental moisture. Beyond its conventional uses, specialized formulations of the material are created by blending phosphogypsum with soil, resulting in a distinct finishing compound specifically utilized to coat adobe walls. Through these varied manufacturing methods and functional applications, plaster effectively transforms treated phosphogypsum into a durable, water-resistant building solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plaster is a product in which gypsum serves as the main constituent.&lt;SEP&gt;Plaster is a construction material that utilizes recycled phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
