<node id="Activity Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Activity Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Activity ratio refers to the constant assumed ratio between Uranium-238 and Uranium-235 activities (21.73) used for estimation.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity ratio indicates the proportion of activity between different radionuclides and serves as an indicator of partitioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity ratio is a quantitative measure comparing the radioactivity of two isotopic pairs across different sample fractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity Ratio is a quantitative metric measuring the relative concentration of specific isotopes, such as Thorium-228 to Radium-228.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791313927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emission Lines">
  <data key="d0">Emission Lines</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Emission lines refer to specific gamma ray energies used to identify and quantify radionuclides in gamma spectrometry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791313927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Processing">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical processing is the industrial procedure that transforms phosphorite ore into phosphogypsum and phosphoric acid, causing radionuclide fractionation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical Processing is the industrial procedure applied to phosphorite ore that influences the retention and distribution of lead and radium isotopes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-016</data>
