<node id="Figure 3">
  <data key="d0">Figure 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 3 is a generic figure label utilized across multiple distinct scientific publications and research contexts, with its specific content and analytical purpose varying significantly depending on the study. In investigations focused on phosphogypsum and gypsum, Figure 3 functions as a comparative visualization for activity ratio values across analyzed samples, specifically mapping isotopic pairs across various phosphogypsum fractions. Within this same domain, it diagrams the primary forms of trace element presence in phosphogypsum, outlines the methodological procedures for solubility studies, and visually represents the unconfined compressive strength of both raw and treated phosphogypsum samples.

In the context of material synthesis, characterization, and hydroxyapatite analysis, Figure 3 presents a variety of analytical data. It displays Scanning Electron Microscopy images of samples fabricated with varying NTA:Ca molar ratios and illustrates X-ray diffraction patterns of hydrothermally synthesized materials across different temperatures. For synthetic hydroxyapatite specifically, it provides Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy results detailing functional groups and the specific spectrum of the sample. Additionally, it plots the zeta potential of the hydroxyapatite solution interface as a function of pH, compares X-ray diffraction patterns between synthetic hydroxyapatite and natural bone and tooth samples, including animal bones, tooth enamel, and HAp nanopowders, and tracks X-ray diffraction patterns of as-prepared hydroxyapatite over varying reaction times.

In broader methodological contexts, Figure 3 also serves as a visual flowchart. It outlines the general experimental procedures of a given study and, in specific metallurgical research, details the experimental workflow for a carbothermal reduction smelting study. Across all applications, Figure 3 adapts to serve as a critical data visualization or procedural guide tailored to the specific scientific domain of its respective publication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
