<node id="Wet Precipitation Method">
  <data key="d0">Wet Precipitation Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet precipitation method is a chemical synthesis route used to prepare hydroxyapatite powders under controlled processing parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;A complex synthesis process where achieving pure HA depends on the combined effect of multiple reaction conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791330170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B-TCP">
  <data key="d0">B-TCP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">B-TCP is a calcium phosphate phase whose evolution is suppressed by the addition of surfactant during hydroxyapatite synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791330579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Light Scattering">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Light Scattering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic light scattering is a characterization technique used to measure particle size distribution in hydroxyapatite suspensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic light scattering is a technique used to measure particle size distribution and detect agglomeration in the synthesized powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791330579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen Adsorption">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Adsorption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen adsorption is a characterization technique used to analyze the pore size and surface area of hydroxyapatite powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791330579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
