<node id="Agglomerates">
  <data key="d0">Agglomerates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agglomerates are clustered particle formations observed in the NoSurf powder morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;Agglomerates are clumped particles visible in the SEM micrograph, representing a coarser secondary population.&lt;SEP&gt;Agglomerates are formed by bonded hydration products that fill pores and enhance interfacial adhesion in PGCM.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
