<node id="Crystallite Size">
  <data key="d0">Crystallite Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallite Size is a physical, microstructural, and structural parameter that represents the average dimension of individual crystalline domains or crystals within polycrystalline materials, nanoparticles, and synthesized powders. Typically expressed in nanometers, it is a fundamental property that directly contributes to diffraction peak broadening and correlates directly with the overall degree of crystallinity. The parameter is primarily estimated using X-ray diffraction (XRD) models and equations, most notably the Scherrer equation (also referred to as the Sahadat-Scherrer Model). Calculation methodologies involve analyzing XRD peak intercepts, accounting for lattice contraction or expansion, and utilizing the slope of plotted graphs to derive the mean particle size.

In the specific context of hydroxyapatite (HAp) powders and nanoparticles, Crystallite Size is frequently measured as a structural property along the c-axis or c direction. For instance, it has been recorded at 33.6 nm for the (002) crystallographic plane. The size exhibits distinct behavioral trends: it increases with heat treatment and expands along the c-axis when surfactants, particularly Brij-93, are incorporated during the synthesis process. Overall, Crystallite Size serves as a critical microstructural metric for characterizing the nanoscale architecture and crystalline quality of advanced materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property representing the dimensions of crystalline domains within the nanopowder, measured in nanometers.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite Size is a measured physical property indicating the dimensions of individual crystals in the nanopowder.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallite Size is a physical property of the prepared samples estimated using the Scherrer equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791965185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallinity Degree">
  <data key="d0">Crystallinity Degree</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallinity Degree is a measured structural property of hydroxyapatite powders, expressed as a percentage.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of structural order in the powders that improves with heat treatment and correlates with crystallite size.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallinity degree is a structural parameter of hydroxyapatite powders influenced by heat treatment and surfactant use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-009</data>
