  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bragg Angle is a geometric parameter representing the diffraction angle used in crystallite size calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;The diffraction angle corresponding to the position of a specific analyzed peak, used in the cosine term of the formula.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bragg Angle is a parameter representing the angle of the highest intensity diffracted peak used in the Scherrer equation.</data>
