  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical process studied by calculating crystallite size from diffraction peak widths.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal growth is a process during hydrothermal synthesis whose orientation is influenced by hydrocarbon chains.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystal Growth refers to the formation and expansion of hydroxyapatite crystals, often controlled by amino acids.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a6c42f76034cfa4338bd156b7179fc5-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008</data>
