<node id="Civil Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Civil Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Civil engineering is the discipline that explores the application and future growth prospects of phosphogypsum in construction.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil engineering is the field where PG has various potential applications, including in mass concrete and retaining walls.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil engineering is the discipline that can benefit from interdisciplinary growth in Phosphogypsum-based materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil engineering is the construction field where phosphogypsum-based materials are developed and applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil engineering is a field exploring the resource utilization and development of phosphogypsum-based construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil engineering is a broad field where phosphogypsum-based materials are utilized for resource development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-016</data>
