  <data key="d2">Air curing is a treatment method applied to cement samples during strength testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Air curing is a curing condition under which mortar compressive strength decreases between 10 and 53% with PG addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Air curing is a long-term curing method applied to samples to determine compressive strength at specified ages.</data>
