<node id="Slag">
  <data key="d0">Slag</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Slag is a versatile byproduct material generated during industrial processes, particularly carbothermal reduction smelting of PGI and PGI-1.4, as well as general chemical processing and smelting operations. Initially produced as a molten material, it solidifies upon cooling and is routinely analyzed for its phase composition, microstructure, chemical distribution, pH, and viscosity. Chemically, slag typically contains sulfides and sulfates, with its sulfur content fluctuating according to the C/S molar ratio, and it may retain sulfide residues.

In construction and cementitious engineering, slag functions as a supplementary cementitious material and mineral additive. It is frequently blended with binders such as ordinary Portland cement, limestone, gypsum, phosphogypsum, and fly ash to enhance the mechanical properties, compressive strength, and long-term durability of concrete, mortar, and specialized cementitious systems. Notably, when combined with phosphogypsum and fly ash, slag optimizes geopolymer cement formulations, refines material microstructures, and supports the development of cemented phosphogypsum filling materials. Beyond structural applications, slag plays a critical role in chemical processing and sustainable resource management. It serves as a concentration medium for impurities during treatments like phosphogypsum carbonation with ammonium acetate and is integrated into hybrid systems that maximize waste valorization. By transforming industrial byproducts into high-performance construction components or further processing them into high-value materials, slag consistently operates as a sustainable, performance-enhancing agent that advances both structural integrity and resource efficiency in modern material synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006</data>
