<node id="Microcracks">
  <data key="d0">Microcracks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microcracks are structural defects caused by Mg(OH) expansion that diminish compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Microcracks are surface fissures that appear on PGCM samples under 25 cycles, correlating with dissolution rate fluctuations.&lt;SEP&gt;Microcracks are small fractures in PGCM that widen under stress and eventually connect into larger cracks.</data>
