  <data key="d0">Drying Shrinkage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical property measured at 28 days for hemihydrate phosphogypsum composite containing recycled waste glass.&lt;SEP&gt;A dimensional stability property that increases substantially when phosphogypsum is added to mortar or concrete, restricting application scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Drying shrinkage is a physical property of adobe that decreases as the phosphogypsum content increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Drying shrinkage evaluates dimensional changes in adobe samples during air and oven drying periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Drying shrinkage is a physical property measured to assess dimensional stability during the drying process of adobe samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The reduction in volume of adobe samples during drying, which is reduced by the addition of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002</data>
