<node id="226Ra">
  <data key="d0">226Ra</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">226Ra is a radioactive contaminant that can be leached from phosphogypsum using specific chemical and water combinations.&lt;SEP&gt;226Ra is a radioactive isotope whose dissolution characteristics from phosphogypsum were analyzed in environmental studies.&lt;SEP&gt;226Ra is a radioactive impurity successfully removed from PG using organic solvent leaching methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is a radioactive isotope measured in phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791771443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="75% Clean Recovery Rate">
  <data key="d0">75% Clean Recovery Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 75% clean recovery rate is the estimated gypsum recovery efficiency achieved through the crystalline lattice formation approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010</data>
