</node>
<node id="Semi-hydrated Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Semi-hydrated Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Semi-hydrated Gypsum is a chemical compound formed during the Non-immersing Method, possessing a permeable and disordered microstructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dihydrate Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Dihydrate Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Dihydrate Gypsum is a chemical compound formed when semi-hydrated gypsum undergoes complete hydration and recrystallization.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydrate Gypsum is a gypsum compound within PGCM whose dissolution is accelerated during moisture loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydrate gypsum is a component in PGCM that dissolves during the drying stage, accelerating material degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A mineral phase whose dissolution rate increases with curing age and whose crystals form on complexes during hydration.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydrate gypsum is the crystalline product formed from hemihydrated gypsum that enhances the mechanical properties of PGEF.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydrate Gypsum is the final crystalline product formed from the hydration of hemihydrate gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydrate gypsum is a calcium sulfate phase identified in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydration-Recrystallization Technique">
  <data key="d0">Hydration-Recrystallization Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration-Recrystallization Technique is an innovative manufacturing process that transforms semi-hydrated gypsum into dihydrate gypsum, enhancing brick properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two-Step Hydration Method">
  <data key="d0">Two-Step Hydration Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Two-Step Hydration Method is a manufacturing process for finished unfired PG bricks that results in a uniform, compact microstructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Green Bricks">
  <data key="d0">Green Bricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Green Bricks are unfired brick specimens containing original gypsum, characterized by an uneven and porous microstructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unfired Bricks">
  <data key="d0">Unfired Bricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Unfired Bricks are bricks manufactured without firing, whose crystalline phase and strength depend on the hydration method used.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire-dried Brick">
  <data key="d0">Fire-dried Brick</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire-dried Brick is a brick subjected to hot temperatures, causing the crystalline phase to transform into semi-hydrated gypsum with a dispersed structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Hydration-Recrystallization Method">
  <data key="d0">Non-Hydration-Recrystallization Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-Hydration-Recrystallization Method is a manufacturing process for unfired bricks that excludes hot drying and water immersion steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
