<node id="CeSeH gel">
  <data key="d0">CeSeH gel</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">CeSeH gel is a primary hydration product found alongside portlandite and ettringite in concrete microstructures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoclaved aerated concrete">
  <data key="d0">Autoclaved aerated concrete</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoclaved aerated concrete is a construction material analyzed for its microstructural properties and hydration products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement-PG with GGBFS">
  <data key="d0">Cement-PG with GGBFS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement-PG with GGBFS is a composite material that exhibits high stability and forms wedge crystals after carbonization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement-PG with FA">
  <data key="d0">Cement-PG with FA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement-PG with FA is a composite material susceptible to corrosion, producing less calcite and corroded gel after carbonization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FA">
  <data key="d0">FA</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">FA is an aluminum-silicon compound that results in low calcium levels and increased corrosion in the cement-PG system.&lt;SEP&gt;A material added to raw PG to reduce natural moisture content and neutralize acidity.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash additive providing strong alkaline buffering to significantly reduce PG acidity.&lt;SEP&gt;A material component used in mixtures P1 through P5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEM analysis">
  <data key="d0">SEM analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM analysis is a microscopic examination technique used to identify hydration products and microstructural features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XRD analysis">
  <data key="d0">XRD analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XRD analysis is a characterization technique used to evaluate concrete samples before and after autoclaving.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoclaving">
  <data key="d0">Autoclaving</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoclaving is a thermal treatment process that decomposes ettringite and transforms CeSeH gel into tobermorite.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaving is a curing process applied to aerated concrete that influences hydration and maintains structural strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tian et al.">
  <data key="d0">Tian et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Tian et al. reported that PG primarily functions as a filler in concrete systems, with its activating role requiring further study.&lt;SEP&gt;Tian et al. are researchers whose experimental data is cited in the XRD analysis and compressive strength comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;Tian et al. are researchers who conducted SEM analysis on concrete samples to examine microstructural changes from Phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 15ab">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 15ab</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 15ab provides a microscope image of autoclaved aerated concrete without PG, highlighting hydration products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 16">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 16</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 16 illustrates the microstructural changes and corrosion effects caused by carbonization on cement-PG composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 14">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 14</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 14 displays XRD analysis results from studies conducted by Yang et al. and Tian et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 14 is a figure illustrating fluorine re-release in CPGFM filling slurry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023</data>
