<node id="Autoclaved Aerated Concrete">
  <data key="d0">Autoclaved Aerated Concrete</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoclaved aerated concrete is a material produced through autoclaving, characterized by high tobermorite content and decomposed ettringite.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a novel construction material developed using unprocessed PG, cement, FA, and chemical additives.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a specialized product whose anhydrite content increases when Phosphogypsum is added to the batch.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoclaved aerated concrete is a lightweight building material prepared using untreated phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight concrete material prepared using waste red gypsum and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight building material evaluated through dry-wet cycle testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-004</data>
