<node id="C-S-H Gel">
  <data key="d0">C-S-H Gel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">C-S-H gel is an amorphous hydration product present in large quantities in concrete mixes without PG.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H gel is a hydration product generated from calcium and sulfate ions that contributes to the consolidation and strength of phosphogypsum filling bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H gel is a flocculent hydration product that forms around phosphogypsum particles at low phosphorus levels.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H gel is a hydration product that interlaces with ettringite to form a dense network structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791716064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydration Process">
  <data key="d0">Hydration Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration process is the chemical reaction in concrete where PG acts as an activator and filler, consuming compounds like calcium sulfate dihydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waste Wood Fibre">
  <data key="d0">Waste Wood Fibre</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Waste wood fibre is added to phosphogypsum specimens to improve their thermal and acoustic insulation properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791365947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
