</node>
<node id="Time Spent in Contact">
  <data key="d0">Time Spent in Contact</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Time spent in contact with the substance is a parameter that, when increased, decreases phosphate and fluoride impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791366062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Removal Efficiencies">
  <data key="d0">Removal Efficiencies</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Removal efficiencies are metrics evaluated using analytical techniques to assess the purification of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791366062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Use">
  <data key="d0">Energy Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy use is a drawback of the calcination process, though its benefits in mitigating contaminants are undeniable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791366062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Contamination">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Contamination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary contamination is a risk avoided by combining calcination with L neutralization.&lt;SEP&gt;Secondary contamination refers to environmental pollution caused by the filler, which PGEF avoids.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002</data>
