<node id="Gypsum Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Crystals are mineral formations in the mortar microstructure whose shape and size are altered by phosphate ions and citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Microscopic crystals that precipitate and clump together during the chemical reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystals that precipitate and clump together during the chemical reaction to form agglomerates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-018</data>
