<node id="Direct Leaching">
  <data key="d0">Direct Leaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct leaching is a conventional extraction method involving the use of strong inorganic acids to dissolve rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct Leaching is a recovery method that is costly and ineffective due to the low rare earth element concentration in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct Leaching is a technique used to extract rare earth elements from phosphogypsum using inorganic acids.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct leaching is a conventional extraction technique that dissolves rare earth elements directly from phosphogypsum, noted as expensive and unfeasible.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct leaching is a technique overviewed for recovering rare earth elements directly from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct Leaching is an extraction method requiring control of parameters including contact time, solid to liquid ratio, temperature, and agitation speed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792041352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
