<node id="Potassium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium hydroxide is a chemical reagent utilized in the transformation of phosphogypsum to produce calcium carbonate and potassium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium hydroxide is a starting material used in the hydrothermal synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium Hydroxide is a reactant that can substitute calcium ions into the hydroxyapatite crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound utilized as a titrant for determining carbon dioxide content, with its concentration derived from calcium carbonate mass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-008</data>
