<node id="Government Departments">
  <data key="d0">Government Departments</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Government Departments are public administrative bodies encouraged to prioritize PG-Based Products in procurement and implement policy interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791450403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphorus Chemical Companies">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus Chemical Companies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Companies that lack recognition of PG recycling and are targeted for transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial enterprises traditionally focused on phosphoric acid and phosphate fertilizers that now face scrutiny to manage PG waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial entities undergoing supply-side structural reform and transformation to treat PG as a reusable resource.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus Chemical Companies are industrial entities compelled to prioritize the reduction, reuse, and recycling of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus chemical companies are currently characterized by a lack of recognition regarding phosphogypsum recycling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791450403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Producer Responsibility System">
  <data key="d0">Extended Producer Responsibility System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">This regulatory framework compels phosphorus chemical companies to balance PG production and consumption to mitigate stockpile expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;A policy mechanism proposed to reinforce top-level design and enhance accountability in the PG recycling industry.&lt;SEP&gt;The Extended Producer Responsibility System is a regulatory approach mandating phosphorus chemical companies to manage phosphogypsum waste lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Extended Producer Responsibility System is a policy mechanism proposed to reinforce top-level design and improve PG recycling coordination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791450403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Value Technologies">
  <data key="d0">High-Value Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-value technologies refer to innovative solutions for PG recycling that are currently deficient in the sector.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Value Technologies are advanced innovations targeted for intensification to transform phosphogypsum into commercially valuable materials.&lt;SEP&gt;High-value technologies refer to advanced methods that enhance the economic and practical utility of phosphogypsum recycling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791450501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tax Preferential List">
  <data key="d0">Tax Preferential List</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tax Preferential List is a policy instrument updated to incentivize the widespread adoption of PG-Based Products in municipal engineering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791450501</data>
