<node id="Polymer Materials">
  <data key="d0">Polymer Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polymer Materials are synthetic or semi-synthetic substances, encompassing resins and plastics, that serve as a foundational category for various industrial applications. Within sustainable resource management, they represent a primary and innovative application domain for recycled phosphogypsum (PG). The integration of PG into these materials requires specific processing techniques, including calcination and milling, to transform the phosphogypsum into inert compounds that ensure optimal compatibility with polymer matrices. This approach enables the conversion of industrial byproducts into advanced materials targeted for high-value technological development.

The utilization of Polymer Materials extends to the production of high-value municipal infrastructure items, highlighting their practical engineering potential. Despite these promising applications, the widespread adoption of polymer materials derived from recycled phosphogypsum currently remains in the experimental phase in certain regions. In specific classification frameworks and data legends, these materials are formally listed as industrial substances, characterized by a 0.89% value and designated with red color coding. Collectively, Polymer Materials bridge advanced manufacturing with circular economy principles, transforming phosphogypsum waste into functional, high-performance industrial products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791900752</data>
