<node id="High-Temperature Calcination">
  <data key="d0">High-Temperature Calcination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">High-temperature calcination is a modification process that eliminates moisture and impurities from phosphogypsum to form inert pyrophosphate.&lt;SEP&gt;High-temperature calcination is a thermal treatment process applied to PG for material modification and recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Temperature Calcination is a treatment step for PG processing.&lt;SEP&gt;High-temperature calcination heats phosphogypsum to reduce soluble phosphorus and fluorine activity, transforming it into an inert material with improved whiteness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008</data>
