  <data key="d2">PVA is a polymer used to peel and prepare HAP samples for spectroscopic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyvinyl alcohol used as a mounting medium to peel and prepare HAP layers for SEM imaging.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a water-soluble polymer used to successfully separate the HAP layer from the substrate without altering particle morphology.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a polymer structure whose characteristic vibrations decreased after washing, indicating its removal from the sample.&lt;SEP&gt;PVA is a polymer used to peel the Hydroxyapatite layer without causing distinct morphological changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PO3- Group">
  <data key="d0">PO3- Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The PO3- group is a chemical moiety whose vibrations increased after washing, signaling the effective removal of PVA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water/Ethanol Mixture">
  <data key="d0">Water/Ethanol Mixture</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The water/ethanol mixture is a solvent treatment used to wash the sample, successfully removing almost all PVA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469697</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AL Molecules">
  <data key="d0">AL Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AL molecules are bisphosphonate compounds containing one hydroxyl group and two phosphate groups that bind to HAP.&lt;SEP&gt;AL molecules are organic compounds containing -NH2 groups that bind to HAP surfaces to alter chemical and physical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;AL Molecules are functional compounds used to modify the surface of Hydroxyapatite powders, confirmed by chemical shifts in spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Phosphate Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate crystals are crystalline structures to which AL molecules exhibit high affinity due to their chemical composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate crystals are synthesized with controlled size and shape for various biomedical and material science applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XPS Spectra">
  <data key="d0">XPS Spectra</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS spectra are analytical measurements used to determine binding energies and elemental assignments for HAP, HAP-AL, and pure AL samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FE-SEM Images">
  <data key="d0">FE-SEM Images</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">FE-SEM images are microscopic visualizations that reveal no morphological changes in AL-treated HAP microparticles compared to peeled particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hierarchical Microspheres">
  <data key="d0">Hierarchical Microspheres</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hierarchical microspheres are spherical structures composed of HAP that were peeled and subsequently surface-modified with AL molecules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quan">
  <data key="d0">Quan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Quan is a researcher whose observations indicated that high concentrations of AL molecules enhance the bioactivity of surface-modified HAP nanocrystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Quan is a researcher who observed that surface modification of HAP nanocrystals with high concentration of AL increases bioactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tridentate Binding">
  <data key="d0">Tridentate Binding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tridentate binding is a chemical attachment mechanism where AL molecules connect to calcium within HAP, enhancing affinity for calcium phosphate crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bisphosphonates">
  <data key="d0">Bisphosphonates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bisphosphonates are a class of chemical compounds to which AL molecules belong and which show varying affinities for calcium phosphate crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Bisphosphonates are a class of compounds used to prevent bone loss and deliver therapeutic agents to bone tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S4T">
  <data key="d0">S4T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific HAP sample fabricated at 180 °C with a 1:1 NTA/Ca molar ratio, used for peeling experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;S4T is a sample identifier used to denote a specific batch of HAP in the XPS analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAP-AL">
  <data key="d0">HAP-AL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAP-AL is a composite sample representing HAP modified with AL molecules, analyzed via XPS.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-AL is the functionalized form of Hydroxyapatite modified with AL molecules, analyzed via XPS and ATR-FTIR.&lt;SEP&gt;An alendronate-modified hydroxyapatite material variant analyzed via infrared spectroscopy, exhibiting distinct spectral peaks.&lt;SEP&gt;A material sample exhibiting broad OH and NH₂ groups, with shifted phosphate peaks indicating structural differences from PVA-peeled HAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pure AL">
  <data key="d0">Pure AL</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Pure AL is an unmodified sample of AL molecules used as a reference in the XPS analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Pure AL is the unmodified AL baseline used for comparative binding energy measurements in XPS analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="O1s">
  <data key="d0">O1s</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">O1s is an XPS peak representing the oxygen 1s electron state, measured at specific binding energies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
