  <data key="d0">P2p</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">P2p is an XPS peak representing the phosphorus 2p electron state, measured at specific binding energies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Central Carbon">
  <data key="d0">Central Carbon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The central carbon is the structural backbone of the AL molecule to which hydroxyl and phosphate groups are bound.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Solution">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The aqueous solution serves as the reaction medium where NTA and calcium ions interact.&lt;SEP&gt;The aqueous solution is the liquid medium in which AL molecules are dissolved for treating HAP microspheres.&lt;SEP&gt;The aqueous solution serves as the electrolyte medium for the photoelectrochemical measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791967780</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 mM">
  <data key="d0">8 mM</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">8 mM is the concentration of the AL aqueous solution used to treat the peeled hierarchical microspheres of HAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 5e and f">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 5e and f</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 5e and f are references to FE-SEM images showing the morphology of AL-treated HAP microparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Binding Energies">
  <data key="d0">Binding Energies</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Binding energies are quantitative measurements in eV obtained from XPS results to identify elemental states.&lt;SEP&gt;Binding Energies are determined using XPS to establish a data basis for Fe and S reference compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Co-workers">
  <data key="d0">Co-workers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-workers are research associates of Quan who contributed to observations on AL concentration and bioactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791469856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Bonds">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Bonds</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical bonds such as C-O, C-H, and C=O stretching and bending are analyzed via IR spectroscopy to identify PVA structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural connections within molecules that can be identified through infrared spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-006</data>
