</node>
<node id="120 °C">
  <data key="d0">120 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">120 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S1.&lt;SEP&gt;120 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature yielding plate-like structures with irregular shapes.&lt;SEP&gt;120 °C is the temperature at which the hydrothermal treatment was conducted to synthesize the hydroxyapatite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791486667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="150 °C">
  <data key="d0">150 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">150 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S2.&lt;SEP&gt;150 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature where needle-like rods self-assemble into microparticles.&lt;SEP&gt;150 °C is a synthesis temperature at which quartz impurities dissolve, leaving calcium hydroxide as a side phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791628323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="165 °C">
  <data key="d0">165 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">165 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Sample S3.&lt;SEP&gt;165 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature producing uniform flower-like hierarchical microparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="180 °C">
  <data key="d0">180 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">180 °C is the hydrothermal temperature applied to Samples S4 through S8.&lt;SEP&gt;180 °C is a hydrothermal synthesis temperature yielding larger flower-like hierarchical microparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791470547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="400 °C">
  <data key="d0">400 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">400 °C is the temperature used for thermal treatment of HAP samples.&lt;SEP&gt;400 °C is the thermal treatment temperature applied for 30 minutes to evaluate morphological changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-001</data>
