<node id="BSA">
  <data key="d0">BSA</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">BSA is the abbreviation for Bovine Serum Albumin, used as a model protein in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Bovine Serum Albumin, a protein analyzed for its adsorption and release behavior on HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA is a negatively charged protein that adsorbs onto positively charged HAp sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Bovine Serum Albumin, an acidic protein used to evaluate drug-loading and sustained release properties of the synthesized material.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA is a protein used to modify hydroxyapatite samples, whose thermal decay and binding properties are analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;BSA is a protein whose adsorption onto hydroxyapatite is studied through thermal stability and electrostatic interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791747499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSZ">
  <data key="d0">LSZ</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">LSZ is the abbreviation for Lysozyme, used as a model protein in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;LSZ is a positively charged protein that adsorbs onto negatively charged HAp sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysozyme, a protein analyzed for its adsorption and release behavior on HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysozyme, a positively charged protein compared against BSA to assess differential release characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791485610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Langmuir Behavior">
  <data key="d0">Langmuir Behavior</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Langmuir behavior describes the adsorption kinetics where proteins form a monolayer on HAp surfaces, with adsorption amount increasing with initial concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-006</data>
