<node id="Sulfate Group">
  <data key="d0">Sulfate Group</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical group highly characteristic of gypsum, indicated by strong absorption bands in the 1000–1100 cm⁻¹ range.&lt;SEP&gt;The sulfate group is a chemical moiety identified in hemi-hydrate gypsum and anhydrous calcium sulfate through characteristic FT-IR absorption bands.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sulfate Group is a chemical moiety within calcium sulfate compounds, identified by characteristic infrared absorption bands.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical group (S-O) whose asymmetric stretching vibration corresponds to a strong absorption peak at 1095 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;The sulfate group is identified in the infrared spectra through characteristic stretching vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate Group is a chemical component of ammonium sulfate, exhibiting symmetric deformation and stretch vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sulfate Group is a chemical moiety referenced in the analysis of prepared compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-004</data>
