<node id="Hydroxyapatite (HAp)">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite (HAp)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite (HAp) is a synthesized rod-shaped material with a typical apatite structure and mesoporous properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a nanocrystalline material synthesized from industrial waste for various applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a calcium phosphate mineral synthesized hydrothermally, characterized by rod-like crystals and a specific hexagonal crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A nanocrystalline material successfully synthesized from industrial waste phosphogypsum and potassium dihydrogen phosphate using a hydrothermal method.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a naturally occurring calcium phosphate found in bones and teeth, synthesized and modified in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthesized nanocrystalline material whose structural and morphological properties were analyzed in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound used as the base material for synthesized nanoparticles analyzed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM)">
  <data key="d0">Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) is a high-magnification imaging technique used to confirm the crystalline nature and lattice fringe spacing of the HAp sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmission electron microscopy is a characterization technique used to examine the morphology and structure of synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging technique used to observe the nanorod structure and aspect ratio of the HAp particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) is a microscopy technique utilized to investigate the microstructural and morphological features of the powders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791664251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
