<node id="Pure HAp">
  <data key="d0">Pure HAp</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pure HAp, or pure hydroxyapatite, is an unmodified, synthesized nanoparticle variant of hydroxyapatite that serves as a fundamental baseline for comparison in spectroscopic analyses. It is typically produced through hydrothermal synthesis, which imparts specific crystallographic characteristics to the material. Morphologically, Pure HAp nanoparticles often exhibit a monodispersed nanorod shape, with reported average lengths reaching approximately 53.44 nm. Optically, the material demonstrates a measured band gap of 5.25 eV.

A notable feature of Pure HAp is the variation in its measured crystallite size across different experimental preparations and characterization contexts. Reported values for the crystallite size range from 5.43 nm to 23.5 nm, with specific samples documented at 5.43 nm, 12.37 nm, 15.57 nm, and 23.5 nm. These discrepancies reflect differences in synthesis parameters, processing conditions, or measurement methodologies rather than inherent contradictions, as Pure HAp encompasses a family of unmodified hydroxyapatite nanoparticle samples tailored for various comparative studies. Collectively, these attributes define Pure HAp as a versatile, structurally defined reference material in materials science and spectroscopic research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f1fb5c243f2539cf7be6b6021b63c36f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
