<node id="Mass Loss">
  <data key="d0">Mass Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mass loss is a measured parameter indicating the reduction in phosphogypsum weight during thermal treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass loss is a quantitative measurement (3.42%) indicating the sample is not bihydrated.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass loss refers to the reduction in sample weight recorded during thermal analysis, annotated at specific temperature intervals.&lt;SEP&gt;A phenomenon where the sample loses weight, correlating with thermal decomposition or dehydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-008</data>
