<node id="66°C">
  <data key="d0">66°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">66°C is the temperature at which the first endothermic peak occurs, marking the onset of phosphogypsum dehydration.&lt;SEP&gt;66°C is the temperature of the first endothermic dehydration stage of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;66°C is a low temperature point where Curve 2 exhibits a small peak.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific temperature marking the start of a dehydration thermal event in the phosphogypsum analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="133°C">
  <data key="d0">133°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">133°C is the temperature of the second endothermic peak, corresponding to the completion of gypsum transformation to anhydrite III.&lt;SEP&gt;133°C is the temperature of the second endothermic dehydration stage of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;133°C is a temperature point where Curve 2 shows a sharp dip or valley.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific temperature marking the main dehydration step in the phosphogypsum analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient-280°C Interval">
  <data key="d0">Ambient-280°C Interval</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The ambient-280°C temperature interval where powdery phosphogypsum dehydration occurs in one stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-007</data>
