<node id="Heating Rate">
  <data key="d0">Heating Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Heating Rate is an experimental parameter measured in degrees Celsius per hour that influences the temperature and timing of phosphogypsum dehydration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Heating Rate is an experimental parameter that influences the thermogravimetric analysis results and sample transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Heating rate is a critical process parameter that differs between synthesis methods, influencing particle growth and nucleation speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Heating rate is the 10°C/min parameter used during the thermogravimetric analysis of dried hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Heating Rate is the controlled temperature increase speed of 10 °C/min applied during thermal analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pellets">
  <data key="d0">Pellets</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Pellets are a solid sample form of phosphogypsum prepared under mechanical pressure, exhibiting higher humidity absorption than powdery samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Powdery Form">
  <data key="d0">Powdery Form</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Powdery Form is a granular sample state of phosphogypsum used as a baseline for comparing thermal behavior against pelletized samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
