<node id="Arrhenius Law">
  <data key="d0">Arrhenius Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Arrhenius Law is a scientific principle describing the relationship between heating rate, reaction temperature, and maximum dehydration rate observed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrogen Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen Atmosphere is a gaseous environment used during thermal treatment to determine that the gas has no effect on the phosphogypsum reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen atmosphere is a specific sintering condition used in Xiao and coworkers' three-step metal recovery method.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen Atmosphere is the inert gaseous environment used during thermogravimetric studies to prevent oxidation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097396</data>
