<node id="Endothermic Process">
  <data key="d0">Endothermic Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A thermal transformation type characterized by heat absorption during phosphogypsum heating.&lt;SEP&gt;Endothermic process describes thermal transformations that absorb heat, such as dehydration at 66°C and 133°C.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical process that absorbs heat, where increasing temperature shifts equilibrium toward higher extraction percentages.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal event involving heat absorption, indicated by a sharp downward trend in the DSC curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exothermic Process">
  <data key="d0">Exothermic Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A thermal transformation type characterized by heat release during phosphogypsum heating.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic process describes thermal transformations that release heat, such as the phase change at 428°C.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic Process is a thermal reaction connected with the decay of BSA molecules, generating peaks on thermal curves.&lt;SEP&gt;Exothermic Process describes the heat-releasing nature of the neutralization reaction used to synthesize HAp Type 1.&lt;SEP&gt;The heat-releasing nature of the hydroxyapatite synthesis reaction, providing sufficient energy for crystallization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulfate III">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate III</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulfate III is an intermediate phase formed during the thermal transformation of calcium sulfate hemihydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-004</data>
