<node id="428°C">
  <data key="d0">428°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">428°C is the temperature of the exothermic peak indicating the transition of soluble anhydrite III to insoluble anhydrite II.&lt;SEP&gt;428°C is the temperature of the exothermic transformation from anhydrite III to anhydrite II.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific temperature marking a major thermal event and the phase transition of calcium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1184°C">
  <data key="d0">1184°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1184°C is the temperature of an endothermic peak corresponding to the transition of anhydrite II to anhydrite I.&lt;SEP&gt;1184°C is the temperature of the endothermic transformation from anhydrite II to anhydrite.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-temperature thermal event marking melting or formation of high-temperature phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1250°C">
  <data key="d0">1250°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1250°C is the temperature at which the final endothermic peak occurs, marking the decomposition of calcium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water of Humidity">
  <data key="d0">Water of Humidity</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water of Humidity is the moisture content eliminated from the sample at 66°C, causing the initial mass loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="130°C">
  <data key="d0">130°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">130°C is the temperature of the first endothermic peak observed by Grin and Rowland during gypsum dehydration studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="180°C">
  <data key="d0">180°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">180°C is the temperature of the second endothermic peak observed by Grin and Rowland, and the first peak observed by West and Suiton.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="215°C">
  <data key="d0">215°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">215°C is the temperature of the second endothermic peak observed by West and Suiton during gypsum dehydration studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="149°C">
  <data key="d0">149°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">149°C is the temperature of the first endothermic peak observed by Ould Chameikh during Mauritanian gypsum analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
