  <data key="d0">169°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">169°C is the temperature of the second endothermic peak observed by Ould Chameikh during Mauritanian gypsum analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Molecules">
  <data key="d0">Water Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Molecules are present in the raw sample and contribute to specific absorption features in the spectrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Water Molecules penetrate the PGCM matrix during the immersion stage and seep out during the drying stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H-O-H Bending Vibration">
  <data key="d0">H-O-H Bending Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A molecular vibration corresponding to the bending motion of water molecules, detected at a specific wavenumber.&lt;SEP&gt;H-O-H Bending Vibration is a molecular motion of water molecules observed around 1630 cm⁻¹.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asymmetric Stretching Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Asymmetric Stretching Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asymmetric Stretching Vibration is a vibrational mode of the sulfate ion observed around 1150–1170 cm⁻¹.&lt;SEP&gt;Asymmetric stretching vibration corresponds to the sharp, strong peak around 1100 cm⁻¹ in the sulfate ion spectrum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symmetric Stretching Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Symmetric Stretching Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symmetric Stretching Vibration is a vibrational mode of the sulfate ion identified in the spectral attribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dehydration Process">
  <data key="d0">Dehydration Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dehydration Process involves heating the sample to remove crystallization water and convert dihydrate to anhydrite forms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791498992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crystallization Water">
  <data key="d0">Crystallization Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallization water refers to water molecules bound within the crystal structure of gypsum that are removed upon heating.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791499087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wavenumbers">
  <data key="d0">Wavenumbers</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Wavenumbers are the units of measurement used to express spectral peak positions in inverse centimeters.&lt;SEP&gt;Wavenumbers are measured values in inverse centimeters representing specific spectral peaks for sulfate ion vibrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Curve (a)">
  <data key="d0">Curve (a)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Curve (a) represents the spectral data of the raw phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A blue line on the infrared transmittance spectrum graph representing one set of transmittance measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Curve (b)">
  <data key="d0">Curve (b)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Curve (b) represents the spectral data of the treated or calcined phosphogypsum sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A red/orange line on the infrared transmittance spectrum graph representing another set of transmittance measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8c22d31cfad5421c936a23705a3bc6e0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792002686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peak Positions">
  <data key="d0">Peak Positions</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Peak positions are the specific numerical values indicating where spectral absorption occurs.</data>
