<node id="Curing in Air">
  <data key="d0">Curing in Air</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Curing in air is a maintenance condition where specimens are exposed to air, leading to slower hydration and varying compressive strength outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing in Air is a baseline curing condition for PGCM samples, showing lower strength improvements from admixtures than water curing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009</data>
