</node>
<node id="Energy Spectrum Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Energy Spectrum Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy Spectrum Analysis is an analytical technique used alongside SEM to identify internal hydration products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expansion and Contraction">
  <data key="d0">Expansion and Contraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Expansion and Contraction describes the dimensional changes of PGCM samples divided into three stages based on curing age.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weathering Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Weathering Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weathering resistance is a durability metric evaluated alongside frost, water, and dry shrinkage performance in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Weathering resistance refers to the ability of PGCM to withstand degradation from environmental cycles like dry-wet exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Weathering Resistance is a durability property of PGCM affected differently by quicklime, cement, and silica fume.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antifreeze Ability">
  <data key="d0">Antifreeze Ability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antifreeze Ability measures PGCM's resistance to frost damage, which improves with silica fume over later cycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Antifreeze Ability is a performance metric of PGCM that silica fume improves in the later stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hardened Body">
  <data key="d0">Hardened Body</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hardened Body refers to the solidified PGCM sample through which water penetrates along micro-cracks.&lt;SEP&gt;The hardened body refers to the solidified PGCM matrix containing internal pores, cracks, and hydration products.&lt;SEP&gt;Hardened body is the solidified PGCM material where hydration products fill pores and cracks.&lt;SEP&gt;Hardened Body refers to the cured PGCM sample where water evaporation and hydration products drive expansion and contraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
