</node>
<node id="J. Plant Nutr. Fertil.">
  <data key="d0">J. Plant Nutr. Fertil.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">J. Plant Nutr. Fertil. is a journal referenced in the study regarding phosphorus productivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry-Wet Cycles">
  <data key="d0">Dry-Wet Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry-wet cycles are a testing procedure involving soaking and drying stages that induce dissolution and cracking in PGCM.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antifreeze Performance">
  <data key="d0">Antifreeze Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antifreeze Performance measures PGCM's ability to withstand structural damage caused by repeated freezing and thawing.&lt;SEP&gt;Antifreeze performance denotes PGCM's capacity to resist damage from freezing conditions, which is reduced by high cement dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Alumina Crystals">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Alumina Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium alumina crystals are hydration products formed inside hardened PGCM that squeeze aggregates and increase micro-cracks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro-Cracks">
  <data key="d0">Micro-Cracks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Micro-Cracks are small fractures within PGCM that facilitate water penetration and contribute to material degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro-cracks are small fractures generated inside the PGCM matrix due to scouring and crystal expansion, weakening the specimen.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro-cracks are pathways in PGCM that the hydrophobic crystal-gel combination blocks to improve water resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quicklime 3%">
  <data key="d0">Quicklime 3%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A 3% quicklime dosage in PGCM that results in poor weathering resistance after 25 dry-wet cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement 12%">
  <data key="d0">Cement 12%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A 12% cement dosage in PGCM that yields the highest strength coefficient below 15 dry-wet cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement 15%">
  <data key="d0">Cement 15%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A 15% cement dosage in PGCM that yields the highest strength coefficient above 15 dry-wet cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cement 18%">
  <data key="d0">Cement 18%</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An 18% cement dosage in PGCM that results in a lower strength coefficient compared to 12% and 15% dosages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry-Wet Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Dry-Wet Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry-Wet Cycle is an environmental stress test used to assess the weathering resistance and structural degradation of PGCM.&lt;SEP&gt;Dry-wet cycle is an environmental condition causing alternating shrinkage and expansion stress, leading to crack propagation in materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing condition evaluated alongside freeze-thaw cycles to assess PGCM durability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immersion Stage">
  <data key="d0">Immersion Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Immersion Stage is the initial phase of the Dry-Wet Cycle where water penetrates the porous structure of PGCM.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drying Stage">
  <data key="d0">Drying Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Drying Stage is the subsequent phase of the Dry-Wet Cycle where evaporation accelerates material dissolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro Aggregates">
  <data key="d0">Micro Aggregates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Micro Aggregates are small particles within PGCM that are scoured by flowing water molecules during the drying stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pores">
  <data key="d0">Pores</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pores are void spaces in the PGCM structure that facilitate water penetration and seepage.&lt;SEP&gt;Pores are voids within PGCM that accumulate water, expand under pressure, and contribute to material damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Integrity">
  <data key="d0">Structural Integrity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural Integrity refers to the condition of the PGCM sample, which remains good at low cycle counts but degrades over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural Integrity is a material property representing the ability of the sample to withstand stress and resist failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural Integrity is the property maintained by the hollow design of the blocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791674157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Antifreeze Ability">
  <data key="d0">Early Antifreeze Ability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early Antifreeze Ability refers to PGCM's frost resistance at low cycle counts, which silica fume does not significantly improve.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Later Antifreeze Ability">
  <data key="d0">Later Antifreeze Ability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Later Antifreeze Ability refers to PGCM's frost resistance at higher cycle counts, which is effectively improved by silica fume.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Frost Resistance Environment">
  <data key="d0">High Frost Resistance Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">High Frost Resistance Environment is the target application setting for PGCM, where silica fume dosage should be controlled at 7%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loading of Alternating Wet and Dry Erosion">
  <data key="d0">Loading of Alternating Wet and Dry Erosion</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Loading of Alternating Wet and Dry Erosion is the stress condition applied to PGCM samples to induce damage morphology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5 Cycles">
  <data key="d0">5 Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">5 Cycles is a low cycle count where silica fume shows little effect on PGCM's antifreeze performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10 Cycles">
  <data key="d0">10 Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">10 Cycles is a cycle count where silica fume begins to exhibit an improvement effect on PGCM's antifreeze performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="20 Cycles">
  <data key="d0">20 Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">20 Cycles is a cycle count where the surface of the PGCM sample begins to fall off under dry-wet cycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="25 Cycles">
  <data key="d0">25 Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">25 Cycles is a cycle count where short but disconnected transverse cracks appear on the PGCM sample surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Cycles">
  <data key="d0">30 Cycles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">30 Cycles is a cycle count where raw phosphogypsum flakes off extensively and the internal skeleton is exposed.&lt;SEP&gt;30 Cycles represents the total duration of freeze-thaw testing tracked in the dissolution rate graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C-S-H">
  <data key="d0">C-S-H</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium silicate hydrate gel that bonds to phosphogypsum particles during hydration and forms complexes with AFt crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H is the abbreviation for calcium silicate hydrate gel, a primary hydration product that bonds to particles.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H is a hydration product promoted by acidic and alkaline solutions in the early stages of chemical erosion.&lt;SEP&gt;C-S-H is a cementitious gel that interlaces with AFt to form a dense network structure for immobilizing toxic elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A yellow squiggly line in the legend representing Calcium Silicate Hydrate in the mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791722879</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phosphogypsum Particles">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphogypsum particles serve as the base material in PGCM that becomes progressively wrapped by hydration products.&lt;SEP&gt;Core particles in PGCM that become wrapped by hydration products like C-S-H and AFt crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gypsum Particles">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum particles are embedded in PGCM and become covered and wrapped by new hydration products during consolidation.&lt;SEP&gt;Particles initially covered and wrapped by C-S-H gel during the hydration process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AFt Crystals">
  <data key="d0">AFt Crystals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystals produced during hydration that intersperse with C-S-H to form complexes and provide attachment points for CaSO4 crystallization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydration Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Hydration Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydration Reaction is a fundamental chemical process that facilitates the hardening and strength development of cementitious materials, particularly within phosphogypsum-based systems. In this context, the reaction involves matrix components interacting to form key hydration products, including calcium silicate hydrate (C-S-H) flocs and gel, AFt crystals, ettringite, and gel adhesive layers that coat phosphogypsum particles. This process primarily occurs during the early curing phase and is responsible for both the progressive gain in mechanical strength and long-term dimensional changes within the material. The reaction dynamics are significantly influenced by various chemical factors; it can be enhanced or catalyzed by specific phosphate products and interacts synergistically with supplementary additives such as silica fume and quicklime. Conversely, the presence of phosphate impurities may hinder the hydration process.

Beyond its application in construction materials, Hydration Reaction also denotes a distinct step in industrial chemistry, specifically serving as a subsequent phase in the thermal phosphoric acid production process that follows yellow phosphorus combustion. In both contexts, the reaction serves as a critical mechanism for material transformation, product formation, and performance evolution over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791937342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erosion Test">
  <data key="d0">Erosion Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A procedure that reduces hydration product content but triggers continuous dissolution of admixtures to form new hydration products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
