</node>
<node id="Freeze-Thaw Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Freeze-Thaw Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Freeze-thaw cycle is a deterioration experiment method applied to PGCM specimens to assess long-term water resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Freeze-thaw cycle is an environmental condition causing hydrostatic pressure buildup and pore enlargement, deteriorating material properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing condition used to evaluate the freeze resistance and strength coefficient of PGCM.&lt;SEP&gt;Freeze-Thaw Cycle is an experimental condition representing time progression tracked over thirty iterations in material testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A temporal variable plotted on the horizontal axis, representing the number of cycles up to 30.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791516319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
