<node id="Water Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Water Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A critical performance metric initially lacking in phosphogypsum materials, requiring enhancement via polymer or organic material incorporation.&lt;SEP&gt;A key property of PGCM enhanced by hydrophobic crystal-gel combinations that prevent water penetration through micro-cracks.&lt;SEP&gt;Water resistance is a property of PGCM enhanced by silica fume-generated gel that resists water erosion.&lt;SEP&gt;Water resistance is a physical property studied to evaluate how adobe samples withstand immersion in water.&lt;SEP&gt;The material's ability to withstand degradation when submerged, indicated by the time to soften in water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-007</data>
