<node id="Admixture">
  <data key="d0">Admixture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Admixture refers to the added substances like cement and silica fume that undergo hydration in PGCM.&lt;SEP&gt;Admixtures are supplementary materials like quicklime, cement, and silica fume that dissolve to release mineral ions and form new hydration products.&lt;SEP&gt;Admixture is a primary material component used in the formulation of reinforced concrete.&lt;SEP&gt;Admixture is a component comprising 0.3%–0.9% of the CPGFM slurry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-026</data>
