  <data key="d2">A controlled environmental parameter maintained at 20 ± 2 °C during long-term water resistance testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing temperature influences the generation of hydration products and inversely affects fluoride leaching rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Curing temperature is a variable investigated for its effect on the unconfined compressive strength of phosphogypsum specimens.</data>
