</node>
<node id="Nanorods Morphology">
  <data key="d0">Nanorods Morphology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nanorods Morphology describes the rod-like structural characteristic of the synthesized hydroxyapatite particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530213</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stoichiometric Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Stoichiometric Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Stoichiometric Ratio is a chemical standard that the HT11-12h sample exceeded in calcium-to-phosphorus proportion.&lt;SEP&gt;The stoichiometric ratio refers to the ideal molar Ca/P ratio of 1.67 for HAp particles, used as a benchmark for purity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791559146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonate Values">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Values</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2 presents the estimated carbonate percentages for all synthesized samples.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791530219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TEM Micrographs">
  <data key="d0">TEM Micrographs</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c4a64a852097fdc910b98ed788503ce4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 4 displays the TEM micrographs used to observe the morphologies of the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;TEM Micrographs illustrate the morphological transition of Hydroxyapatite from rodlike particles to spherical particles after calcination.</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
