<node id="HAp Nanorods">
  <data key="d0">HAp Nanorods</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp Nanorods are the synthesized hexagonal rod-shaped crystals of Hydroxyapatite whose size is influenced by the surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;Rod-like crystalline structures of HAp exhibiting preferential growth along the c-axis direction.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp Nanorods are synthesized hexagonal rods that grow along the c axis and exhibit increased crystallite size when Brij-93 surfactant is used.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp nanorods are rod-like hydroxyapatite nanoparticles desirable for biocompatibility applications.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp nanorods are one-dimensional nanostructures formed during synthesis facilitated by urea.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-011</data>
