<node id="Finland">
  <data key="d0">Finland</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Finland primarily stockpiles PG with minor pilot projects in agriculture and road construction.&lt;SEP&gt;Finland is a source of phosphogypsum that is notably rich in SO3 (53.48 wt%) and CaO (38.60 wt%).&lt;SEP&gt;Finland is a country in Europe with an annual phosphogypsum production of 1.9 Mt.&lt;SEP&gt;A country where by-product and recycle materials in earth construction were assessed for applicability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-005</data>
