<node id="HPA">
  <data key="d0">HPA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HPA is an organic phosphonate chemical compound and molecule characterized by a phosphonic acid group. Its structural formula and optimal molecular configuration have been analyzed using density functional theory, while its interactions with hydroxyapatite (HAP) have been investigated through spectroscopic and diffraction methods.

In materials synthesis, HPA functions as a base material, precursor, chemical dopant, additive, and catalyst. It is specifically incorporated into HAP to modify its structural properties and enhance its adsorption performance, resulting in the formation of the 20HPA-HAP composite adsorbent. The composite is formed through a chemical mechanism wherein HPA acts as a doping agent; upon deprotonation, its functional groups chelate with heavy metal ions, facilitating the integration of HPA into the HAP matrix. Consequently, HPA serves as a critical functional component in the development of advanced adsorbents designed for heavy metal ion removal and structural modification of hydroxyapatite-based materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-06f299b7e723cda1f0de1a647b02b6b4-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791653714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
