<node id="Synthesis Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Synthesis Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthesis Temperature is a controlled experimental parameter ranging from 60 to 150 °C that affects the crystallization and peak sharpness of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesis temperature is a reaction parameter that was observed to have no impact on the Ca/P molar ratio of HAp powders.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesis temperature is a critical factor that determines the stability of carbonate substitutions and the resulting lattice parameters in hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesis Temperature is a process parameter that influences the stability of carbonate substitutions in the hydroxyapatite lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesis temperature is a process parameter that influences hydroxyapatite particle morphology and crystallinity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791856583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="112 and 300 Planes">
  <data key="d0">112 and 300 Planes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The 112 and 300 planes are crystallographic planes in hydroxyapatite whose XRD peak intensities change due to whisker orientation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2196dee89de9694f28ef4eaa0e85f130-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791664401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
