<node id="Grashof Number">
  <data key="d0">Grashof Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dimensionless number used alongside the Rayleigh and Prandtl numbers to model convection.&lt;SEP&gt;A dimensionless number in fluid dynamics that approximates the ratio of buoyancy to viscous force and determines the onset of natural convection.&lt;SEP&gt;Grashof Number is a dimensionless parameter in fluid dynamics and heat transfer used to characterize natural convection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grashof Number Equation">
  <data key="d0">Grashof Number Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Grashof Number Equation is the mathematical formula $Gr = \frac{g \beta \Delta T H^3}{v^2}$ defining the Grashof Number.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Quantities Relationship Equation">
  <data key="d0">Physical Quantities Relationship Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Quantities Relationship Equation is the mathematical formula $y = Y \times 4x^2 / L$ defining a relationship between physical variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
