<node id="Natural Convection">
  <data key="d0">Natural Convection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fluid dynamics phenomenon modeled in PGEF to calculate the optimum air layer thickness.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural convection is a physical process modeled mathematically for PGEF in Fig. 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Convection is a fluid motion mechanism driven by buoyancy forces, analyzed using the Grashof Number in phosphogypsum processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanism of heat transfer driven by buoyancy forces due to temperature differences in a fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alpha">
  <data key="d0">Alpha</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alpha is an angle between the vertical axis and the slanted blue line in the trapezoid diagram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
