<node id="PGEF">
  <data key="d0">PGEF</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PGEF is a modified phosphogypsum-based embedded filler characterized by a regular, dense, and interlocking crystalline microstructure.&lt;SEP&gt;PGEF is a modified phosphogypsum embedded filler whose stress performance, thermal insulation, and microstructure were analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;PGEF is a novel construction material prepared in the research, utilized in cast-in situ concrete hollow floor structures to reduce weight and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modified Phosphogypsum">
  <data key="d0">Modified Phosphogypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Modified Phosphogypsum serves as a primary material component in the formulation of PGEF, characterized by low cost and absence of secondary contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791673626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polypropylene Fiber">
  <data key="d0">Polypropylene Fiber</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Polypropylene Fiber is a locally sourced material used as a 0.5% mass ratio component in the filler mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;Polypropylene Fiber is incorporated as a material component in the PGEF mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-000</data>
