<node id="DPG">
  <data key="d0">DPG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">DPG refers to dihydrate phosphogypsum, characterized by crystals in the form of flakes and plates.&lt;SEP&gt;DPG is a material whose main component is calcium sulfate dihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;DPG refers to inactive phosphogypsum often used as an aggregate in filling materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002</data>
