<node id="Dry Unit Weight">
  <data key="d0">Dry Unit Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry unit weight is calculated by dividing the oven-dried weight of adobe samples by their volume.&lt;SEP&gt;Dry unit weight is a physical property evaluated to assess the density and stability of the adobe samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-002</data>
