<node id="Derivative Thermogravimetry">
  <data key="d0">Derivative Thermogravimetry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Derivative Thermogravimetry is a thermal analysis technique used to identify peaks associated with specific decomposition processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Derivative Thermogravimetry tracks the rate of mass change per minute to pinpoint temperatures of rapid mass loss.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that tracks the rate of mass loss, serving as the derivative of the thermogravimetric analysis curve.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4739e42903c95e1fb7e0ecfbca3a12df-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-021</data>
