</node>
<node id="120°C">
  <data key="d0">120°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">120°C is a specific calcination temperature that effectively converts most phosphogypsum into β-semi-hydrate gypsum within 60 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="60 Min">
  <data key="d0">60 Min</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">60 minutes is the optimal calcination duration at 120°C for converting phosphogypsum into β-semi-hydrate gypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lime Neutralization">
  <data key="d0">Lime Neutralization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical impurity removal technique listed for processing phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime neutralization is a cost-effective process that uses lime or alkaline substances to neutralize the acidity of phosphogypsum and remove soluble phosphorus and fluorine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Citric Acid Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Citric Acid Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical process utilized for decontaminating phosphogypsum and removing impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Citric acid treatment involves soaking phosphogypsum in citric acid solution to react with and remove phosphorus and fluorine impurities, improving microstructure and properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Xie">
  <data key="d0">Xie</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Xie found that phosphogypsum modified by limestone meets ordinary silicate cement production standards when alkali dosage is controlled.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qin">
  <data key="d0">Qin</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Qin demonstrated that calcination is more effective than chemical and physical methods, suggesting advanced techniques like temperature reduction or additives for optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773146</data>
