<node id="Whiteness">
  <data key="d0">Whiteness</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Whiteness is a quality metric of phosphogypsum that can reach up to 81% after optimized flotation treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Whiteness is a visual property of phosphogypsum that initially increases and then decreases with rising calcination temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791773399</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roughing Reverse Flotation">
  <data key="d0">Roughing Reverse Flotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Roughing reverse flotation is a specific flotation technique used to enhance the purity, yield, and whiteness of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Roughing reverse flotation is a separation technique used alongside positive flotation to enhance the purity, yield, and whiteness of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007</data>
