<node id="Stripping Process">
  <data key="d0">Stripping Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Stripping Process is a recovery technique used to extract radionuclides from the organic solvent for reuse or disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;The stripping process removes extracted radioactive materials from the organic layer using alkaline solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Stripping Process recovers extracted radionuclides from the organic solvent using an aqueous phase ratio of 2:1 over a 9-minute duration.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure using water or acidified solutions to back-extract rare earth ions from the loaded ionic liquid.&lt;SEP&gt;Stripping Process is a phase separation technique using acidified water to remove rare earth elements from the loaded ionic liquid.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009</data>
