  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBP-TOPO">
  <data key="d0">TBP-TOPO</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">TBP-TOPO is a solvent mixture used to extract radioactive materials and rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical mixture dissolved in kerosene used to facilitate the extraction of radioactive materials from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;TBP-TOPO is an organic extractant mixture used in kerosene to leach radionuclides from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A solvent mixture component used in the leaching process to extract radioactive isotopes and rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sequential Chemical Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Sequential Chemical Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequential Chemical Treatment is a combined procedure involving washing with sodium carbonate followed by leaching to decompose insoluble agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Sequential Chemical Treatment involves a two-step procedure using hot ammonium carbonate solution followed by TBP-TOPO in kerosene to maximize removal efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decontaminated Product">
  <data key="d0">Decontaminated Product</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Decontaminated Product is the residual material after radionuclide extraction, deemed safe for industrial applications to prepare low-cost products.&lt;SEP&gt;The final treated solid material resulting from the process, containing reduced radioactive concentrations suitable for industrial reuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acidulation of Sebaiya Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d0">Acidulation of Sebaiya Phosphate Rock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Acidulation of Sebaiya Phosphate Rock is the industrial process that generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sebaiya Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d0">Sebaiya Phosphate Rock</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Sebaiya Phosphate Rock is the raw material processed via acidulation to produce phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Applications">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industrial Applications refer to the safe, low-cost uses for the decontaminated phosphogypsum product.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial applications represent the potential uses for the decontaminated product, enabling the preparation of low-cost products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solvent">
  <data key="d0">Solvent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Solvent refers to the organic extractant mixture containing TBP-TOPO and kerosene from which radionuclides are recovered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organic Phase">
  <data key="d0">Organic Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Organic Phase is the solvent layer containing extracted radionuclides prior to stripping.&lt;SEP&gt;The ionic liquid layer that receives and holds the extracted rare earth complexes.&lt;SEP&gt;The ionic liquid phase that separates from the aqueous mixture to extract the target elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic Phase refers to the loaded ionic liquid extractant from which rare earth elements are stripped.&lt;SEP&gt;The organic phase refers to the non-aqueous liquid phase used in solvent extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;The solvent phase into which the phosphonium cation extracts the lanthanum-nitrate complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stripper">
  <data key="d0">Stripper</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Stripper is a chemical agent or solution used to easily strip radionuclides from the organic phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synergism">
  <data key="d0">Synergism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Synergism describes the enhanced extraction efficiency achieved by combining TBP-TOPO with kerosene.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extraction Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Extraction Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Extraction Efficiency is a quantitative performance metric used to evaluate the effectiveness of rare earth element recovery processes, particularly within solvent extraction systems. It measures the percentage of target rare earth elements, ions, or anionic complexes that are successfully transferred from an aqueous phase into an organic or ionic liquid phase. This metric serves as a primary indicator of how well an ionic liquid performs in capturing rare earth species during extraction, providing a direct assessment of phase transfer success and overall recovery performance.

Across various experimental conditions and over time, Extraction Efficiency typically ranges from 25% to 75%, with some experimental datasets reporting ranges between 25% and 60%. However, under optimized or specific conditions, the efficiency can reach significantly higher levels, such as up to 99% for individual elements like Lanthanum. As a primary metric in experimental graphs, it consistently tracks recovery rates to quantify the success of extraction protocols and the capability of the chosen solvent system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sum of Rare Earth Elements">
  <data key="d0">Sum of Rare Earth Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A group of elements found in phosphogypsum waste, targeted for extraction with an efficiency of 80.1% and 89.8% from PG-Se and PG-AT samples respectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Sum of Rare Earth Elements is a chemical group whose extraction efficiency tracks closely with Lead-210.&lt;SEP&gt;Sum of Rare Earth Elements is a group of elements whose extraction efficiency peaks around 50.5% at 4 hours before dropping significantly.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791790789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBP-TOPO Molar Ratio">
  <data key="d0">TBP-TOPO Molar Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TBP-TOPO Molar Ratio is a key experimental parameter investigated to determine the optimum concentration for maximum removal efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;TBP-TOPO Molar Ratio represents the experimental variable defined by pairs of molar amounts of TBP and TOPO.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-005</data>
