<node id="Indirect Leaching">
  <data key="d0">Indirect Leaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indirect Leaching involves altering the microstructure of phosphogypsum to facilitate rare earth element extraction and create commercial products.&lt;SEP&gt;Indirect leaching is a recovery technique that modifies the microstructure of phosphogypsum into compounds for easier rare earth element extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Indirect leaching is the process used to obtain the nitrate leach liquid from PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Indirect Leaching is the chemical process used to extract rare earth elements from phosphogypsum to produce the leach liquor.&lt;SEP&gt;Indirect leaching is a technique overviewed for recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum via intermediate steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Indirect leaching is a proposed method for dissolving phosphogypsum to recover rare earth elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791809956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ionic Liquid">
  <data key="d0">Ionic Liquid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ionic liquid is a specialized solvent used in solvent extraction to recover rare earth elements with high efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The organic solvent phase used to extract rare earth elements from the leach solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A solvent medium used for extraction and stripping processes, capable of loading rare earth elements and nitrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Ionic Liquid is a solvent medium used to load La, Ce, and Nd ions prior to the stripping process.&lt;SEP&gt;The ionic liquid serves as an extraction medium with high capacity and affinity for rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The ionic liquid is a chemical extractant represented as [P66614][NO3] used to form neutral complexes with rare earth elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791810537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ferric Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Ferric Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ferric sulfate is a compound formed when trace iron dissolves in the ammonium sulfate solution during carbonation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811203</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Phase Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase ratio is a controlling parameter representing the volume relationship between aqueous and ionic liquid phases during extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;The volumetric ratio of the two phases used in the extraction process, maintained at 1/1 or 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stripping">
  <data key="d0">Stripping</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stripping is a subsequent process step where loaded ionic liquid is contacted with a stripping fluid to recover rare earth elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811818</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Solution">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A synthetic solution containing varied amounts of rare earth elements is used to evaluate extraction efficiencies.&lt;SEP&gt;A prepared mixture containing rare earth elements used as the aqueous phase in the extraction tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthetic solution containing rare earth elements is used to test the extraction trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811818</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RE Oxalate">
  <data key="d0">RE Oxalate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">RE Oxalate is the solid precipitate formed when oxalic acid reacts with rare earth ions in the stripping solution.&lt;SEP&gt;RE oxalate is the precipitate formed when oxalic acid reacts with rare earth ions in the stripping solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791811934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RE Oxide">
  <data key="d0">RE Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">RE oxide is the final product obtained after applying extraction and stripping parameters to the leachate.&lt;SEP&gt;RE Oxide is the final concentrated product obtained after roasting the rare earth oxalate precipitate.&lt;SEP&gt;RE oxide is the final product obtained after roasting RE oxalate, identified as having 92.67% purity.&lt;SEP&gt;RE oxide is the final extracted product achieved with a reported efficiency of 92.67% in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-edfc4dcbd74cbf0b294f83f2034b209d-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791812053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
