<node id="Halder-Wagner Method">
  <data key="d0">Halder-Wagner Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A versatile XRD model utilized alongside Scherrer's model to estimate crystallite dimensions precisely.&lt;SEP&gt;Halder-Wagner Method is a mathematical approach for analyzing diffraction data to extract particle size and strain.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique employed to analyze peak broadening as a symmetric Voigt function, addressing limitations of Gaussian and Lorentzian approximations.&lt;SEP&gt;Halder-Wagner Method is a calculation technique used to determine elastic properties and crystallite size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791834567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sahadat-Scherrer's Model">
  <data key="d0">Sahadat-Scherrer's Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sahadat-Scherrer's Model is a mathematical model used to compute crystallite size from X-ray diffraction data.&lt;SEP&gt;Sahadat-Scherrer's Model is a theoretical framework used to calculate nanoparticle size from diffraction patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-001</data>
