<node id="Strain">
  <data key="d0">Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strain is a computed mechanical property of synthesized hydroxyapatite, ranging from -0.0006 to 0.0062.&lt;SEP&gt;Lattice distortion in nanocrystals measured by the slope of UDM plots, indicating either expansion or compression.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain is a measure of deformation representing the displacement between particles in the material.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain is a microstructural property estimated using the Williamson-Hall approach and UDM.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical deformation or stress within a material, represented by epsilon in the strain broadening equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniform Deformation Model (UDM)">
  <data key="d0">Uniform Deformation Model (UDM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A modification of the Williamson–Hall method that assumes homogeneous and isotropic strain across crystallographic planes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniform Stress Deformation Model (USDM)">
  <data key="d0">Uniform Stress Deformation Model (USDM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A modified Williamson–Hall equation that accounts for anisotropic crystals by ensuring uniform lattice deformation stress with minimal microstrain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791835756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
