<node id="Hydrothermal Technique">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hydrothermal Technique is a synthesis method used to alter the crystal structure of HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthesis method involving heating mixtures in sealed autoclaves to produce PPG-derived HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesis method used to prepare PPG-derived HAp nanorods in the presence of surfactants.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrothermal technique is the synthesis method used to produce nanorod-shaped hydroxyapatite structures from waste phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthesis method used to produce hydroxyapatite microplates with controlled structural and morphological properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a52951853fd542b78835b677936c557b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-018</data>
