  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural Apatite refers to the apatite found in biological samples, used as a reference standard for synthetic hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Apatite refers to biological mineral structures found in bones and teeth, serving as a comparison baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural apatite is the biological mineral found in bones that synthesized hydroxyapatite correlates with due to carbonate content.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Apatite is a naturally occurring mineral that serves as a reference for synthetic hydroxyapatite types.</data>
