<node id="Ecotoxicity">
  <data key="d0">Ecotoxicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ecotoxicity is an impact category under ecosystem quality evaluated by the assessment method.&lt;SEP&gt;Ecotoxicity is an impact category accounting for a significant portion of the impact from air emissions and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Ecotoxicity is an impact category attributed to negative emissions in the soil amendment scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Ecotoxicity is an environmental impact category measured during the assessment of management scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Ecotoxicity refers to the harmful effects of phosphogypsum on aquatic organisms, a key focus of environmental impact studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Ecotoxicity is an environmental impact category listed in the chart's legend, associated with the color teal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791877924</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Material Transport">
  <data key="d0">Material Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Material transport is a process contributing to environmental burden, primarily involving lorry transport and fossil fuel consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Material transport is a process contributing to negative environmental impacts in the road construction scenario.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-008</data>
