</node>
<node id="Effective Cohesion">
  <data key="d0">Effective Cohesion</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Effective Cohesion is a shear test parameter used to evaluate the peak criterion of soil strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Effective Cohesion is a shear strength parameter measured at 2 KPa, indicating the pulverulent behavior of PG material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Swelling Index">
  <data key="d0">Swelling Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Swelling Index is a measurable parameter used to assess the expansion potential of soil materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter indicating swelling potential, measured at a very slight value of 0.012 for raw phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Average Particle Diameter">
  <data key="d0">Average Particle Diameter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Average Particle Diameter represents the size at which 50% of the cumulative distribution is reached, measured in mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immediate Bearing Index">
  <data key="d0">Immediate Bearing Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Immediate Bearing Index is a percentage-based metric used to assess the load-bearing capacity of pavement materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immersion Resistance Index">
  <data key="d0">Immersion Resistance Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Immersion Resistance Index is a metric used to evaluate the durability of materials when submerged in water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Friction Angle">
  <data key="d0">Internal Friction Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal Friction Angle is a shear strength parameter measured in degrees for the peak criterion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Optimum Moisture Content">
  <data key="d0">Optimum Moisture Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimum Moisture Content is the ideal water percentage for compaction tests, including modified and standard Proctor tests.&lt;SEP&gt;The water content at which a soil material achieves its maximum dry density during compaction testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimum Moisture Content is a critical moisture threshold where maximum bearing capacity is achieved, beyond which capacity drops significantly.&lt;SEP&gt;The moisture level at which maximum density is achieved, decreasing from 18.3 wt% to 17 wt% with increased compaction energy.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical parameter that decreases with the addition of SM to raw PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Dry Unit Weight">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Dry Unit Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum Dry Unit Weight is a compaction parameter measured in kN/m³ for modified and standard Proctor tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical parameter that increases with the addition of SM to raw PG.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preconsolidation Stress">
  <data key="d0">Preconsolidation Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Preconsolidation Stress is a geotechnical parameter measured in KPa indicating the maximum past stress on soil.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress parameter measured at 35 KPa, corresponding to a specific permeability coefficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress parameter that increases in E2 Mix, reflecting enhanced load-bearing resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical parameter indicating stress history, improved by SM addition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diametric Compression Strength">
  <data key="d0">Diametric Compression Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Diametric Compression Strength is a mechanical property measured in MPa to assess material resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property representing tensile strength under compression, measured during diametric compression testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanical property measured for P12 Mix, showing notable values after CM addition.&lt;SEP&gt;Diametric compression strength is a mechanical property measured in MPa, showing values like 0.18 MPa at 7 days for P12 Mix.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured mechanical property used to classify mixes and assess pavement suitability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compression Index">
  <data key="d0">Compression Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Compression Index is a parameter related to the compressibility of calcareous materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A consolidation parameter measuring settlement decline by compression, recorded at 0.25 for raw phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Compressibility parameter that decreases in E2 Mix, indicating reduced soil compressibility.&lt;SEP&gt;A geotechnical parameter indicating compressibility, improved by SM addition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791936533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
