  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XPS Analysis">
  <data key="d0">XPS Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS Analysis is a surface-sensitive technique employed to determine the chemical state and elemental composition of the sample surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical technique used to confirm the presence of oxygen vacancies.&lt;SEP&gt;A surface analysis technique where Carbon peaks are commonly observed due to surface contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;A characterization technique used to analyze the surface composition of PGI-1.4 samples reduced at specific temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS analysis is an analytical technique used to confirm the content and form of sulfur in the slag.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS analysis is utilized to determine chemical environments, oxidation states, and bonding characteristics of iron and sulfur compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1792097902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrothermal Synthesis Process">
  <data key="d0">Hydrothermal Synthesis Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrothermal Synthesis Process is the preparation method used to produce the PPG-derived Hydroxyapatite samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791964406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="P123">
  <data key="d0">P123</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">P123 is a non-ionic surfactant composed of a triblock copolymer that serves as a templating agent in the hydrothermal synthesis and modification of hydroxyapatite (HAp) samples. Frequently employed alongside CTAB, P123 is instrumental in directing particle morphology, crystallite size, and phase formation. By self-assembling into larger micelles, it effectively increases the surface area of the synthesized materials while simultaneously enhancing the overall crystallinity of the modified HAp structures.

In terms of structural development, P123 templates the growth of hydroxyapatite into nanorod and two-dimensional flaky-crystal-like architectures. However, comparative evaluations indicate that when benchmarked against CTAB, P123 yields shorter nanorods and a reduced proportion of flaky structures. This morphological difference correlates with a comparatively poor photoelectrochemical (PEC) performance relative to CTAB-based alternatives. Consequently, P123 functions as a versatile morphological director and crystallinity enhancer, though its application involves trade-offs in nanostructure dimensions and electrochemical efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791964831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Band Gap">
  <data key="d0">Band Gap</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Band gap is a structural property of hydroxyapatite that influences its light absorption capability and optoelectronic performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Band Gap is a key electronic property measured for the prepared samples, indicating their semiconducting characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-000</data>
