<node id="Oxygen Vacancies">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Vacancies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen vacancies are structural defects present in HAp, inferred from spectral peak differences and EDX data.&lt;SEP&gt;Defects in the crystal structure associated with a reduction in intensity at 3540 cm^-1 and loss of OH- ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural defects within the HAp structure that reduce optical band gap energies.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural defects in the material that act as charge traps and adsorption sites, influencing charge recombination rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxygen vacancies are structural defects that create energy levels for trapping electrons and holes, facilitating charge transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791965185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surfactant Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Surfactant Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surfactant concentration is a variable that positively correlates with the degree of crystallinity in prepared samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The varying amounts of surfactant used during synthesis, which correlates with changes in peak intensity and oxygen composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006</data>
