<node id="PPG">
  <data key="d0">PPG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Polypropylene glycol waste used as a precursor for synthesizing HAp.&lt;SEP&gt;PPG is a precursor material whose phase composition was analyzed before hydroxyapatite derivation.&lt;SEP&gt;PPG is waste polypropylene glycol converted into PPG-derived HAp through hydrothermal synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;PPG is a polymer precursor that was successfully converted into HAp during the synthesis process.&lt;SEP&gt;PPG is a precursor or derivative source for the HAp samples analyzed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002</data>
