<node id="HAp-CTAB-9">
  <data key="d0">HAp-CTAB-9</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-CTAB-9 is a specific variant of PPG-derived hydroxyapatite synthesized with a 9 wt% concentration of CTAB surfactant. This modification yields a distinct nanostructure composed primarily of well-defined one-dimensional nanorods and elongated features, combined with two-dimensional flaky structures, a morphology that arises from the specific and relatively higher surfactant concentration used during preparation. Detailed analyses have confirmed the sample's elemental and chemical bonding composition, while physical characterization indicates a BET surface area of 136.01 m²/g and a flat band potential of 0.51 V.

In terms of optoelectronic performance, HAp-CTAB-9 exhibits exceptional photocatalytic and charge transport properties. It demonstrates superior photoinduced electron-hole pair generation, high charge carrier density, and the lowest charge transfer resistance among comparable tested samples. These attributes collectively facilitate superior electron transport efficiency and result in the highest photocurrent intensity, establishing HAp-CTAB-9 as a highly effective surfactant-modified hydroxyapatite material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791965487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
