<node id="HAp-CTAB-3">
  <data key="d0">HAp-CTAB-3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-CTAB-3 is a specific variant of PPG-derived HAp synthesized with 3 wt% CTAB surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-CTAB-3 is a specific hydroxyapatite sample synthesized with 3 wt% CTAB surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesized hydroxyapatite sample formed with a shorter nanorod and flaky structure, exhibiting slight agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-CTAB-3 is a Hydroxyapatite sample synthesized with 3 wt% CTAB surfactant, included in the comparative data table.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-CTAB-3 is a synthesized sample modified with CTAB surfactant at a specific concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific variant of the HAp-CTAB sample evaluated for photocurrent density.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite sample modified with CTAB surfactant that exhibits intermediate photocurrent response and stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp-P123-3">
  <data key="d0">HAp-P123-3</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-P123-3 is a specific variant of PPG-derived HAp synthesized with 3 wt% P123 surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesized hydroxyapatite sample forming a shorter nanorod structure with more agglomeration compared to HAp-CTAB-3.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-P123-3 is a prepared hydroxyapatite sample modified with P123 surfactant at a specific concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-P123-3 is a synthesized sample modified with P123 surfactant at a specific concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific variant of the HAp-P123 sample evaluated for photocurrent density.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite sample modified with P123 surfactant that exhibits intermediate photocurrent response and stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp-P123-6">
  <data key="d0">HAp-P123-6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-P123-6 is a specific variant of PPG-derived HAp synthesized with 6 wt% P123 surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthesized hydroxyapatite sample exhibiting less agglomeration and a shorter nanorod structure.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-P123-6 is a prepared hydroxyapatite sample modified with P123 surfactant at a moderate concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;HAp-P123-6 is a synthesized sample modified with P123 surfactant at a specific concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;A hydroxyapatite sample modified with P123 surfactant that demonstrates intermediate photocurrent response and photoelectrochemical stability.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific variant of the HAp-P123 sample evaluated for photocurrent density.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pristine HAp">
  <data key="d0">Pristine HAp</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pristine HAp is a baseline variant of PPG-derived HAp synthesized without the addition of any surfactant.&lt;SEP&gt;Native hydroxyapatite derived from PPG without surfactants, characterized by an irregular, flaky shape and obvious agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Pristine HAp is a baseline Hydroxyapatite sample listed in the experimental data table for comparison of physical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Pristine HAp is the unmodified hydroxyapatite sample used as a baseline for crystallinity comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Pristine HAp refers to the unmodified hydroxyapatite sample used as a baseline for textural analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Unmodified hydroxyapatite that exhibits the lowest photocurrent response due to rapid recombination of photo-generated electrons and holes.&lt;SEP&gt;Unmodified hydroxyapatite sample used as a baseline for comparison in photocatalytic and electrical property tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAp-CTAB-6">
  <data key="d0">HAp-CTAB-6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HAp-CTAB-6 is a specific variant of hydroxyapatite synthesized from a PPG-derived precursor and modified with a CTAB surfactant at a precise concentration of 6 wt%. This formulation yields a distinct nanostructure characterized by well-defined nanorods that exhibit significantly reduced agglomeration. The controlled synthesis process ensures consistent material properties, making it a standardized sample within its class.

In terms of functional performance, HAp-CTAB-6 demonstrates an intermediate photocurrent response and stability. Electrochemical evaluations specifically record a photocurrent density of 2.5 μA cm⁻² for this variant. Due to these measurable characteristics, the sample is routinely included in comparative data tables to benchmark the structural and electrochemical properties of other hydroxyapatite formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791966148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H3 Hysteresis Loop">
  <data key="d0">H3 Hysteresis Loop</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">H3 hysteresis loop is a feature of the N2 sorption isotherms observed in the relative pressure range of 0.8–1.00.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3fd8439e859e3dd0c96328384e1761f0-chunk-010</data>
