  <data key="d0">Type I Collagen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type I collagen is a biological surface where phosphate groups can be introduced to induce mineralization.&lt;SEP&gt;Type I collagen serves as a surface substrate for the nucleation of biomimetic hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.</data>
