  <data key="d0">Glutamic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A compound whose carboxyl group and charged side chain chelate calcium ions to promote cluster formation without entering the clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Glutamic Acid is an amino acid acting as a surfactant to regulate crystal growth direction by chelating calcium ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Glutamic acid acts as a regulatory molecule influencing the growth mechanism of hydroxyapatite nanoparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
