  <data key="d2">The inner core is a structural component of the porous HA coreeshell microspheres with a diameter of about 4-6 mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outer Shell">
  <data key="d0">Outer Shell</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The outer shell is a structural component of the porous HA coreeshell microspheres with a thickness of about 0.3-0.8 mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Average Diameter">
  <data key="d0">Average Diameter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Average diameter is a physical measurement indicating the microspheres have an average size of about 7 mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Specific Surface Area">
  <data key="d0">High Specific Surface Area</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">High specific surface area is a physical property of the as-obtained microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Loading">
  <data key="d0">Drug Loading</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug loading is a process facilitated by the complex pore channels in the microspheres.&lt;SEP&gt;Drug loading refers to the capacity of the microspheres to carry therapeutic agents, showing high potential in applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slow Drug Release">
  <data key="d0">Slow Drug Release</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Slow drug release refers to the controlled delivery mechanism of the microspheres due to their special structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fine Structure">
  <data key="d0">Fine Structure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fine structure refers to the detailed morphological characteristics of the microspheres that can be regulated by the synthesis strategy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biological Performance">
  <data key="d0">Biological Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biological performance refers to the in vivo or in vitro efficacy of the microspheres, which requires further study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Release Behavior">
  <data key="d0">Drug Release Behavior</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug release behavior refers to the kinetics of drug delivery from the microspheres, which requires further investigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791985383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="L-Glutamic Acid">
  <data key="d0">L-Glutamic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">An amino acid additive used to influence the nucleation and morphology of hydroxyapatite crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;L-Glutamic Acid is an amino acid used to regulate the size and uniformity of carbonated hydroxyapatite porous microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-001</data>
