  <data key="d0">Decaphosphate Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Decaphosphate ion (P3O10 5-) is an intermediate phosphate species generated from STMP hydrolysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Phosphate Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate clusters are formed when calcium and phosphate ions reach supersaturation levels in the solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nano Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Nano Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nano clusters are self-assembled structures of apatite that accumulate to form the porous shell of the microspheres.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Porous Shell">
  <data key="d0">Porous Shell</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The porous shell is the outer layer of the HA coreeshell microspheres, formed by the accumulation of nano clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alkaline Environment">
  <data key="d0">Alkaline Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alkaline environment is created by urea hydrolysis, facilitating the nucleation and growth of HA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supersaturation Level">
  <data key="d0">Supersaturation Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Supersaturation level refers to the concentration threshold of calcium and phosphate ions required to initiate cluster formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54b92b2ad16a2528ff6a863329c5d403-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791986136</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ion Migration">
