  <data key="d0">ICP-MS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to quantify trace elements within phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-MS is a mass spectrometry technique used to analyze trace elements in the prepared phosphogypsum solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to determine the chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-MS is an analytical instrument used to determine the chemical composition of residual phases.&lt;SEP&gt;A laboratory technique used to analyze trace elements in the provided dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;ICP-MS is an analytical technique used to determine the concentration of elements in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-005</data>
