  <data key="d0">Calcium Phosphate Rock</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium phosphate rock is a Chinese rock source containing ~15% silicon dioxide that enters phosphogypsum during wet phosphoric acid production.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium phosphate rock is the raw material for phosphoric acid production, containing approximately 15% silicon dioxide in China.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-001</data>
