<node id="Decomposition Rate">
  <data key="d0">Decomposition Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Decomposition rate is a process metric decreased when liquid phases wrap phosphogypsum in the rotary kiln.&lt;SEP&gt;A calculated metric representing the decomposition ratio of calcium sulfate in the raw materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative measure of calcium sulfate breakdown over time and temperature, influenced by additives and eutectic formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Decomposition rate measures the extent of material breakdown, increasing significantly between 1200 and 1300 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-011</data>
