<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Building Materials">
  <data key="d7">27.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Building Materials and Phosphogypsum establishes construction products as the primary, high-volume, and global pathway for the resource utilization of this industrial byproduct. Phosphogypsum is extensively evaluated and employed worldwide as a raw material and integral component across the building materials sector. It is specifically recommended and utilized in the preparation of various construction supplies, including gypsum blocks, boards, cement, cement mortar, bricks, and load-bearing materials.

Beyond standard manufacturing, the integration of phosphogypsum into construction products serves multiple strategic purposes. It enhances the physical properties of the resulting materials while functioning as an effective mechanism for industrial waste management. This application provides a sustainable disposal route that actively alleviates shortages of conventional construction resources and supports closed-loop resource utilization. Consequently, the production of purified phosphogypsum for construction represents a critical industrial practice that effectively balances resource recovery with broader market demands.

Despite its established and significant role in the industry, the widespread adoption of phosphogypsum faces notable market constraints driven by public perception regarding its potential to release radioactivity into the environment. Nevertheless, through rigorous purification processes and controlled manufacturing practices, these safety concerns are effectively mitigated. As a result, the utilization of phosphogypsum in building materials remains a vital, widely implemented practice across multiple countries, continuing to support sustainable construction resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;Building materials represent the main application field for phosphogypsum in China, accounting for the majority of current utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material in the production of building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is incorporated into various building materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Building materials utilize phosphogypsum as a binding material or component.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,application sector,component of,constituent,construction,construction use,hazard,high-volume use,industrial application,industrial use,industrial utilization,low-value utilization,manufacturing,material improvement,material usage,primary application,raw material,utilization,utilization field,utilization pathway,utilization route,valorization</data>
