<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sulfuric Acid">
  <data key="d7">28.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Phosphogypsum and Sulfuric Acid is a multifaceted, bidirectional interaction that spans industrial production, resource recovery, material purification, and scientific analysis. Industrially, sulfuric acid serves as a primary reactant that digests and dissolves phosphate rock or ore to produce phosphoric acid. This chemical process yields phosphogypsum as a solid waste byproduct. Due to the reaction dynamics, phosphogypsum naturally retains unreacted or residual sulfuric acid, which functions as a key acidic substance and directly imparts an acidic character to the material.

This compositional link establishes a practical industrial cycle where phosphogypsum acts as a foundational feedstock for sulfuric acid recovery and co-production. Through established methodologies such as thermal decomposition, wet decomposition, and solid-solid reaction technologies, the residual acid is extracted to yield commercial-grade sulfuric acid. Additionally, elemental sulfur can be recovered from phosphogypsum via microbiological processes and subsequently converted into sulfuric acid, reinforcing the material's traditional and contemporary role in acid production.

Beyond production and recovery, sulfuric acid is extensively utilized to treat and purify phosphogypsum for broader applications. Acid leaching with sulfuric acid efficiently extracts valuable rare earth elements, particularly when applied to pre-treated phosphogypsum, while simultaneously removing hazardous impurities and contaminants. This purification process enables the safe and economically advantageous utilization of phosphogypsum in construction sectors, including cement manufacturing and road building. In analytical and research contexts, diluted sulfuric acid is employed to evaluate the solubility constants of phosphogypsum, supporting the scientific characterization of the material. Together, these interactions highlight a dynamic relationship where sulfuric acid drives both the formation and the valorization of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is used to chemically attack phosphate ores to produce phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric Acid is used to process phosphogypsum in conventional rare earth recovery techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as the foundational material for the joint preparation process that yields sulfuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfuric acid is synthesized from sulfur recovered through phosphogypsum decomposition processes.</data>
  <data key="d9">acid leaching,application,by-product,chemical composition,chemical conversion,chemical industry,chemical production,chemical property,chemical reagent,chemical synthesis,co-product,co-production,composition,contains,contains residual chemical,conventional technique,decomposition,digestion,extraction,extraction agent,extraction process,impurity removal,leaching,processing,product derivation,production,production by-product,production process,production reactant,production source,purification,raw material,resource recovery,solubility testing,solvent,treated by,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-009</data>
