<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Cement">
  <data key="d7">26.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Cement and Phosphogypsum encompasses a multifaceted industrial application where phosphogypsum functions as both a foundational raw material and a specialized additive in construction chemistry. Chemically, phosphogypsum serves as a primary source of calcium oxide and a reactive material that interacts with water. In Portland cement manufacturing, it is specifically employed to stabilize the cement matrix, act as a set retarder or regulator, and modulate the hydration process to optimize workability and curing characteristics. Beyond traditional cement production, processed, neutralized, or pre-treated phosphogypsum is extensively integrated as a supplementary component and partial substitute across various binder formulations, mortar mixtures, and concrete applications. When mixed with cement, it can form a high-activity binder, though the use of impure phosphogypsum is known to reduce clinker strength. Additionally, processed phosphogypsum is utilized as an additive during cement grinding.

Empirical studies indicate that phosphogypsum can successfully replace up to 10% of cement in construction mixtures while maintaining required structural properties. Although phosphogypsum has been historically utilized and is actively proposed for large-scale adoption as a sustainable, resource-efficient alternative, its widespread commercial promotion is currently hindered by technical bottlenecks. To mitigate these challenges and facilitate broader industrial integration, phosphogypsum is frequently combined with other solid wastes, highlighting its evolving role as a valuable, eco-friendly resource in modern cementitious systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is used in the chemical industry to co-produce cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum replaces natural gypsum as a cement retarder, affecting setting time and compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement production is identified as a potential future valorization method for phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,application pathway,cement retarder,co-production,component,construction,future research target,historical use,industrial application,material alternative,material integration,material modification,material production,material replacement,material substitution,mixing,modification,partial replacement,performance modification,production,raw material,reactivity,replacement,set retardation,stabilization,strength impact,substitution,valorization</data>
