<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Potassium Sulfate">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and Potassium Sulfate are linked by a chemical relation that defines the industrial pathway through which phosphogypsum is transformed into potassium sulfate. In this process, phosphogypsum functions primarily as a raw material and a dedicated sulfur source. The conversion is achieved through multiple chemical methodologies, including co-reaction processes, wet conversion techniques, and general chemical synthesis methods. These approaches enable the efficient extraction and production of potassium sulfate from the phosphogypsum feedstock.

Within the broader chemical industry, this transformation is utilized to manufacture potassium sulfate, a compound that is frequently applied as an agricultural fertilizer. By leveraging phosphogypsum as a foundational input, the process not only facilitates the synthesis of potassium sulfate but also demonstrates a practical method for the industrial valorization of phosphogypsum into commercially useful chemical products.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,chemical conversion,chemical extraction,chemical industry,chemical production,product manufacturing,production,production source,production target,sulfur source,utilization</data>
