<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Chemical Looping Gasification">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Chemical Looping Gasification, in relation to Phosphogypsum, is a specialized thermochemical process applied to treat and utilize this industrial byproduct. Within this system, Phosphogypsum functions as an oxygen carrier, facilitating the core gasification reactions. Specifically, the process employs Phosphogypsum as the oxygen carrier to convert lignite into syngas, thereby integrating waste valorization with clean energy generation.

Beyond fuel conversion, the use of Phosphogypsum as an oxygen carrier in Chemical Looping Gasification is critical for managing the behavior of fluorine and phosphorus compounds. By controlling these elements during the reaction, the process mitigates potential environmental hazards and improves operational efficiency. This application effectively transforms a problematic waste material into a functional component of a sustainable gasification technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum acts as a feedstock for chemical looping gasification processes.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,application method,energy conversion,energy process,feedstock,fuel conversion,industrial application,oxygen carrier,thermochemical conversion</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792099328</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Ammonium Sulfate">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Ammonium Sulfate and Phosphogypsum describes the industrial process of converting phosphogypsum waste into ammonium sulfate. In this chemical synthesis, phosphogypsum serves as the primary raw material and feedstock. The conversion is typically achieved using ammonium hydroxide through a specialized two-step ammonia-carbonation process, during which ammonium sulfate is recovered as a valuable by-product or secondary chemical compound. Because the industrial conversion involves the controlled flow of radionuclides, the process requires careful technical management to ensure both safety and operational efficiency.

From an economic and industrial standpoint, the production of ammonium sulfate from phosphogypsum waste is utilized within the chemical industry to transform an industrial waste stream into a commercially viable product. This application strongly supports circular economy principles by addressing waste management and resource recovery objectives. However, the synthesized ammonium sulfate operates within a competitive market landscape, frequently competing with cheaper alternative products that are also derived from broader phosphogypsum recycling efforts. Despite these market challenges, the relationship underscores a sustainable and economically strategic method for valorizing phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as the primary raw material for synthesizing ammonium sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d9">by-product recovery,chemical conversion,chemical conversion product,chemical industry,chemical preparation,chemical process,chemical synthesis,co-production,competition,conversion,industrial byproduct,preparation,product manufacturing,production,production input,production source,production target,raw material,recycling challenge,synthesis,utilization,waste utilization</data>
