<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Fly Ash">
  <data key="d7">21.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Fly Ash and Phosphogypsum centers on their combined use to enhance material properties, facilitate industrial waste reuse, and support sustainable construction and environmental applications. Fly Ash is primarily utilized to stabilize Phosphogypsum, significantly improving its strength, durability, and physical characteristics, which makes the composite highly suitable for infrastructure projects such as road construction. This synergistic pairing is frequently expanded by incorporating additional additives like lime or steel slag to further optimize mechanical performance and mitigate greenhouse gas emissions from agricultural fields. The combination is extensively studied and applied in the production of bricks and other building products, with research consistently comparing and evaluating their performance in these applications.

Scientific investigations also explore the composite's behavior under magnetic fields and its broader material science potential, highlighting the synergistic value of pairing these two industrial byproducts. However, the interaction presents specific technical challenges; impurities present in Phosphogypsum can inhibit the pozzolanic reaction of Fly Ash during the later curing stages, necessitating careful formulation management. Despite this constraint, the Fly Ash and Phosphogypsum relationship remains a promising avenue for transforming waste materials into valuable construction resources while advancing material research and environmental sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is combined with treated phosphogypsum and lime for building applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is blended with fly ash to produce construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is blended with treated phosphogypsum to form strong cementitious bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is used as a stabilizer combined with phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly Ash is mixed with lime and phosphogypsum to create tested pavement layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is blended with Fly Ash to modify the properties of the mix.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive combination,application,blending,brick production,cementitious bond,chemical interaction,combination,combined application,combined use,comparative study,complementary material,composite formation,composition,construction application,formulation,industrial combination,inhibition,material blending,material combination,material composition,mitigation,mixing,stabilization,stabilizing additive,strength enhancement</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002</data>
