<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Thermal Treatment">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Phosphogypsum, Thermal Treatment) describes a current processing method utilized to alter the properties of phosphogypsum. This technique is primarily applied to modify the material's structural and chemical characteristics. A key objective of the process is the removal of phosphorus pentoxide (P2O5) and other specific components from the raw material.

During thermal treatment, phosphogypsum undergoes significant transformations, including mass loss, chemical decomposition, and the elimination of water of crystallization. These physical and chemical changes result in distinct structural modifications and alter the material's diffraction pattern. Despite its effectiveness in achieving these material modifications, the process is recognized as being expensive, which influences its practical implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal treatment is applied to phosphogypsum to alter its properties for use in Portland slag cement.</data>
  <data key="d9">current method,pretreatment,process application,processing,processing method,property alteration,property modification,purification,structural change,subject,subjected to,transformation,treated by</data>
