<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphorus Pentoxide">
  <data key="d7">20.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Phosphogypsum and Phosphorus Pentoxide is defined by a complex industrial and chemical interdependence. Phosphogypsum is generated as a byproduct during the extraction of phosphorus pentoxide, yet the material retains a significant portion of this compound. Phosphorus pentoxide constitutes a major component of the phosphogypsum matrix, representing its overall phosphorus content and generally existing at concentrations higher than those of fluorine. Specific analyses indicate a phosphorus pentoxide content of 0.50% within the material. Despite being a primary chemical constituent, it is simultaneously characterized as a soluble impurity and contaminant.

This dual status presents both challenges and opportunities for industrial processing. As a contaminant, phosphorus pentoxide influences functional properties such as retarder action and is typically targeted for elimination or reduction through specific treatment processes to ensure the safe reuse of phosphogypsum. In certain applications, its concentration may be considered low, which necessitates the addition of supplementary phosphorus sources. Conversely, rather than being entirely discarded, the entrained phosphorus pentoxide can be effectively recovered alongside rare earth elements through sulfuric acid cycle leaching processes. This multifaceted interaction highlights how a residual byproduct component functions both as a managed impurity and as a recoverable resource within chemical and industrial cycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus pentoxide is a major impurity component contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Phosphorus Pentoxide as a minor constituent at 1.56 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus pentoxide is a component of phosphogypsum at 1.45 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus pentoxide is present in low amounts in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains phosphorus pentoxide as a component.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical analysis,chemical composition,chemical compound,composition,contains,contains impurity,contamination,impurity,limitation,phosphorus content,phosphorus source,production byproduct,retarder effect,waste composition,weight percentage</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2760dc2a11fedad02d24741a978cf20d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35aef6efc801611130c5dd196fe513df-chunk-001</data>
