<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Calcium">
  <data key="d7">23.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Calcium and Phosphogypsum centers on calcium's role as a primary, dominant, and predominant chemical constituent within the material. It consistently appears as a major element, accounting for over ninety percent of the substance alongside sulfur, with specific analytical measurements recording a concentration of 38.14 ± 1.70. This consistent presence serves as a key identifier for confirming phosphogypsum's identity. Within the compound, calcium is frequently characterized as chemically activated, which enhances its overall reactivity and utility. From a processing standpoint, calcium can be successfully extracted from phosphogypsum using a preparative vertical-flow electrophoresis system.

In environmental and chemical contexts, the leaching characteristics of calcium within phosphogypsum are actively studied, particularly under acid rain conditions. Additionally, calcium ions within the structure can be replaced by rare earth elements through isomorph substitution. In agricultural and environmental applications, phosphogypsum functions as a significant calcium source for plant nutrition. When utilized as a soil amendment, it plays a vital role in soil reclamation by displacing excess sodium and hydrogen ions, thereby facilitating soil improvement. Collectively, these attributes highlight calcium's integral chemical presence in phosphogypsum and its practical value in material verification, industrial processing, and sustainable soil management.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains a considerable amount of Calcium, which is beneficial for generating hydration elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium is a major chemical species analyzed in the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium concentration in phosphogypsum decreased by 22% following the leaching process.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is chemically composed of calcium as a major element.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium is a major component widely distributed throughout the phosphogypsum matrix.</data>
  <data key="d9">agricultural component,chemical activation,chemical analysis,chemical component,chemical composition,chemical constituent,chemical extraction,chemical structure,composition,concentration analysis,confirmation,contains,distribution,dominance,elemental makeup,hydration,leaching,leaching effect,major component,major element,major species,measurement,nutrient source,nutrient supply,predominant element,primary composition,primary constituent,resource recovery,soil supplementation,source,substitution target</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-025</data>
