<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphate Rock and Phosphogypsum is defined by an industrial manufacturing process in which phosphate rock serves as the primary raw material. During the chemical processing of this rock within phosphoric acid factories, phosphoric acid is synthesized, and phosphogypsum is generated as a direct byproduct. This production pathway establishes a direct material dependency, where the extraction and processing of phosphate rock inherently yield phosphogypsum as a secondary output.

The physical and chemical characteristics of the resulting phosphogypsum are fundamentally shaped by the specific type of phosphate rock utilized. The mineralogical, chemical, and overall mineral composition of the byproduct vary significantly depending on the geological source of the rock. Additionally, phosphogypsum inherits various impurities and radioactive content directly from the phosphate rock, meaning its final properties and purity levels are intrinsically tied to the quality and composition of the original raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rock is digested with sulfuric acid to convert it into phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is generated as a waste by-product when phosphate rock is processed with sulfuric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate rock is a natural mineral source closely associated with phosphogypsum production in fertilizer factories.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains unreacted phosphate rock.&lt;SEP&gt;The composition of phosphate rock influences the morphology of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is a waste byproduct generated during the industrial processing of phosphate rock.</data>
  <data key="d9">byproduct generation,composition,composition dependency,composition variation,conversion,geological origin,impurity source,industrial association,industrial by-product,industrial byproduct,industrial origin,mineralogical variation,morphological factor,production by-product,production source,raw material,raw material influence,source material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-007</data>
