<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Thorium">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and thorium are intrinsically linked through the industrial processing of phosphate materials, particularly during sulfuric and phosphoric acid manufacturing. Naturally occurring thorium, primarily Thorium-232, is partitioned during this production cycle, with approximately 70% of the original thorium content transferring to the phosphoric acid product, while the remaining 30% is retained in the phosphogypsum byproduct. Within phosphogypsum, thorium is present at trace concentrations, typically measured around 10 ppm. Scientific analyses reveal that thorium exhibits a strong preferential retention and incorporation tendency, particularly within the coarse grain size fractions of the material. This distinct partitioning across grain sizes, alongside other naturally occurring radioactive elements, necessitates thorough characterization to ensure safe handling and disposal.

Regarding its behavior within the phosphogypsum matrix, thorium demonstrates high retention and low to intermediate mobility. Its movement is significantly restricted due to the formation of insoluble complexes, meaning that thorium remains tightly bound within the material and generally requires full matrix dissolution for release. As a radioactive element, the presence of thorium in phosphogypsum poses notable environmental risks, underscoring the critical need for strict management protocols throughout its lifecycle to mitigate potential hazards associated with its long-term storage and disposal.</data>
  <data key="d9">accumulation,byproduct composition,composition,contains,dissolution requirement,distribution,grain size preference,hazard,impurity,management,mobility,mobility classification,mobilization,occurrence,preferential retention,presence,radioactive content,radioactive distribution,radioactive retention,radionuclide content,radionuclide distribution,recovery,retention,trace composition,trace element,waste accumulation</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013</data>
