<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Portland Cement">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and Portland Cement share a manufacturing and chemical relationship wherein phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material and additive in cement production. Processed into purified or weathered forms, phosphogypsum serves as a direct substitute for natural gypsum and is incorporated into Portland cement production to act as a set retarder. This application allows manufacturers to precisely adjust setting times while simultaneously lowering the required clinkerization temperature.

Chemically, the soluble components within phosphogypsum actively influence the hydration process of Portland cement, which directly impacts its setting behavior and overall mechanical properties. While the additive effectively modulates the setting rate, it is documented to considerably reduce the final compressive strength of the resulting cement. Beyond these technical modifications, phosphogypsum is also integrated into cement-based materials to support eco-efficient construction practices, underscoring its value as both a performance-adjusting agent and a sustainable industrial byproduct in the cement industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement hydration is studied in relation to the addition of phosphogypsum as a setting retarder.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum can be combined with Portland cement and fly ash for reuse in the building industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a set retarder in Portland cement manufacturing.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is utilized as a raw material in the production of Portland cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Treated phosphogypsum is compared to Portland cement based on calcium oxide content.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,comparison,construction application,construction valorization,hydration interaction,hydration study,industrial combination,material application,material compatibility,material interaction,material substitution,production,property alteration,property modification,raw material,raw material for,retarder,set retarder</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006</data>
