<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Organic Matter">
  <data key="d7">14.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Organic Matter and Phosphogypsum centers on the presence, characterization, and management of organic matter as a significant impurity within phosphogypsum solids. Organic matter is recognized as a distinct chemical component and a category of undesirable contaminants that is routinely measured in phosphogypsum samples. It exists as both a residual and soluble impurity, necessitating targeted removal strategies. To mitigate its presence, organic matter can be effectively reduced through citric acid treatment and washing processes. However, its persistence poses notable challenges, as it interferes with industrial processing and significantly hinders the material's reuse in construction applications.

Beyond industrial and processing concerns, organic matter also presents environmental implications when associated with phosphogypsum. It tends to accumulate in the vicinity of phosphogypsum storage or disposal sites, where it degrades local soil quality by diminishing nutrient retention and supply capacity. This accumulation affects surrounding ecosystems and limits the environmental sustainability of phosphogypsum handling. Overall, the interaction between organic matter and phosphogypsum highlights a critical impurity that requires careful monitoring, treatment, and environmental management to optimize industrial utility and minimize ecological impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains organic matter as a harmful impurity.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter includes inherent substances and additives attached to phosphogypsum surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is an impurity contained in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains organic matter like amines and ketones adhered to its crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is associated with phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">causes accumulation,chemical analysis,chemical composition,composition,contains,contains contaminants,contains impurity,impurity,impurity classification,impurity composition,impurity content,limitation,reduces fertility</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000</data>
