<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate Fertilizer Production">
  <data key="d7">16.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Phosphate Fertilizer Production, Phosphogypsum) defines a direct industrial output where the manufacturing process of phosphate fertilizers yields phosphogypsum as a byproduct. This relationship highlights that phosphogypsum is generated as an inherent and unavoidable outcome of the production workflow, resulting from the chemical transformations that occur during phosphate processing. Consequently, phosphogypsum is consistently identified as a major byproduct of the phosphate fertilizer industry, with substantial volumes produced alongside primary fertilizer outputs.

This documented connection underscores a direct causal relationship between phosphate fertilizer manufacturing and the resulting phosphogypsum stream. Regional trends further illustrate this dynamic, as the rise in phosphate fertilizer production has directly driven significant increases in phosphogypsum generation, notably observed in China where expanded fertilizer manufacturing activities correspond to substantial growth in phosphogypsum output.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is generated as a byproduct of phosphate fertilizer production.</data>
