<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Fluorides">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Fluorides, Phosphogypsum) encompasses the presence of fluorides as significant chemical impurities within the phosphogypsum matrix. These fluorides originate as residues from the wet processing of rock phosphate and are found in phosphogypsum solids primarily as various sodium and calcium compounds. Recognized as primary potentially toxic elements among the material's chemical constituents, fluorides are inherently embedded in the industrial byproduct.

Due to their classification as potentially toxic elements, fluorides pose substantial ecological pollution risks, necessitating their removal to ensure the material complies with established safety and quality standards. Environmental research actively investigates the behavior of these fluorides in natural settings, particularly examining fluoride sorption and mineral stability in soils that interact with phosphogypsum leachate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains fluorides as chemical impurities from the production process.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,chemical impurity,composition,contains,contains impurity,impurity,impurity content,leachate interaction,primary component,sorption,toxicity</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1adcb38defdd04a271ddba318999ba67-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000</data>
