<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Hemihydrate Process">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum is produced as a byproduct of the hemihydrate process for phosphoric acid manufacture.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process yields phosphogypsum with relatively high impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process yields phosphogypsum with a higher uranium content of 5 to 100 μg/g due to its crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;This process is a source reduction technology developed to improve phosphorus recycling rates and enhance phosphogypsum quality.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process used in phosphoric acid manufacturing influences the crystal shapes of phosphogypsum.</data>
