<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Radioactive Elements">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and radioactive elements are intrinsically linked through the presence of naturally occurring, trace hazardous impurities within the industrial byproduct. Derived from the processing of phosphate rocks, phosphogypsum inherently contains radioactive components, particularly radium and uranium, with concentrations varying based on the geological origin of the source material.

These radioactive elements pose significant environmental and health risks, as their release during phosphogypsum applications can lead to soil contamination, impaired plant growth, and adverse effects on human health. Consequently, the presence of these radionuclides substantially restricts the practical application and widespread utilization of phosphogypsum. To mitigate these hazards, specialized management strategies are required, including fixation methods and harmless treatment processes designed to immobilize the radioactive impurities and prevent their uptake into the surrounding environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Radioactive elements are present in trace amounts in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">application limitation,composition,contains hazard,contamination,environmental impact,environmental risk,fixation requirement,hazardous component,impurity,impurity composition,monitoring,toxic uptake</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-160a0fe95f7c82b193c6af751106ab6d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791938501</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Uranium-238">
  <data key="d7">20.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and Uranium-238 share a direct relationship defined by the presence of this radioactive isotope as a naturally occurring component within the industrial byproduct, originating from radioactive decay chains. This inherent presence classifies Uranium-238 as a radioactive contaminant that significantly shapes the material's overall radiological profile. The concentration and activity of Uranium-238 in phosphogypsum are not uniform; they fluctuate based on specific operational conditions at phosphoric acid plants and are notably higher within coarse particle fractions. Reported activity levels vary considerably, with documented concentrations ranging from 9.0 Bq/kg to 164 ± 12.5 Bq/kg.

Due to these radiological characteristics, phosphogypsum serves as a primary source material for extracting Uranium-238, though its natural contamination necessitates purification processes to ensure safe industrial application. Consequently, the isotope is routinely quantified and tracked during radiological and trace element assessments. Researchers measure Uranium-238 activity concentrations, often employing conversion factors derived from Uranium-235 to ensure accuracy, to monitor its distribution and the migration of its daughter isotopes. These analytical efforts are critical for managing the associated radiological implications, particularly regarding leaching risks posed by Uranium-238 and other uranium isotopes. Furthermore, environmental monitoring reveals that long-term amendments using phosphogypsum can lead to the accumulation of Uranium-238 in reclaimed marsh soils, underscoring the need for careful management of this industrial material.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity concentration,analysis,component of,composition,contains,environmental contamination,extraction target,isotopic measurement,material,measured concentration,measured in,measurement,presence,radioactive component,radioactive content,radioactive source,radioactivity analysis,radiological analysis,radiometric analysis,radionuclide,sample measurement,soil accumulation,source,source material,trace element analysis,variable content</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791792257</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Radium-226">
  <data key="d7">29.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphogypsum and Radium-226 centers on the latter's role as a naturally occurring, entrained radioactive contaminant and the primary source of radioactivity within the former. Originating from phosphate rock, Radium-226 is generated through the alpha decay of Thorium-230 and becomes significantly enriched during the chemical production of phosphogypsum. During this process, it preferentially accumulates and coprecipitates with calcium sulfate, with approximately 80 to 90 percent of the radionuclide retained in the material. Consequently, phosphogypsum serves as a primary source material for extracting Radium-226, while its high radioactivity simultaneously necessitates purification for safe industrial applications.

Activity concentrations of Radium-226 in phosphogypsum vary significantly across different regions and are routinely quantified as part of trace element analyses and particle fraction assessments. Measured levels range widely, with documented values including 22 Bq/kg and 482 ± 13.2 Bq/kg. These concentrations frequently exceed European Commission safety limits and surpass typical activity levels found in fly ash and natural soil. Due to these elevated levels, Radium-226 remains a central focus of environmental monitoring and regulatory assessment.

When phosphogypsum is utilized in land applications, such as long-term soil amendments, Radium-226 can leach into the environment and accumulate in various soils, including reclaimed marsh ecosystems. Under specific environmental conditions, the radionuclide dissolves and increases overall soil radioactivity, leading to its subsequent uptake and measurement in agricultural crops. This mobility underscores the critical importance of tracking the distribution and concentration of Radium-226 throughout the soil-plant system to mitigate environmental and agricultural impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum retains approximately 80% of Radium-226 from the phosphoric acid process.</data>
  <data key="d9">accumulation,analysis,byproduct composition,chemical property,component of,composition,concentration comparison,contains,decay product,dissolution,enrichment,environmental contamination,extraction target,found in,geochemical distribution,isotopic measurement,major component,measured concentration,measured in,measurement,partitioning,radioactive component,radioactive content,radioactive retention,radioactive source,radioactivity analysis,radioactivity measurement,radioactivity source,radiometric analysis,radionuclide,regulatory exceedance,retention,sample measurement,soil accumulation,source,source material,trace element analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4a551024f80f822f3f35e38ec278151-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791917532</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Lead-210">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lead-210 and phosphogypsum are linked by a relationship that defines Lead-210 as a radioactive contaminant and isotope present within phosphogypsum. Lead-210 is primarily incorporated into the phosphogypsum matrix through coprecipitation with calcium sulfate, accounting for approximately 80–90% of its retention. Analytical protocols consistently measure and quantify Lead-210 activity concentrations across various phosphogypsum samples.

The isotope exhibits moderate concentration fluctuations throughout the material, with notably higher activity levels concentrated in the coarse fractions. Furthermore, due to its radioactive nature, Lead-210 in phosphogypsum is actively assessed for bioavailability, particularly when phosphogypsum is evaluated for use as a soil amendment.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead-210 is monitored in phosphogypsum to track radioelement concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum naturally contains Lead-210, which necessitates purification for safe industrial use.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Lead-210 at a concentration of 418 ± 11.7 Bq/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum naturally contains lead-210 as a radioactive contaminant.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as the primary source material from which Lead-210 is extracted.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,component of,composition,concentration tracking,contains,coprecipitates in,extraction target,measured in,measurement,radioactive content,radioactivity,radioactivity analysis,radioelement monitoring,radiometric analysis,radionuclide,sample measurement,source,source material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d18c456289f64c1e16c73a0dfd6595b3-chunk-007</data>
