<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="P2O5">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">P2O5 is a chemical constituent in phosphogypsum that investigators aimed to mitigate.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 comprises less than 1% of phosphogypsum material, but high application rates increase available soil phosphorus.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a component of phosphogypsum that provides essential soil nutrients and benefits agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains P2O5, which is beneficial for agriculture without requiring purification.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 represents a quantified impurity component with an average mass fraction of 1.31%.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains P2O5, which exists in various forms like H3PO4 and Ca(H2PO4)2.H2O4.</data>
