  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Nitric acid is studied as a strong acid leaching agent to extract rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric acid serves as a diluted acidic medium to study phosphogypsum solubility and leaching efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric Acid was used in the acid digestion process to prepare Phosphogypsum samples for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitric Acid is used to process phosphogypsum in conventional rare earth recovery techniques.</data>
