<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Table 2">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Table 2, which documents comprehensive data related to Phosphogypsum, provides a detailed chemical assessment of the material. It outlines the weight percentages of major chemical species and impurities present in raw phosphogypsum, while also detailing the specific types and primary forms of these impurities. Supplementary chemical composition data for typical phosphogypsum samples is included to further characterize the substance.

The table also addresses environmental and safety considerations by presenting leaching data and toxicity results for phosphogypsum. Specifically, it summarizes leaching measurements from samples sourced in Hubei, Yunnan, and Guizhou provinces, alongside broader leaching toxicity assessments.

In addition to chemical and environmental metrics, Table 2 covers physical and thermal properties. It documents the geotechnical properties and associated measurements for phosphogypsum samples. Furthermore, it summarizes the kinetic parameters governing phosphogypsum dehydration, including the maximum reaction rate, operating temperature, and required time.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 presents the average chemical composition of phosphogypsum samples in weight percent.</data>
