<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Ra-226">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Major amounts of Ra-226 remain in phosphogypsum solid wastes after processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Ra-226 partitions primarily into phosphogypsum and is the largest source of radioactivity in the material.&lt;SEP&gt;Ra-226 is present in airborne particulate matter from phosphogypsum stacks and measured for environmental impact assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Ra-226, which is the main source of radioactivity in the waste product.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains significant amounts of Ra-226, contributing to its radiological profile.&lt;SEP&gt;Ra-226 is a radioactive isotope naturally present in phosphogypsum, prompting safety and mobility studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Ra-226 is a radioactive substance present in PG that restricts its utilization in the United States.</data>
