<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Potassium-40">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains Potassium-40 alongside other natural radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Potassium-40 at a concentration of 11 Bq/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum naturally contains Potassium-40, which necessitates purification for safe industrial use.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Potassium-40 at a concentration of 72 ± 4.9 Bq/kg.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum naturally contains potassium-40 as a radioactive contaminant.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as the primary source material from which Potassium-40 is extracted.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium-40 contributes minimally to the overall radioactivity measured in phosphogypsum.</data>
