<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Cemented Paste Backfill">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Cemented Paste Backfill and Phosphogypsum centers on the integration of phosphogypsum as a primary constituent and raw material within cemented paste backfill systems, primarily utilized for mining and construction applications. In this process, phosphogypsum is typically subjected to purification or water-washing pre-treatment to remove impurities and optimize the mixture's structural integrity. Following treatment, phosphogypsum functions predominantly as a primary aggregate and filler, though it may also contribute to the binding matrix, with its inherent physical and chemical characteristics directly governing the mechanical performance and stability of the resulting backfill.

This application serves a dual purpose by addressing geotechnical requirements and advancing environmental remediation objectives. Specifically, cemented paste backfill technology provides an effective in-situ management strategy for phosphogypsum stockpiles, facilitating the secure immobilization and storage of the material while balancing industrial utility with ecological risk mitigation. The stabilized matrix effectively retains hazardous pollutants, particularly phosphorus and fluorine, thereby preventing environmental contamination. Collectively, the utilization of phosphogypsum in cemented paste backfill represents a sustainable engineering approach that transforms a hazardous industrial byproduct into a functional construction material while simultaneously mitigating exposure risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Citric acid pre-treated phosphogypsum is used to enhance the performance of cemented paste backfill.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,component,composition,construction use,industrial application,management,material application,material composition,material improvement,mining application,mining waste management,mixture formulation,pollutant retention,raw material,remediation,retention,storage application,utilization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2674917fb6c60e75303effeaa10768e-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791775071</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Ordinary Portland Cement">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ordinary Portland cement serves as the primary binder for treating phosphogypsum, facilitating its solidification and stabilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is frequently blended with ordinary portland cement in binder formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw phosphogypsum can be used directly in the production of ordinary Portland cement.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified phosphogypsum is applied as an additive or component in ordinary portland cement.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,binder,construction,material application,material composition,remediation</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-018</data>
