<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Concrete">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Concrete and phosphogypsum share a relationship centered on the integration of phosphogypsum as a supplementary material, additive, or partial replacement for cement within cement-based concrete production. Concrete, a foundational construction material, increasingly utilizes recycled phosphogypsum as a raw material to modify its physical and mechanical properties. This application is primarily driven by ongoing research aimed at enhancing material performance and exploring sustainable construction practices.

Scientific investigations focus on creating concrete specimens that incorporate phosphogypsum to systematically evaluate its impact on workability and structural integrity. Experimental testing has demonstrated that mixing phosphogypsum into concrete batches at an optimal content level of approximately 12% effectively maximizes compressive strength. Consequently, phosphogypsum is actively studied and experimentally validated as a viable partial replacement for traditional cement in concrete mixtures, confirming its potential as a functional and efficient additive in modern concrete production.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,component,composite material,composition,construction use,manufacturing,material additive,material application,material substitution,partial replacement,potential use,strength optimization,structural application</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
