<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher phosphogypsum fractions decrease the compressive strength of construction materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The addition of phosphogypsum influences compressive strength, optimizing it at 10% substitution but reducing it at higher levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The compressive strength of bricks peaks at 75% phosphogypsum content, reaching 21.8 MPa.&lt;SEP&gt;Increasing PG content reduces the mechanical strength of minibricks, though they remain above industry norms.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum significantly impacts the compressive strength of cement mortar, with effects varying by concentration and composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum replacement levels significantly impact the compressive strength of mortar specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Addition of phosphogypsum increases the compressive strength of adobe samples.</data>
