<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains phosphates that are often fixed with metals, reducing their bioavailability.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate is a key component of phosphogypsum that can enhance crop fertility but risks causing eutrophication.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains phosphate as a soluble impurity that affects industrial processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphates alter the crystal structure of phosphogypsum, which is detrimental to setting and hardening processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate in the form of Ca(PO3)2 contributed 0.2% to the overall constituents in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate exists in raw phosphogypsum as Ca(PO3)2.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,composition,constituent,contribution,detrimental effect,fixation,impurity,morphology alteration,nutrient source,percentage</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791918459</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
