<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sulfate">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sulfate is a primary chemical constituent of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfate is a dominant ion in the chemical composition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Excess sulfate enhances the partitioning of uranium into the gypsum crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains sulfate ions that can be extracted into aqueous solutions.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,contains,enhanced partitioning,extraction target</data>
