<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Flotation">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Flotation for phosphogypsum is a developed pretreatment and purification technique designed to enhance the material's quality. The process primarily separates gypsum from phosphogypsum while effectively eliminating organic debris, fine mud, and other organic contaminants, typically through a scraping mechanism. When implemented alongside lime, the flotation method also reduces phosphorus and fluorine concentrations within the phosphogypsum. Beyond chemical purification, the technique is specifically employed to whiten and further refine the material, making it a comprehensive purification approach.

Despite its established theoretical framework and demonstrated efficacy, flotation for phosphogypsum currently remains predominantly at the laboratory scale. The technology faces significant scalability challenges that hinder its transition to large-scale industrial deployment. Consequently, while the method successfully addresses multiple contamination issues and improves material properties, its widespread commercial application is still constrained by practical implementation barriers that require further research and optimization.</data>
  <data key="d9">organic removal,pretreatment,purification,purification method,purification technique,purification technology,scalability challenge,separation,treatment target</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
