<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Chromium">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Chromium and Phosphogypsum indicates that phosphogypsum contains chromium as a trace element and potential toxic heavy metal impurity. This chromium exists as heavy metal ions that can be released into the environment, posing environmental risks and contributing to contamination. Despite these potential hazards, tabular data indicates that chromium concentrations in phosphogypsum generally remain below the rare effect concentration.

From a processing perspective, chromium exhibits high liquid/solid fractionation during leaching, meaning it readily partitions into the liquid phase when exposed to water. Consequently, this element can be effectively eliminated from phosphogypsum through simple water washing. Overall, the association highlights both the environmental considerations of chromium presence in phosphogypsum and the straightforward remediation methods available for its removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is the sample matrix analyzed to determine the percentage content of chromium.</data>
  <data key="d9">analytical target,composition,contains,elimination,fractionation,hazard,presence,sample composition,threshold compliance,toxic metal,trace content,water washing</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-60e237a0a1045feedf76d35d654a79bd-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792069232</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Lead">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between lead and phosphogypsum is defined by the presence of lead as a heavy metal impurity within the phosphogypsum matrix. Tabular data confirms that phosphogypsum contains lead at concentrations significantly exceeding geological averages, though these levels remain below the rare effect concentration. Within the material, lead exists primarily as heavy metal ions and insoluble precipitates, with a distinct tendency to concentrate in the coarser grain size fractions.

Despite being classified as a toxic metal that poses potential environmental risks, lead exhibits intermediate mobility within phosphogypsum. The formation of insoluble precipitates substantially restricts its release rate into the surrounding environment. Conversely, the chemical properties of phosphogypsum and its slag byproducts are utilized in environmental remediation, where cementitious materials derived from phosphogypsum are applied to stabilize and treat lead-contaminated soils. Consequently, the interaction encompasses both the retention characteristics of lead within the phosphogypsum structure and its practical application in mitigating environmental contamination.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,contains,distribution,hazard,immobilization,mobility classification,preferential retention,presence,release rate,remediation,threshold compliance,toxic metal,trace content,trace element</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f6434914b6de99019386e4bdcbc57e-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792042025</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Nickel">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains nickel, a heavy metal that poses environmental risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a trace element analyzed in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains nickel at concentrations lower than the rare effect concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains nickel as indicated in the tabular data.</data>
