<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Bricks">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Bricks, Phosphogypsum) encompasses the utilization of phosphogypsum as a key material in brick manufacturing. Phosphogypsum can serve as a primary raw material, a supplementary component, or an additive during production. This integration applies to various brick types, including both fired and clay bricks.

The incorporation of phosphogypsum into brick production is proposed as a method for large-scale waste utilization, which significantly enhances resource efficiency. Additionally, the material can be used in manufacturing processes that maintain low radiation exposure risks, ensuring its application remains both sustainable and safe for industrial use.</data>
  <data key="d9">additive,application,application pathway,composition,construction,manufacturing,material application,material composition,material integration,raw material</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-019</data>
