<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Table 3">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Phosphogypsum and Table 3 provides a comprehensive overview of the material's chemical, thermal, environmental, and industrial properties. Chemically, it presents analytical data on the major element composition, including the mass fractions of primary elements alongside specific P2O5 and Fluorine contents typical of the samples. The table also examines impurities by detailing their various existence forms and associated harmful effects, while tracking the composition of major species and impurities both before and after treatment. Furthermore, it documents post-treatment compositional changes using X-ray diffraction (XRD) analysis following exposure to various reagents. Regarding thermal behavior, the table outlines the temperature values and characterizes the nature of each thermal transformation the material undergoes.

On an application and global scale, the relation outlines the primary benefits and environmental risks associated with Phosphogypsum applications. It also supplies worldwide statistical data covering the generation, disposal, and utilization of Phosphogypsum across different countries, offering a broad perspective on its industrial footprint and management practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 3 lists the chemical species examined using LA-ICP-MS in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 3 documents the trace element composition of minerals in phosphogypsum.</data>
