<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Hubei Province">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hubei Province ranks second in phosphogypsum utilization rates, with substantial improvements driven by regional policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province is a major producer of phosphogypsum within the Yangtze River Basin.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province produces phosphogypsum characterized by high silicon dioxide, phosphorus pentoxide, and fluoride content.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province focuses on utilizing phosphogypsum for cement retardants and building materials due to convenient transportation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province is a major production area for phosphogypsum due to its rich phosphate rock resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province serves as a primary regional focus for tracking phosphogypsum production and utilization metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;Hubei Province is a location where phosphogypsum samples were collected.</data>
  <data key="d9">building materials,chemical composition,data tracking,location,policy implementation,production concentration,production location,regional focus,regional production,resource concentration,sample source,utilization focus,utilization rate</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791900900</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Yunnan Province">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum in Yunnan Province represents a significant industrial byproduct within China, where the region stands as a major production area. The phosphogypsum generated in Yunnan is distinguished by its high purity, specifically characterized by low concentrations of iron(III) oxide, aluminum oxide, and other overall impurities. Due to its substantial output and distinct material properties, Yunnan Province serves as a key regional focus for monitoring phosphogypsum production and utilization metrics, and it has been a designated location for the systematic collection of phosphogypsum samples.

Despite its status as a leading producer, Yunnan Province encounters notable challenges in phosphogypsum management, primarily due to limited local market capacity and relatively low comprehensive utilization rates when compared to other regions within the basin. To address these constraints, the region has widely adopted phosphogypsum filling technology as a primary disposal and reuse method. Concurrently, Yunnan Province places a strong strategic emphasis on advancing the high-value utilization of this material, actively promoting its application in ecological restoration projects and the manufacturing of building materials to improve overall resource efficiency and environmental outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum was obtained from Yunnan Province, China.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,data tracking,ecological restoration,geographic adoption,location,low efficiency,production concentration,production location,regional focus,regional production,resource concentration,sample source,source location,utilization focus,utilization rate</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-afe70f2d82515df80906bf3babd4e4eb-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b19ca721a4da4422ee10228d88a4c292-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1792099334</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
