<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Wet Phosphoric Acid Process">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Wet Phosphoric Acid Process is a chemical method that generates phosphogypsum as a primary solid waste byproduct. This industrial pathway fundamentally determines the major elemental composition and characteristic morphology of the resulting material. Due to the specific chemical reactions inherent to the process, the produced phosphogypsum consistently exhibits high impurity levels.

Additionally, the Wet Phosphoric Acid Process disrupts natural radioactive equilibrium, effectively partitioning various radionuclides into the phosphogypsum. Consequently, the relationship between the Wet Phosphoric Acid Process and phosphogypsum is defined by the former's role as the standard manufacturing method that chemically yields this solid waste, while simultaneously governing its physical structure, chemical makeup, impurity profile, and radiological characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d9">by-product generation,byproduct generation,compositional influence,impurity generation,phase partitioning,production,production method,production methodology</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7797768798fcd1152bdc10ff73139e35-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791774154</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
