<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Radon-222">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains elevated levels of radon-222 radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;Radon-222 is exhaled from phosphogypsum stacks, with emission rates varying by several orders of magnitude.&lt;SEP&gt;Radon-222 exhalation occurs from phosphogypsum fractions, with rates decreasing in coarser fractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum serves as a source of Radon-222 exhalation, necessitating careful radiological evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum stacks are studied as sources of radon-222 transport into open air.&lt;SEP&gt;Radon-222 exhalation rate is measured to evaluate radiological risks associated with phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d9">composition,emission source,exhalation,exhalation source,impurity,radioactive emission,radiological hazard,transport modeling</data>
