<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Soluble Phosphorus">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum and soluble phosphorus are characterized by the latter's role as a primary and highly significant impurity within the former. Soluble phosphorus constitutes one of the main phosphorus forms naturally present in phosphogypsum and is consistently identified as a key contaminant. Its presence fundamentally alters the material's properties and handling requirements.

From an industrial and environmental standpoint, soluble phosphorus poses notable challenges. In construction applications, it adversely affects the reuse of phosphogypsum by significantly increasing the gelling time of building materials. Additionally, it presents a potential environmental hazard due to its tendency to leach into surrounding ecosystems. To mitigate these issues, the concentration of soluble phosphorus can be effectively reduced through calcination-modified treatment processes, thereby improving the material's suitability for various applications.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical composition,chemical form,composition,contains,contaminant,environmental hazard,impurity,impurity form,impurity presence,limitation,reduction target</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98d8b2df45924e721bfa570f652f33e3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9c8cdabf609cc047d173d4ff8dbb5187-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ac8d630b9aa4d874707445e2552a09-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791774249</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
