<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sodium Chloride">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sodium chloride solutions are used to treat phosphogypsum for rare earth concentrate production.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride solutions significantly increase the solubility of phosphogypsum compared to pure water.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride in saline water is used to wash phosphogypsum and remove water-soluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium chloride is used to study phosphogypsum solubility, with high solubility attributed to ionic strength effects.</data>
  <data key="d9">impurity removal,ionic strength,pre-treatment,purification,solubility enhancement,solubility study,solvent,treatment reagent</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791594892</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Sodium Carbonate">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sodium carbonate solutions are used to treat phosphogypsum for rare earth concentrate production.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate is used in a carbonated solution to treat phosphogypsum, solubilizing water-soluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate is utilized as a leaching reagent for phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate is used as a leaching reagent on phosphogypsum, increasing the relative proportion of radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate is used to treat phosphogypsum, producing calcium sulfate hemihydrate and lanthanum silicate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate treatment transforms phosphogypsum into hemihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium carbonate is applied to phosphogypsum to reduce radionuclide concentration to 0.600 wt%.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical transformation,chemical treatment,impurity removal,leaching,leaching reagent,pre-treatment,purification,radionuclide reduction,transformation,treatment,treatment reagent,treats</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-e1871f90fba8192d1aa537b2a9f4555c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28fbd4302bba090e667215c840757ff7-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791917675</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
