</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Brick Production">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Brick Production and Phosphogypsum centers on the utilization of phosphogypsum waste as an alternative raw material in the manufacturing of bricks. In this industrial process, phosphogypsum is incorporated into conventional brick formulations to replace a portion of traditional ingredients, specifically clay and sand. This application functions as an alternative waste management strategy for phosphogypsum, effectively valorizing the byproduct and yielding significant material and resource savings.

Despite these economic and resource benefits, brick production utilizing phosphogypsum is ranked as the third most preferred management method for phosphogypsum waste. This lower ranking is primarily attributed to the process's higher environmental footprint and associated negative environmental impacts. Nevertheless, the method remains a recognized practice where the substantial resource savings help offset these environmental drawbacks, establishing a functional, albeit environmentally complex, synergy between brick manufacturing and phosphogypsum waste management.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative method,application,environmental performance,industrial application,management,material substitution,material usage,ranking,recycling,utilization,valorization,waste management,waste utilization,waste valorization</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0060991ac74a9675ce0293eccdc023cd-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
