<edge source="Gypsum" target="Rare Earth Elements">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The gypsum matrix structurally contains Rare Earth Elements, which are released only upon its dissolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Strong chemical bonds between gypsum crystals and rare earth elements explain the low recovery rates in direct leaching.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum serves as the primary vector and surface host for Rare Earth Elements in the studied samples.&lt;SEP&gt;The majority of rare earth elements in phosphogypsum are associated with the gypsum phase.</data>
  <data key="d9">association,chemical bonding,elemental deportment,extraction barrier,primary vector,structural containment,surface hosting</data>
