<edge source="Rare Earth Elements" target="Acid Leaching">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Acid leaching (Rare Earth Elements) is a primary chemical method utilized for the extraction, dissolution, and recovery of rare earth elements from various industrial byproducts and mineral deposits. This process is predominantly applied to phosphogypsum, but it is also effectively employed to recover valuable rare earth elements from phosphate rock and other mineral sources. By utilizing acidic solutions, the technique successfully breaks down these materials to isolate the targeted elements.

In addition to initial extraction, acid leaching serves a critical purification role in the processing chain. The method refines the dissolved rare earth solutions, achieving high-grade outputs with purity levels ranging from 97% to 99%. Through this dual function of extraction and purification, acid leaching provides a reliable pathway for recovering and concentrating rare earth elements from both waste streams and conventional mineral ores.</data>
  <data key="d9">dissolution process,extraction,extraction method,extraction process,extraction target,processing,purification,recovery,recovery process,target,target recovery</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb86340ba0851c06e97600104fca25c9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5d09b48f57a4e888bb729aaf988c936-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791613229</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
