<edge source="Rare Earth Elements" target="Isomorphous Substitution">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Isomorphous Substitution governs the occurrence state of Rare Earth Elements embedded in the gypsum structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earth elements occur in phosphogypsum in the form of isomorphous substitution within the mineral matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Isomorphous substitution describes one of the three chemical states where rare earth elements are integrated into the phosphogypsum structure.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical binding,chemical structure,governs,occurrence state</data>
