<edge source="Cu(II)" target="HAP-BC">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">HAP-BC adsorbs Cu(II) ions with a higher maximum capacity than unmodified BC.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC is used as an adsorbent to remove Cu(II) ions from solution.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC removes Cu(II) ions primarily through electrostatic interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Cu(II) ions with a maximum capacity of 854.70 mg/g in the ternary system.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC adsorbs Cu(II) in multilayers, with removal capacity slightly affected by ionic strength variations.&lt;SEP&gt;HAP-BC effectively adsorbs and removes Cu(II) ions from water solutions.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,capacity measurement,electrostatic interaction,enhanced capacity,heavy metal removal,multilayer formation,removal</data>
