<edge source="Water" target="Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hydroxyapatite decomposition yields water as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Water participates as both a reactant and a product in the hydrothermal conversion reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Water, in the form of OH groups, is a chemical component present within the hydroxyapatite structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is the sole by-product of the hydroxyapatite synthesis reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is the sole byproduct generated during the synthesis of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Nanoscale hydroxyapatite contains considerable amounts of structural and adsorbed water, reaching up to 10 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;The dehydroxylation of Hydroxyapatite releases Water during high-temperature calcination.</data>
  <data key="d9">by-product,byproduct,byproduct formation,composition,decomposition,product,reactant,reaction output,structural content,synthesis,thermal decomposition</data>
