<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Calcium">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Calcium is the original element in the hydroxyapatite crystal that is replaced by titanium.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium serves as a primary precursor combined with phosphate to synthesize Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium ions form part of the hydroxyapatite structure, though biological apatites often exhibit calcium deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The presence of Calcium is consistent with the sample being Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium is detected as a major element in the Hydroxyapatite sample via EDX analysis.</data>
