</edge>
<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="X-Ray Diffraction">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">X-Ray Diffraction is employed to characterize the crystalline structure of synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-Ray Diffraction is used to characterize the crystal structure of hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-Ray Diffraction is used to validate the formation and determine the crystal phase of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-Ray Diffraction is used to analyze the hexagonal structure and crystallite size of Hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray diffraction is employed to verify the phase purity and crystal structure of the synthesized hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite powders are analyzed using X-ray diffraction to determine crystallite structure and size.</data>
  <data key="d9">analysis,characterization,crystallite size,phase identification,structural analysis,validation</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f2534f7a997df3f80305323317b15be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4d02158bbc770d7c6bd9657b3f3defc-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f5dcf59bedaa00614f1acc222b1fb7b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6825862084b162a4b16cd1037c76e3d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4a38fcc1b0f33a17d23e7a4407a9cf9-chunk-003</data>
