<edge source="Hydroxyapatite" target="Nickel">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hydroxyapatite removes nickel ions primarily through an ion exchange mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a heavy metal whose sorption mechanism in the presence of hydroxyapatite has been studied in literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Nickel is a metal dopant incorporated into hydroxyapatite, resulting in slower degradation of 17α-methyltestosterone compared to undoped hydroxyapatite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is doped with Nickel to enhance its photocatalytic activity.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption study,doping,heavy metal,ion exchange,material modification,performance comparison,removal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5563c80c4fd1f68b4442f73621a281-chunk-016</data>
