<edge source="Fluoride" target="Groundwater">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fluoride and other mobile anions from phosphogypsum pose a risk of groundwater pollution if leached downwards.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride concentrations up to 32 mg/l were detected in groundwater, far exceeding background levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride is released into groundwater as a liquid emission.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluoride from phosphogypsum readily migrates into groundwater through leaching processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorides from phosphogypsum leach into and migrate through groundwater.</data>
