<edge source="Uranium-238" target="Radium-226">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Radium-226 and Uranium-238 share a direct parent-daughter relationship within a natural radioactive decay series, wherein Uranium-238 acts as the parent nuclide that decays into Radium-226. This fundamental isotopic connection is routinely utilized to evaluate radioactive equilibrium conditions, with researchers frequently pairing the two elements to compute the Radium-226 to Uranium-238 Activity Ratio.

The activity levels between these isotopes are highly context-dependent, reflecting varying degrees of secular equilibrium across different materials. In undisturbed geological formations and Florida phosphate ore, Uranium-238 and Radium-226 typically maintain equal activity levels, indicating a state of approximate secular equilibrium. A similar balance occurs in phosphogypsum, where Uranium-238 activity can match that of Radium-226, a phenomenon that has prompted significant environmental concerns. In contrast, certain waste samples exhibit an activity ratio below unity, demonstrating that the equilibrium state is not universally preserved. Collectively, these variations underscore the utility of monitoring the Radium-226 and Uranium-238 relationship as a precise indicator of radioactive decay processes and material-specific environmental radioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is a direct decay product of uranium-238.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity equivalence,activity ratio,decay,decay chain,decay sequence,environmental concern,equal activity,equilibrium indicator,forms,parent-daughter,progeny,radioactive balance,radioactive decay,relationship,secular equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70650e5cb032fce744763706d8701e36-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c4b1b446b8362051476593a7c1a0d7c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791429304</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
