</edge>
<edge source="Radium-226" target="Bismuth-214">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Radium-226 decays into Bismuth-214, which is used alongside Lead-214 for activity concentration determination.&lt;SEP&gt;Bismuth-214 emission lines are used to determine the activity concentration of Radium-226.&lt;SEP&gt;Bismuth-214 is used alongside Lead-214 to estimate Radium-226 activity concentrations in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is measured via its decay product Bismuth-214.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is measured in equilibrium with Lead-214 and Bismuth-214.</data>
  <data key="d9">activity derivation,analytical method,daughter isotope,decay chain,decay product,equilibrium,isotope correlation,measurement association,radioactive decay</data>
