<edge source="BC" target="Pb(II)">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">BC adsorbs Pb(II) ions, with the interaction fitting the Langmuir Isotherm Model.&lt;SEP&gt;BC is used as an adsorbent to remove Pb(II) ions from solution.&lt;SEP&gt;BC adsorbs Pb(II) ions from mixed solutions primarily through electrostatic interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;BC adsorbs Pb(II) ions with a maximum capacity of 438.60 mg/g in the ternary system.&lt;SEP&gt;Pb(II) likely forms monolayer coverage on BC.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,adsorption mechanism,capacity measurement,heavy metal removal,monolayer modeling,removal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791289149</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="BC" target="Zn(II)">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">BC adsorbs Zn(II) ions, with the interaction fitting the Freundlich Isotherm Model.&lt;SEP&gt;BC is used as an adsorbent to remove Zn(II) ions from solution.&lt;SEP&gt;BC adsorbs Zn(II) ions from mixed solutions primarily through electrostatic interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;BC adsorbs Zn(II) ions with a maximum capacity of 840.34 mg/g in the ternary system.&lt;SEP&gt;Zn(II) is adsorbed in multilayers on BC.</data>
  <data key="d9">adsorption,adsorption mechanism,capacity measurement,heavy metal removal,multilayer modeling,removal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e17ad262bd9835860df552d7ff475f1-chunk-006</data>
